{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles","id":416,"title":"The Wolf Must Hunt: What do you want to see in Idigam Chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T13:17:25-07:00","id":416,"title":"The Wolf Must Hunt: What do you want to see in Idigam Chronicles?","content":"With <span style=\"color:#993300\"><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b></span> receiving its own Chronicle treatment, what do you want to see in <span style=\"color:#993300\"><b>Idigam Chronicles</b></span>? Lots of powerful new foes like the Idigam? More focus on the dual-duality of Man/Wolf, Flesh/Spirit? More cowbell? What's on your mind for this, and what would make an already great game even better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:18:13-07:00","id":479,"title":"","content":"Here are some of the ideas I posted on the other forum. I'd rather not lose them, so here they are, hunting in a new territory.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Wolf. Emphasize it. This is one of the things I love that <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> did, really putting the &quot;wolf&quot; in &quot;werewolf.&quot; I'd take it a bit further, emphasizing instincts, primal animism and the savagery of nature in the World of Darkness. Not just running around the woods, mind. On <i>both</i> sides of the Gauntlet even in cities is a rich ecosystem of predators, prey, territories and struggles \u2014 and I mean humans, spirits, werewolves and other things.<br /> \u2022 Abominations. No, not vampiric Lupines. Stuff like magath should be more common in this unbalanced post-Urfarah world. I might make it easier for them to escape into the material world. Wolf packs hunt large, dangerous prey. Werewolf packs hunt large, dangerous supernatural prey.<br /> \u2022 Magic. One of the big advantages of werewolves over spirits is the versatility of their magic, born of Flesh and Spirit. They adapt. They're fluid. They're shapeshifters \u2014 Luna is ever-changing, and werewolves inherit some of mama's magical prowess. They can learn from spirits, they can develop their own tricks, they are dangerous in that way.<br /> \u2022 The Shadow. I love it. Looooove it. Emphasize it more right from the get-go, with detailed information on how things work there. If it was up to me, I'd change some of the dynamic. Most spirits wouldn't automatically hate werewolves, and Forsaken would in turn be more powerful overall. Mid-rank spirits are still a big threat, and higher-level ones can't be beaten by brute force, but even weaker spirits would be more populous and impossible to control through savagery alone. No pack could hope to control their territory just by killing everything they felt like it and browbeating everything into submission. Same thing goes for spirits, too.<br /> \u2022 The Shadow, pt. 2. Make it integral, as it is in <b>Forsaken</b>, but make it more apparent in what you do and how it fits into a territory and your chronicle. Explore how werewolves gain power and influence in the mortal world by gaining it in the spirit world, and how they grow into lords of their domain through such efforts.<br /> \u2022 Savage fury. Werewolves are hunters, yes. They don't need to be capable of individually tearing apart everything in the world. Still, make them stronger, deadlier, a scary-ass thing to face even one-on-one. Facing a whole pack? You'd better <i>bring it</i>, because they're gonna tear you up. For Gauru in particular, this means either making it usable all the time or giving it <i>much</i> more of an impact in the short while it's used. I favor the latter.<br /> <br /> Oh, another thing I think I'll suggest: shapeshifting should be automatic under normal circumstances. Werewolves are all about shapeshifting. It's what they do. Cutting down on unnecessary rolls works well for play, and also it removes a potential denial of getting to be cool. I mean, where is the fun in wanting to change forms into a wolf and failing because you failed the roll? Werewolves shouldn't have to worry about that except under extreme duress. Otherwise, I think it should just be automatic, though it'd still take an instant action unless Essence is spent. And probably not automatic into Gauru form, but that depends on what ends up happening with Gauru. Partial changes should, I think, still require a roll, because that's a lot trickier.<br /> <br /> And I mean extreme by &quot;extreme duress.&quot; Werewolves are no strangers to hunting and combat. Even normal fights and such shouldn't give you so much trouble that you can't instinctually shapeshift. Guys blasting off silver rounds at you while a train thunders by, deafening your lupine senses? Okay, that works. And that's when you spend Essence for a little something extra, because you can't afford the time it takes to shapeshift normally, anyway.<br /> <br /> On Requiem and Masquerade equivalents:<br /> <br /> Reason: This is the face of reason, the influence of Man. Werewolves let this side of their existence guide them in the mortal world, because Man's world is the domain of Reason. It's how inhuman predators keep from falling into unthinking savagery, and how the Uratha use their unique heritage to their advantage. Clever and adaptable is Man the Monkey, and werewolves use that ingenuity to master their world in ways spirits cannot.<br /> <br /> When a werewolf lets Reason find a solution to a problem brute force would only aggravate, she gains a point of Willpower. When committing terrible acts that defy the Harmony of the predator, she regains all spent Willpower points.<br /> <br /> Instinct: The Wolf lurks just beneath the surface and its instincts are strong. Survive, prosper, hunt. A werewolf is born on not one but two axes, Man and Wolf, Spirit and Flesh. Both her Wolf side and her spiritual side are primal, connected to the ancient heartbeat of the world. Wise werewolves learn to trust their instincts, honed over millennia, making them the finest hunters the world has ever known.<br /> <br /> When an Uratha embraces her instinctual side and rejects the tools of Man to overcome a problem, she gains a point of Willpower. If instead she lets instinct dominate her mind in the desperation of survival, she regains all spent Willpower points.<br /> <br /> You are a creature of not just duality, but two kinds of duality set along two different axes: Man and Wolf, Spirit and Flesh. It'd be a shame not to play that up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:46:21-07:00","id":529,"title":"","content":"Here's my list, copied from the old forums:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Splats</b>:<br /> <br /> I'd like to see Auspices reworked to resemble core werewolf archetypes; much like how Venture are the lordly Count Dracula types of vampire and Deeva are the sexy vampires. I would phrase this as Luna giving a Blessing/Curse to each werewolf. It really depends on your point of view (but Forsaken typically say that they're blessings).<br /> <br /> The Y-Splat would be your role in the pack, and would strongly resemble the current Asupices. This does mean that each Archetype would have to be broad enough to cover all five roles, so some tweaks may be required. E.G. the werewolf as a savage monster driven only to hunt is a strong archetype, but dialling it back just a bit to &quot;boundless passion and energy&quot; creates something that can be that savage beast but also a scout or a diplomat.<br /> <br /> For Lodges I'd like to see them as Werewolf university rather than large projects. You don't join a Lodge, you graduate from a Lodge. In addition graduating from a Lodge will give your entire pack bonuses so they can join in your new fun. For example: The Lodge of the Purifying Atom deal with Wounds, like radiation sterilises medical equipment. Graduates get an awesome wound sterilisation power and a passive defence so they can enter wounds and use it, their pack gets the passive defence so that they can also enter wounds and assist.<br /> <br /> Finally, I would like the pack to have it's own splat separate from the individual member's splat. Tribe could work here. The pack's splat would set the goal for the pack. Since Werewolves theme has the strongest bonds between PCs having an extra splat choice that every PC shares would strengthen that theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers:</b><br /> <br /> I'd like to see Werewolves' powers split into Gifts and Instincts:<br /> <br /> Instincts would be anything archetypically werewolf. At the very least: Hunting, tracking, super-senses, fighting and forming a pack. Probably more. A Werewolf can learn instincts through practice and experimentation or being shown by an older werewolf. Instincts also let all the people who want less Spirit in there werewolves hit the important archetypical powers without ever speaking to spirit without making Spirits any lesser for people who like them.<br /> <br /> Gifts would be mostly unchanged, though LOOK would be in charge of writing them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I might have more to say about indiivudal Gifts but in general I would want them to come from Spirits, but not just from begging or buying them. There should be at least five different ways to get a Gift. One for each of the (pre-GMC) Asuprices. E.G. Sneak up to Serpent and steal it's skin.<br /> <br /> Rituals: I'd like to see a Blood Sorcery style update to Rituals based around bargaining with the spirits for miracles. It would need to hit the perfect balance, the spirits personality and wishes should matter, but the Werewolves shouldn't feel like they have to beg for magic while vampires and Mages run around doing cool stuff. I'd try and portray Werewolves as spirit millionares, yes they have to haggle the essence price but they control the territory, the loci, so whatever the final price is they can probably afford it. (I've written rules for this already <img src=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/Images/Emoticons/emotion-1.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>And the big one: Territory</b><br /> <br /> This is I think the most important one on my list. I think the Chronicles should include both fluff and mechanics to answer the following questions:<ul><li>What is a healthy spiritual ecosystem in harmony with the material?</li> <li>How do you create a healthy spiritual ecosystem.</li> <li>Why do you want a healthy spiritual ecosystem.</li> <li>How do you shape a healthy ecosystem to your packs taste and what are the benefits of doing so?</li> <li>You love your territory's ecosystem. How do you make it better yet the same?</li> <li>What is an unhealthy ecosystem.</li> <li>How is an unhealthy ecosystem created.</li> <li>Why is an unhealthy ecosystem bad.</li> <li>Why would werewolves want an unhealthy ecosystem anyway?</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T00:10:09-07:00","id":971,"title":"","content":"Definitely more cowbell. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:58:23-07:00","id":1316,"title":"","content":"A thorough treatment of Gifts and Renown, and how, but also <i>why</i> they interact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T15:21:59-07:00","id":1329,"title":"","content":"As well as the Wolf Blood families being more of a &quot;thing&quot; I'd quite like the topology of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Additionally I'd quite like the topology of the spirit world to be dealt with more. As well as the basic not-reflection of the material, I'd like it explored (heh) how werewolves can go on a spirit journey, to the deep dark places of the Shadow which doesn't have a material reflection.Giving me somewhere to start would be grand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T15:27:55-07:00","id":1331,"title":"","content":"You know, I'd quite like it if Werewolves could have children together and packs of mom, dad and the kids were common. Not exclusive, but common. (Being creatures of primal passion, wild oats will be common after all)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T16:09:18-07:00","id":1351,"title":"","content":"Make the WAR FORM actually mean what it implies and make it the go to combat form by first removing that time limit. Seriously, I've been thinking about this for some time and honsetly, there's absolutly no reason why the Gauru form should have a time limit and such. What's the point? If this revamp is going to do for Forsaken what Blood &amp; Smoke did for Requiem, then just flat out remove this silly drawback. No need to gimp something for no reason. Heck, I'm still not entirely sure why this was put in the game in the first place. Do Gauru a favor and get rid of those limits.<br /> <br /> Whew, glad I got that off my chest.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But seriously, that's the one thing I'd be the happiest to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:15:13-07:00","id":1392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1351#post1351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Gauru a favor and get rid of those limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I am fond of the *risk* of going into Gauru, that &quot;will I rip this guy to shreds, or we I rip my packmate&quot; question is interesting. Plus it and the Rage (not the book) is definately one of the areas that makes this a werewolf game. Vampire have the incredible hunger. Werewolves should have that unlimited Rage, and by extension the most recognisable form should be linked to the Rage.<br /> <br /> That said, a more mechanically scary Gauru would be nice.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:37:19-07:00","id":1405,"title":"","content":"I see two options for Gauru, really:<br /> <br /> 1) It remains mostly as it is in power level, not much stronger than Urshul. But in return, it can be maintained mostly indefinitely and you're not totally so angry you can't concentrate on stuff. It's used for rituals, and isn't as fast as Urshul but has hands and so on.<br /> 2) Unleashing Gauru is unleashing a fraction of the mighty Rage that burned within Father Wolf's breast. Even your packmates worry a little when you Rage. It is power. It is killing instinct personified. Wolf and Spirit lash out with every instinct they have. This is an echo of Urfarah the Destroyer, Urfarah the greatest hunter to ever walk the Earth. I want this raw, bloody, primal in every way. This is power and fury. This is not something you take on lightly, because you weren't meant to handle this kind of ferocity like Father Wolf was. It's fucking <i>scary</i>, something the others herd your prey into fighting. That kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:22:15-07:00","id":1424,"title":"","content":"My shopping list is massive on this end (and I don't feel like reiterating it too wholesale from the old forum), but I'm already working on a revamp/overhaul with my Co-ST for the TT and Larp we run to cover those bases. Still lets start with a couple, and go from there later:<br /> <br /> -Get rid of Renown. It's a tacked on system. It's a holdover. It's one of the, if not -the- most complained about aspect of W:tF I've ran into. It's unwieldy. What it's presented to do makes little to no sense in the spiritual concept, especially regarding effective rank. As a power cap it makes even -less- sense. It's precepts make little sense in regards to the Shadow and Spirits as a whole. Look at merits like Mantle; Danse Macabre's Status merits and similar. That's more on track. I could get into this much, much more in-depth but lets leave this as is for now and move on.<br /> <br /> -Emphasis on Werewolves as hunters of -man- and -beast-. Enough pussyfooting around; they should be a threat to humans, humans shouldn't be a gross exception on the menu of prey items. They're common available prey with Essence, even compared to wolves. Spirits eat things related in concept. Werewolves shouldn't be treating it with quite the level of taboo they are. Flesh addiction much like Vitae addiction should be around. And to emphasize these, the mind-bogglingly -easy- and -abundant- ways werewolves gain Essence should be curtailed. Hunting and eating others should be the focus for this, not farming Essence batteries and hokey rites. Right now there's little incentive or reason for them to be threats to humans, or humans to be relevant. Lets make them what they are; vicious hunters. Things to fear, things humans told horror stories about for a reason. I'm not really getting that enough. There's a reason a lot of new players I find find a disconnect with that game. &quot;Wait, I thought I was playing a werewolf? Why am I a furry spirit cop?&quot;. Probably because unlike vampire, it's resemblance to folks expectations is minimal. If you're trying to -sell- the game, you need something more to latch onto coming from the popular culture and mythological references that people consider intrinsic to the critter.<br /> <br /> Claire Redfield has posted some ideas that I find help reinforce the tug of instinct and ones manifold nature, but I want it to go further. I also want it to be far more savage in regards to humans and the threats werewolves pose to them (and vice versa for that matter).<br /> <br /> -Get rid of Lunacy, flat out. Another bad holdover and system that outright neuters the human threat to werewolves. I've used the system in place from War Against the Pure with other shapeshifters for some time, and even that I've found... isn't necessary. Werewolves should have to be careful about donning their other forms. It should be a -risk- to go into Death Rage above and beyond the usual facts. This build in Jedi-mind-trick is bad baggage. I'd like to see things like this partially dovetailed into the Predatory Aura, and something you specifically target an -individual- with. Making them feel like prey, instinctively fleeing if they get the condition. Mind recoiling in abject terror of being eaten and panicked flight, perhaps with skewed memories due to terror... things like that. &quot;The Secret Must be Kept&quot; is kind of a farce with this in place, and I can safely say the treatment I've seen from Lunacy in regards to Veil issues is that it makes them hardly an issue at all, both from personal experience and the statements of others. Just. Get. Rid. Of. It. There are better ways of treating it beyond an ever present mind-wipe/debuffer, and Predatory Auras are on the right track.<br /> <br /> There's quite a few more, but these two are what come first to mind. Things like adjusting the power sets, form tweaks (I'm in the camp that outside of a couple mild adjustments, Gauru form is more than fine as is as far as it's overall stats and duration, though I've seen a couple ways to extend the duration with cumulative Death Rage penalties that I've liked quite a bit), emphasizing Wolf-blooded and diversifying them more, the issues as is between the Pure and Forsaken and quite a few more I'll tackle later.<br /> <br /> When things are a bit more complete and ready on our end to playtest, we'll fire them up on these forums for perusal; pretty much everything I want to see in Idigam Chronicles we're already reworking into the game during the wait and in case, you know, it doesn't give us what works best for our games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T19:35:34-07:00","id":1448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1392#post1392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, I am fond of the *risk* of going into Gauru, that &quot;will I rip this guy to shreds, or we I rip my packmate&quot; question is interesting. Plus it and the Rage (not the book) is definately one of the areas that makes this a werewolf game. Vampire have the incredible hunger. Werewolves should have that unlimited Rage, and by extension the most recognisable form should be linked to the Rage.<br /> <br /> That said, a more mechanically scary Gauru would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't get me wrong. I think Rage is an awewsome thing and I don't want it to go away. Very much an aspect of being a Werewolf. I just don't want it to be at the expense of one of my forms. Let alone my most powerful. You can keep Rage and still have a functioning War Form. The more I go over it, the more I see no need for such a weakness. The only thing stopping me from house ruling such a thing is Rage Gifts. That's it. There is no other reason to have a time limit for Gauru, at least from what I've seen. Get rid of Rage Gifts, and the last two Half Moon Gifts, and BOOM! You have no justification for Gauru having such a drawback.<br /> <br /> However, if Gauru is still subject to a time limit in Idigam Chronicle, then I to would like to see it beefed up to make up for it. But at the end of the day, I can no longer see any justification in Gauru being so limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T04:02:38-08:00","id":1651,"title":"","content":"Rahuman101, so if you were writing the Idigam Chronicles Gauru form, how would you put the Rage and an unlimited time Gauru form together?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1405#post1405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2) Unleashing Gauru is unleashing a fraction of the mighty Rage that burned within Father Wolf's breast. Even your packmates worry a little when you Rage. It is power. It is killing instinct personified. Wolf and Spirit lash out with every instinct they have. This is an echo of Urfarah the Destroyer, Urfarah the greatest hunter to ever walk the Earth. I want this raw, bloody, primal in every way. This is power and fury. This is not something you take on lightly, because you weren't meant to handle this kind of ferocity like Father Wolf was. It's fucking <i>scary</i>, something the others herd your prey into fighting. That kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was imagining the perfect Gauru form to be. It's not just powerful, but damn well frightening.<br /> <br /> <b>Mental tangent time</b>: Although maybe each Tribe has a different 'flavour' of Gauru, the Blood Talon form is definately the most destructive, but the Bone Shadow Gauru is more like the inevitablity of death, scary but in different ways. To be honest, I don't even need mechanical differences for these (although Tribal Instincts could do the job) - a short discussion in the book to what this different forms are when you take a Tirbal Totem bond (which is, when you think about it, a big supernatural covenant).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To be clear, I'm not against a time limit for Gauru, but I would like to keep the dangers of it, I think it's keeping with Forsaken that your biggist and nastiest form is a risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T10:12:25-08:00","id":1858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1651#post1651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rahuman101, so if you were writing the Idigam Chronicles Gauru form, how would you put the Rage and an unlimited time Gauru form together?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good question. If I were to do it, I'd use one of two different but similar options.<br /> <br /> Option1: Use the rules in Alec Humphrey's (aka LOOK on the White Wolf forums) Werewolf the Forsaken House Rules google document. With this rule, Gauru can be assumed as often as one likes and be held for as long as one likes. However, being in Gauru form imposes a -3 penalty to resist Death Rage and your Harmony is considered two lower when seeing what stimulis might triigger Death Rage. When Death Rage is triggerd, the player rolls Harmony + Purity Renown to resist. If a Dramatic Failure, you enter Death Rage and attack all present for the scene. Packmates included. If a Failure, Enter Death Rage, but attack enemies first then packmates for the scene. If a Success, enter a Controled Rage. This is mechanically the same thing as Gauru as we know it now. Can only attack or move towards an opponent, ignores wound penalties, etc,etc. You even have a time limit of sorts. You have until Harmony + Primal Urge turns to either escape from your source of Rage or destroy said source before you enter Death Rage as if you failed the roll. On an Exceptional Success, you don't Rage at all.<br /> <br /> Option 2: Use the rules found in the Werewolf Translation Guide for untimed Gauru and Frenzy. Failure means Death Rage, Succes means Gauru as we know it. Otherwise, it's kinda similar to LOOK's idea above.<br /> <br /> Out of the two presented above, I'm more fond of the former. But yeah, this is what I'd do. So you see, it is possible to have Rage without screwing over your most powerful form.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T12:11:54-08:00","id":1937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1651#post1651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mental tangent time</b>: Although maybe each Tribe has a different 'flavour' of Gauru, the Blood Talon form is definately the most destructive, but the Bone Shadow Gauru is more like the inevitablity of death, scary but in different ways. To be honest, I don't even need mechanical differences for these (although Tribal Instincts could do the job) - a short discussion in the book to what this different forms are when you take a Tirbal Totem bond (which is, when you think about it, a big supernatural covenant).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really quite like this idea and would like to see that get some more traction.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T13:25:41-08:00","id":1992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1424#post1424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Get rid of Renown. It's a tacked on system. It's a holdover. It's one of the, if not -the- most complained about aspect of W:tF I've ran into. It's unwieldy. What it's presented to do makes little to no sense in the spiritual concept, especially regarding effective rank. As a power cap it makes even -less- sense. It's precepts make little sense in regards to the Shadow and Spirits as a whole. Look at merits like Mantle; Danse Macabre's Status merits and similar. That's more on track. I could get into this much, much more in-depth but lets leave this as is for now and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or renown could be an extra. If your PC does something super special awesome he should get renown but renown being something not necessary at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1424#post1424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Get rid of Lunacy, flat out. Another bad holdover and system that outright neuters the human threat to werewolves. I've used the system in place from War Against the Pure with other shapeshifters for some time, and even that I've found... isn't necessary. Werewolves should have to be careful about donning their other forms. It should be a -risk- to go into Death Rage above and beyond the usual facts. This build in Jedi-mind-trick is bad baggage. I'd like to see things like this partially dovetailed into the Predatory Aura, and something you specifically target an -individual- with. Making them feel like prey, instinctively fleeing if they get the condition. Mind recoiling in abject terror of being eaten and panicked flight, perhaps with skewed memories due to terror... things like that. &quot;The Secret Must be Kept&quot; is kind of a farce with this in place, and I can safely say the treatment I've seen from Lunacy in regards to Veil issues is that it makes them hardly an issue at all, both from personal experience and the statements of others. Just. Get. Rid. Of. It. There are better ways of treating it beyond an ever present mind-wipe/debuffer, and Predatory Auras are on the right track.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or humans could use common sense, if i see a bear size wolf coming to eat me... i run period.<br /> <br /> Things i would like to see:<ul><li>Lodges fixed: This is a problem with Lodges, Bloodlines (specially bloodlines <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and legacies. Some suck (in the case of bloodlines, a lot suck), most are highly restrictive, requires a lot and give too little and they have a clear disconection between intent and mecanics. Those things should be enticing. I should be able to look at the benefits and say &quot;sweet, i wanna make one of those&quot; but as they stand now normally im better off just playing a normal uratha/vampire/mage. For example Lodge of the lone wolf that for the price of my furry friends to back me up i get +2 a survival.... oh yeah, that is a equal exchange <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . That one could be fixed using the rules in chronicles guide for lone wolves. Another one i remember is the lodge of lunas tears in wich its member rips the souls of pure and craft them as tatoo wich in theory is all and good however for the loss of harmony and the danger of doing it all you get was <b><u>some extra dices in a roll.</u></b></li> <li>Bale Hounds: I would like to see more about them. They only have one chapter in a book wich is sad but my bigger problem is that for all they sell you that they are &quot;wrong&quot; as beings. I dont see that mirrored in their powers. The eclipse gift are meh, they dont stink of &quot;wrong&quot; and the tainted moon while nasty its only one gift and the price of flaying a lune for it is too much.</li> <li>Wolf blooded as kinfolk. Why this was removed i wonder. Having humans parts wolf with a little edge was nice. Now the wolf blooded has a +something to resist lunacy wich is meh (as many have pointed out lunacy should be out) so why dont they make wolf blooded as something cool to play instead of a waste of merit points.</li> <li>I would like it if they gave emphasis on the urban shaman aspect and what it can do. I would love a urban shaman but im way to dependent of the DM on wheter or not there are spirits in arround.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">werewolf getting a power up as reading the demo for new new vampire they got nasty and now they could wipe the floor with werewolfs</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That mental powers of werewolf work on everyone instead of just humans and uratha as most of all other mental powers from the other flavors of supernatural do.</span></span></li> <li>That the game takes a stand on wheter the werewolves in a city have a social structure or not. The game now sends mixed signals about it a lot of fluff goes in that every pack it its own island but then you have social rites that work in all werewolves, you have renowns accepted by all werewolf and such.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":".  Found the name of the other lodge! 11-03-2013, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T13:51:59-08:00","id":2004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1992#post1992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or renown could be an extra. If your PC does something super special awesome he should get renown but renown being something not necessary at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or humans could use common sense, if i see a bear size wolf coming to eat me... i run period.<br /> <br /> Things i would like to see:<ul><li>Lodges fixed: This is a problem with Lodges, Bloodlines (specially bloodlines <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and legacies. some suck (in the case of bloodlines, a lot suck), most are highly restrictive, requires a lot and give too little and they have a clear disconection between intent and mecanics. Those things should be enticing. I should be able to look at the benefits and say &quot;sweet, i wanna make one of those&quot; but as they stand now normally im better off just playing a normal uratha/vampire/mage. For example Lodge of the lone wolf that for the price of my furry friends to back me up i get +2 a survival.... oh yeah, that is a equal exchange <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . That one could be fixed using the rules in chronicles guide for lone wolves. Another one i remember is a lodge (dont remember the name) in wich its member rips the souls of pure and craft them as tatoo wich in theory is all and good however for the loss of harmony and the danger of doing it all you get was <b><u>temporal</u></b> powers or skills and even then not many.</li> <li>Bale Hounds: I would like to see more about them. They only have one chapter in a book wich is sad but my bigger problem is that for all they sell you that they are &quot;wrong&quot; as being i dont see that mirrored in their powers. The eclipse gift are meh, they dont sting of &quot;wrong&quot; and the tainted moon while nasty its only one and the price of flaying a lune for it is meh.</li> <li>Wolf blooded as kinfolk. Why this removed? i wonder. Having humans parts wolf with a little edge was nice. Now the wolf blooded has a +something to resist lunacy wich is meh (as many have pointed out lunacy should be out) so why dont they make wolf blooded as something cool to play instead of a waste of merit points.</li> <li>I would like it if they gave emphasis on the urban shaman aspect and what it can do. I would love a urban shaman but im way to dependent of the DM on wheter or not there are spirits in arround.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">werewolf getting a power up as reading the demo for new new vampire they got nasty and now they could wipe the floor with werewolfs</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">That mental powers of werewolf work on everyone instead of just humans and uratha as most of all other mental powers from the other flavors of supernatural do.</span></span></li> <li>That the game takes a stand on wheter the werewolves in a city have a social structure or not. The game now sends mixed signals about it a lot of fluff goes in that every pack it its own island but then you have social rites that work in all werewolves, you have renowns accepted by all werewolf and such.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>You might like some of the revisions/overhauls myself and my Co-ST are working on regarding the domination powers (Dominance Instincts that work on -anyone-) and there powers seeing something of a clean up and beef up as a whole. We're on our last set of the main Instincts before we start putting them up for general perusal. I'd say overall they get a boost, though in most instances it's from cutting out the dead weight and introducing stuff -people would want to use and have- or amplifying existing advantages.<br /> <br /> If you're interested I can send some of what we've got completed (there's much, much more) your way sometime. They're not finalized, but we're not really waiting until it's completed to overhaul the Werewolves to more readily fit the games we run.<br /> <br /> Lodge benefits and their place I'd liked to see cleaned up more as well. Already tinkering with that myself and with others, but I do think they'd benefit from a better system. The current prerequisite systems are slap-dash, the benefits are all over the place (and often nonsensical in scope or ability) and a lot of times their niche seems a bit touch and go once you starting looking at relevance regarding Packs and Tribes. I love them... but they need some work.<br /> <br /> As is, (except for the unilateral buffing because of vampires, I very much disagree there) I do agree with a lot of what you'd like to see, though I'm already taking a fairly different take on what I want Wolf-Blooded to actually be as a setting consideration and capable of. I want them much more relevant and important, but I don't think the W:tA kinfolk is the best approach. I'm entirely on board with you wanting them to be cooler though, when I get more time I'll explain this in more detail because wow... is there some untapped potential to work with regarding them, werewolves, spirits and the shadow and even their relevance to entities like the Shartha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T14:37:00-08:00","id":2056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2004#post2004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might like some of the revisions/overhauls myself and my Co-ST are working on regarding the domination powers (Dominance Instincts that work on -anyone-) and there powers seeing something of a clean up and beef up as a whole. We're on our last set of the main Instincts before we start putting them up for general perusal. I'd say overall they get a boost, though in most instances it's from cutting out the dead weight and introducing stuff -people would want to use and have- or amplifying existing advantages.<br /> <br /> If you're interested I can send some of what we've got completed (there's much, much more) your way sometime. They're not finalized, but we're not really waiting until it's completed to overhaul the Werewolves to more readily fit the games we run.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2004#post2004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As is, (except for the unilateral buffing because of vampires, I very much disagree there) I do agree with a lot of what you'd like to see, though I'm already taking a fairly different take on what I want Wolf-Blooded to actually be as a setting consideration and capable of. I want them much more relevant and important, but I don't think the W:tA kinfolk is the best approach. I'm entirely on board with you wanting them to be cooler though, when I get more time I'll explain this in more detail because wow... is there some untapped potential to work with regarding them, werewolves, spirits and the shadow and even their relevance to entities like the Shartha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont get what you mean by unilateral buffing. What i mean by kinfolk of WtA was in the fact they had minor powers that they were able to learn. Same with sorcerer (or second sighters in NwoD) i would love more small talents to be arround.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:01:35-08:00","id":2077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1858#post1858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snip: &quot;Option1&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, option one works, and the way it includes Rage is nice and elegant. I do confess to have forgotten about LOOK's good work. Sorry LOOK <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T15:44:14-08:00","id":2121,"title":"","content":"I meant to the werewolves regarding unilateral buffing, in response to Kindred being able to (with enough investment in the right powers) being able to hand Werewolves their asses here and there. Werewolves don't need to be -more- powerful by default because a vampire might kick their ass with the right power set. This isn't to say that I don't want their own powers refined and cleaned up (and in some cases their outright crap, and in others -really fucking broken- as is). That's going to happen regardless of how things are set up when you've got individuals purchasing and investing heavily into combative powers. It turns into anything but skewed in one or the other's favour, or a given &quot;I win&quot; button once either party starts buying and using those kinds of powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of knee-jerk reactions of &quot;What, that splat got beefed up? Shit, we better beef up ours to be more powerful&quot;. Vampires got some heavy buffs -because they needed them- and to more readily have them jive with the material as presented syncing with the mechanics. With werewolf, it's less of an issue of them falling behind, so much as messy power sets that require cherry picking when they should otherwise be more streamlined and consistently useful. I've never found werewolf to be too weak in years and years of playing; with a proper GMC ruleset conversion they're still not doing badly if you cut the rancid fat off their mechanical bones.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is, a physically invested -anything- splat is often going to hand a werewolf it's ass who invests nothing or very little in those areas. Their physical advantage is an out of the gate edge when comparing one of them to a similarly built supernatural of another stripe at the start; it requires merit and power support to pay off later once others start playing around in those areas and usually more investiture in the form of Experience and combative powers to catch up and exceed a werewolf. You get a quick and beefy edge at the start; it just isn't a be all end all once characters actually start growing in power across the splats, the werewolves still need to invest too, and that's how it should be if that makes sense. They're not always going to be the apex of ass-handing by nature of what they are alone.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Wolf-blooded; oh boy, so many options. I definitely want to see more for them. Book of Spirits has some tidbits in there (not Wolf-Blooded related directly) in the form of Merits I could see using as a basis, along with quite a few others. I definitely want to see them have more love and options available, though with my distaste of Lunacy I suppose that could be said to be that I am wanting them buffed up in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-03-2013, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T16:50:32-08:00","id":2169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2121#post2121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant to the werewolves regarding unilateral buffing, in response to Kindred being able to (with enough investment in the right powers) being able to hand Werewolves their asses here and there. Werewolves don't need to be -more- powerful by default because a vampire might kick their ass with the right power set. This isn't to say that I don't want their own powers refined and cleaned up (and in some cases their outright crap, and in others -really fucking broken- as is). That's going to happen regardless of how things are set up when you've got individuals purchasing and investing heavily into combative powers. It turns into anything but skewed in one or the other's favour, or a given &quot;I win&quot; button once either party starts buying and using those kinds of powers.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of knee-jerk reactions of &quot;What, that splat got beefed up? Shit, we better beef up ours to be more powerful&quot;. Vampires got some heavy buffs -because they needed them- and to more readily have them jive with the material as presented syncing with the mechanics. With werewolf, it's less of an issue of them falling behind, so much as messy power sets that require cherry picking when they should otherwise be more streamlined and consistently useful. I've never found werewolf to be too weak in years and years of playing; with a proper GMC ruleset conversion they're still not doing badly if you cut the rancid fat off their mechanical bones.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is, a physically invested -anything- splat is often going to hand a werewolf it's ass who invests nothing or very little in those areas. Their physical advantage is an out of the gate edge when comparing one of them to a similarly built supernatural of another stripe at the start; it requires merit and power support to pay off later once others start playing around in those areas and usually more investiture in the form of Experience and combative powers to catch up and exceed a werewolf. You get a quick and beefy edge at the start; it just isn't a be all end all once characters actually start growing in power across the splats, the werewolves still need to invest too, and that's how it should be if that makes sense. They're not always going to be the apex of ass-handing by nature of what they are alone.<br /> <br /> On the matter of Wolf-blooded; oh boy, so many options. I definitely want to see more for them. Book of Spirits has some tidbits in there (not Wolf-Blooded related directly) in the form of Merits I could see using as a basis, along with quite a few others. I definitely want to see them have more love and options available, though with my distaste of Lunacy I suppose that could be said to be that I am wanting them buffed up in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, knee jerk reaction shouldnt direct the course of the game. However vampires as it is now are way more powerfull and if i were to place both a combat oriented vampire (B&amp;S demo) and a combat oriented werewolf (as now) the vampire would not just wipe the floor, he will wipe it with the werewolf as mop (wich insidentally is the effect of potency) I tested 3 times and they need some gift fixed. For example the Celerity of both games used to a little one sided (vampire was a little better than father wolf speed) but now its not even a contest. Same with potency, vampire potency was a little better than werewolf version of potency but now, a werewolf would be bleeding essence all day long while the vampire would be using the werewolf as a mop... that ideed happened expending maybe 1 or 2 points of blood. All im saying is that they should strive to make all the splat more or less equal in power, if i make combat oriented pcs of all the splats, all should be able to bring something to the table.<br /> <br /> If B&amp;S is a sign i think all the new new splats are going with a up in their powers. And werewolf have a complicated advantage. On the fluff, the pack of werewolves have the advantage of both numbers and loyalties as per fluff most vampire go alone and even groupe of vampire are very distrutfull between them. However in play, the party of vampires player is united as any pack so it gets difficult to balance power for crossover sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:02:22-08:00","id":2181,"title":"","content":"If I was working on it, I can tell you this: the power level of other splats is not going to factor heavily into my thinking. I do want to see werewolves beefed up, but not because everything must have white room parity (which doesn't exist). It's because we've learned a lot since the nWoD early days and design intentions have changed accordingly. The system is much more refined and dynamic now. B&amp;S, and even the later games, demonstrate the depth and flexibility possible, and also after years of experience, new themes and concepts emerge, as well as new ways to reinforce those things. Yes, there does seem to be a significant boost in power level for vampires, and I expect there will be one for werewolves \u2014 not because vampires got one, or because there's some specific level werewolves need to reach, but because of the evolution of setting expectations and concomitant game design.<br /> <br /> Tell you what, though, one of the things I'd like to see with a heightening on the emphasis of &quot;wolf&quot; in &quot;werewolf&quot; is more detail for pack tactics and lupine instincts. Facing a lone werewolf should be scary enough, but facing a pack should be a death sentence unless you are<i> very </i>badass and <i>very </i>prepared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 11-03-2013, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:19:29-08:00","id":2192,"title":"","content":"Im gonna say something i also said in the New New Mage thread. I havent seen that much knee jerk reaction in NWoD splat on the side of combat but i have seen it a lot in setting/system. Things that were forced on the game because the others splats did it &quot;Mage have magic fairy dust that wipe memory.... so must werewolf&quot; &quot;5auspices/watchtower and 6 orders/6 tribes&quot;. All the semi beings should be powerless (sleepwalker and wolfblooded).<br /> <br /> I think now that the lines are being revised things could change in that reggard. But you are right Claire Redfield, they should get a buff because of need and not because vamp\u00edres did it.<br /> <br /> Another thing i also would like for this new new werewolf is:<br /> <br /> Ron Spencer.... not being allowed 1000 meters near the artwork of this game. His art wich looks like a 90s cover metal band may work in WtA... might being the key word here as i reggard him in the same place as michael bay but on Forsaken it doesnt work it hurst the game themes a lot.<br /> Because when i think about people in this day and age being werewolf, this is what comes to mind:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 90s vest with fangs or bones on it. A chain with a mace and a metal gauntlet.... sure, i can picture that guy as a real person. Drinking coffe on a starbucks with his head tatoos like anyother person there. That picture, the feel of forsaken right there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously i would pay money in a kickstarter for Ron Spencer not being hired to work on New New Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":".  Wanted to add Ron Spencer art to clarify my point. 11-03-2013, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:29:59-08:00","id":2203,"title":"","content":"Funny ... I thought <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>core had the best art of the Big Three core books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:55:00-08:00","id":2234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2203#post2203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny ... I thought <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken </b>core had the best art of the Big Three core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>its complicated for me. Mage has a the most consistent art wich is a plus as it transmit this whole feeling that the book are notes from a made up book (the stitches in the middle are a great detail) and almost all the illustration if not all of them have this simple feeling that they were made with just a pen whoever sometimes the fancy caligraphy in the golden titles makes it difficult to read.<br /> <br /> Forsaken is a close second but suffers for a couple of things. Its color theme is light brown and its cover is a uratha skull wich when i glanced over the first time with a friend we though it was western game. When if one thinks about it, werewolf should feel a very urban games as the worst of the spirits are in the city. And the art is great Abrar Ajmal makes some nice arts pieces (my favorite cover of all times &quot;blasphemies&quot; is made by him), Dave Allsop can make very silent hill like spirits wich is how i always picture the spirit world and there are two more i love one is the man/woman who make the illustration for page 35 of the core wich very lean and clean in his designs and the man/woman who made the picture of the lodge of lunas tears and many other changeling illustration wich are great.<br /> <br /> The book has great art until you stomp into ron spencer wich is the same feeling of eating a cereal and biting a screw that was in the bowl and he makes every chapter start and more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:58:02-08:00","id":2237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2192#post2192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ron Spencer.... not being allowed 1000 meters near the artwork of this game. His art wich looks like a 90s cover metal band may work in WtA... might being the key word here as i reggard him in the same place as michael bay but on Forsaken it doesnt work it hurst the game themes a lot.<br /> Because when i think about people in this day and age being werewolf, this is what comes to mind:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 90s vest with fangs or bones on it. A chain with a mace and a metal gauntlet.... sure, i can picture that guy as a real person. Drinking coffe on a starbucks with his head tatoos like anyother person there. That picture, the feel of forsaken right there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously i would pay money in a kickstarter for Ron Spencer not being hired to work on New New Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... I can't. I just can't do it. I cannot bring myself to agree with this. Dude, Ron Spencer has some of the best Werewolf artwork I've ever seen. His work in the Forsaken core is the best art in that book. I don't see how his artwork hurts the game. I love it. And the image you linked? I'm pretty sure that image in meant to show Werewolves on the hunt or going into combat or something like that. You know? Something Werewolves do quite often? I think that image feels right for Forsaken, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:58:22-08:00","id":2239,"title":"","content":"1) I want an overhaul of the game, not to dish out the core concepts and make something completely new.<br /> 2) Matt said that Werewolves were meant to dominate melee. Make that happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T18:22:58-08:00","id":2260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2237#post2237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... I can't. I just can't do it. I cannot bring myself to agree with this. Dude, Ron Spencer has some of the best Werewolf artwork I've ever seen. His work in the Forsaken core is the best art in that book. I don't see how his artwork hurts the game. I love it. And the image you linked? I'm pretty sure that image in meant to show Werewolves on the hunt or going into combat or something like that. You know? Something Werewolves do quite often? I think that image feels right for Forsaken, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The why on why do i think it hurts the game comes from the following idea. Thats the art of Apocalypse wich is way different than WtF.<br /> WtA is a game about righteous violence, blacks &amp; white, transforming into gauru to peek over a fence and headbutting tanks (those strangely are actual play examples) and Ron Spencer arts sells that idea. Like another guy in the previous forum says, if WtA had a soundtrack i wouldnt be a metal song it would be a metal guitar riff...... of 8 hours.<br /> <br /> His arts is too 90s over muscle, it gives me the idea of EXXXXTREEEEME!!!!!!! (put the intro of the Ultraforce animated serie for the EXXXTREEEME!!!! concept im talking about). So his art transmit this feeling of righteous violence and feeling like an invincible bad-ass which in forsaken you are not. The game is about being subtle, you cannot punch every spirit, sometime you have make changes in the human world, its a game about the pack, about a desperate battle not in the sense of WtA of glorious last stand and taking as many as i can but a more depressing losing battle, think of cold trenches few resources and surrounded by enemies and just trying to survive.<br /> <br /> Its a game about getting and maintaining resources, allies and trying to blend in the human world.... not standing like a flare with a 90s vest. Think about it, most fetishes are day to day objects most of the time. A key, a light switch, a knife, thing a normal person could wear in his body without calling attention to himself (a full metal gauntlet thought?).<br /> <br /> Its a game in wich you are relatively weaker also: While in WtA unless they had silver bullets human were om nom nom in forsaken even in gauru a shotgun blast can end you quickly. I see one PC drop 3 werewolf with an automatic shotgun. So aside from the fact that i consider Ron Spencer the Michael Bay of illustration world and it baffles me how he keeps getting work to draw humans beings i honestly think his art hurts Forsaken as it generate an expectative of the game thats isnt truth. Players who like a gritty, more down to earth supernatural game would be a fend of by the overmuscles 90s cover metal band art while players who would like that sort of thing are gonna get disappointed when they cannot headbutt a tank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-03-2013, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T18:27:35-08:00","id":2263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2237#post2237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... I can't. I just can't do it. I cannot bring myself to agree with this. Dude, Ron Spencer has some of the best Werewolf artwork I've ever seen. His work in the Forsaken core is the best art in that book. I don't see how his artwork hurts the game. I love it. And the image you linked? I'm pretty sure that image in meant to show Werewolves on the hunt or going into combat or something like that. You know? Something Werewolves do quite often? I think that image feels right for Forsaken, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I guess I'm just missing which pieces are his, but overall, I really like the art in the core, so I agree with you. There are a few pieces here and there that just don't &quot;click&quot; with me, but that's just art in general. There will be things like that.<br /> <br /> As a whole, the art in the core is, in my opinion, pretty freaking awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T19:13:14-08:00","id":2294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2263#post2263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I guess I'm just missing which pieces are his</div> </div> </div> </div>This one <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg</a> for example and every illustration at the start of a chapter in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T20:08:52-08:00","id":2314,"title":"","content":"Something I wasn't a big fan of recently myself was the Rituals stat. After Hunter and Geist, it seems like Rituals as a Merit type would just work better, so essentially there's no sacrifice of a Gift at character creation as its purchased from the Merit pool, as the then increasing Rites as Merit (Rituals) would just be new dots * 2 across the board, rather than new dots * 5 for the stat; then rite dots * 2 for each additional Rite within the current rating.<br /> <br /> Regarding any dynamic Rite creation, I'd like it to be less &quot;flexible magic system&quot; and more tied in with the development of the Pack's Totem. Possibly the option for a pack to forge (and teach) a new Rite when their totem increases in Rank. Allowing the deeds of the Pack over the course of a chronicle actually &quot;game-mechanically&quot; shape Uratha culture as a whole. It would seem more in line with the animistic themes of the game as opposed to Blood Sorcery/Gutter Magic mechanics (which are appropriate to their respective games themes in their own right). While not having an &quot;improvised&quot; feel, it does add an extra &quot;cash in on your investment&quot; to Totem development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T20:18:27-08:00","id":2316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2260#post2260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The why on why do i think it hurts the game comes from the following idea. Thats the art of Apocalypse wich is way different than WtF.<br /> WtA is a game about righteous violence, blacks &amp; white, transforming into gauru to peek over a fence and headbutting tanks (those strangely are actual play examples) and Ron Spencer arts sells that idea. Like another guy in the previous forum says, if WtA had a soundtrack i wouldnt be a metal song it would be a metal guitar riff...... of 8 hours.<br /> <br /> His arts is too 90s over muscle, it gives me the idea of EXXXXTREEEEME!!!!!!! (put the intro of the Ultraforce animated serie for the EXXXTREEEME!!!! concept im talking about). So his art transmit this feeling of righteous violence and feeling like an invincible bad-ass which in forsaken you are not. The game is about being subtle, you cannot punch every spirit, sometime you have make changes in the human world, its a game about the pack, about a desperate battle not in the sense of WtA of glorious last stand and taking as many as i can but a more depressing losing battle, think of cold trenches few resources and surrounded by enemies and just trying to survive.<br /> <br /> Its a game about getting and maintaining resources, allies and trying to blend in the human world.... not standing like a flare with a 90s vest. Think about it, most fetishes are day to day objects most of the time. A key, a light switch, a knife, thing a normal person could wear in his body without calling attention to himself (a full metal gauntlet thought?).<br /> <br /> Its a game in wich you are relatively weaker also: While in WtA unless they had silver bullets human were om nom nom in forsaken even in gauru a shotgun blast can end you quickly. I see one PC drop 3 werewolf with an automatic shotgun. So aside from the fact that i consider Ron Spencer the Michael Bay of illustration world and it baffles me how he keeps getting work to draw humans beings i honestly think his art hurts Forsaken as it generate an expectative of the game thats isnt truth. Players who like a gritty, more down to earth supernatural game would be a fend of by the overmuscles 90s cover metal band art while players who would like that sort of thing are gonna get disappointed when they cannot headbutt a tank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. You and I have some pretty different out looks on Forsaken. For one thing, I've never seen the Forsaken to be as weak as you make them sound. I mean seriously, if they're that weak and such, how the Hell did these guys become top predator? No, the fluff would argue with you on some of that. It's no surpise that the fluff and the mechanics have issues when put side by side. Your example of the PC killing 3 Werewolves with a shotgun? Flaw with the system. There's fluff to suggest that Werewolves can shrug off shotgun blasts and can destroy any life form on the planet. It's my hope that this is fixed in the Idigam Chronicle<br /> <br /> But back to artwork, The images at the beginning of every chaper are awesome and show aspects of being Forsaken that are cool. You make Werewolves sound not cool. Being a Werewolf, I should feel powerful. Very powerful. Like, the most powerful thing in the world. I know their not, but bare with me. Werewolves in pop culture are dipicted as these powerful things. Ron Specers art shows them as powerful things.<br /> <br /> But now that you mention it, you might be right and I've been looking at it all wrong. If that's the case, then that might explain why this game hasn't done that well as it should of. I'm mean, nobody wants to play a &quot; weak&quot; Werewolf. I know I don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:09:57-08:00","id":2345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2294#post2294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg</a> for example and every illustration at the start of a chapter in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, at least if my memory is still intact, that guy is the Predator King signature character isn't he? On the one end, yep, he looks like a cheesy high-fantasy barbarian mixed with some modern concepts. On the other end, if he's who I think he is, he doesn't really give a sweet fuck about blending in with humans or their concepts of fashion. He only wears what he's made himself. Other artists have portrayed him the same way as well (and there's more than Ron Spencer). I wouldn't lay that squarely at his feet.<br /> <br /> That and I'm mostly with the rest; I thought Forsaken had some of the tightest overall artwork of the early cores. I definitely wasn't a fan of Mage's overall, and Vampire was all over the place. Until Changeling came out, and later Promethean and Geist (I've not really had a go through Mummy yet, too much else on the platter) I thought it was the most consistent in feel, overall quality and pushing the vibe of what Forsaken was aiming for. Ron wasn't who stuck out to me the most though, it was Abrar Abjmal (see the Blasphemies and The Pure cover for an example). It was nice to see quite a bit of -very- good work from folks I hadn't really been exposed to much in the game lines previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-04-2013, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:10:39-08:00","id":2391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2316#post2316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. You and I have some pretty different out looks on Forsaken. For one thing, I've never seen the Forsaken to be as weak as you make them sound. I mean seriously, if they're that weak and such, how the Hell did these guys become top predator? No, the fluff would argue with you on some of that. It's no surpise that the fluff and the mechanics have issues when put side by side. Your example of the PC killing 3 Werewolves with a shotgun? Flaw with the system. There's fluff to suggest that Werewolves can shrug off shotgun blasts and can destroy any life form on the planet. It's my hope that this is fixed in the Idigam Chronicle<br /> <br /> But back to artwork, The images at the beginning of every chaper are awesome and show aspects of being Forsaken that are cool. You make Werewolves sound not cool. Being a Werewolf, I should feel powerful. Very powerful. Like, the most powerful thing in the world. I know their not, but bare with me. Werewolves in pop culture are dipicted as these powerful things. Ron Specers art shows them as powerful things.<br /> <br /> But now that you mention it, you might be right and I've been looking at it all wrong. If that's the case, then that might explain why this game hasn't done that well as it should of. I'm mean, nobody wants to play a &quot; weak&quot; Werewolf. I know I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I've seen proficient mortals with heavy weapons like that take down multiple vampires and pretty beefy changelings alike. Even with bullets dealing Bashing, it wraps around really damn fast unless you're one -tough- SOB between that and the 9-again. Then again, I've seen a coterie of vampires get offed with nothing more than a lighter and a jerry-can of gas. Shotguns in general have a pretty good time blasting the snot out of things; an automatic shotgun is going to make mince-meat of a lot of things. Without weighing in any additional gifts and powers, fetishes or anything else from that situation (that's pretty sparse in info) even without it being loaded with silver, it's going to suck. <br /> <br /> Know what takes down werewolves well unless the werewolf gets into melee range or outflanks their aggressor? Shotguns loaded with silver rounds. And yet one Gift out of the Technology set or Shaping (neither of which I thought were any good) can end that problem right fast. Or Ward vs Technology. You're not going to find many splats that can easily survive ongoing automatic shotgun fire without quite a bit of problems. Again; having a strong physical edge is not the same as HULK SMASH and Werewolves needing to be living tanks.<br /> <br /> I've no clue where that crap is coming from in pop culture or elsewhere; it really seems more like a W:tA artifact, and this from a big horror movie (and genre in general) buff. Crazy regeneration after you -think- they're dead or severely wounded without silver? Yep. Incredible Hulk? No. The more this comes up, the more it reads to me like folks basically just wanting a &quot;I go to Gauru form and win physical combats&quot; button to me. That's definitely I -don't- want to see, it's boring as hell and takes away a lot of the risk of getting into combats. Yet, you keep getting folks with one raging (no pun intended) hard-on to push for the forms to be enhanced more and more until that's effectively what they become.<br /> <br /> Want that? There's W:tA now in 20th Edition and it's Translation Guide. I -really- don't want to see Forsaken regressing into the W:tA style and mindset in this regard. If I want furry tanks, I can go play a Lunar Exalted, Scion or W:tA. The old vibes of &quot;It's not fun until I can make puree of other splats&quot; that consistently raises it's ugly head was old before nWoD even came into existence. And for the record; you don't build these games with some contrived sense of inter-game parity in mind. You build them to support their own internal logic and thematics; at some point one just has to suck it up that their pet splat isn't always going to be the be all-end-all in a particular category when comparisons are made. What vampire is doing -really- doesn't matter to Werewolf whatsoever, it really doesn't, outside of good ideas and mechanics that can be re-jiggered to help update it. It isn't an arms race. It's not even all that relevant in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:34:22-08:00","id":2401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2391#post2391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've no clue where that crap is coming from in pop culture or elsewhere; it really seems more like a W:tA artifact, and this from a big horror movie (and genre in general) buff. Crazy regeneration after you -think- they're dead or severely wounded without silver? Yep. Incredible Hulk? No. The more this comes up, the more it reads to me like folks basically just wanting a &quot;I go to Gauru form and win physical combats&quot; button to me. That's definitely I -don't- want to see, it's boring as hell and takes away a lot of the risk of getting into combats. Yet, you keep getting folks with one raging (no pun intended) hard-on to push for the forms to be enhanced more and more until that's effectively what they become.<br /> <br /> Want that? There's W:tA now in 20th Edition and it's Translation Guide. I -really- don't want to see Forsaken regressing into the W:tA style and mindset in this regard. If I want furry tanks, I can go play a Lunar Exalted, Scion or W:tA. The old vibes of &quot;It's not fun until I can make puree of other splats&quot; that consistently raises it's ugly head was old before nWoD even came into existence. And for the record; you don't build these games with some contrived sense of inter-game parity in mind. You build them to support their own internal logic and thematics; at some point one just has to suck it up that their pet splat isn't always going to be the be all-end-all in a particular category when comparisons are made. What vampire is doing -really- doesn't matter to Werewolf whatsoever, it really doesn't, outside of good ideas and mechanics that can be re-jiggered to help update it. It isn't an arms race. It's not even all that relevant in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pop culture is more than movies dude. There are novels, comics, whatever. You should try reading some. Also, I never said Gauru should be an &quot;I win&quot; button. I didn't even mention Gauru in my last post. You know, the one you're quoting? You're putting words in my mouth and I don't care for that. What I'm saying is playing a Werewolf should make the player feel powerful. It doesn't mean he wins every fight. Nor did I ever compare Forsaken to B&amp;S's level of power. I couldn't care less. What I'm saying is make Werewolves powerful, not invincible. There's a difference.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;play W20 with the Tranlation Guide&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you for being very dismissive and condisending. That's certainly helpful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T23:06:21-08:00","id":2420,"title":"","content":"I was using movies as -one- example of my familiarity, don't be patronizing. And I was expanding on ideas past the initial quote as well (including Kaho's), it wasn't purely orientated towards what you said alone, it was simply addressing part of it. That's not me putting words into your mouth; that's me explaining -my own perspective- on how these notions play out. You're picking a fight without need.<br /> <br /> If you found that the notion that there are -multiple games already in print that really already play up some of the notions you've repeatedly presented here and on the old forums both dismissive and condescending, I don't know what to tell you. They're there, they exist, and the already support in one fashion or another truly badass shapeshifters more readily. I don't find aping the game's predecessor further to be a benefit when it's trying to revise itself into it's own thing. I don't feel the need to take these elements and rework the Forsaken/Pure into that image, and that's precisely the vibe I've gotten both from you and others in the past. I don't need nor want an aggregated slew of buffs just to make one segment feel 'badass' because shrugging off shotgun blasts isn't a given out of the gate.<br /> <br /> That's is what I've consistently seen a small segment say; they're not powerful enough. They die too easily. I don't feel badass enough so lets buff up their Gauru more. In all my years with this game I've not really found it to be necessary beyond some trivial tweaks, so go figure, I'm not going to advocate that approach. I've done a couple of mild tweaks at best; what exactly is it that you want to see the beef them up? Forgive me if it's asking for reiteration from the old forums (and yes, I am familiar with quite a few of your posts by the way), but what package do you expect is going to give you that feel of being 'powerful' that you're not getting now with what they do get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T03:23:24-08:00","id":2497,"title":"","content":"When the Uratha go Gauru, everything around them, spirit world included, should go OH SH-. Enuff said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T04:43:51-08:00","id":2516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2316#post2316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. You and I have some pretty different out looks on Forsaken. For one thing, I've never seen the Forsaken to be as weak as you make them sound. I mean seriously, if they're that weak and such, how the Hell did these guys become top predator? No, the fluff would argue with you on some of that. It's no surpise that the fluff and the mechanics have issues when put side by side. Your example of the PC killing 3 Werewolves with a shotgun? Flaw with the system. There's fluff to suggest that Werewolves can shrug off shotgun blasts and can destroy any life form on the planet. It's my hope that this is fixed in the Idigam Chronicle<br /> <br /> But back to artwork, The images at the beginning of every chaper are awesome and show aspects of being Forsaken that are cool. You make Werewolves sound not cool. Being a Werewolf, I should feel powerful. Very powerful. Like, the most powerful thing in the world. I know their not, but bare with me. Werewolves in pop culture are dipicted as these powerful things. Ron Specers art shows them as powerful things.<br /> <br /> But now that you mention it, you might be right and I've been looking at it all wrong. If that's the case, then that might explain why this game hasn't done that well as it should of. I'm mean, nobody wants to play a &quot; weak&quot; Werewolf. I know I don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said werewolf are weakling or that they should be but they are not at the power level of WtA nor they should be. They are cool but they arent cool because they can kill stuff willy-nilly, they are cool because they are hunters, the stalk, they plan, they set ambush and use resources at they disposal that normally only they have acess to. A promethean or a vampire with potence and celerity can drop any werewolf sure does that make them the most coolest supernatural? hardly. Does their speed and brute force help them when a pack stalk them, wears them down, use spirits against them or make pacts with the others packs of a city to hinder them? No. <br /> I remember this game in wich the DM sent of this vampire wich had 5 in all the physical diciplines so at the start he bitch slap my PC (the alpha) into doing his quest. So i make my PC mission in life to kill him. I gather allies, the correct convination of gift, ritual and allies to counter all his discipline. So when the pack bring the pain to this vampire is was glorious in a city wide chase in wich he couldnt run from the city. We didnt had his level of strenght or speed but we damm well compensate with teamwork, resources and allies.<br /> <br /> its not a flaw in the system or a disconection in fluff and mechanics as a automatic shotgun to the face is gonna drop you, even blood of the wolf says that brain damage is a difficult to fix and can only regenerate a partial part of the brain.<br /> <br /> You say it yourself that you feel in the art of Ron Spencer, that werewolf are the most powerfull thing in the world even though they arent. Thats the disconnect in theme im talking about.<br /> <br /> Werewolf in pop culture are despicted as these powerful being, that is true but many of those despiction use 1 werewolf as an antagonist. 1 werewolf as an antagonist in a movie/book should feel like a hulk but if to that we add the rest of the pack? then i just becomes implausible for the protagonist to survive. Example: take the movie Van Helsing or the wolfman (the remake) now take the werewolf antagonist and multiple by 5. Do you think they would have had any chance of lossing then?<br /> <br /> How the became top predator? easy, numbers. Setting wise, you rarely fight one werewolf you fight a pack while normally you fight a vampire or a mage. The cotery of vampires is more an exception than the rule and to a extent so is the mage cabal. Problem is when we play other splats we dont see that because the party of players is a united as any pack but setting wise werewolf normally have numbers. The problem with making them up as hulk is that the setting has to be able to counter always 3-5 hulks. You dont have to think if one werewolf is more badass than a vampire because the vampire is almost always one while the pack are 3-5. So lets say for the sake of argument that one werewolf could headbutt a tank, fine. One werewolf is the apex of the supernaturals but them werewolf dont travel alone so often, right? no they go in pack so how any supernatural group can withstand 5 tank headbutting werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T04:52:10-08:00","id":2522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2420#post2420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's is what I've consistently seen a small segment say; they're not powerful enough. They die too easily. I don't feel badass enough so lets buff up their Gauru more. In all my years with this game I've not really found it to be necessary beyond some trivial tweaks, so go figure, I'm not going to advocate that approach. I've done a couple of mild tweaks at best; what exactly is it that you want to see the beef them up? Forgive me if it's asking for reiteration from the old forums (and yes, I am familiar with quite a few of your posts by the way), but what package do you expect is going to give you that feel of being 'powerful' that you're not getting now with what they do get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats an insteresting question, what would we want the werewolf buff at. I would say i would like their rites more buff in the sense of less social and more practical, some rite that target others supenaturals they dont need to outright kill them but at least inconvenience them. Better mental gifts, i hate how most only work in humans and werewolves. I would like that the lodge of the lone wolf be free for all tribes/auspices and give some badass bonus. Because then one can use 1 werewolf for an antagonist without feeling forced. And i always felt it was one of those lodges designed to use in crossover games (party compose of a vampire, a werewolf, a changeling and geist for example) so if said character renounce to his furry friend he should get A LOT more than a +2 to survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T05:01:17-08:00","id":2525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2497#post2497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Uratha go Gauru, everything around them, spirit world included, should go OH SH-. Enuff said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely put. xD<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I am looking forward to, and want to see, is what &quot;the Wolf must Hunt&quot; actually means, mechanic and thematics-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:50:46-08:00","id":2614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2420#post2420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was using movies as -one- example of my familiarity, don't be patronizing. And I was expanding on ideas past the initial quote as well (including Kaho's), it wasn't purely orientated towards what you said alone, it was simply addressing part of it. That's not me putting words into your mouth; that's me explaining -my own perspective- on how these notions play out. You're picking a fight without need.<br /> <br /> If you found that the notion that there are -multiple games already in print that really already play up some of the notions you've repeatedly presented here and on the old forums both dismissive and condescending, I don't know what to tell you. They're there, they exist, and the already support in one fashion or another truly badass shapeshifters more readily. I don't find aping the game's predecessor further to be a benefit when it's trying to revise itself into it's own thing. I don't feel the need to take these elements and rework the Forsaken/Pure into that image, and that's precisely the vibe I've gotten both from you and others in the past. I don't need nor want an aggregated slew of buffs just to make one segment feel 'badass' because shrugging off shotgun blasts isn't a given out of the gate.<br /> <br /> That's is what I've consistently seen a small segment say; they're not powerful enough. They die too easily. I don't feel badass enough so lets buff up their Gauru more. In all my years with this game I've not really found it to be necessary beyond some trivial tweaks, so go figure, I'm not going to advocate that approach. I've done a couple of mild tweaks at best; what exactly is it that you want to see the beef them up? Forgive me if it's asking for reiteration from the old forums (and yes, I am familiar with quite a few of your posts by the way), but what package do you expect is going to give you that feel of being 'powerful' that you're not getting now with what they do get?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright so, first off let me say I'm sorry. I was tired and in bad mood. I didn't mean to take it out on you or any one else. I just find the &quot;there's other games&quot; approch to be dismissive at best and it doesn't help improve the game being discussed. It's a pet peeve of mine, so again I'm sorry. But if I may be so bold, your suggestions for &quot;fixing&quot; Forsaken would require an entire game rewrite. Removing Renown and Lunacy and such? These things are part of the setting and system. My suggestions aren't nearly has game changing as yours. However, that's what you want to see, I'm not going to criticize you for that, I'm just saying.<br /> <br /> Werewolves do need a power buff though. I'm not entirely sure what they really need, only what I've seen work. In my experience, giving them the higher of Wits or Dexterity, 8 again in Gauru form, and healing 1 Bashing or Lethal a round in Gauru does the job nicely. I even ran a scenario were a Werewolf, using what I just mentioned, went up against a Vampire. I used GMC rules for combat and B&amp;S rules for the Vampire, which was Count F#cking Dracula. The Werewolf was a Rahu Blood Talon from the Lodge of the Starless Sky and had 35 or so XP on him. Using GMC rules, like I said, actually made this fight awesome. It was tit for tat, both giving as good as they took. In the end, it was a draw. The egde went to the Werewolf only because Drac was losing Vitae faster then he could deal damage. Oh, Gifts were involved, don't worry about that. It wasn't just Gauru alone. Clarity and Hone Rage are awesome!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So, given my personal experience, those things I mentioned would be a good place to start. Also, removing Gauru's time limit.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:14:50-08:00","id":2632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2516#post2516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said werewolf are weakling or that they should be but they are not at the power level of WtA nor they should be. They are cool but they arent cool because they can kill stuff willy-nilly, they are cool because they are hunters, the stalk, they plan, they set ambush and use resources at they disposal that normally only they have acess to. A promethean or a vampire with potence and celerity can drop any werewolf sure does that make them the most coolest supernatural? hardly. Does their speed and brute force help them when a pack stalk them, wears them down, use spirits against them or make pacts with the others packs of a city to hinder them? No.<br /> I remember this game in wich the DM sent of this vampire wich had 5 in all the physical diciplines so at the start he bitch slap my PC (the alpha) into doing his quest. So i make my PC mission in life to kill him. I gather allies, the correct convination of gift, ritual and allies to counter all his discipline. So when the pack bring the pain to this vampire is was glorious in a city wide chase in wich he couldnt run from the city. We didnt had his level of strenght or speed but we damm well compensate with teamwork, resources and allies.<br /> <br /> its not a flaw in the system or a disconection in fluff and mechanics as a automatic shotgun to the face is gonna drop you, even blood of the wolf says that brain damage is a difficult to fix and can only regenerate a partial part of the brain.<br /> <br /> You say it yourself that you feel in the art of Ron Spencer, that werewolf are the most powerfull thing in the world even though they arent. Thats the disconnect in theme im talking about.<br /> <br /> Werewolf in pop culture are despicted as these powerful being, that is true but many of those despiction use 1 werewolf as an antagonist. 1 werewolf as an antagonist in a movie/book should feel like a hulk but if to that we add the rest of the pack? then i just becomes implausible for the protagonist to survive. Example: take the movie Van Helsing or the wolfman (the remake) now take the werewolf antagonist and multiple by 5. Do you think they would have had any chance of lossing then?<br /> <br /> How the became top predator? easy, numbers. Setting wise, you rarely fight one werewolf you fight a pack while normally you fight a vampire or a mage. The cotery of vampires is more an exception than the rule and to a extent so is the mage cabal. Problem is when we play other splats we dont see that because the party of players is a united as any pack but setting wise werewolf normally have numbers. The problem with making them up as hulk is that the setting has to be able to counter always 3-5 hulks. You dont have to think if one werewolf is more badass than a vampire because the vampire is almost always one while the pack are 3-5. So lets say for the sake of argument that one werewolf could headbutt a tank, fine. One werewolf is the apex of the supernaturals but them werewolf dont travel alone so often, right? no they go in pack so how any supernatural group can withstand 5 tank headbutting werewolf.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You make soild points here. However, comparing a Werewolf to what basically sounds like an Elder Vampire? Yeah, of course your Werewolf is going to get his ass kicked. The guy's pushing probably 150+ XP. I'm not saying the hunt, gathering resources and allies is a bad thing. It's very fun and a great part the game, yeah. But individually, a Werewolf should be able to stand on his own. This isn't Power Rangers or Sailor Moon. This is Werewolf. Werewolves are scary. How are they scary? They possess superhuman strength, stamina, speed, and either amazing regenerative abilities or amazing durablity against damage, sometimes both. You just can't kill them without silver (by the way, this is from human perspective). Do I want Hulk Werewolves? Kinda, but not really. The buffs I mentioned to Tatterdemalion King above are a good place to start, IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, I've read some Werewolf books and seen movies were the Werewolf protagonist was pretty powerful. It's not just the antagonists that are scary. Sometimes, great power is itself a burdon or curse. Ask Superman, or the Hulk, since he's quite popular I see.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:20:34-08:00","id":2634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Removing Renown and Lunacy and such? These things are part of the setting and system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, so was Predator's Taint in Requiem. In fact it mimicks well Renown as they were mechanics very argued against in its respective games. Scraping Lunacy as it is and substitute it for a Predatory Aura (as it seems they left the door open for) and just forget about Renown and use Tribe/Auspice Status Merits (or turn Renown into a Merit with an actual mechanical effect besides acting as cap to powers) would be completly feasible.<br /> <br /> And you could say that Renown already have mechanical effects besides capping powers, but which ones? Social bonuses? That would be better covered by a Tribe Status Merit. Adding to Gifts Dice Pools? The way it is done is a mess. There are far more things to be gained by scrapping it or at least greatly rework it than to keep it mostly as it is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:25:59-08:00","id":2637,"title":"","content":"I'm not against altering Renown or Lunacy. I'm against removing them entirly. That's what I was getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:35:39-08:00","id":2643,"title":"","content":"But if you get them so changed that are unrecognizeable,what's the difference from removing them? Was Predator's Taint removed or just changed, for comparisson*?<br /> <br /> *<i>From your point of view, I want to understand how you frame such changes</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:54:22-08:00","id":2651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2643#post2643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you get them so changed that are unrecognizeable,what's the difference from removing them? Was Predator's Taint removed or just changed, for comparisson*?<br /> <br /> *<i>From your point of view, I want to understand how you frame such changes</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, Predator's Taint was changed. And for the better. Just note, however, I don't really care for Vampire. But I like what I've seen of the revisions. As long as Renown and Lunacy are kept in one form or the other, I'm cool with that. Heck, I like the idea of Renown being more like Mantle and Lunacy being tied to a Predator's Aura equivalant. I just don't want them gone ENTIRELY. That's all I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:07:39-08:00","id":2662,"title":"","content":"Then you and I are on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:09:11-08:00","id":2664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2632#post2632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You make soild points here. However, comparing a Werewolf to what basically sounds like an Elder Vampire? Yeah, of course your Werewolf is going to get his ass kicked. The guy's pushing probably 150+ XP. I'm not saying the hunt, gathering resources and allies is a bad thing. It's very fun and a great part the game, yeah. But individually, a Werewolf should be able to stand on his own. This isn't Power Rangers or Sailor Moon. This is Werewolf. Werewolves are scary. How are they scary? They possess superhuman strength, stamina, speed, and either amazing regenerative abilities or amazing durablity against damage, sometimes both. You just can't kill them without silver (by the way, this is from human perspective). Do I want Hulk Werewolves? Kinda, but not really. The buffs I mentioned to Tatterdemalion King above are a good place to start, IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, I've read some Werewolf books and seen movies were the Werewolf protagonist was pretty powerful. It's not just the antagonists that are scary. Sometimes, great power is itself a burdon or curse. Ask Superman, or the Hulk, since he's quite popular I see.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Im not saying they should be weak or not be able to stand of their own but is my opinion they dont need to be the physical powerhouse of the game when in setting they always travel in packs. Prometheans for example are the powerhouses because they are too few and they dont have a social structure and most are alone. You mention fiction of werewolves see the differences between fiction with 1 werewolf and fiction in wich there is a pack of them. The power level of the later is lower because otherwise not many settings can sustains them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2614#post2614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But if I may be so bold, your suggestions for &quot;fixing&quot; Forsaken would require an entire game rewrite. Removing Renown and Lunacy and such? These things are part of the setting and system. My suggestions aren't nearly has game changing as yours. However, that's what you want to see, I'm not going to criticize you for that, I'm just saying.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>im curious as to why. Why lunacy should be kept? Why it cannot be replace with common sense (human see giant bearsize wolf, human runs). Why there need to be pixie dust BS as failsafes. A human sees a werewolf and who he gonna tell? who is gonna believe him? i never saw the use for it.<br /> <br /> Removing renown entirely doesnt chage the core game that much either, i have done it. Its function is both a social thingies (replaced with RP) and a power cap. As a power cap is very much useless as i as a DM i have fiat to decide wich gift the players can learn and wich they cannot by the need of werewolf to learn from spirits.<br /> <br /> But even if that would mean a entire game rewrite, would that be that bad? New New Werewolf could be the moment to make bold changes in the system and the fluff. Check everything in the game again and remove what doesnt work, add based on need. I would like it the be treated like another edition altogether.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-04-2013, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:44:08-08:00","id":2703,"title":"","content":"Not Exactly Copy/Pasted but I Wanted to see the intense feelings that Werewolves apparently feel through Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:51:17-08:00","id":2706,"title":"","content":"I don't see why Lunacy needs to be removed, on the opposite side of that coin. Just because in modern times people do not believe in such things and dismiss anyone who says otherwise, does not mean it has always been the case. In times when werewolf reports caused witch burnings and other tragedies, Lunacy would have been a very necessary tool. You can't dismiss something based on the modern world's reactions when it likely was a major necessity in earlier eras.<br /> <br /> Keeping the secrets for a splat that is not tailored towards social control and influence is not the same as having things that make it blatantly harder to keep the secret for say vampires. While a vampire can ghoul the right people, has a bent towards slavery and mind control, werewolves have more physical bents and influence with spirits. Having a spiritual blessing that helps maintain their secret is not getting in the way of anything.<br /> <br /> If anything I would see Lunacy have a revamp into how powerful it is, I'd like to see it lessened some to make it always a threat in say a suburban neighborhood that someone might see through it. But I feel its rather silly to remove it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:54:44-08:00","id":2708,"title":"","content":"One way to vary Gauru is let renown/some variant of renown affect gauru - and thus each tribe/auspices form would be slightly different. Something like:<br /> <br /> Glory: +1 strength in Gauru/dot<br /> Cunning: +1 Def in Gauru/dot<br /> Purity: Adds damage to claw/bite, scaling from 1/2 lethal to 2/3A<br /> Honour: Adds armour in gauru/dot<br /> Wisdom: adds +1 lethal healed per essence spent/dot.<br /> <br /> This would up the power of garou, vary each tribe's garou, and give some game reason to purchase these beyond the gift-dice-pools. <br /> <br /> Renaming each renown something a touch more feral might shift the focus from a social reputation to something more feral and inborn in the wolf; something like Rage instead of glory; Eldritch/mystic instead of Wisdom etc. <br /> <br /> Its one neat way to up the power without dumping the lot.<br /> <br /> hoodedclaw<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:43:53-08:00","id":2763,"title":"","content":"Just want to remind something to those that want werewolfs to be buffed in the combat aspect:<br /> <br /> Humans are not physical powerhouses(as if it needs to be said) we exel at two things in nature; our capacity to travel great distances (something to do with the fact that we stand in two legs) and our capacity for abstraction (im not even going to say inteligence or cunning)<br /> <br /> Wolves are NOT physical powerhouses, a wolf is not a match for any of the great &quot;cats&quot;, wolves target the sick and the young when they hunt, they are pack animals, they rely on stealth and coperation, on separating the prey from their herd, and then atacking all at once against the weakest foe posible trying to make it fall and restrain him, they are, in a way, &quot;coward&quot; animals, much like humans<br /> <br /> so why in the fuck does human + wolf = super strength?<br /> <br /> i think this is a bad interpretation of the myth, a werewolf is scary not because it can kill ten men in 3 seconds but rather because he is a dopelganger, a &quot;wolf in sheeps clothers&quot; you dont know who's the werewolf, and when a mythilogical werewolf kills it kills one person, when the two of them where alone, but when the village knows who the werewolf is and they form a mob, well... hes fucked (also lunacy fucks this posibility in the ass, werewolfs arents scared of mobs in the game as it is today. And basides, why are there lodges dedicated to protecting the secret of werewolf existence?)<br /> <br /> should uratha be more powerfull in combat? certainly, but should they be &quot;stronger&quot;? no<br /> The power of the werewolf should come from the pack, a pack of werewolfs should be able to win over a coterie of vampires, who are &quot;stonger&quot; by way of tactics and manuvering, by stealth and having the sort of instinctual conection that even the most tight-knit-telepahtycaly-linked-mutualy-blood-bonded-BFF coterie<br /> <br /> and also, the lone wolf should be POWERFUL, why? it's only usable as an antagonist or in a cross over game, he should be his own pack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:59:01-08:00","id":2777,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm all for upping the forms power, but I'd say base it on PU, much like vampire's new frenzy mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:38:57-08:00","id":2802,"title":"","content":"Clarification's sake does push me to say, I want them adjusted into merits for Renown vs their current iteration and mechanics. The very notion I don't take issue with; the current implementation I do. Lunacy though? No. I really find it both overblown and detrimental. I honestly believe a Status-like, or Mantle-like (or lets say, GMC Cult-like) merit fits the bill a bit more effectively, and it certainly doesn't require a full game rewrite, but honestly? I'm already doing a heavy overhaul with my Co-ST. I'm not going to short-change a game's potential because it'd be more work and may require some drastic shifts. Not going far enough was the precise problem W:tF and V:tR had in it's former iteration; I'd be heavily disappointed if they dialed things back and didn't take heart from the Chronicler's Guide and go a bit wild with the ideas they've tinkered with.<br /> <br /> For the record Rahuman, some of what you'd like to see I do agree with. I've been going with the notion that buffing the Gauru form's accelerated healing to cover 1 L a round makes it worth while to take in other situations (and makes those in prolonged frenzies scarier) without the need of Essence expenditure. Especially when it comes to a blow that might knock them unconscious, the prior roll to see if they Death Rage has a bit more of a survival-based oomph to do that even if you're lacking Essence. That and it makes Death Rage a more dangerous proposition; not only for those in your way, but those around you in general; taking you down by physical force hoping to &quot;tire you out of the form&quot; is rather difficult when you're raging, healing 1L or 1B a turn, getting back up right pissed off and still having some Essence to spare for other things.<br /> <br /> Given many of the powers we're working on for Instincts are Reflexive... it means Gauru form most certainly has an arsenal of abilities it can use and that's more of what I wanted to see on my end in general. When you talk, Rahuman about buffing of Gifts, and cleaning them up, I'm in full agreement there, it's why many of the Instincts I've been tinkering with emphatically -can- be used in Gauru form, and in Death Rage (for good or ill). I'm going rather divergent there, some of the Instincts are revisions to old Gifts while others have no correlation. &quot;Gifts&quot; are being shifted into what you gain primarily from hunting down and consuming spirits; converted Numina, as well as the occasional blessings one gets from Totems and spirit pacts (which have their own pitfalls that makes hunting and consuming spirits the more common Forsaken approach).<br /> <br /> For me it's been far less the forms being problematic (though I've done something perhaps drastic in the eyes of others with Dalu and Urshul) in their stats and capabilities, and more of being hamstringed in what you can do in some of them. I'm still iffy on 9-agains (let alone 8-agains) in that form; that's more something I'd prefer to see as part of a Death Rage/Gauru Form fighting style, taking to heart we're getting a frenzy based one for the vampires, I think it's been -long- in coming that there are some fighting styles that give you options for these in combat. Same with the highest of Wits or Dex; with GMC Defense I don't think it's necessary at all save perhaps as part of a Combat Merit rather than an innate.<br /> <br /> What I do want to see shifted overall though, is Gauru form's utility in hunting; right now it's a bit iffy in how it's presented (despite a nice sensory bonus), especially with Death Rage's description. I'm not a fan of frenzy states that make you &quot;stupid&quot;; with the change to Vampires, I think that's a much cleaner way of presenting it. Focused, vicious targeted acts that can spin even more wildly out of control when things go sour in the pursuit. I'm probably not articulating this too clearly, but the basic idea I want is that Death Rage is the hunter killer instinct gone out of control, rather than say, being a spinning spazzing Taz in presentation that sometimes comes to mind. Other individuals most certainly can run afoul of it or make themselves targets (and things going more protracted and sour as a result from provocations), but it's more of a description shift if that makes sense. I see adopting Gauru form and Death Rage as much a survival instinct as a bloody killing juggernaut, I'd like to see a bit more tweaking to emphasize that more than portion we currently have.<br /> <br /> With that in mind... I've introduced a rule where Werewolves with 0 Essence that enter Death Rage -will- attack and consume others that are viable for Essence some time ago (though they may make attempts to steer it's course some; nobody wants to eat a packmate, and yep... I do put other werewolves as viable sources in opposition to the current rules). Being spiritually 'hungry' is a dangerous, dangerous state for temptation alone; spirits just don't appear on hand to keep you fed, they're tough and tenacious compared to the much more ubiquitous humans and we heavily revised Loci so they no longer act as essence batteries, which means you get Essence from hunting and eating, not much else. Raging on an empty spiritual belly is like a spirit -desperate- for any Essence it can get; it's going to get ugly. Toss in a system where addiction to human/wolf flesh is quite possible (similar to Vitae Addiction in mechanical approach), and sometimes you get those classic werewolves that just can't help themselves, made worse if they Death Rage. They're dangerous to those around them. They run the risk of becoming more dangerous, or falling into the classic werewolf man-eater trope more readily than the after-thought it is now.<br /> <br /> That's something I -really- want to see. Essence farmers can go into the recycle bin. If you Death Rage, people are quite possibly going to get eaten, and you're going to be left with the mess on every front left after. And yes; I go by the notion that you do get some Werewolves out there who specifically hunt, kill and eat other werewolves, going looney tunes into their spirit-nature and the whole &quot;like eats like&quot; they have going. Werewolves banding together as a pack is more than just instinct; it's survival. The Pure, rogue 'man-eaters' and low-harmony cannibals, spirits and more are all out there. You're on the menu as a new werewolf. Band together to survive, because you're going to have to be one cunning, tenacious and vicious fuck to survive on your own, and odds are without the help of the pack, you're going to do some ugly things to get Essence.<br /> <br /> I don't need a mind-wiping, debuffing built in power of doom to reflect a common sense thing of &quot;Oh shit, I better run, it's big, it's huge and it's coming right for me.&quot; The only thing I've found it adds is 1) less concern for the Veil, less precautions and less thought in general on the part of PCs and NPCs regarding taking alternate forms and it (aka laziness), and 2) making human antagonists unless their build with ridiculously high Composure and Resolve ratings pretty damn irrelevant. I got utterly tired of it being a built in consequence dodge. It hasn't added anything for me, at all. Roses suggestion on the werewolf Predatory making others feel like prey (and in turn inflicting a condition on somewhat that reinforced that, potentially with options including madness for another iteration, or the whole animal magnetism thing as the third) works for me. It requires active effort. Lunacy as is is an afterthought.<br /> <br /> I've used it for a while (and that's changing in the next two months in my game) using the rolled system in War Against the Pure for the alternate shape shifter equivalent as a place mat for the last few years, and it's -helped- and I find it better, but I still find that a switch to a more targeted Predatory Aura (and definitely cranking it down in overall potency or group affecting capacity) would do best. Something where you could separate the weak and scared from the 'herd' from a brief panic, put them in general more to flight than fight etc. rather than a passive &quot;You're just fucked if you're anyone but the most exceptional of people.&quot; So I suppose it's less &quot;Lunacy is gone&quot; and more &quot;what it does and how it's implemented is shifted away from it's current incarnation&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, apologies for the massive posts, doubly so if they seem confrontational at all, I'm addressing a lot of things at once, some which haven't came up in this discussion (yet, but inevitably do). Quite a bit of what I want to see changed is due to many prior experiences reinforcing something I found just didn't work for me for a host of factors. I like to get everything out of my head before I get distracted and forget it. Hopefully most of that made sense. Obviously I'm going to have some very different ideas and wants from Idigam chronicles than some folks, but man... if you've got the opportunity to overhaul a game, nothing bugs me more than tip-toeing and not going wild with it. It's a new edition; it shouldn't be held back due to prior supplements. I can safely say I've liked Claire's ideas consistently however, so here's hoping we see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-04-2013, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:45:18-08:00","id":2808,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I think that Werewolf would have been, or make more use of, the subtitle &quot;The Legendary.&quot; Why? Admittedly this is more of my interpretation of Renown than anything, but it does seem like Renown is a formal codification of a werewolf's personal legend among the spirits. A werewolf preforms feats of Cunning, why he <i>must </i>be Clever...and when he spirits recognize that, he becomes supernaturally clever and is able to apply that to his powers or whatever use the new system makes of Renown. After all, werewolves have spiritual qualities, and spirits can be interpreted to be essentially living meanings. <br /> <br /> Basically, werewolves are living legends and Renown is what they're legendary for. Now, the thing about legends is that they're exaggerations as well, lies that have become folk-truths. This could play into what Talum was talking about earlier on how werewolves should fear the mobs and the emphases on Pack vs Lone wolves, and how that silly &quot;Legendary&quot; Idea could apply. <br /> <br /> Basically, a werewolf would have to decide who's legend to promote. Should a Werewolf sacrifice the potential of his deeds to the pack, take up Gifts or whatever that makes the pack's legend as a whole stronger? He is personally weaker and is in more danger if caught by his enemies alone, but his pack as a whole benefits and they are more potent as a result. Or should a werewolf be selfish, and advance only his own legend and become the monster he has played himself up as? His pack, if any, would resent him, but he would mutate to become the played up super strong monster that lurks in many posters mind as the &quot;ideal werewolf&quot;. Hell, this divide could also play into the Tribes with the Ivory Claws and Storm Lords preferring the personal approach, Hunters in Darkness and Fire Touched prefering the pack, and so on. <br /> <br /> TLDR, I suppose the point of this rambling is that I'd like to see Renown being played up as personal significance for the PC, and for Werewolf1.9 (2.9?) to play up the choice between the self or the pack. Focus too much on the pack, and you'll all be vulnerable to being split up and picked off. Focus too much on yourself, and you'll be alone when the mob comes to deal with you.<br /> <br /> ANYWAY, moving on from this pointless rambling, I do hope the werewolf writers have played a little of Magic: the Gathering's Innistrad block. The werewolves there were pretty rad and fun, and I think a good example of how I hope the Idigam Werewolvs should be: Tough, certainly capable of tearing shit up, but vulnerable without some support from each other or spells and still have the need to be cautious of their enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T12:31:38-08:00","id":2835,"title":"","content":"Tatterdemalion King, would you please create a topic with the modifications and the Istincts you and your Co-ST did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T12:54:40-08:00","id":2842,"title":"","content":"All I'm gonna say, if Tatterdemalion gets his game, I'll say fuck it with the Idigam Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T13:33:27-08:00","id":2867,"title":"","content":"I'd like the benefits of the various forms to grow with the character. A whelp in Gauru may easily double in strength. I'd like to see a werewolf who has trained their mind and spirit for war having a War-Form that is dramatically more powerful than any whelp could muster, even without taking gifts into consideration.<br /> <br /> Some form of Wolf/Man balance could be found in this sort of growth. Harmony and Instinct could play a role here, too.<br /> <br /> ( I could see gifts and skills playing a role in this, but simply by having bonuses that can be purchased to improve forms, you can achieve this. Scope might be limited to specific groups of forms based on what they are. Scope groupings: Man (&amp; Near man), Gauru (&amp; near man, near wolf), Wolf (&amp; near wolf), Boosting a group instead of overall would be cheaper, and could later be extended to full scope. I'd limit which attributes fit which sets. Only Man should be able to get Intelligence, say, (or at least not Gauru) but I rather like restricting Presence to non-man. Wits clearly fits Wolf-like senses and attention to surroundings... etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T13:41:51-08:00","id":2872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2664#post2664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> im curious as to why. Why lunacy should be kept? Why it cannot be replace with common sense (human see giant bearsize wolf, human runs). Why there need to be pixie dust BS as failsafes. A human sees a werewolf and who he gonna tell? who is gonna believe him? i never saw the use for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are people with rage issues that can turn into nine foot tall monsters and they aren't exactly blessed with a plethora of memory altering powers. Heck, in the age of cell phone cameras all it takes is one werewolf flipping out because a cop decided to tase him to ruin everything for all the other werewolves.It's better if magic makes everyone even more likely to disbelieve photographic and video evidence and rationalize the ensuing carnage as the werewolf having freaky PCP strength and a handful of knives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:03:00-08:00","id":2879,"title":"","content":"Regarding Renown. I like it, although I am aware there are some mechanical issues but Renown is not a stat that is as broken as it seems some people think it is. The main thing that I like about Renown is, in a world where the Forsaken are beset by ALL the enemies Renown is one of the only ways Forsaken (and the Pure, for different reason) can literally wear on their sleeves how much respect should be given due to their deeds. That is a really nice concept, and I'd rather it be kept.<br /> <br /> Regarding Gauru power levels versus the feeling that werewolves should not be a &quot;war-splat&quot; but a &quot;hunt-splat&quot;, I imagine (with the current rules set) that if you're hunting with Gauru, you're not exactly the most subtle hunter. Hunting a human in the know? You're hunting with human and wolf forms. Gauru form should be used for when the going is tough and the risk is worth it.<br /> <br /> This way you get the hunting werewolves, and well as the werewolf of unbridled rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your milage may vary of course, but this is my opinion of the themes of these subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:03:31-08:00","id":2880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2835#post2835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tatterdemalion King, would you please create a topic with the modifications and the Istincts you and your Co-ST did?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will do ASAP. We're trying to finish off Shapeshifting Instincts right now, the rest are completed in their rough drafts. I want to have the entire initial shebang available first for later input and further cleaning up/tweaks. We're going under the assumption there are alternate Instinct levels (wer'e just not worrying about them just yet) and potentially room for additional Instincts. I'm hoping to have Shapeshifting up for posting in the next few days; a lot of the other setting revisions (such as Totem, Resonance, Loci an others) will be tossed up for people to peek through fairly soon. Keep an eye peeled for the new topic. Right now I definitely want to see more on the Wolf/Man balance; it's definitely something I'd use.<br /> <br /> As for Ephys; different strokes for different folks. It's impossible to please everyone, all of the time. If what I got with what thus far you've presented that you'd like here or in the old Forums and that's about it... I'd say fuck it to purchasing it much the same. I'm not a fan of new editions that only tweak some of the veneer and tweak a handful of systems; those work better as errata or short booklets to convert, rather than full on game books for me.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, screw it. I'll see how quickly we can toss up with what we have complete for the initial drafts first rather than waiting. Give me a bit to present some of the game/system changes, or quite a bit of them won't make sense if presented in a vacuum, Jesuncolo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:44:31-08:00","id":2917,"title":"","content":"@ Tatterdemalion King: You do have some good ideas. But, I'm not to fond of the &quot;humans as default food&quot; idea. While it is a trope of Werewolf fiction, I just don't think it'll work in Forsaken. I mean, while Werewolves aren't human, Forsaken take human lovers and have human families. In Werewolf fiction, Werewolves eat people because they have no control of their actions. To WILLING do it is something different altogether. it just doesn't click in my mind. How could I ever eat a human if I have a human wife and kids? I'd see them every time I did it. Of course, that adds to the whole personal horror thing, but I've never really cared for that either.<br /> <br /> Also, you and I have a very diferent out look on Lunacy. IMO, Lunacy is not a &quot;get outta jail free card&quot;, like you make it sound. If my understading is correct, whether or not the human remembers the event is irrelevent. If you reveled yourself to a human, it's still a Harmony sin because you just betrayed you predatory nature and the People because of you carelessness. But mostly the former. That's how I alway understood it. Not mention there's no way of telling whos Willower is high or not. Not to mention ST fiat. You still need to be careful. Other than that, most of you ideas are pretty solid.<br /> <br /> @ Kaho: I do see where your coming from, I really do. But I can't agree that Werewolves should be weaker because of numbers. You shouldn't judge a indivduals ability by the company he keeps. He needs to be able to stand on his own. The &quot;we fight together because we're weak&quot; is a Hunter the Vigil theme. It should never be a theme slapped on Werewolves, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Also, since you like to bring up Werewolves vs tanks, I feel the need to point out to you that in the Blood Talon chaper of Tribes of the Moon, there is a piece of fiction that has Forsaken tearing apart tanks. So, it's not as to far fetched as you'd think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 11-04-2013, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:55:07-08:00","id":2925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2294#post2294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one <a href=\"http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://ronspencer.files.wordpress.com/2011/12/fmooo.jpg</a> for example and every illustration at the start of a chapter in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's his work? Well then, other than I'd prefer to have the upper fangs more prominent than the lower, I like that sort of art and I think that fits Forsaken. While most Uratha are in hishu form, sure, they look completely normal (apart from the Predator's Menace, of course). However, when they shift into other forms - particularly the three &quot;intermediate&quot; forms between hishu and urhan - they should look like they're going to rip you to pieces. Just my opinion, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:30:51-08:00","id":2946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2917#post2917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Tatterdemalion King: You do have some good ideas. But, I'm not to fond of the &quot;humans as default food&quot; idea. While it is a trope of Werewolf fiction, I just don't think it'll work in Forsaken. I mean, while Werewolves aren't human, Forsaken take human lovers and have human families. In Werewolf fiction, Werewolves eat people because they have no control of their actions. To WILLING do it is something different altogether. it just doesn't click in my mind. How could I ever eat a human if I have a human wife and kids? I'd see them every time I did it. Of course, that adds to the whole personal horror thing, but I've never really cared for that either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i agree with you there, canibalism is a touchy subject and before someone throws the &quot;but vampires drink blood response&quot; eating someone is way more personal and thraumatic than drinkings his blood. The idea of leaving the farmville aspect of werewolf is good but it need to be another thing aside from canibalism. It would make thing messy for a table of players, it either it would become a little unconfortable to dm/play or you would get a mix of player who take the moral implication of that and players who OM NOM NOM every human they dont like, like it was candy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2917#post2917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you and I have a very diferent out look on Lunacy. IMO, Lunacy is not a &quot;get outta jail free card&quot;, like you make it sound. If my understading is correct, whether or not the human remembers the event is irrelevent. If you reveled yourself to a human, it's still a Harmony sin because you just betrayed you predatory nature and the People because of you carelessness. But mostly the former. That's how I alway understood it. Not mention there's no way of telling whos Willower is high or not. Not to mention ST fiat. You still need to be careful. Other than that, most of you ideas are pretty solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, you are miss informed there. It is a free &quot;get outta jail free card&quot;. The descripcion of the harmony sin you mention is<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character of appropriate Harmony who reveals<br /> his true nature or that of the People to ordinary humans<br /> (but not the wolf-blooded) is subject to a degeneration<br /> roll. Instances include public displays of bestial forms or<br /> Gift <b><u>uses that prove to have witnesses who understand</u></b><br /> <b><u>and remember what happened.</u></b> </div> </div> </div>For a human to remember the incident (only if he/she needs to, meaning actively trying to remember it and normally at this level is against his/her will) his/her willpower should be 5-7 min and even then he/she need a roll of intelligence + composure -3 and get an exceptional success and repeat this roll everytime he/she want to remember it. Even in 8-9 they have to spend a willpower point per turn to take any action except running. Its true that there is no way to determine NPCs willpower but to be a true threat to a werewolf they need willpower 8-9 min and thats facing a human with no willpower to spend. There are those alternate rules in the DM fiat section but it seems like a fix for a problem the same game creates for no reason. What would be lost of the game if you remove lunacy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2917#post2917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Kaho: I do see where your coming from, I really do. But I can't agree that Werewolves should be weaker because of numbers. You shouldn't judge a indivduals ability by the company he keeps. He needs to be able to stand on his own. The &quot;we fight together because we're weak&quot; is a Hunter the Vigil theme. It should never be a theme slapped on Werewolves, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, im not saying they should be weaker that they are now or that they shouldnt get a buff but i say that the buff shouldnt make them the physical powerhouse of the game. And you said that i shouldnt judge a individual by his company but you have to keep in mind that werewolves have by defaults the most tight knit parties in all the supernatural. They always have company thats the norm rather that the exception wich isnt true about the rest supernatual. If we use the marvels example im saying that they should be buffed to be like wolverine rather than hulk or if we want to get nerdy about it, i would say more like Daken than hulk. Again, if you think thats still too weak then i guess we should have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2917#post2917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since you like to bring up Werewolves vs tanks, I feel the need to point out to you that in the Blood Talon chaper of Tribes of the Moon, there is a piece of fiction that has Forsaken tearing apart tanks. So, it's not to far fetched as you'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you tell me that, i lost my faith in the world now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-04-2013, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:47:07-08:00","id":2961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, you are miss informed there. It is a free &quot;get outta jail free card&quot;. The descripcion of the harmony sin you mention is</div> </div> </div> </div>You are acting on bad faith here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character of appropriate Harmony who reveals<br /> his true nature or that of the People to ordinary humans<br /> (but not the wolf-blooded) is subject to a degeneration<br /> roll. Instances include public displays of bestial forms or<br /> <b><u>Gift uses</u> that prove to have witnesses who understand<br /> and remember what happened</b> </div> </div> </div>Just public displays of bestial forms require a roll, no matter if it's remembered or not. Gift uses, that you so apropiately left out of the bolded part, are the ones who require witnesses remembering things to qualify for Degeneration. If you use a Gift that no one can notice or remember then you are fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:52:13-08:00","id":2965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2961#post2961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just public displays of bestial forms require a roll, no matter if it's remembered or not. Gift uses, that you so apropiately left out of the bolded part, are the ones who require witnesses remembering things to qualify for Degeneration. If you use a Gift that no one can notice or remember then you are fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>IWhat bad faith? the part of remember what happened it seems to be geared toward lunacy. You could apply it only for gift but then that last line just dont make that much sense. You can interpret that uses of bestial form and/or gifts that proves to have withness and remember what happens applied or just gifts. It could be taking on both ways depending of the DM and rule lawyers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-04-2013, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:58:27-08:00","id":2969,"title":"","content":"Wich bad faith? The part when you deliberately left out of the bolded quote the part that could lead to a different interpretation than yours. That bad faith.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it could be interpreted <b>both</b> ways depending if you understood that &quot;or&quot; as inclusive or not, so no, Rahuman101 is not more &quot;missinformed&quot; than you or me or anyone else. Different interpretations of the same text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-04-2013, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:05:00-08:00","id":2979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2969#post2969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wich bad faith? The part when you deliberately left out of the bolded quote the part that could lead to a different interpretation than yours. That bad faith.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it could be interpreted <b>both</b> ways depending if you understood that &quot;or&quot; as inclusive or not, so no, Rahuman101 is not more &quot;missinformed&quot; than you or me or anyone else. Different interpretations of the same text.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIt was never bad faith, i understood that uses applies to both forms and gift. I read it that way and bolded the part relevant to it. All the tables of players i have play or DM with have that same understanding that i do all and i have alway had such understanding of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: you know what thorbes? i said he was missinformed for the reason i said that such rule should be interpreted that way, your way only has whether or not the phrase is inclusive. My definition has the last part of remembering wich ties to lunacy. So I only bold that part because i think is inclusive but if you gonna accuse me of being fraudulent about it you can stick you damm accusation where the sun dont shine because i pointed out my unsderstanding of a rule and you jump the gun to say im acting in bad faith? i didnt alter the text of the core or left a part relevant part of it and even the part after that proves more the point by saying that the lunacy is not so an absolute failsafe. And i didnt say rahuman was informed as an insult, i just pointed out why i think he was misreading the rule. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-04-2013, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:13:33-08:00","id":2988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2917#post2917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Tatterdemalion King: You do have some good ideas. But, I'm not to fond of the &quot;humans as default food&quot; idea. While it is a trope of Werewolf fiction, I just don't think it'll work in Forsaken. I mean, while Werewolves aren't human, Forsaken take human lovers and have human families. In Werewolf fiction, Werewolves eat people because they have no control of their actions. To WILLING do it is something different altogether. it just doesn't click in my mind. How could I ever eat a human if I have a human wife and kids? I'd see them every time I did it. Of course, that adds to the whole personal horror thing, but I've never really cared for that either.<br /> <br /> Also, you and I have a very diferent out look on Lunacy. IMO, Lunacy is not a &quot;get outta jail free card&quot;, like you make it sound. If my understading is correct, whether or not the human remembers the event is irrelevent. If you reveled yourself to a human, it's still a Harmony sin because you just betrayed you predatory nature and the People because of you carelessness. But mostly the former. That's how I alway understood it. Not mention there's no way of telling whos Willower is high or not. Not to mention ST fiat. You still need to be careful. Other than that, most of you ideas are pretty solid.<br /> <br /> @ Kaho: I do see where your coming from, I really do. But I can't agree that Werewolves should be weaker because of numbers. You shouldn't judge a indivduals ability by the company he keeps. He needs to be able to stand on his own. The &quot;we fight together because we're weak&quot; is a Hunter the Vigil theme. It should never be a theme slapped on Werewolves, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Also, since you like to bring up Werewolves vs tanks, I feel the need to point out to you that in the Blood Talon chaper of Tribes of the Moon, there is a piece of fiction that has Forsaken tearing apart tanks. So, it's as to far fetched as you'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Harmony relation to Lunacy isn't the motivating factor. It plays into it a portion, but it's much, much more to do with keeping humans a relevant threat to werewolves. The interpretations of what constitutes a Veil Breach and how it related to Harmony is actually fairly trivial to me by comparison, but you can bet I want to see Harmony heavily revised regardless given the near entire absence of human considerations in regards to it.<br /> <br /> Less so the default food, just abundant and an ongoing temptation. Wolves aren't nearly as common as they once were in many areas; werewolves by comparison often have heavy exposure to humans, even compared to spirits. They're an ongoing, tempting and (sometimes) easy source of Essence; most werewolves would prefer instead to go after spirits for what they need. That said, there was constant talk about how tasty humans were, how tempting, even addictive it was to eat one; there just wasn't any mechanical basis for it. I've given them one. Hence why the first time I treat it as usually happening, is your first (or a later) Death Rage when you're out of Essence. You may get some very nasty werewolves that do it willingly (see Predator Kings) with more consistency than others, but for most, it's a violent rampage and the taste of blood and flesh in your mouth after coming back to your senses. It's delicious, viscerally and supernaturally satisfying, and in turn, addictive.<br /> <br /> It's not a very hard compulsion to resist unless you indulge in it frequently (and in turn develop a cumulative -1 penalty to each later roll to avoid giving into the hunger). Frequent eaters are very likely to just do it uncontrollably after a while. Those who fight against it eventually triumph over their addiction and the urges until they decide to relapse, or have another Death Rage where they overtax themselves spiritually again. It basically works like this; your first taste of flesh gives you a Resolve + Composure roll (modified depending on circumstances; someone who did so via Death Rage won't start with a penalty; someone who -willingly- decided to eat, may). If you fail, you're addicted. Each time you willingly decide to indulge again, take a -1 Penalty. Each time you're presented with the chance to eat, fail the Resolve + Composure roll to resist eating, take a -1. If you succeed and resist giving in, you gain a +1 bonus to resisting it the next time. Get an Exceptional success at any point, and you shake off the addiction. Get a Dramatic Failure and... well... that varies depending on what seems most appropriate.<br /> <br /> One screwup isn't insurmountable. It'll give you cravings, but odds are you'll be able to triumph over them initially. Deciding to give into to consuming other wolves and humans and such though... well, that's when the problems arise. Constantly burning through your Essence reserves and going into Death Rage... that will eventually do a number on you. You don't walk into the game going &quot;mmm, long pork, I want my baby back baby back riiiibs&quot;, but it may certainly happen if things aren't kept in check. One thing of note is with the house revision I'm working on, we are thinking of borrowing a nod from Requiem in that prey animals may give you a bit of Essence at 1-2 Primal Urge if it appears that our harsher &quot;you get Essence from Hunting, -maybe- from other rare situations&quot; is too harsh. <br /> <br /> As for Tank Tearing... and? Never heard of the Strength, Rage, Shaping or other powers that can let you tear the shit out of things like that? That's not remotely to me any incentive that Gauru form alone can do that. That's effing ridiculous. Go figure, the Blood Talons are also the group that have common Affinity for Rage and Strength. Iron Rending. 'nuff said. It's not so much as being far-fetched; there are powers that will let werewolves do just that, and I've no problem with that. I just don't see it necessary as being an innate thing of being a werewolf. You're also entirely misunderstanding the context I was using; I wasn't talking Werewolves vs Literal Tanks (that's being more than a little pedantic), I was talking the idea of Werewolves as the RPG &quot;tank&quot; sorts. You know, being hit with mortar fire, running over land mines, taking a few shots from an automatic shotgun to the chest and brushing it off... really, really not my thing. To use a Marvel example; when I think Werewolf, I think someone more like Wolverine. He gets hurt, -badly- but he recovers eventually from what would kill a normal person and ready to tear some new assholes. I don't think The Incredible Hulk or Juggernaut (oddly, if I were to make a very, very loose comparison I'd say I think that with Promethean a bit) who pretty much just pushes past it . That could just be my internal paradigm there, but that's where I'm at. Let purchased powers cover the potential to 'tank out'. <br /> <br /> I think folks are intentionally going for absolutes that by not being like that, that means your werewolf is weak. On my end, I see little reason for them to band together as packs for strength when each one individually is a &quot;tank&quot; like that. They don't need to be -weaker- compared to their current iteration to justify roaming in packs. On the other end, I don't really see much benefit to turning it into a situation of an antagonist arms-race/escalation to pose their antagonists as consistently challenging or meaningful threats. That's part of the problem when things just start getting beefed up and more beefed up especially out of the gates; there should be incentive beyond simple instinct to need packs, and (this from an experienced W:tA player by the way), I really shouldn't be hitting a situation where literal heavy military weaponry is a cake walk early on. If I bring out a Thunderwyrm (using W:tA here), I expect it to be a big, very challenging, meaningful antagonist. Yet... I've seen a pack of rank 1s and 2s make mincemeat out of it in less than 5 rounds without some crazy ass rolls.<br /> <br /> That's precisely the sort of thing I don't want to be running into here if you get what I'm trying to say. I don't want them puny, weak or otherwise pushovers, and I don't believe they are right now remotely within the context of their own game. I don't want them de-buffed as it were all over the place to support their pack natures. I just don't want the equivalent of a nuclear Cold War escalation and proliferation of armaments (ugh, see Exalted in the early editions when new Exalts came out for an example of that, until Solars became less relevant in the role they were intended to be), just because another splat finally got some much needed beefing, or because the werewolves used to be much more tank-like in the games predecessor. Make sense? That's really the reason I bring it up; I've gotten folks constantly pushing that angle and now with Blood and Smoke, it's rearing it's head right back again. Not a fan of that. Not a fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:19:53-08:00","id":2992,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Lunacy: with the existence of the new Integrity rules for mortals, and particularly their Breaking Points for witnessing violence and/or the supernatural, I'd like to see Lunacy scrapped as a supernatural phenomenon in its own right. People still freak out when they see a man turn into a beast that starts shredding everything around it; but they do so because seeing a person transform is unsettling, and seeing a monster tear things apart is <i>scary</i> \u2014 <i>not</i> because werewolves generate some sort of spiritual \u201caura of fear\u201d. To the extent that special rules should exist for mortals freaking out when they see a werewolf, they should be \u201cmook rules\u201d that are designed to make the Storyteller\u2019s bookkeeping job easier by not having to track Integrity levels and Breaking Point rolls for mooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:21:37-08:00","id":2993,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was never bad faith, i understood that uses applies to both forms and gift. I read it that way and bolded the part relevant to it. All the tables of players i have play or DM with have that same understanding that i do all and i have alway had such understanding of it.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> Ok then, sorry about that (Rule number 1 and all that). Although it depends on how you read it, it could mean that just showing forms calls for Degeneration while Gift uses needs witnesses to remember and understand what they saw for it to call for a roll.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I also object is a &quot;free get out of jail card&quot;. Mages Disbelief works in similar ways, and it is still frowned upon to work any magic (even spells that can't be witnessed) before regular people. For one, you don't know how many Willpower does a given person have (worst if there are many), sooner rather than later someone will remember too much.<br /> <br /> Even if I'm ok with Lunacy, I rather have the Predatory Aura instead. The idea of triggering prey responses on others is just so much more thematic that regular PTSD-related amnesia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaho</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">[...]you can stick you damm accusation where the sun dont shine[...]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-04-2013, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:50:44-08:00","id":3024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2988#post2988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Tank Tearing... and? Never heard of the Strength, Rage, Shaping or other powers that can let you tear the shit out of things like that? That's not remotely to me any incentive that Gauru form alone can do that. That's effing ridiculous. Go figure, the Blood Talons are also the group that have common Affinity for Rage and Strength. Iron Rending. 'nuff said. It's not so much as being far-fetched; there are powers that will let werewolves do just that, and I've no problem with that. I just don't see it necessary as being an innate thing of being a werewolf. You're also entirely misunderstanding the context I was using; I wasn't talking Werewolves vs Literal Tanks (that's being more than a little pedantic), I was talking the idea of Werewolves as the RPG &quot;tank&quot; sorts. You know, being hit with mortar fire, running over land mines, taking a few shots from an automatic shotgun to the chest and brushing it off... really, really not my thing. To use a Marvel example; when I think Werewolf, I think someone more like Wolverine. He gets hurt, -badly- but he recovers eventually from what would kill a normal person and ready to tear some new assholes. I don't think The Incredible Hulk or Juggernaut (oddly, if I were to make a very, very loose comparison I'd say I think that with Promethean a bit) who pretty much just pushes past it . That could just be my internal paradigm there, but that's where I'm at. Let purchased powers cover the potential to 'tank out'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read your post and I understand where you're coming from. I don't fully agree, but that's going to happen. However, I feel the need to address the above quote so as to clairify what I was getting at. I never said Werewolves in Gauru should be able to tear apart tanks without the aid of Gifts or be unstoppable tanks themselves. I think this should be covered by Gifts as well. The reason I was pointing out that fiction was to show Kaho that the idea of Werewolves in Forsaken being capable of doing such a thing is there. The fiction makes no mention of Gift use, but we can assume that Gifts were used.<br /> <br /> I also think Wolverine is better example than Hulk when thinking of Werewolf. It's a much better comparison.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:50:44-08:00","id":3025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=2993#post2993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok then, sorry about that (Rule number 1 and all that). Although it depends on how you read it, it could mean that just showing forms calls for Degeneration while Gift uses needs witnesses to remember and understand what they saw for it to call for a roll.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I also object is a &quot;free get out of jail card&quot;. Mages Disbelief works in similar ways, and it is still frowned upon to work any magic (even spells that can't be witnessed) before regular people. For one, you don't know how many Willpower does a given person have (worst if there are many), sooner rather than later someone will remember too much.<br /> <br /> Even if I'm ok with Lunacy, I rather have the Predatory Aura instead. The idea of triggering prey responses on others is just so much more thematic that regular PTSD-related amnesia.<br /> <br /> <br /> Duly noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for that and i accept your apologie. Maybe being acused of being fraudulent is not so much for some but i take that insult very seriously. You can call me a lots variaton on the word bastard i wouldnt mind but that its a very personal insult to me. You didnt knew that so lets leave at that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-04-2013, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:54:53-08:00","id":3029,"title":"","content":"Works for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Now let's back to try to improve this game to its full potential <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T17:03:05-08:00","id":3035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=3024#post3024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I read your post and I understand where you're coming from. I don't fully agree, but that's going to happen. However, I feel the need to address the above quote so as to clairify what I was getting at. I never said Werewolves in Gauru should be able to tear apart tanks without the aid of Gifts or be unstoppable tanks themselves. I think this should be covered by Gifts as well. The reason I was pointing out that fiction was to show Kaho that the idea of Werewolves in Forsaken being capable of doing such a thing is there. The fiction makes no mention of Gift use, but we can assume that Gifts were used.<br /> <br /> I also think Wolverine is better example than Hulk when thinking of Werewolf. It's a much better comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAh I gotcha, I totally misunderstood where you were going with that, my bad. But on the note of Lunacy; after looking at the Kindred Predator Auras, for something that's got a somewhat 'light' effect Condition wise, wow do they ever work well. There's a whole lot of traction with these as a Lunacy replacement; you can already get the Spooked etc. Conditions as a mortal from what Dataweaver mentioned on a Breaking point loss for witnessing a supernatural event that covers gut fear and the like.<br /> <br /> The notion that you can create a condition that makes someone feel like prey via the Predatory Aura, more prone to fleeing, hiding and the like while you get an advantage on hunting with them is just too juicy to pass up. It's easy enough to present additional manifestations; breaking down the rational mind as a nod to Luna as being noted as being, well... mother madness, or the whole &quot;Dangerously sexy, predatory allure&quot; that sometimes got presented via Merits and elsewhere for the whole werewolf animal magnetism. I can already see 3 ways to cover Physical, Mental and Social manifestations for it that could be a lot of fun, but the ideas need some refining and tinkering. The Predatory Aura plays heavily on the Territorial Instincts I've been working on recently, but unfortunately the actual Auras themselves need some gelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T17:15:33-08:00","id":3041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=3035#post3035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAh I gotcha, I totally misunderstood where you were going with that, my bad. But on the note of Lunacy; after looking at the Kindred Predator Auras, for something that's got a somewhat 'light' effect Condition wise, wow do they ever work well. There's a whole lot of traction with these as a Lunacy replacement; you can already get the Spooked etc. Conditions as a mortal from what Dataweaver mentioned on a Breaking point loss for witnessing a supernatural event that covers gut fear and the like.<br /> <br /> The notion that you can create a condition that makes someone feel like prey via the Predatory Aura, more prone to fleeing, hiding and the like while you get an advantage on hunting with them is just too juicy to pass up. It's easy enough to present additional manifestations; breaking down the rational mind as a nod to Luna as being noted as being, well... mother madness, or the whole &quot;Dangerously sexy, predatory allure&quot; that sometimes got presented via Merits and elsewhere for the whole werewolf animal magnetism. I can already see 3 ways to cover Physical, Mental and Social manifestations for it that could be a lot of fun, but the ideas need some refining and tinkering. The Predatory Aura plays heavily on the Territorial Instincts I've been working on recently, but unfortunately the actual Auras themselves need some gelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Predatory Aura mechcanics are steller. Lunacy or something similar can easily be applied using those rules. I believe I heard somewhere that the Splats will be getting an equivalant Aura power like the Kindreds. I'm wanting to call it Primal Aura for Werewolves.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. It's all good. I think what was happening between us was just a bunch of misunderstandings.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No hard feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 11-04-2013, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T19:29:40-08:00","id":3100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1424#post1424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Get rid of Renown. It's a tacked on system. It's a holdover. It's one of the, if not -the- most complained about aspect of W:tF I've ran into. It's unwieldy. What it's presented to do makes little to no sense in the spiritual concept, especially regarding effective rank. As a power cap it makes even -less- sense. It's precepts make little sense in regards to the Shadow and Spirits as a whole. Look at merits like Mantle; Danse Macabre's Status merits and similar. That's more on track. I could get into this much, much more in-depth but lets leave this as is for now and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Say that Renown as it currently stands is removed. What would you have replace it in Gift dice pools?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T22:36:43-08:00","id":3188,"title":"","content":"Assuming Gifts themselves remained in their current fashion? Primal Urge (as it always was a measure of spiritual potency regardless, and it'd likely be used to determine effective Rank without the Renown system anyhow) or like many splats, ones rating in the Gift set if one needed a quick and dirty.<br /> <br /> I'd honestly treat Rank as equal to half the Werewolf's Primal Urge rounded up (yes, this would mean as a brand new werewolf you'd get far less respect and may get spiritual harassment for being low man on the totem pole), or Half your Primal Urge rounded up +1 if you want to present the situation as less dire for new werewolves. To reflect the Pure's advantage in that arena, I'd give them a +1 bonus to that, or just give them access to a Pure merit that bolsters their honorary rank in social dealings (not on gift dice pools).<br /> <br /> You could be generous and keep it just a straight Primal Urge, or you could use honorary spirit Rank for it. Keep in mind that, while costly for initial merit points, you could start as a Primal Urge 3 with a starting werewolf (meaning by this notion, you'd start as effective Rank 2, having 2 dice to each Gift on top of an attribute + skill, or 3 dice if using straight Primal-Urge). Given the costs and limitations of the old Renown set and GMC experience, I don't feel it'd be a big problem given how costly it was as is to get high Renown-based bonuses. As is, I'm not all that keen on keeping Gifts in their current incarnation and common means of garnering; they're one of the biggest messes W:tF has at the moment. Powers gained from spirits? Sure. Gift lists with renown requirements? Not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T03:50:45-08:00","id":3350,"title":"","content":"So regarding the Lunacy with conditions point - a &quot;Prey's Mind&quot; condition is added onto the mortal?<br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________<br /> <br /> <b>Condition: &quot;Prey's Mind&quot; </b>(<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">it's a terrible name, but I can't think of anything else without coffee - I'm tempted to just leave the name Lunacy, but I like the prey response theme</span>)<br /> <br /> If a mortal suffers a breaking point witnessing a werewolf's obvious supernatural ability (for example shapeshaping and obvious Gift displays) the mortal gains the condition &quot;<b>Prey's Mind</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Whilst under this condition the mortal must get herself from the source of werewolf power in the quickest way. This includes attacking and destroying obstacles in her way, but never the source of &quot;<b>Prey's Mind</b>&quot;. She acts only on instinct and is incapable of complex thought.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Once the mortal cannot percieve or believe that she is pursued or in the presence of the origin of the condition, the condition ends. Immediately roll willpower penalised by the werewolf who caused this condition's Primal Urge. A dramatic failure indicates no memory from the cause of the condition to the end, and she suffers -2 to composure tests for a month, a failure indicates only half memories of a frightful beast and piss-your-pants terror. Success indicates she remembers most details of the incident, but unless has cause otherwise to, fills in the gap by assuming she was attacked by a large animal or some other coincidence. Exceptional success indicates that she remembers all of it, even if she doesn't necessarily believe it, the werewolf who caused this may have issues within the future.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat</b>: <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">No idea. Any thoughts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b>: Should stuff like sidestepping be included as triggers?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:37:00-08:00","id":3439,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Primal Aura&quot; should be more proactive. As was said, the way Integrity works now it will automatically be a Breaking Point for most people to se a giant man-wolf doing man-wolf things around. As failed Breaking Points can already give you Conditions (there are some suggested but nothing prevents the Storyteller and the Player to decide to apply one different from those, like Amnesia), there's no need of a passive mechanic like that.<br /> <br /> The Primal Aura should be something you actively use on others to put the fear of Father Wolf in them. The effects of the Condition are probably in the right track. I would change the Resolution part, though. It almost seem as a different Condition on its own with all those memory effects and Penalties to rolls.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T09:05:21-08:00","id":3548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=3188#post3188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly treat Rank as equal to half the Werewolf's Primal Urge rounded up (yes, this would mean as a brand new werewolf you'd get far less respect and may get spiritual harassment for being low man on the totem pole), or Half your Primal Urge rounded up +1 if you want to present the situation as less dire for new werewolves. To reflect the Pure's advantage in that arena, I'd give them a +1 bonus to that, or just give them access to a Pure merit that bolsters their honorary rank in social dealings (not on gift dice pools).<br /> <br /> You could be generous and keep it just a straight Primal Urge, or you could use honorary spirit Rank for it. Keep in mind that, while costly for initial merit points, you could start as a Primal Urge 3 with a starting werewolf (meaning by this notion, you'd start as effective Rank 2, having 2 dice to each Gift on top of an attribute + skill, or 3 dice if using straight Primal-Urge). Given the costs and limitations of the old Renown set and GMC experience, I don't feel it'd be a big problem given how costly it was as is to get high Renown-based bonuses. As is, I'm not all that keen on keeping Gifts in their current incarnation and common means of garnering; they're one of the biggest messes W:tF has at the moment. Powers gained from spirits? Sure. Gift lists with renown requirements? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Primal Urge being the rank is better suited, especially if at any time there were to be a later book detailing more higher level play, Werewolves, even newer ones are supposed to be frightening to spirits. Spirits dislike them, but it doesn't necessarily mean they should consider them so much lesser<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T09:43:28-08:00","id":3573,"title":"","content":"So Honorary Rank = Primal Urge?<br /> <br /> It could work as normal games run between PU 1-5 and a t PU 6+ we are getting into uncharted territory, so why not?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they are only half spirit, that sure makes then less respeted by pure ephemeral beings, so PU/2 would also work fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:54:31-08:00","id":3613,"title":"","content":"I definitely wouldn't use a straight Primal Urge to effective Spirit Rank; Werewolves aren't -that- badass when it comes to the spirit ecology that early on. Halve it, or Halve it and add +1, otherwise it just gets plain out silly (if not putting little emphasis on going higher than PU 6 in regards to spirits). A straight conversion is simply too much. Honestly though, for Forsaken I'd just keep it at half; they're in a shitty situation with the Shadow, they're actively hated outside of the Elunim and wolf spirits, they shouldn't be catching a break let alone sky-rocketing in clout (or if you use the 2 Rank difference = attacks akin to Banes for spirits) or ability to tear through them. Let other Merits tweak around with it.<br /> <br /> That and the notion that a PU 8+ Werewolf could effectively outrank Luna seems ridiculous. They should fall within the 1-5 Rank scale, with some goodies that may push them into the lofty legends of Incarnae as far as their social clout goes once you hit those crazy high PU levels. It doesn't really work with a straight translation, but then, old Renown had it's own calculation rather than the Primary Renown alone being your measure of rank too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:18:55-08:00","id":3633,"title":"","content":"Divide by three, round up and add 1 if you're going to go for Primal Urge as a Rank indicator \u2014 that puts the breakdown in roughly the same range bands as Changeling does with Wyrd Evolution in play (kiths opening up at the first point of the first band, the second of the second, the third of the third, and borderline godhood at the last) as well as keeping the Lodge of Scars' established precedent of &quot;if you have an honorary Rank of 4 or more you're pretty definitely some flavor of badass.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with Renown, personally, and I don't find it remotely likely that it's going to go away in Idigam Chronicle, so I'm just sitting here reading the existing books and biding my time until April.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T12:29:58-08:00","id":3684,"title":"","content":"I like that calculation as well. Though I should clarify when I say I want Renown gone, I mean in it's current functional incarnation. I'm imagining it'll stick around, though more in the context of social merits or something that dovetails with the notion of Tribal and Auspice accord, potentially with the inclusion of something like a Legend merit. Some of the spitballing by the writers on board previously points to some very divergent shifts being bandied about regarding Renown (including some ideas like it's removal and replacement with Influences) among other ideas. I doubt it'll be entirely omitted; even I'm using a form of it in the current tinkering, but it's function and form is drastically different. <br /> <br /> Either way, I may stick with the divide by 3, round up and add 1, it seems pretty good for how Rank flows, and inevitably getting to the loft Rank 5 requiring some -serious- supernatural potency. Leaves quite a bit of room for merits and other things to fiddle with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:46:42-08:00","id":3725,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you stick with spirit rank as renown, you can actually become the bane of huge ass spirits by virtue of it alone, which is pretty awesome.<br /> <br /> I kinda wonder how that would work with y'know, your totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-05-2013, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:09:24-08:00","id":3747,"title":"","content":"Another thing I want to see in the Idigam Chronicles is a section on Aspects from Signs of the Moon. Aspects are super cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:25:42-08:00","id":3759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=3747#post3747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I want to see in the Idigam Chronicles is a section on Aspects from Signs of the Moon. Aspects are super cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, adding some omph to some of them wouldn't be a bad idea, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T15:35:05-08:00","id":3804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=3548#post3548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Primal Urge being the rank is better suited, especially if at any time there were to be a later book detailing more higher level play, Werewolves, even newer ones are supposed to be frightening to spirits. Spirits dislike them, but it doesn't necessarily mean they should consider them so much lesser</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I disagree. I think - and mind, this is (perhaps obviously) personal opinion here - that it would be very interesting if spirits viewed lesser-Ranked werewolves as prey. I think the Shadow should be entirely dangerous to enter into, especially alone. If you're a new werewolf with Honorary Spirit Rank 1 (however that's calculated) and you run into a Rank 2 spirit or, Luna forbid, a Rank 3, then shit just got dangerous for you. Now, if you're with your pack? Okay, then the spirit might get a lot more cautious. about things.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of a very Darwinian approach to the Shadow. If you're strong enough, or lucky enough - maybe alone, but much safer with a pack - then you can get through. Or if you're strong enough, weaker spirits will respect your abilities at least. Stronger spirits may evaluate your threat level and determine their responses based on their personalities, the situation, and so on. I want the Shadow to be a scary damn place for even werewolves to go, where they might feel like or end up as prey to one or more spirits who are bigger and stronger than them. (Or can swarm them.) I want the pack to matter - a lone werewolf might be prey, but an entire pack is a force to be reckoned with. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts on the matter anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T02:16:52-08:00","id":4163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're a new werewolf with Honorary Spirit Rank 1 (however that's calculated) and you run into a Rank 2 spirit or, Luna forbid, a Rank 3, then shit just got dangerous for you. Now, if you're with your pack? Okay, then the spirit might get a lot more cautious. about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That remind me of a thought I had when that thing about &quot;2 Ranks above counts as Bane&quot; was first mentioned. What about if Packs have a Rank too? Maybe individuals are low Ranked, but when acting as a Pack they are considered of a higher Rank. That's another thing for the spirits to fear Werewolf Packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:16:31-08:00","id":4246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4163#post4163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That remind me of a thought I had when that thing about &quot;2 Ranks above counts as Bane&quot; was first mentioned. What about if Packs have a Rank too? Maybe individuals are low Ranked, but when acting as a Pack they are considered of a higher Rank. That's another thing for the spirits to fear Werewolf Packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that could definitely work. Now what to base that from that is simple, clean, and intuitive...hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:50:05-08:00","id":4267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4246#post4246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that could definitely work. Now what to base that from that is simple, clean, and intuitive...hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>A group of werewolves of a minimum number (3+) would count, collectively, as one (or two, depending on how extreme you want this to be) higher than the maximum virtual Rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:03:43-08:00","id":4276,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely qualified to talk here (Forsaken is one of my least favorite gamelines, despite what seems like nearly universal love from folks), but I want to see more horror in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Forsaken suffers from a few similar gripes I have with Awakening; you're a normal person who one day sort of gets superpowers (this is a vast oversimplification, I know). Now you can shift into a wolf (or wolf-man, or man-wolf) and your job is to police some animistic spirits and fend off the Pure. The jarring peek behind the curtain (becoming a blood-drinking undead thing after an Embrace that you didn't ask for, being snatched away by horrifying 'aliens' and having your life replaced, outright dying and having to make a deal with a very insane monster in order to return, or even Hunter's &quot;holy shit, the supernatural is real and it is a threat&quot;) is lacking in Werewolf (and Mage even moreso, but that hardly belongs here), as is a strong motivation to do what a Garou is expected to do. <br /> <br /> It seems much less like a game of personal horror and more a game about becoming a spirit-themed superhero. Maybe this is what people like, but the themes I associate with werewolves (loss of control, an inability to live in society well, a terrifying &quot;this isn't me&quot; sensation) are lost in favor of blindly accepting your new job as a magic, fuzzy cop, as dictated to you by a group of strangers. Most games are played as 'rookies,' and yet Forsaken are expected to just take on their role in the world after a traumatic First Change and a group of nutjobs track you down and give you a bunch of mythology that you've never heard of before.<br /> <br /> Again; I don't terribly enjoy W:tF, and I may well be ignorant of (or unreceptive to) what folks like about the game. I'm just pitching my two cents in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:20:07-08:00","id":4289,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: They aren't 'garou', they're Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:23:43-08:00","id":4292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the themes I associate with werewolves (loss of control, an inability to live in society well, a terrifying &quot;this isn't me&quot; sensation)</div> </div> </div> </div>All of those are on Werewolf already. For once you suddenly realise you weren't never, ever human in the first place, that has to come as a shock and make you re-think about your identity till the moment. Second, they do have dificulties to live in <i>human</i> society (they get penalties to social rolls from Primal Urge) as they are feral and humans sort of sense it. And finally they have a very, very short fuse, so the lost of control them is there too, a werewolf can never know when a heated argument with a familiar or your couplecould end with a fade to black only to recover your senses covered in gore that used to be your beloved ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:33:02-08:00","id":4302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4289#post4289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick: They aren't 'garou', they're Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rats, I always make that mistake. Whoops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:09:17-08:00","id":4387,"title":"","content":"I love Werewolves, but WtF has left me. . . cold, for some reason. Not that I think the most common complaint I've heard about it -- that it's solely about protecting your magic rock from the Monster of the Week -- is entirely valid, the game's focus seems a bit too narrow.<br /> <br /> The fundamental unit of Werewolf is the Pack. The Pack is all-important, you need one to survive. Beyond Pack, you have Auspice, which is what you do (you can, perhaps uncharitably, boil it down into a &quot;class&quot; system: rogue, caster, leader, support, warrior), Tribe and Lodge are how you do it. Auspice is most useful at the Pack level. . . the gifts of your Auspice let you work well with other Pack members of different Auspices, letting the Pack tackle a wider array of challenges. A pack made up of all Rahu is very quickly going to fall into that old adage about only having a hammer, for example. However, Tribe and Lodge can, and should, represent vast differences in philosophy, some of which are simply not compatible with each other, but are forced to work together because, as a wise man once said, &quot;The whole fuckin' world's against us, Silent Bob.&quot; Pack members of different Tribes will have vastly different philosophies on how to handle a given situation, and the Pack must come up with some way of reconciling those differences, at least on a case-by-case basis. In short, Auspice brings the Pack together, Tribe threatens to tear it apart, and that's the source of great interpersonal conflict and character development. You know what you call a group of people who always think the same way, always get along, and never disagree? Well, I was going to go with &quot;boring,&quot; but another word that applies is &quot;sheep.&quot; Werewovles are NOT sheep.<br /> <br /> I agree somewhat on the idea that Werewolf isn't D&amp;D, and you shouldn't need one of every Auspice to form a viable group. I do, however, like the concept of &quot;Blessed Packs&quot; that DO have one member of every Auspice, and how their versatility is more than the sum of its parts. That should be the fundamental function of a pack. . . being more than just the werewolves who comprise it. A pack of all Rahu is certainly going to be terrifying to fight in straight battle, but they are going to have certain deficiencies in other areas. How much that actually hampers them is up to the game the ST and players want to play. I'm sure there are groups out there who would get a kick out of a chronicle that is actually focused on the idea of four Rahu trying to be sneaky, subtle, and political.<br /> <br /> The problem is, unless Auspice is fundamentally changed, it's always going to be likened to forming a D&amp;D party, because at its most basic level Auspice IS your role in werewolf society, what kind of gifts (and Gifts) you have to offer a potential pack. And I really think any attempt to move away from that would be doomed to failure, since if Auspice doesn't highlight what abilities you have as a werewolf. . . well, then what DOES it do? Any other approach, in my mind at least, runs the risk of Auspices becoming 'samey' and ultimately irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:10:13-08:00","id":4388,"title":"","content":"One thing I would like to see, perhaps related to Auspice and perhaps divorced from it, is the concept of Pack Rank. The whole Alpha, Beta, Gamma, Delta, Omega thing. Wolves and humans both crave rank and hierarchy, so why would a werewolf pack be any different? They'd want one wolf to be the leader, and to follow that leader (which certainly doesn't imply that others would give up aspirations of leadership, or always agree with, or even necessarily obey, said leader.) A structure something like:<br /> <br /> Alpha: The leader. (Usually) only one in a given pack.<br /> Beta: Just under the leader. Could be the leader's right-hand wolf, the next strongest wolf, or several wolves relatively-equal to each other. If there's only one Beta, she'll probably take over the pack if the Alpha dies. If there are several Betas, there's probably one who is clearly intended to be the Alpha's successor, &quot;more-than-equal,&quot; you might say.<br /> Gamma: Probably the bulk of any given pack. An Alpha, one or two Betas, and the rest likely Gammas.<br /> Delta: The newest or weakest member of a pack.<br /> Omega: The Lone Wolf, with no pack.<br /> <br /> Exactly what Pack Rank would mean, or do, in play is something I don't have any ideas on at the moment. Just about anything I can think of to mechanically reinforce the concept either runs into enforcing player behavior (giving higher-ranking pack members abilities or bonuses related to abilities that let them control lower-ranking pack members), or overlaps with other aspects (giving Alphas abilities that let them co-ordinate the pack in combat, for instance.)<br /> <br /> It should be noted that modern wolf researching is challenging the old idea that wolf packs have a strict dominance hierarchy based on physical challenge. The old model was that the wolf pack is run by the Alpha, the biggest, strongest, meanest wolf, who beats down any other wolf who challenges him, and is the only wolf allowed to get busy with the lady wolf. The other wolves sort themselves into order based on strength and power, challenging each other for position in the pack, a sort of sorting algorithm of furry badassery. More modern research suggests that dominance is tied to breeding, not the other way around. Wolves are dominant because they are the genetic parents of most of the pack, they don't get to breed because they are dominant. The pack structure above follows the old, perhaps flawed model, for two reasons. First, the human part of the Uratha will try and make sense of things, make rules to govern what is, in essence, instinct. Thus, they have adopted the human understanding of how wolf packs work to put into words what their instincts are telling them. Second, since Uratha should not mate with Uratha, basing pack dominance on mated pairs and genetic parentage just doesn't work. Perhaps there are groups of younger Uratha challenging the old pack structure, looking to base it on something more modern, both in terms of newer understanding of wolves and a more equality-based human society. . .<br /> <br /> All of this is to put more focus on the game's pack level, which I believe is where it needs to be. There should be forces (Tribe, Lodge, even Rank, and especially basic personality conflict) that want to tear the pack apart, but when it really matters, and the pack bands together, they should be able to move mountains (perhaps literally.) Some of the most compelling stories ever told are about groups of people on the verge of hating each other, but when they DO come together they are unstoppable. Buffy's Slayerettes, the crew of <i>Serenity</i>, and the Avengers just to name three off the top of my head (and it's no mistake Joss Whedon was involved in all three. There are are worse people to learn the storytelling craft from.) As Tony Stark said of the Avengers, it takes them awhile to get any traction. But remember how amazing it was when the whole team finally coalesced, and what they were able to accomplish together as a group. They'll never see eye-to-eye on some things, and that's okay, because when it counts, all that matters is the goal in front of them.<br /> <br /> Determining pack structure: Like I said, this could possibly be tied to Reknown, with relative Reknown ranks informing overall pack structure, or it could be determined solely within the pack itself by whatever means they deem fit. The classic example is that the werewolf who can beat the snot out of all the others is Alpha, but some werewolves realize that simple physical prowess tells you jack-all about a given Uratha's actual leadership ability.<br /> <br /> Benefits: I had a thought about Pack Structure benefits, making use of Conditions/Tilts. Essentially, different Ranks within a pack can give each other Conditions/Tilts. For instance:<br /> <br /> <b>Followed</b><br /> The Pack has rallied behind their leader, ready to follow.<br /> <b>Requirement:</b> A Gamma can give this Condition/Tilt to an Alpha.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> If the Alpha's next action is to declare a teamwork or hunting pattern action, all secondary actors in that action gain a +2 bonus to their rolls.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Pack, by being willing to follow the Alpha, gives the Alpha a bonus to lead the Pack, but only if the Alpha actually leads the Pack.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to another point. Something I miss from WtA is the concept of Pack Tactics. I remember tripping over those after running a Werewolf game for quite some time, and thinking &quot;holy crap, factor in Crinos form, and these are EPIC!&quot; While I don't think we need quite that level of awesome in this game, if the core of WtF is bringing the Pack together, they should have some means to actually work as a Pack. So, in a similar vein as Tactics from HtV, I submit that Idiagm Chronicles needs to bring back Pack Tactics. I choose to call them Hunting Patterns, both because of its focus on &quot;the Wolf must Hunt&quot; and in slight reference to one of my favorite Werewolf novels, <i>Bitten</i> by Kelly Armstrong. In it she mentions the various patterns wolf packs use to hunt being engraved in her brain through instinct, and how she and her pack can select a pattern and use it without actually talking to each other (since they can't talk in wolf form.) They use the pattern I example below to take down a deer. Later, they use the same pattern to take down a lone werewolf, and she notes that, while the pattern was in his instinctual brain just like it is in hers, because he's a lone wolf he's never used it, and thus fails to recognize it when it's employed against him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:11:03-08:00","id":4389,"title":"","content":"<b>Running Down The Prey</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Urshul or Urhan form, Stamina 3 (pursuit wolves), Stealth 3 (ambush wolves.)<br /> <b>Requires:</b> 1 &quot;Ambush&quot; wolf, 2 &quot;Pursuit&quot; wolves, each additional &quot;pursuit&quot; wolf adds +1.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> &quot;Ambush&quot; wolf Wits + Stealth, &quot;Pursuit&quot; wolves Intelligence + Survival<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended/Instant and Contested<br /> <b>Description:</b> At least two wolves pursue the prey, nipping at its heels and forcing it to flee. Very carefully, they control the direction of its flight, wearing it down and driving it into the waiting jaws of their comrade.<br /> The &quot;ambush&quot; wolf rolls Wits + Stealth, opposed by the prey's Wits + Composure (or Survival.) Success indicates that the ambush wolf may successfully declare a surprise attack on the prey when it comes within range. Multiple wolves may lie in ambush if desired, each making a separate roll. The &quot;pursuit&quot; wolves roll extended Intelligence + Survival rolls to keep the prey on course and running towards their waiting comrade.<br /> <b>Potential Modifiers:</b> Open terrain (+1 to pursuit wolves, -1 to ambush wolves), unfamiliar terrain (-1 to pursuit wolves), low visibility (+1 to ambush wolves, -1 to pursuit wolves), pursuit wolves have five or more speed than the prey (+2 to pursuit wolves)<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The pursuit wolves chase the prey in the wrong direction, leading it away from the ambush wolf and potentially becoming lost themselves. The ambush wolf somehow alerts the prey to her presence, allowing the prey to avoid her attack.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The prey breaks in an unexpected direction, and must be brought back on course. The ambush wolf fails to conceal herself, losing the benefit of a surprise attack (though she may still attempt a regular attack.)<br /> <b>Success:</b> The wolves chase the prey towards the ambush wolf. The ambush wolf conceals herself in preparation for a surprise attack.<br /> <b>Dramatic Success:</b> The pursuit wolves panic the prey, causing it to pour everything it has into an escape attempt, unaware that it is only driving closer to its doom. The prey takes a -2 penalty on its Wits + Composure (or Survival) check to spot the Ambush wolf. The Ambush wolf's extra successes are their own reward.<br /> <br /> <b>Modification: Stalking the Prey</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Hishu form, Intimidation 3 and Streetwise 3 (pursuit wolves), Stealth 3 (ambush wolf).<br /> <b>Requires:</b> 1 &quot;Ambush&quot; wolf, 2 &quot;Pursuit&quot; wolves.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> &quot;Ambush&quot; wolf Wits + Stealth, &quot;Pursuit&quot; wolves Intelligence + Streetwise.<br /> <b>Action:</b> &quot;Ambush&quot; wolf Instant and Contested, &quot;Pursuit&quot; wolves Extended<br /> <b>Description:</b> The same pattern that allows a pack of wolves to run down, ambush, and kill a deer in the woods can be applied to stalking bipedal prey in the glass-and-steel forest. Rather than chase the prey down, however, the pursuit wolves simply drive the prey forward by appearing to be someone you'd rather cross the street to avoid. It is exactly this behavior that drives the prey towards the ambush wolf.<br /> As above, the Ambush wolf rolls Wits + Stealth, contested by the prey's Wits + Composure. Again, multiple wolves may lie in ambush, each making their own roll. Because this stalk takes place in Hishu form, the ambush wolves have a much greater range of ambush responses at their disposal, including guns and grapples, depending on their intent towards this prey. The Pursuit wolves roll Intelligence + Streetwise, since navigating the streets and alleyways and flushing their prey down the correct paths is more important to this exercise than looking dangerous, which is something werewolves tend to do by default.<br /> <b>Potential Modifiers:</b> Intimately familiar terrain (+2 to all wolves), Unfamiliar terrain (-2 to pursuit wolves), Pursuit wolf with Intimidation 4 (+1), Pursuit wolf with Intimidation 5 (+2), Pursuit Wolf with high Primal Urge (+1 per -1 Social penalty), Ambush wolf with ranged weapon (+1 per ten yards of range).<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The prey, terrified at these creepy folks following him around, does something completely human: he finds other people. He walks into a public space, or worse, finds a cop or two. The ambush wolf alerts the prey to her presence, allowing him to avoid her trap.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The pursuit wolves drive the prey off-course. The ambush wolf fails to conceal herself, losing the benefits of a surprise attack.<br /> <b>Success:</b> The pursuit wolves drive the prey towards the ambush wolf. The ambush wolf successfully conceals herself, gaining the benefits of a surprise attack.<br /> <b>Dramatic Success:</b> The pursuit wolves so successfully draw the prey's attention that he is heedless of the danger he's being driven towards. The prey takes a -2 penalty on his Wits + Composure roll to notice the ambush wolf. The ambush wolf's extra successes are their own reward.<br /> <br /> Sticky Widgets: This breaks a lot of the conventions about teamwork and Tactics from Hunter, since these rolls do not have Primary and Secondary actors. In essence, each wolf is acting on its own as part of the pack, rather than all helping each other as in a straight Teamwork roll. This has the &quot;drawback&quot; that, if one wolf fails, the whole thing could collapse. . . however, that is integral enough to the way packs actually work that I feel confident in declaring feature, not bug. Other Hunting Patterns may play the Teamwork rules more straight, but I feel that most would probably still focus on each wolf's individual contribution, rather than abstracting it out to roll bonuses for a Primary Actor. Roll timing would be another issue that could arise. The Ambush wolves make their rolls as the prey closes, at the end of the chase. The Pursuit wolves are making their rolls right up until the prey closes to within range of the ambush wolf. Again, this could lead to the ambush wolf screwing up at the last minute, making the whole thing fruitless (but again, this is something of truth in RPG.) It also means that the Ambush wolf has nothing to do but wait while the pursuit wolves chase/stalk the prey to them. Personally, I find the potential of scenes using this tactic engaging, but I could understand some players &quot;relegated&quot; to the role of Ambush Wolf being bored while their packmates are chasing the prey thither and yon. There's also the question of further modification. Personally, were Hunting Patterns or something similar to make it into Idiagm Chronicles, I'd like to see a section about creating and modifying them like Hunter Tactics. After all, there's nothing physically preventing a pack of wolves from chasing prey into, instead of the waiting jaws of their packmate, the waiting crosshairs of his sniper rifle. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:21:15-08:00","id":4479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4246#post4246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that could definitely work. Now what to base that from that is simple, clean, and intuitive...hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>An idea I like as well. Though with individual Rank potency being what it is, it seems like it's a mechanic that'd work better if by default Forsaken/Pure ranked low and by working in packs they become more of a threat. If they're individually a threat via Rank it may turn into overkill depending on treatment. There's also the consideration of what a high-Ranking werewolf in a pack might do to impact this when in an otherwise low-Ranking pack; do these individuals increase it more than a base expectation? Is it purely based on numbers? Average of the pack members? A straight conversion where there's an effective low Rank (1 or 2) for the members, but each additional one increases it by 1?<br /> <br /> Definitely requires more thought, but I can definitely see some potential there. Right now we're working on revised merits, and Pack Bond is one of them; you don't -need- a Totem merit, nor that one really to work as a pack, but you get increasing benefits with that one. It makes me think that tossing in a rating where it increases the overall members effective rank by 1 where they work together wouldn't be a bad idea, reflecting collective supernatural potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:34:29-08:00","id":4486,"title":"","content":"I always found it odd that despite being a combo of two highly social species (and yes, I know, half-spirit too), <i>Werewolf</i> ends up being the least social of all the games - it's just you and your pack, with occasional run ins with neighboring Uratha/Anshega. I'd like to see a fix for this, or at least more options for different 'Tiers', like in HtV. I didn't care much for the <i>Circuit/Conclave </i>offered in the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide.<br /> <br /> And I'd like to see more variety/importance in the Tribes. They feel, to me, like a secondary class to be stacked on top of your character's auspice, not like actual groups with goals and a way of looking at the world. They're barely relevant when compared to, say, <i>Vampire's</i> Covenants. I highly doubt it'll happen, but I'd love it if each Tribe had a different take on the werewolf origin story, or a different story altogether. Give us options beyond <i>'descended from Father Spirit Cop,'</i> let there be tensions between the Tribes, but have the Pure be so vile that they band together to take them down - oh, and make the Pure actually tempting to join.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/542-witch","name":"Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T21:49:45-08:00","id":4849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4388#post4388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to another point. Something I miss from WtA is the concept of Pack Tactics. I remember tripping over those after running a Werewolf game for quite some time, and thinking &quot;holy crap, factor in Crinos form, and these are EPIC!&quot; While I don't think we need quite that level of awesome in this game, if the core of WtF is bringing the Pack together, they should have some means to actually work as a Pack. So, in a similar vein as Tactics from HtV, I submit that Idiagm Chronicles needs to bring back Pack Tactics. I choose to call them Hunting Patterns, both because of its focus on &quot;the Wolf must Hunt&quot; and in slight reference to one of my favorite Werewolf novels, <i>Bitten</i> by Kelly Armstrong. In it she mentions the various patterns wolf packs use to hunt being engraved in her brain through instinct, and how she and her pack can select a pattern and use it without actually talking to each other (since they can't talk in wolf form.) They use the pattern I example below to take down a deer. Later, they use the same pattern to take down a lone werewolf, and she notes that, while the pattern was in his instinctual brain just like it is in hers, because he's a lone wolf he's never used it, and thus fails to recognize it when it's employed against him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In &quot;The Rage&quot; pages 156 to 159, there are Pack Tactics !<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T22:20:12-08:00","id":4861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4849#post4849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In &quot;The Rage&quot; pages 156 to 159, there are Pack Tactics !</div> </div> </div> </div>They should totally be covered in the Idigam Chronicles instead of tucked away in the back of a supplement though. They add such a nice extra factor to being a part of a pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:25:09-08:00","id":5019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4479#post4479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An idea I like as well. Though with individual Rank potency being what it is, it seems like it's a mechanic that'd work better if by default Forsaken/Pure ranked low and by working in packs they become more of a threat. If they're individually a threat via Rank it may turn into overkill depending on treatment. There's also the consideration of what a high-Ranking werewolf in a pack might do to impact this when in an otherwise low-Ranking pack; do these individuals increase it more than a base expectation? Is it purely based on numbers? Average of the pack members? A straight conversion where there's an effective low Rank (1 or 2) for the members, but each additional one increases it by 1?<br /> <br /> Definitely requires more thought, but I can definitely see some potential there. Right now we're working on revised merits, and Pack Bond is one of them; you don't -need- a Totem merit, nor that one really to work as a pack, but you get increasing benefits with that one. It makes me think that tossing in a rating where it increases the overall members effective rank by 1 where they work together wouldn't be a bad idea, reflecting collective supernatural potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is something I will ponder more and post what I come up with to see what folks think of it (whatever it is, once it forms in my brainmeats).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:55:48-08:00","id":5037,"title":"","content":"<b>Some posible ways of calculating Pack Rank:</b><br /> <br /> 1) Lowest individual Rank in the Pack, +1 per additional member of a higher Rank.<br /> <br /> 2) Highest Rank in the Pack, +1 per additional member of that same Rank.<br /> <br /> 3) Average Rank of the members, +1 per additional member of a higher Rank.<br /> <br /> 4) Highest Rank in the pack, +1 per as many Ranks among the rest of the Pack.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Pack: 5 members with individual Ranks: 1, 1, 2, 2, 3</b><br /> <br /> 1) Pack Rank would be: 1 + (1x3) = 4<br /> <br /> 2) Pack Rank would be: 3 + (1x0) = 3<br /> <br /> 3) Pack Rank would be: 1 (1.8) + (1x3) = 4 (if always rounding down) or 2 (1.8) + (1x1) = 3 (if rounding up)<br /> <br /> 4) Pack Rank would be: 3 + (1+1+2+2)/3 = 3 + 2 = 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:55:54-08:00","id":5172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4861#post4861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They should totally be covered in the Idigam Chronicles instead of tucked away in the back of a supplement though. They add such a nice extra factor to being a part of a pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It should be part of where I think Idiagam Chronicles needs to tighten its focus, which is on the concept and power of the Pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T11:14:08-08:00","id":5250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4276#post4276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most games are played as 'rookies,' and yet Forsaken are expected to just take on their role in the world after a traumatic First Change and a group of nutjobs track you down and give you a bunch of mythology that you've never heard of before.<br /> <br /> Again; I don't terribly enjoy W:tF, and I may well be ignorant of (or unreceptive to) what folks like about the game. I'm just pitching my two cents in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you are right in that part is common problem with mage too. But way worse in Forsaken, as the game sells you the idea that your pack in isolated from the rest to a degree so how do you learn all the stuff? the do and dont of The forsaken? <br /> <br /> The official explanation is that you always were a little sociopath and now you know the why with harmony replacing morality but i always felt it was a little empty maybe a mechanic that after you first chance you retain humanity until it sink to 0 and then you get hamony. Or what i do in my game is add a flaw or merit that you can have human morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=4486#post4486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't care much for the <i>Circuit/Conclave </i>offered in the Forsaken Chronicler's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the problem with that one is that it doesnt tell you what happen when for example the beta or delta of the pack has more status in the conclave than the alpha<br /> <br /> <br /> Something i wanna ask, what your (meaning the people who read this tread) position with the pack totem? I havent read almost anything about it on the this thread. Personally i just remove it from the game for a couple of reason:<br /> <br /> 1) If i can avoid it i would preffer no to use NPCs for members of the party.<br /> 2) Players dont like that the way of their pack is dictated by an NPCs they preffer to be able to change without worrying if their totem is gonna get offended.<br /> 3) Why would they trust a spirit when they should police them<br /> 4) It inst necesary. Whats the use if noone has it? Werewolfs are gonna do what they do for their reason not because their totem tells them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:05:45-08:00","id":5344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=5250#post5250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something i wanna ask, what your (meaning the people who read this tread) position with the pack totem? I havent read almost anything about it on the this thread. Personally i just remove it from the game for a couple of reason:<br /> <br /> 1) If i can avoid it i would preffer no to use NPCs for members of the party.<br /> 2) Players dont like that the way of their pack is dictated by an NPCs they preffer to be able to change without worrying if their totem is gonna get offended.<br /> 3) Why would they trust a spirit when they should police them<br /> 4) It inst necesary. Whats the use if noone has it? Werewolfs are gonna do what they do for their reason not because their totem tells them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I've always seen it is as a way to make a family (Pack) out of people who are not really a family. It's a way to establish a family identity. That's why they pick a name for the pack, get a territory and bond with a totem. It formalizes and cements in the spiritual what they are already starting to feel is a proper connection. The totem, in turn, gets some Essence benefits and provides the pack with a little extra edge. One of the lovely little bits of spirit magic that get overlooked is that the bonded totem can provide a (small) bonus, but it can be anything that would be thematically appropriate to the totem. Speed bonuses from spirits of rabbits or hawks. Perception bonuses from spirits of eagles or bloodhounds. As the totem increases in power, so can the bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T16:56:15-08:00","id":5569,"title":"","content":"While I like the spirit, and how the game revolves around it, I've come to appreciate that some people don't. So maybe, without diminishing their involvement with the spirit, at least emphasizing more of their goals and things to do outside of it. Even if it leads to more divides between the spirit-oriented trying to get their less-spiritual brethren to help out, or the other way around, at least it'd be open to more people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:27:13-08:00","id":6334,"title":"","content":"Okay, in regards to the idea about the pack causing an increase in Honorary Spirit Rank, this is the simplest idea I've come up with so far:<br /> <br /> First, you count up how many werewolves of each Rank you have in your pack. Whichever Rank has the most is the baseline. In the case of a tie, use the higher of the two. Any additional different Ranks adjust that number up or down. So, let's say you have a pack of seven werewolves. Four of them are HSR 3, two of them are HSR 2, and one is HSR 4. The base would be 3, adjusted down one for the two HSR 2's, then back up one for the HSR 4, so it still balances out at 3. Narrative explanations can included the higher ranked werewolves are giving tactical advice to their younger packmates in downtime (to justify a higher pack HSR) or maybe the higher-ranked pack members are watching out for the younger members (to justify dropping the pack HSR), and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T15:15:02-08:00","id":6394,"title":"","content":"Seems good, but then isn't the HSR 4 Werewolf penalized for being in the company of those noobs? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T15:21:56-08:00","id":6410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=5344#post5344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I've always seen it is as a way to make a family (Pack) out of people who are not really a family. It's a way to establish a family identity. That's why they pick a name for the pack, get a territory and bond with a totem. It formalizes and cements in the spiritual what they are already starting to feel is a proper connection. The totem, in turn, gets some Essence benefits and provides the pack with a little extra edge. One of the lovely little bits of spirit magic that get overlooked is that the bonded totem can provide a (small) bonus, but it can be anything that would be thematically appropriate to the totem. Speed bonuses from spirits of rabbits or hawks. Perception bonuses from spirits of eagles or bloodhounds. As the totem increases in power, so can the bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually my post was my question about what could be change or should be change about totems in New New Werewolf. After that i just describe what i have done with it. But im curious about how in 8 pages of ideas (both great and ..... questionable) about New New Werewolf nobody said anything about totems. Everyone like them the way they are? or the just forget they exist as i do often :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T16:32:31-08:00","id":6458,"title":"","content":"I always forget they exist until someone brings them up...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T21:20:10-08:00","id":6603,"title":"","content":"To Kaho (and this is going to be very long) regarding some Totem ideas:<br /> <br /> Totems were brought up on the old forum thread. I'm not a fan on their necessity for a pack to be, well a pack whatsoever. An alien spirit with it's own agenda... one you're almost by necessity going to have kicking around in the material world to &quot;help&quot; you out... that's what is necessary?. Talk about about the pot calling the kettle black when it comes to Forsaken pointing the finger at the Pure for allowing spirits to pull shit in the material world; Forsaken do it all the time. They aren't constantly watching it, nothing is stopping it form using it's own Influences to promote the resonance it wants to harvest Essence, and given the ban (that's a tickler me: the ban does what for the spirit? It should be a task that generates it Essence to give it more incentive to stick around, in general)... but this is a good idea?<br /> <br /> Yeah, no. Cutting that out entirely with the revisions being tinkered with (which I'll be posting soon, got pretty busy and am trying to hash out a preliminary Predatory Aura as to give one of the Instinct, well... some context in what it does for y'all). Pack Bond as a merit to reflect the connection to ones pack and the benefits, and Totem just being a spirit one managed to convince to work in service to you or... vice versa for benefits on both's end. Most certainly -not- built by the PCs entirely to cherry pick a quick buff via metagame (it's a NPC for christ-sakes with it's own agenda... no), and using actual merit costs to reflect it's benefits instead of the current system. If you want it to do more than alter your Essence to give you it's &quot;Gifts&quot; in return for doing a ban/task that keeps it sustained... you buy things like, I dunno, Mentor and similar.<br /> <br /> We're also looking at what an individual pack member gets is equal to the 1-5 rating they take in the Totem; some people reap more from the Totem than others, favoured or otherwise, but this can be a double edged sword especially with potent ones. A spirit doesn't stop being like, and acting like a spirit just because of the Totem bond, but I can see using the new conditions for Ephemeral entities such as Open as part of the totem package with some tinkering (something I've been thinking about after looking at my Co-STs and my own initial ideas some months back)<br /> <br /> That's what I'm going with regardless of where Idigam Chronicles goes; complete with those who bite off more than they can chew with powerful totems starting to &quot;urge&quot; you more an more in line with it's desires. For those of a Rank more than you or your pack can contend with, say hello to fighting with it's desires attempting to override your own; additional incentive as to why some Pure (Fire Touched, I'm looking at you) really get looked upon negatively by the Forsaken above and beyond the other factors; the tendency of some Pure to take or to be, well, taken by powerful Totems may have more insidious consequences beyond letting it run roughshod in the material realm.<br /> <br /> This will give a reason why many Packs -if- they take a Totem prefer weaker and more manageable lower ranked ones; they're easier to keep in check and far less likely to start influencing you from the connection of Essence you made with it. Even among the Forsaken in this system... you occasionally run into packs or individuals that have been entirely suborned by a powerful spirit, making them exceedingly dangerous problems to the Forsaken mindset; Balehounds with the Maeljin, Maelintents and Wound spirits become just the tip of the iceberg as other spirits may cause the same. The plus side is powerful Totems are likely to give you more... but it's still looking after its -own- best interests like any spirit, not yours except when they overlap. Rather than a hard and fast Rank cap outside of those funky crusades with powerful Elunim, anyone can take a weaker or more potent one. There's just issues when you take a stronger bond than your effective Spirit Rank with potent spirits; extra reward, but with drawbacks. Pure have a bit less in that their effective Spirit Rank (socially) is considered higher... but unfortunately as per The Pure and elsewhere, often potent spirits actively seek them out to make these pacts to get more of a foothold in the material world. In turn you see Pure influenced by spirits more often when it comes to powerful totems in more ways than one.<br /> <br /> The other issue I had that it was basically a PC made NPC that just... stuck around in Twilight to help your ass out for what was invested as part of the package, and that it was mobile without Essence Bleed seemingly (yet you never paid into it to get Essence directly, especially given many totem bans made little sense for essence generation); some won't like this or want to use it, but we're keeping Totem mobility tied to Rites rather than having one just offsetting essence bleed; it's not your tag-along buddy by default, and primarily -it- will be what guards the packs Loci if they have one, rather than having them stuck at home to defend it all the time. Normally what will happen is that it will anchor to something or slumber (with the right numina, rites or it travelling in the shadow) if being moved; we're treating Totem spirits being brought to other Loci as a form of warfare, and it's ongoing help treated more like Mentor and similar Merits rather than part and parcel.<br /> <br /> After years of using Totem as it was, it's been nothing but a headache as presented. No more tag-along-buddy. It's a spirit; not your loving slave effectively getting very little out of the bargain. I want more to the agreements made with the Totem. Sure a werewolf pack may force a weaker one into service, or one fearing it will be consumed by other spirits might offer it's services to a pack to save it's own ass but I want it more of a two-way street and more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Entirely cutting out the Totem granting you Essence as well; it's -the- precious commodity to spirits; they're not going to just give it (where's it getting it anyhow if the pack isn't letting it run roughshod outside of what the pack does to maintain it in the material world?) to a bunch of werewolves beyond what it takes to establish the pact. I can see more intelligent and potent spirits -possibly- offering it, but it's not out of the goodness of their &quot;heart&quot;; it's because they want to twist the resonance of the werewolves own essence bit by bit more in order to what they want. If you want to tie your Essence and Resonance up to connect with a Spirit, odds are it's going to influence you in ways above and beyond buffs. I've always wanted this more reinforced and the choice of which totem, and even -if- a totem is a good idea touched on more.<br /> <br /> The same is holding true for Elunim for those with Auspices under this idea, as well as Tribal Totems; they're all spirits in the end. They still follow the tendencies of spirits. They don't have purely your best interests in mind. The Pure can at times point at the Forsaken with their connections to Lunes and go &quot;How is what you're doing any real different beyond giving the Bitch Mother and her Choirs more of a monopoly on the Shadow and the Material World? And -why- is that a good idea you numb-nuts, if you truly know what they're like? Driving packs mad, a Celestine noted for duplicity, inconsistency and madness? And you point the finger at us when we shun those things?!&quot; with just enough conviction to cast doubt on how 'good' a position the Forsaken really are in with Luna. Chosen favourites to some. Duped slaves to others.<br /> <br /> My Co-ST is working on these ideas at the moment with me chiming in. I'm hoping to get some completed chunks posted pretty soon; I was going to post the Instincts flat out until I realized how much they tied into heavy overhauls elsewhere, so I'd rather have a cleaner rough draft to pop up before flinging it in your collective direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T21:36:47-08:00","id":6614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6334#post6334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, in regards to the idea about the pack causing an increase in Honorary Spirit Rank, this is the simplest idea I've come up with so far:<br /> <br /> First, you count up how many werewolves of each Rank you have in your pack. Whichever Rank has the most is the baseline. In the case of a tie, use the higher of the two. Any additional different Ranks adjust that number up or down. So, let's say you have a pack of seven werewolves. Four of them are HSR 3, two of them are HSR 2, and one is HSR 4. The base would be 3, adjusted down one for the two HSR 2's, then back up one for the HSR 4, so it still balances out at 3. Narrative explanations can included the higher ranked werewolves are giving tactical advice to their younger packmates in downtime (to justify a higher pack HSR) or maybe the higher-ranked pack members are watching out for the younger members (to justify dropping the pack HSR), and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm kinda iffy on more convoluted systems like that. Honestly, I'm thinking of just taking the highest ranking member's effective spirit rank (if using the Primal Urge systems to determine it, because getting high is rare and costly) and adding +1 for being part of a bonded pack. You're not going to get honorary ranked 4's and 5 Werewolves with any consistency; those are high, HIGH Primal Urge types under this idea, legends really. If using the idea that being two ranks higher makes your natural attacks like banes to spirits, it's still keeping things reasonable even if you do get an honorary rank 5 Werewolf in your pack; you're still just getting the benefits on rank 4 and less spirits, and that's in a rare case hunting alongside a true supernatural paragon among werewolves. In most cases your packs effective rank is going to sit from 2 (if you go by the notion their honorary rank is at the bottom for harsher chronicles) to 3 more commonly (going by the idea they start around effective rank 2), with 4, 5 and the very, very rare 6 being seen much less given Primal Urge Costs (even old style Renown Costs for that matter).<br /> <br /> That Rank 5 is considered scary as shit; he's effectively backed by his adopted half-flesh &quot;choir&quot;. Spirits likely see them with the pack bond as more or less a singular choir or entity as far as ranking goes, and would be hard pressed not to take the threat seriously even if the individual only has effective Rank 1s or 2s at his side. Numbers are always the great equalizer. They won't be tearing the near-god Rank 5's a new asshole as easily, but even those very, very potent spirits sure have to consider if just butting heads with a pack with members that potent is worth the while.<br /> <br /> This would make starting packs who default around rank 2 treatment individually consistently very dangerous threats to rank 1 spirits. That said, I'm honestly more of a fan of werewolf claws and teeth being able to directly rip away Essence from spirits than the aggravated damage/Bane thing (or both). Discorporating them is all fine and well easily; I like the idea that a pack can have members attack and tear away or consume it's Essence without esoteric powers while others go in to rip apart it's Corpus more personally, but using the tentative idea presented in GMC this still works well too. It's something I'm using; hunting spirits for essence being part of the package, rather than requiring a Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T04:10:20-08:00","id":6728,"title":"","content":"What if the Totem is not an alien spirit with its own agenda and is literally &quot;the Spirit of the Pack&quot;. Spirits get created by all kind of things, maybe the ritual bond of the pack creates an spirit that represents that packs interests and theme.<br /> <br /> Influence: My Pack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T04:37:42-08:00","id":6737,"title":"","content":"I had the same idea at the subway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the bonding of a pack creates the totemspirit the wish, the hope and the emotion of every member takes an influence, so that new members can bring new power to the spirit (the hate of the pure can be a greate origin of the higher power of their totems ) sorry for spelling mistakes: german and mobile phone user <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:32:25-08:00","id":6750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6728#post6728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Totem is not an alien spirit with its own agenda and is literally &quot;the Spirit of the Pack&quot;. Spirits get created by all kind of things, maybe the ritual bond of the pack creates an spirit that represents that packs interests and theme.<br /> <br /> Influence: My Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely another option, but not one I'm too sure I'd go with. Too much &quot;And then we get a big buff with little consequences, with something that comes out of nowhere like a deus ex machinae to hand us goodies, but little reason to pose an issue.&quot; I suppose if it could outgrow the pack and have it's own agendas, or if it was something made as a guardian/watchdog spun out of essence temporarily via a Rite it'd be worth the while (in fact that would be an interesting rite; Summon the Guardian or whatever, though I wouldn't be surprised if something like it exists in some book already with W:tF that I'm not remembering). Otherwise it pushes heavily into the territory of &quot;we just got a spirit that acts as a Retainer, but does much much more than a Retainer, and it's only real drawback is we gotta do some task to keep it around and not falling under general spirit mechanics and assumptions&quot;. I suppose my problem there is that it's too much like the existing totem mechanic while being even more contrived.<br /> <br /> What happens when it gets destroyed? Infected by the resonant essence of something else from feeding on the wrong types of spirits/essence? What happens if an Idigam reshapes it? Bound into a Talen or Fetish? What about when the pack disbands or loses members or gains them? There's some potential there for quite a few stories, but... I dunno. Something about it doesn't rub me right. It's a spirit; a good chunk of what spirits do and why along with a chunk of their mechanics shouldn't get tossed or glossed over. It's effectively a &quot;werewolf spirit&quot;, without being a two werewolf mating consequence. Why not just seek out a wolf or a pack spirit at that point? How common is this to happen?<br /> <br /> Personal tastes obviously, but it reminds me of some super sentai-esque &quot;and then we create some avatar of our friendship and camaraderie to do battle for us&quot; in a not-so-good way, complete with cliche words of comfort and wisdom now and then and handing out goodies. Ugh.<br /> <br /> Blame my insomniac mind for that one. Honestly, I'd rather not blunt the impact of spirits with packs just springing them into existence by sheer existence as a pack. A &quot;spirit of whatever we needed&quot; seems extremely contrived if there's too much direct control over it's creation and end result. A packs actions creating a spirit (and likely not what they specifically cultivated to a T) that later takes an interest on them as an Essence source? Sure. But some innate, nebulous (very nebulous going by the existing W:tF books) tie to them, or reliance and utterly subservient or with only the packs best interests in mind? Eh... a spirit so specific and tied to a material extension (the werewolves) that way would default to being very low ranked by dint of W:tF's explanation. This seems more the territory of exceptions, or at least, extraordinary actions to me rather than a default assumption (though with room for it to possibly occur).<br /> <br /> This is one of the areas where I was looking at Geist Krewes for some inspiration some time back, and a way to show how packs grow into Lodges (or potentially other Tribes) as they expand and gain a powerful spiritual patron. It could definitely work, but I think there would need to be quite a few considerations to keep it from going into the land of &quot;I've got an NPC at my beck and call unless this -one- thing is not done who acts more like a favourable Deus Ex Machinae rather than a character itself that just so happens to likely trump both the Retainer and the Mentor merits in what it does&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some idle musings; I'm running on fumes and being horribly overtired (and rambling), but that's what initially popped to mind; I can definitely see some ways to work with it and keep it interesting, but I really don't think packs should get a spirit &quot;get out of spirit jail free card and get a sycophantic buddy spirit&quot; by their very nature alone. There should be some room to question whether it is the pack itself making them using this option, or if they're simply drawing the attention of a pre-existing spirit that the packs trends, habits and actions resonate with. It should also get folks wondering about the actual nature of Tribal Totems and Lodge Totems if this occurs with any frequency. The more I think about it, the less predisposed I am against it, but I feel it should not be made concrete, rather than a possibility of that being what may occur if that makes any sense. *Tired chin rubs*.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T05:44:32-08:00","id":6759,"title":"","content":"Well, I dn't think Totems could work as Retainers. Mentors, sure, but not a Retainer. Also, they still are spirits, they were created by the Pack so its survival is in their own best interests, but some of their decisions may be counter to the individual desires of the members, Totems will be literal embodiments of &quot;the Group before the Individual&quot;, so right there you have reasons for conflict. Also, if they had actual Influence over the pack a Totem could screw with them big time if they don't work in harmony (or Harmony).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T07:56:44-08:00","id":6826,"title":"","content":"So I'll toss my 2 cents in. First of all, I'm going to echo the sentiment of more emphasis on the wolf nature. Forsaken has never really grabbed me, because in my mind I feel like werewolf should have the potential for personal horror out of any game line. But in practice it always ends up being the most pulpy and focused on external horror. That's my experience, anyway. I mean, monstrous spirit abominations are horrifying in their own way, but it's all very focused on the monsters &quot;out there&quot; when what I want out of a werewolf game is to focus on the monster within. You have an eight foot raging wolf monster inside of you just waiting for a chance to rip its way out of your skin and kill something, how do you deal with that? Do you suppress it and hope it never finds its way out? Or do you embrace it and let the wolf run free in hopes you'll find some measure of balance between your dual natures? And all the while, you're still a human with a family and friends and bills to pay, how do you reconcile the two worlds? That's what I feel Werewolf should be about in theory and friends of mine who love Forsaken tell me that's a big part of it. But every time I play, I never see that side of it. I hate to use the &quot;fuzzy spirit cops&quot; cliche, because I know that's an oversimplification and doesn't represent the game well. Besides, I do very much like all of the spirit stuff. I just don't want the personal horror of never knowing when you might turn into a giant wolfbeast and rip someone you care about to shreds to be overshadowed by it. On the setting end of things... More of the Rocky Mountains <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm from Denver and I like having a local setting, so more on werewolves in my home town is always good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T09:04:55-08:00","id":6868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Totems were brought up on the old forum thread. I'm not a fan on their necessity for a pack to be, well a pack whatsoever. An alien spirit with it's own agenda... one you're almost by necessity going to have kicking around in the material world to &quot;help&quot; you out... that's what is necessary? </div> </div> </div>Yes. The totem is the spirit side of the pack. Take away their necessity and you take away the plot hook of traitorous totems. It's not bug, its a feature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Talk about about the pot calling the kettle black when it comes to Forsaken pointing the finger at the Pure for allowing spirits to pull shit in the material world; Forsaken do it all the time. </div> </div> </div>No. The Pure get spirits to possess helpless humans and use the claimed or nanutari as cannon fodder. The Forsaken, generally, would only allow a spirit to aid them naturally: thru influences. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't constantly watching it, nothing is stopping it form using it's own Influences to promote the resonance it wants to harvest Essence, and given the ban (that's a tickler me: the ban does what for the spirit? It should be a task that generates it Essence to give it more incentive to stick around, in general)... but this is a good idea? </div> </div> </div>Using your influences to harvest essence is a natural way to do it, there's nothing wrong with that. The ban cements the bond with the pack. It's a give and take. Again, it's a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's a NPC for christ-sakes with it's own agenda... no </div> </div> </div>You can, and it's advised, as ST make the totem on your own. If you wanna let the players build it, it's your own prerogative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're also looking at what an individual pack member gets is equal to the 1-5 rating they take in the Totem </div> </div> </div>Totem doesn't have that cap. There's NPCs depicted with 12 points in Totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This will give a reason why many Packs -if- they take a Totem prefer weaker and more manageable lower ranked ones </div> </div> </div>That's the expressive reason given. Forsaken totems are cajoled, tamed, tricked or otherwise forced to submit to them. With the Pure? it's the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other issue I had that it was basically a PC made NPC that just... stuck around in Twilight to help your ass out for what was invested as part of the package </div> </div> </div>If this is how you portray your totems, sir, you suck at this game. You won't be able to &quot;fix&quot; Storytelling games by having mechanics to address for your own lack of aptitude as an ST. That's not the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After years of using Totem as it was, it's been nothing but a headache as presented. </div> </div> </div>I'd wager it's probably because you've no idea how to portray a compelling totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Entirely cutting out the Totem granting you Essence as well; it's -the- precious commodity to spirits </div> </div> </div>Because every spirit is essence starved. /Sarcasm<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it's not out of the goodness of their &quot;heart&quot; </div> </div> </div>What do you think the ban is for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same is holding true for Elunim for those with Auspices under this idea, as well as Tribal Totems; they're all spirits in the end. They still follow the tendencies of spirits. </div> </div> </div>Read Signs of the Moon. The Elunim who &quot;blesses&quot; you with Silver Jaws is doing it because it's jealous of you, and wants to see you spiral into degeneration. The Cahalunim who visits you at night with terrible portents will eventually drive you insane.<br /> <br /> The sun spirit you freed from an Azlu cocoon has no other way to show it's gratitude than to brand your hide with searing fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;How is what you're doing any real different beyond giving the Bitch Mother and her Choirs more of a monopoly on the Shadow and the Material World? And -why- is that a good idea you numb-nuts, if you truly know what they're like? Driving packs mad, a Celestine noted for duplicity, inconsistency and madness? And you point the finger at us when we shun those things?!&quot; </div> </div> </div>Because the spirits associated with the forsaken aren't crossing over whenever they wish and establishing spirit cults. The spirit which drive you mad normally don't take you as it's adopted children, the Moon is distant, while the Pure totems enslave you to their every, alien whims.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR </b>I'd try to understand the setting before going about fixing it. Otherwise it's like trying to conduct an open heart surgery with an engineer's degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:12:41-08:00","id":6901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6868#post6868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. The totem is the spirit side of the pack. Take away their necessity and you take away the plot hook of traitorous totems. It's not bug, its a feature.<br /> <br /> I'd wager it's probably because you've no idea how to portray a compelling totem.<br /> <br /> If this is how you portray your totems, sir, you suck at this game. You won't be able to &quot;fix&quot; Storytelling games by having mechanics to address for your own lack of aptitude as an ST. That's not the way to go.<br /> <br /> Because every spirit is essence starved. /Sarcasm.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR </b>I'd try to understand the setting before going about fixing it. Otherwise it's like trying to conduct an open heart surgery with an engineer's degree.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you say that the guy doesn't fit your particularly narrow vision of the game and because of that he doesn't get the game? or is unable to fix it? or at least give advice about it? I think that Tatterdemalion King has some great ideas for the game in general while your ideas go from bashing his, to saying &quot;OMG URATHA SHULD RLZ MELEE!!!!&quot; which i could say that in my opinion is you who doesn't get the game and shouldn't be giving advice about it but i wont say that to you. Why? because its your opinion and you are entitled to it. You have as much of a right to share as him or me or anyone else in this forum. I may discuss or downright ignore some of your ideas but i would not ever tell you to shut up.<br /> <br /> I may think that your suggestion of werewolf are just an immature reaction of wanting your pet supernatural to win everything and be the strongest that is or a blind fan boyish mentality that the game is utterly perfect and those who don't agree are wrong and don't &quot;get&quot; the game. Again i may think that but i would never and think most people here would tell you to shut your <u>opinions of the game</u> as we are posting in this thread to throw around ideas of what we like the game to be. You have your opinions and Tatterdemalion has his and i have mine. I disagree strongly with every single one of your ideas but i don't think you are not entitled to share them here nor im gonna call you ignorant about it or tell you that you are incompetent. So please drop the thought internet guy attitude and don't attack people who havent done anything more to you than share their vision of the game or experience with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-09-2013, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:30:45-08:00","id":6905,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Keep it calm folks.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:47:41-08:00","id":6918,"title":"","content":"Narrow? heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T12:59:20-08:00","id":6986,"title":"","content":"As totems are now I find them fairly narrow, and more restrictive than necessary. Not all packs need to be defined through a single spirit, removing the <b>requirement </b>of a single totem opens up additional possibilities, while providing the <b>option </b>to have one retains the story-hooks that were already there.<br /> <br /> Some pack structures I've used that don't work with the current approach, but are totally appropriate to the setting:<ul><li>A pack of ronin like peacekeepers who venerate no spirit above others. They enforce peace and stability on both sides of the Gauntlet without picking favorites.</li> <li>A 'Wolves First' pack that believes Uratha are the true inheritors of the earth, and spirits that intend to live there must be subservient. They take the roll of totem themselves, subjugating and ruling over a swath of lesser spirits.</li> <li>A nomadic mercenary pack, that travels territory to territory offering power in exchange for essence. They form a temporary bond with a single spirit, accomplish the goal it desires, collect their essence tithe and move on.</li> <li>The trickster wolf of many totems, who secretly venerates several different spirits at a time, gaining power from each (and hoping none figure out what he's doing).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:02:49-08:00","id":6991,"title":"","content":"Kaho, you may not see it, but the World of Darkness as a whole other than Werewolf has had a major change in capability. Even before Blood &amp; Smoke's revisions Vampire had gained quite a bit. Right now, as is, a Vampire built for combat using the new rules, especially one with at least 3 Blood Potency would be rough for a small PACK of equivalent PU werewolves to handle in a physical confrontation.<br /> <br /> Werewolf needs some power increases.<br /> <br /> Ephsy has a good understanding of the game as written. You and Tatter are suggesting wild setting changes and what may as well be close to as difference from Forsaken as it is from Apocalypse in some cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:21:47-08:00","id":6999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6986#post6986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As totems are now I find them fairly narrow, and more restrictive than necessary. Not all packs need to be defined through a single spirit, removing the <b>requirement </b>of a single totem opens up additional possibilities, while providing the <b>option </b>to have one retains the story-hooks that were already there.<br /> <br /> Some pack structures I've used that don't work with the current approach, but are totally appropriate to the setting:<ul><li>A pack of ronin like peacekeepers who venerate no spirit above others. They enforce peace and stability on both sides of the Gauntlet without picking favorites.</li> <li>A 'Wolves First' pack that believes Uratha are the true inheritors of the earth, and spirits that intend to live there must be subservient. They take the roll of totem themselves, subjugating and ruling over a swath of lesser spirits.</li> <li>A nomadic mercenary pack, that travels territory to territory offering power in exchange for essence. They form a temporary bond with a single spirit, accomplish the goal it desires, collect their essence tithe and move on.</li> <li>The trickster wolf of many totems, who secretly venerates several different spirits at a time, gaining power from each (and hoping none figure out what he's doing).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be blunt: literally all of these sound more like lodges, particularly when the word &quot;venerate&quot; is thrown around to refer to the reciprocal aspect of the patronage of beings that have been noted to <i>need</i> some sort of payment for services rendered even if they very much want to give a gift for free.<br /> <br /> Near as I've found, a pack totem fills a void. It's there as an anchor to the identity of members of a group whose work can see a fairly high rate of turnover. The persistence of the werewolf soul is extremely ambiguous and the nearest thing to a home the species had was destroyed with the rise of the Gauntlet. This is to say nothing of having a liaison that can interact with the spirit world without the stigma of being a half-flesh kinslaying freak; it's a flag to meet spirits under that the Hisil can understand.<br /> <br /> I thoroughly agree that the mechanics need updating, but I look askance at all the talk about how the group of monsters stuck in liminal space don't need a foothold in the world that largely despises them in order to be treated by that world with any significant legitimacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:37:28-08:00","id":7007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6999#post6999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be blunt: literally all of these sound more like lodges, particularly when the word &quot;venerate&quot; is thrown around to refer to the reciprocal aspect of the patronage of beings that have been noted to <i>need</i> some sort of payment for services rendered even if they very much want to give a gift for free.<br /> <br /> Near as I've found, a pack totem fills a void. It's there as an anchor to the identity of members of a group whose work can see a fairly high rate of turnover. The persistence of the werewolf soul is extremely ambiguous and the nearest thing to a home the species had was destroyed with the rise of the Gauntlet. This is to say nothing of having a liaison that can interact with the spirit world without the stigma of being a half-flesh kinslaying freak; it's a flag to meet spirits under that the Hisil can understand.<br /> <br /> I thoroughly agree that the mechanics need updating, but I look askance at all the talk about how the group of monsters stuck in liminal space don't need a foothold in the world that largely despises them in order to be treated by that world with any significant legitimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I despise the notion that Werewolves have to depend on something other to gain legitimacy. But personal preference aside, I agree that a Totem should be an enticing <b>option </b>with many benefits befitting a heavily invested merit. But also feel that there should be other paths to power and legitimacy for those who don't want to tie themselves to a single spirit, and for storytellers who want to downplay the spirit world side of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:47:02-08:00","id":7042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7007#post7007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I despise the notion that Werewolves have to depend on something other to gain legitimacy. But personal preference aside, I agree that a Totem should be an enticing <b>option </b>with many benefits befitting a heavily invested merit. But also feel that there should be other paths to power and legitimacy for those who don't want to tie themselves to a single spirit, and for storytellers who want to downplay the spirit world side of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be because I've spent most of the last year or two having this lesson reinforced over and over or because in that same amount of time I've had a bit of a problem with fetishizing my own contempt, but I can no longer muster the patience to long suffer through people demanding they be rewarded for indecision or lack of commitment. I didn't spend two semesters agonizing over ambiguities for my health, nor did I spend three months yelling at people for demanding something be all things to all people so I would have to do it forever.<br /> <br /> The thematics of the setting work against successful totem-hopping that doesn't include pack-hopping. Spirits give their respect to werewolves on an individual basis, for the most part, and exhibit a strong degree of expectation for roles and rules to be adhered to \u2014 the magath are reviled because they stepped out of the bounds of their nature as much as because they violate the conventional dictates of what is predator and prey to what. Predators take hesitation as weakness and treat the hesitant accordingly.<br /> <br /> The Uratha are typically yanked out of their human lives and, courtesy of the same tenet that says they can't let anybody find out about them, thrust into an environment that is strange and unfamiliar to them. They don't properly belong in either world and the Border Marches are gone \u2014 that's what a liminal state is, it's stressful as hell for a psyche to maintain, and it doesn't tend to lead to healthy behavior with a lasting constructive impact unless the state is transitioned out of and a new identity constructed; until then, the changes that stick are more likely to be destructive.<br /> <br /> Spirits are rocks in the stream of the Shadow. Despite their gradual change over time, they're solid objects upon which werewolves can ground their organizations. Going without a totem is like trying to swim from one end of a pool to another without pushing off from any midpoints when there's barely any water resistance and you've only got half an idea of how to swim \u2014 the going is slower and the highest odds are on you thrashing around fruitlessly and drowning, possibly killing fellow swimmers in the process.<br /> <br /> The reward for not having a pack totem is exactly the same as the reward for being a Ghost Wolf: it's one less ban to attend to. That's all you <i>should </i>get for it; passing up on paired advantages and disadvantages typically means playing without any of those advantages.<br /> <br /> Now if you'll excuse me, I need to go scream into something. This wasn't fun to type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-09-2013, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:09:18-08:00","id":7059,"title":"","content":"Okee dokee, I'm gonna just...walk away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T17:29:34-08:00","id":7113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6991#post6991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kaho, you may not see it, but the World of Darkness as a whole other than Werewolf has had a major change in capability. Even before Blood &amp; Smoke's revisions Vampire had gained quite a bit. Right now, as is, a Vampire built for combat using the new rules, especially one with at least 3 Blood Potency would be rough for a small PACK of equivalent PU werewolves to handle in a physical confrontation.<br /> <br /> Werewolf needs some power increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they need some power increase, im not against that and im not sure anyone really is against that but one thing that Tatter or Claire (dont remember who) remind me of is that there are 2 kind of power increase. The first one in wich the power increase is made because the game needs it and it goes in accordance to that. The second type is the knee jerk reaction of &quot;because if B&amp;S are more powerfull so werewolf should be even more powerfull&quot; the idea of that Ephsy goes to is that Werewolf should be the top melee fighter by default and while i dont agree with him. I dont see why he has to attack another person for his views about the game and say he is incompetent because some element of the game dont work for him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6991#post6991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephsy has a good understanding of the game as written. You and Tatter are suggesting wild setting changes and what may as well be close to as difference from Forsaken as it is from Apocalypse in some cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes we are (though i would say that on the totems i just ask whats the people wanted from them) but thats whats we are doing &quot;suggesting&quot; i havent told anyone that they are incompetents or dont have any rights to talks about the possibilities of the game just because i dont agree with him so why should he get away on doing the same? i just call on Ephsy\u00b4s BS and leave it at that. Besides having a great knowledge of the rules as written doesnt give him any more right to share his opinion than anyone else or allow to insult him other people. It just means he has a lot of free time in his hand.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the matter of wild setting changes: Some are suggesting wild setting changes ..... so what? they are just suggestion or what we personally want to see. It doesnt mean is gonna come true and even if it does and it became a complete different game there is still New old Werewolf as an entire line. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7042#post7042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be because I've spent most of the last year or two having this lesson reinforced over and over or because in that same amount of time I've had a bit of a problem with fetishizing my own contempt, but I can no longer muster the patience to long suffer through people demanding they be rewarded for indecision or lack of commitment. I didn't spend two semesters agonizing over ambiguities for my health, nor did I spend three months yelling at people for demanding something be all things to all people so I would have to do it forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your personal problem should influence the game? i dont get it. Im lost in translations here or are saying that? Im honestly asking here, im not being funny or sarcastic but i just dont get this paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7042#post7042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha are typically yanked out of their human lives and, courtesy of the same tenet that says they can't let anybody find out about them, thrust into an environment that is strange and unfamiliar to them. They don't properly belong in either world and the Border Marches are gone \u2014 that's what a liminal state is, it's stressful as hell for a psyche to maintain, and it doesn't tend to lead to healthy behavior with a lasting constructive impact unless the state is transitioned out of and a new identity constructed; until then, the changes that stick are more likely to be destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This i wish got more attention sometimes. The fluff says that every uratha was kinda a sociopath from birth who never got human morality and that after the first change everything made sense. But what you are saying sounds so much more interesting as a normal human mind has to come to grips with werewolf morality besides the instant change from Morality seems like a switch button sometimes. My only solution was to allow players who wanted to play said character to be able to have human morality instead of harmony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7042#post7042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits are rocks in the stream of the Shadow. Despite their gradual change over time, they're solid objects upon which werewolves can ground their organizations. Going without a totem is like trying to swim from one end of a pool to another without pushing off from any midpoints when there's barely any water resistance and you've only got half an idea of how to swim \u2014 the going is slower and the highest odds are on you thrashing around fruitlessly and drowning, possibly killing fellow swimmers in the process.<br /> <br /> The reward for not having a pack totem is exactly the same as the reward for being a Ghost Wolf: it's one less ban to attend to. That's all you <i>should </i>get for it; passing up on paired advantages and disadvantages typically means playing without any of those advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of alternatives to &quot;power&quot; isn't bad on itself. Could be made into an alternative of sorts with DM approval kinda thing. On the foothold in the spirit world i don't think a totem is necessary. Spirits are gonna be hostile or distrustful of forsaken by default . But again something i also like about the totem mechanics is that it feels almost modular as i can remove it from a game and the everything goes OK. So people who like totems can have them and make it a requirement in their setting for a pack in order to become a true pack.<br /> <br /> I handle it the following way. Are this a group of werewolf who identify themselves as a pack? Have they spend enough time together for their pack instinct to kick in? if the answer is yes, on my setting such group of werewolf is a pack. However thats me, in the games i usually play and DM. But i honestly think it should remain a modular thing something that you can remove entirely from the game and not a single thing about the system would change for that. Some like it, some dont.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-09-2013, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T20:21:12-08:00","id":7160,"title":"","content":"My first idea is to go full force with making them the physical splat. If spirits and other Ephemeral Entities are still major powerhouses in the stats department might as well make Werewolves more capable of taking a beating since these are the things they have to deal with as antagonists on a daily basis. <br /> <br /> My viewpoint is to, much like Vampire, increase the toughness of the characters. However, instead of making damage all bashing I'd rather they were more capable of taking it and regenerating it away. I'd go with Healing bashing per turn equal to Primal Urge, and spend a point of essence to heal that amount in lethal or twice your normal amount in bashing. Possibly having the limit that you can't spend more than 1 essence in a turn in this way, but if Instincts or whatever become a thing that's definitely room to have expansions on within the powerset.<br /> <br /> Fights among Werewolves should be more about showing dominance and power instead of straight to the kill. So with this hack you show they aren't too worried about just jumping into a fight with each other and doing bodily harm. However, when they DO go for the kill its a conscious decision and worthy of the Degeneration roll you're going to get hit with for killing one of your kin. <br /> <br /> From this thread and the previous one it seems some people are fine with Werewolves being not very good on their own. That's one viewpoint, and its fine that they have it, but I'd rather have all splats capable in their fields of focus on their own rather than explicitly requiring group cohesion. Definitely would be nicer for crossover play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:09:57-08:00","id":7189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7160#post7160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first idea is to go full force with making them the physical splat. If spirits and other Ephemeral Entities are still major powerhouses in the stats department might as well make Werewolves more capable of taking a beating since these are the things they have to deal with as antagonists on a daily basis. My viewpoint is to, much like Vampire, increase the toughness of the characters. However, instead of making damage all bashing I'd rather they were more capable of taking it and regenerating it away. I'd go with Healing bashing per turn equal to Primal Urge, and spend a point of essence to heal that amount in lethal or twice your normal amount in bashing. Possibly having the limit that you can't spend more than 1 essence in a turn in this way, but if Instincts or whatever become a thing that's definitely room to have expansions on within the powerset. Fights among Werewolves should be more about showing dominance and power instead of straight to the kill. So with this hack you show they aren't too worried about just jumping into a fight with each other and doing bodily harm. However, when they DO go for the kill its a conscious decision and worthy of the Degeneration roll you're going to get hit with for killing one of your kin. From this thread and the previous one it seems some people are fine with Werewolves being not very good on their own. That's one viewpoint, and its fine that they have it, but I'd rather have all splats capable in their fields of focus on their own rather than explicitly requiring group cohesion. Definitely would be nicer for crossover play.</div> </div> </div> </div> That seems like a bit much in the healing department for me, but in principle I agree. One werewolf on its own should be scary. A whole pack that works well together should be terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:29:39-08:00","id":7212,"title":"","content":"Here's a nice tl;dr post to address some of the ridiculousness folks have pulled regarding Idigam Chronicle changes.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to ignore Ephsy from now on; anything that disagrees with his personal interpretation of the material is patronized, insulted and personally attacked. For someone who points in the direction of a current book (that I've read and have access to by the way; all of them), the selective literacy he displays is pretty insulting, and generally without actually adding any real ideas or content on how to change things.<br /> <br /> So, Ephsy can sit in his corner, suck his thumb and cope; the game is going to change, and in some areas drastically from the sourcebooks that currently exist and his -personal- interpretations on them. Others are going to present new ideas or try to readdress ideas in ways he doesn't like. Once again, he just needs to cope. I've had my game running literally for years with the same people and newcomers coming to it with much of this stemming from their input; I'm pretty sure my ST skills or my Co-St's aren't actually an issue.<br /> <br /> It's looking at existing material, and seeing ways of improving upon them, or otherwise pushing the envelope to see what further potential there may be to bring the game in line with the needs of the players and ST's running it, or simply to reinforce the themes of the game. You know. Like &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;. Hence making Essence a much rarer commodity -that requires hunting for it to gain it- and reinforcing the ideas that spirits are consistently after more further; you know... so they keep not only surviving but growing in power? So they rise the Rank Totem pole? To emphasize the cycles of predation the Shadow has just a -bit- further? That? Much of this material -is- already addressed; it's kind of a no-shit Sherlock situation where the majority of us are well aware of the material that's already in print. It's not a matter of reiteration; it's a matter of looking at the impressions others have gained about the game as is, and ways one can address them via changes in the game. In a lot of areas, it's emphasis less than it is gutting the system and changing it. In others, it's just that.<br /> <br /> I'm entirely speaking from the POV of what -could- be done with the game, not going &quot;Well, Blood of the Wolf treats topic x like this, so therefore it cannot be addressed as not going far enough, being presented poorly, or simply not having room for tweaking. Because, a book already tackles it in one way&quot;. Sorry. No. Beyond the belligerent (and ongoing) attitude problems it kind of makes this thread redundant, let alone the wasted keystrokes involved to basically say &quot;My interpretation of the book is right; never mind that I cherry-pick and intentionally twist what others commenting on it directly or in general are saying, but I'm right. You're just a shitty ST, oh and by the way, too long didn't read; if I didn't read it fully, why am I even commenting anyhow?&quot; I've consistently gotten nothing from him of useful content. He'd rather sit back and shit-fling upon anyone that wants to go further with the game than he likes. There's no point addressing him further; it's a consistent habit and I don't see it changing. What I do appreciate is the Mods getting involved nice and quick, but I don't take well to some internet tough-guy being intentionally ignorant when other folks are actually trying to have an ongoing discussion.<br /> <br /> The 1-5 scale is -our personal house rule for the merit revisions we are working on, to give individual pack members more of a variance on how connected they are to the totem-. It is -not- a reference to the existing material, or a cap there. I know these systems. I've used them, and played with them for years. Given this is now a chance to revise, change and otherwise refine the various mechanics and setting ideas, I'm doing just that along with my co-ST. Hell, even without Idigam Chronicles we would be doing this. We're also doing this because it is what we would like to see in the game; it's going to be suggested as options for the Idigam Chronicles because we believe they -could-, and I emphasize could, be interesting or a good way to refine the existing material.<br /> <br /> Why? Because of player input. Because of our own experiences where we can see where there were rough spots regarding this. Why someone who's only put one &quot;dot&quot; in can ride the coattails of someone who put 8+ and reap the same rewards mechanically. I'm not a fan of it. These ideas aren't coming out of a vacuum; I can't remotely pretend that they'll be the best tweaks and changes though or something that'd work for everyone's game, you can't please everyone. As is, I'm entirely against the idea of &quot;less is more&quot; regarding game changes for Idigam Chronicles and the Fallen World chronicles. That's precisely the issue that early V:tR had, and it's the issue W:tF as it stands right how has. There's a reason we're getting this book; because there's room for change and expansion and many, many people have gotten new ideas as well as past experiences to rejigger it to the nines.<br /> <br /> The tinkering with (and later introduction and play-testing of it) is to see if it does what we intend it to do, as well as bringing the Totem merit more in line with the current Merit system; I want individuals within the pack to -not- have a uniform connection; I want some jockeying within packs with totems for more favour from it, some risk involved with it influencing you back too much and a way to show those who do consistently go above and beyond for the totem reap more rewards than those that don't. That's why we're looking at treating it on a 1-5 scale between each member; I'm fully aware of how the current totem system works; I'm presenting those times when the existing totem system be it by an ST's reading (I play in games too), a players reading or material as currently presented did not work out as one would think was intended. At the end of the day you can reread the material and see if you come to a different understanding; if that fails, you can readjust the material via house rules and see if they work better.<br /> <br /> Right now, it's not even so much as that; it's more &quot;what can we do to highlight that no, spirits are not going to always be knowable, reliable entities for you to call upon, your totem is a distinct entity; not your lap-dog. Totem does not equate to 'domesticated'&quot;. Players always want strong input on their Totems; it's been the exception where I've not seen the players deciding where those totem points are placed. How many people just say to their players &quot;oh, buying some more points of totem? I'll assign that for ya, hush hush like so you can't make assumptions too neatly&quot;. Not many from my personal experience. As someone who enjoyed the Shadowguide system from Wraith (both the inter-PC default and the option for ST portrayal), I want something more... hmm, insidious? Risky? Questionable? <br /> <br /> You can do a lot with it; it's initial presentation, however isn't so peachy-keen. I'm wanting this to become more complex; not so much mechanically, but in the two-way street of the spirit impacting those under it's influence it more (as if you were becoming an adoptive choir); more variance in regards to it with individual pack members, and more to -reinforce- with the core material that it's still going to have it's own agenda whether you like it or not. I want it loaded with more plot potential from the get-go and mechanically reinforced if it's kept as a prominent pack feature. Right now, it's lacking in my eyes, badly.<br /> <br /> I've found a lot of the existing examples for Totems and their Ban to not really jive (especially when they're bans to -not- do an action; the Tasked Condition seems to make more sense here) with generating Essence. It's not an absolute; some do, but many don't. Others sort of seem to fall along with the ideas of Resonance, without really always dovetailing with that. It's inconsistent, and not in a good way. I want things more concise, and to jive more with the existing GMC mechanics regarding Ephemeral entities, as well as to jive with the consistent portrayal of what spirits were previously; I don't find it to do a good job of that currently. It's sloppy.<br /> <br /> Ephysy can continue to be snide and tl;dr; this material if for the folks that actually want to share something with content, brainstorm and see what we'd like to see changed. I'm done with a guy who apparently just wants an echo-chamber and feels the need to attack others when that doesn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":".  Some additional totem thoughts. Mm mm. Rambles. 11-10-2013, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:56:00-08:00","id":7220,"title":"","content":"I'd view it as a bit much in the healing department if werewolves didn't regularly have fights against things with attacks in the double digits for dice pools and Primal Urge(being a power stat) being the most expensive thing they have to buy. Never been in a game that lasted long enough for people to raise it higher than 5(actually, never seen anyone go higher than 4). So I figure only being able to spend 1 essence a turn on healing would be a good limit. <br /> <br /> Oh, and with the way weapons work now the only thing doing bashing to you is unarmed punches and kicks. I'd okay with them being highly resilient against it. And with only being able to spend 1 essence a turn to heal their PU in lethal its still possible to do the American Werewolf in London approach to the issue.<br /> <br /> Or just grab the shiny silver...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T05:16:10-08:00","id":7296,"title":"","content":"Everyone regularly has fights against things with double digit attack pools; a 'puny' mortal antagonist with 2 Strength, 2 Weaponry and anything with a weapon modifier in the old system can go All-Out, spend a Willpower and push into that, never-mind nastier antagonists. It's hardly a reason to go crazy with werewolf Regeneration; the moment you deal with supernatural antagonists or skilled mortals, it's going to start creeping up, especially once specialities, merits, better equipment and other factors get involved. It's hardly a werewolf-only thing as a regular issue; it's across the gamelines.<br /> <br /> The PU in bashing healing? Honestly, I don't have much of a problem with that idea... assuming it was only in Gauru form. I'd keep the Lethal healing as is with the minor tweak that werewolves automatically heal either 1 L, or the PU in bashing each round -before- Essence is spent if going that route. The talk is that all the splats will be using the Changeling: the Lost Wyrd Chart for supernatural resource spending per turn in the new set; that'd mean that PU 2 and 3 etc. type are capable of healing that in Lethal every round they spend the Essence. If it was taken out that spending Essence to heal supersedes and stops the innate healing, I feel that would be enough. I'd keep the Essence healing in other forms intact as is. What you present seems to be going quickly into the realm of overkill with what even a base-creation werewolf is going to be shrugging off for 1 Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T06:38:27-08:00","id":7310,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the game changing. I do mind it not being Forsaken anymore. Removing Renown? Hisil as a focus of half spirit predators? Totems? That's insanity, plain and simple. You don't fix a sprained ankle by amputating the leg. What Tatter suggest it's plain butchery.<br /> <br /> I wasn't the one who stated that werewolves should have been developed to dominate melee. Matthew did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:20:49-08:00","id":7435,"title":"","content":"I actually feel Primal Urge bashing healing is a bit much, even in Gauru, and I'm all for upping the power levels. 1L auto-heal for all forms really should be default with essence spent to increase after the &quot;free&quot; heal.<br /> <br /> I would do something more like this (2B or 1L)/turn for all forms except Guaru. Guaru, I think (4B or 2L)/turn gives them a reason at lower Primal Urge to use it, in addition to say +PU to Strength (Like vampires in frenzy) on top of what they already have now.<br /> <br /> I will say I do not like the renown system as is, but I do like the concept of it as a representation of spiritual rank. I just think it would be more suited as merits and divorced from a Gift Limiter.<br /> <br /> However, I really LIKE lunacy as a concept. I will admit that its a bit over the top in its presentation (The willpower ratings are too high). Just because in modern days skepticism would basically make it irrelevant doesn't mean that in the past it wasn't useful. You can't blanket something that has protected them for thousands of years just because of modern setting. Removing it takes a lot away from using werewolves in past settings. But yes the willpower ratings as presented in the core needs to change.<br /> <br /> I want to see more emphasis on hunting, not just of spirits, and not with a focus of humans, but hunting in general. I want to see werewolves having problems with local ranchers and things because of their need to hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:54:41-08:00","id":7495,"title":"","content":"Its cool that you feel its too much. I'd rather have them shrugging off tons of damage as their big thing in combat. Prometheans getting fuck-you levels of armor, Mages getting fuck-you levels of everything, and Vampires going lolbashing seem like a good spread across the board.<br /> <br /> Mind you, in my first post I did point out how you'd only be allowed to spend 1 essence per turn to heal so the issue of it getting too much with regards to spending multiple essence is headed off at the pass.<br /> <br /> For Gauru Form I'd make it really frightening by following the Mask Rules in that you only take 1 health level of damage from a single source of bashing or lethal. Would retain its current time limit, but everyone knows if you're in it things have gone FUBAR on both sides of the field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:53:27-08:00","id":7588,"title":"","content":"The thing about healing bashing damage based on primal urge is that its fine up until 5+, after that point your essentially unable to take damage from bashing sources at all. A PU 10 werewolf would be basically unstoppable to anything unable to use weapons or magic. There's a difference between awesome and absurd. Whereas 10 offensive dice are equivalent to say 3.3 extra damage, 10 healing is automatically subtracted.<br /> <br /> Also, bashing damage really is nearly non-existent in GMC. ALL weapons are Lethal. So its also somewhat shortchanging while giving absurd theoretical healing. Are spirits mostly doing bashing damage? Sure it sounds awesome until someone uses a firearm or a knife or a crowbar.<br /> <br /> And I find limiting spending on a certain aspect to be relatively clunky and excessive record keeping. Rather, a general flat increase in free healing capability and a physical force increase is more thematic.<br /> <br /> If using the Mask capability in Guaru, I would say that it would still require the time limit, which I think most want to do away with. I think an additional amount of healing, or double as I suggested while in Guaru in addition to increased physical output is far superior in how useful it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T13:12:12-08:00","id":7604,"title":"","content":"My current thinking for a nice hack is the following:<br /> \u2022 Quick Regeneration: A werewolf can regenerate a number of points of bashing damage <br /> equal to half their Primal Urge rating each turn rounded up, minimum <br /> one. In non-Hisu and Urhan forms, they also regenerate one point of lethal every turn.<br /> Their aggravated recovery remains the same.<br /> <br /> So at the most (Primal Urge 9-10) you'll be regenerating 5 Bashing in one turn. Yes this makes fist fights basically pointless, but who ever gets to that point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:13:48-08:00","id":7742,"title":"","content":"5 is certainly fine, I just feel 10 is excessive. And I HAVE played in games that got to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:22:12-08:00","id":7790,"title":"","content":"What about Lethal? As it is now, you can't knock out a werewolf inflicting bashing damage. (You would regenerate the bashing damage on your turn, at the time you would be making the roll to stay conscious). So, Bashing healing it's pretty inconsequential considering that now even a size 2 stick does Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> You <i>would</i> eventually cause him to Kuruth (Inflicting damage over the last three health points).<br /> <br /> The same would apply with Lethal if they can regenerate it automatically that way... the only way to stop a werewolf in Death Rage (virtually speaking) would be to fill him with Aggravated damage, thus killing him. And that would really emphasize that mental state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-10-2013, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T18:24:26-08:00","id":7792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7790#post7790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Lethal? As it is now, you can't knock out a werewolf inflicting bashing damage. (You would regenerate the bashing damage on your turn, at the time you would be making the roll to stay conscious). So, Bashing healing it's pretty inconsequential considering that now even a size 2 stick does lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I hope is clarified in the update, because I've seen a couple of references to werewolves being rendered unconscious as I've read through the line and that seems like the kind of thing that needs a caveat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T19:24:26-08:00","id":7823,"title":"","content":"Again I feel 1L for all forms with 2L for Guaru each turn healing would put them at a very scary &quot;Monster&quot;. I mentioned that over-emphasizing bashing healing is a bit pointless, but I thing some lethal healing would be helpful in comparison to Strix Chronicles (only thing we currently have in comparison).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T21:57:09-08:00","id":7872,"title":"","content":"Even 2L I think wouldn't be bad compared to the 1L I've been trying out for a while. Any amount of costless healing (with an armor rating added in) is a pretty sweet deal to mitigate how deadly attacks are, honestly it'd come down to some play testing to see what creates the best balance of &quot;trivial&quot; threats coming off that way with a beefed up healing, while major threats still pose a reasonable problem. Making sure one's not turning a major threat into a trivial problem when it comes to combat with beefed up healing is the tough balancing act. It's less problematic in of itself, it just takes some consideration on at what point it starts to get too much when their other advantages are added in, and at what point it makes additional advantages such as fetishes etc. that do similar effects become overkill or not enough to be meaningful. I've not tried anything past 1L as of yet, so I'm not sure what that threshold may be between &quot;good, makes them individually frightening but not unmanageable&quot; and &quot;the moment melee combat goes with a starting werewolf, you may as well toss the opponents sheet&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T22:13:53-08:00","id":7877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7588#post7588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about healing bashing damage based on primal urge is that its fine up until 5+, after that point your essentially unable to take damage from bashing sources at all. A PU 10 werewolf would be basically unstoppable to anything unable to use weapons or magic. There's a difference between awesome and absurd. Whereas 10 offensive dice are equivalent to say 3.3 extra damage, 10 healing is automatically subtracted.<br /> <br /> Also, bashing damage really is nearly non-existent in GMC. ALL weapons are Lethal. So its also somewhat shortchanging while giving absurd theoretical healing. Are spirits mostly doing bashing damage? Sure it sounds awesome until someone uses a firearm or a knife or a crowbar.<br /> <br /> And I find limiting spending on a certain aspect to be relatively clunky and excessive record keeping. Rather, a general flat increase in free healing capability and a physical force increase is more thematic.<br /> <br /> If using the Mask capability in Guaru, I would say that it would still require the time limit, which I think most want to do away with. I think an additional amount of healing, or double as I suggested while in Guaru in addition to increased physical output is far superior in how useful it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRegarding the Willpower Ratings; have you played around with the rolled &quot;Lunacy&quot; mechanic for shifters in War Against the Pure at all? I've given it a whirl as a Resolve + Composure roll penalized by Primal Urge but even that still seemed excessive with the PU penalty after a some years using it. It's still effectively keeping the characters Willpower rating in mind (derived trait and all), but really, a lot of folks are going to be taking off when a 9-foot killing machine rampages anyhow from sheer common sense rather than an imposed mechanic.<br /> <br /> The memory effect to me is far more of an issue along with the penalties to do anything meaningful to them until your at extraordinarily high Willpower ratings. It's precisely why the Integrity issues with the conditions it can give regarding supernatural phenomenon, individually backed up with a Predatory Aura that can effectively stoke that instinctive reaction to a horrible supernatural predator seems better to me than an automatic group debuff along with built in mind wiping. Failing to contest the Predatory Aura and getting (or taking) a dramatic failure that may leave with a condition at times to reflect you are so traumatized you have trouble remembering? I could see that being a possibility, just not as a consistent default if that makes sense. At least then you have more occasions for meaningful human hunters who don't need utterly contrived builds to actually target Werewolves like you have right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T22:59:55-08:00","id":7890,"title":"","content":"See the problem with that again still assumes strictly modern settings in a heavily modernized world. Traumatization to the point of memory loss is not a base feature of Integrity, so it would be an added feature to that point. In previous eras people were more willing to accept the supernatural, and would have believed reports, especially from trustworthy individuals. In modern day, sure we think they're cracked.<br /> <br /> While vampires have a wide array of memory altering capabilities and enslavement, werewolves do not. A certain level of built in capability to remove memories is pretty essential for a world that has few enough sightings that end in remembering to develop to the point they simply don't believe anymore. Rather I should say that without some form of memory loss mechanic or widespread countermeasures such that the kindred have, Werewolves would be something still believed in and likely even closer to extinction.<br /> <br /> If they had an active predatory aura mechanic that anyone seeing them suddenly gets contested against, that would be understandable, but getting rid of it, or just relying on default integrity is pretty bad in keeping with a setting where the majority of humanity either doesn't believe in werewolves/supernatural creatures because you likely would have some that would otherwise be too trustworthy to ignore that saw something.<br /> <br /> And integrity isn't really geared towards anything but a modern mindset, its heavily associated with modern beliefs and social norms. Things that are traumatic and terrible today were far more common in past eras when structure was not so widely enforced. Sure war is brutal now with advanced weaponry, chemical warfare and such, but wars in the past were EVERYWHERE, the videos where Syrians are eating their enemies hearts were common place battlefield sights. People BELIEVED in magic and the supernatural.<br /> <br /> In the world of darkness, where the supernatural is real, groups either have capabilities dedicated to keeping their secrets safe (The Mask, Kindred Mind Control/Blood Bond, Whatever makes prometheans seem human, Disbelief), or are adept at creating an infrastructure against revelation(Vampires especially).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want Werewolves to lose Lunacy and memory loss capabilities, I would like to see them lessened to some extent, but not such that its just a &quot;Human reaction based on Integrity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:32:13-08:00","id":7956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7890#post7890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the problem with that again still assumes strictly modern settings in a heavily modernized world. Traumatization to the point of memory loss is not a base feature of Integrity, so it would be an added feature to that point. In previous eras people were more willing to accept the supernatural, and would have believed reports, especially from trustworthy individuals. In modern day, sure we think they're cracked.<br /> <br /> While vampires have a wide array of memory altering capabilities and enslavement, werewolves do not. A certain level of built in capability to remove memories is pretty essential for a world that has few enough sightings that end in remembering to develop to the point they simply don't believe anymore. Rather I should say that without some form of memory loss mechanic or widespread countermeasures such that the kindred have, Werewolves would be something still believed in and likely even closer to extinction.<br /> <br /> If they had an active predatory aura mechanic that anyone seeing them suddenly gets contested against, that would be understandable, but getting rid of it, or just relying on default integrity is pretty bad in keeping with a setting where the majority of humanity either doesn't believe in werewolves/supernatural creatures because you likely would have some that would otherwise be too trustworthy to ignore that saw something.<br /> <br /> And integrity isn't really geared towards anything but a modern mindset, its heavily associated with modern beliefs and social norms. Things that are traumatic and terrible today were far more common in past eras when structure was not so widely enforced. Sure war is brutal now with advanced weaponry, chemical warfare and such, but wars in the past were EVERYWHERE, the videos where Syrians are eating their enemies hearts were common place battlefield sights. People BELIEVED in magic and the supernatural.<br /> <br /> In the world of darkness, where the supernatural is real, groups either have capabilities dedicated to keeping their secrets safe (The Mask, Kindred Mind Control/Blood Bond, Whatever makes prometheans seem human, Disbelief), or are adept at creating an infrastructure against revelation(Vampires especially).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want Werewolves to lose Lunacy and memory loss capabilities, I would like to see them lessened to some extent, but not such that its just a &quot;Human reaction based on Integrity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In lunacys case i think the argument of &quot;in the dark ages was necessary&quot; could be use it against it. In previous eras civilization were more spread and isolated so lets say you have a village of 30 people and a pack is doing their bussiness there. That pack would probably be careful as the tenet of the moon already enforce discretion and on top of that they have the protection of lunacy so to a pack to be discovered the should have to careless in front of the one human in said village with willpower high enough. <br /> <br /> I think that in previous era with the tenet of the moon + lunacy is a miracle modern world have any conception of a werewolf whatsoever. Vampires have masquerade enforcer because they lack an automatic failsafe as efficient as lunacy. Its a thing of internal logic of the setting, why enforce the furry masquerade (werewolves don have a name for the masquerade....why is that? ) as tenet when its magically protects itself.<br /> <br /> I could buy on of the two extremes though. Either the furry masquerade is enforced because they lack lunacy or because of lunacy maintaining the furry masquerade is no longer necessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T03:35:23-08:00","id":7957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7792#post7792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's something I hope is clarified in the update, because I've seen a couple of references to werewolves being rendered unconscious as I've read through the line and that seems like the kind of thing that needs a caveat.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think &quot;wolverine&quot; rules regarding regeneration could applied there. Meaning that is perfectly possible to choke an werewolf into unconsiousness as regeneration wouldnt help a werewolf there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T04:39:15-08:00","id":7975,"title":"","content":"In terms of Totem, why don't we just flip the idea around? A Totem isn't picked by a pack, but something that 'naturally' occurs over a period a time, a Spirit representing the pack's territory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T05:48:44-08:00","id":7996,"title":"","content":"That narrows the idea, and leaves nomadic packs with nothing. You already can have say, the spirit of your neighborhood as totem, in fact, the totem presented in the Quickstart for Forsaken was just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:01:24-08:00","id":8001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7996#post7996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That narrows the idea, and leaves nomadic packs with nothing. You already can have say, the spirit of your neighborhood as totem, in fact, the totem presented in the Quickstart for Forsaken was just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I'm talking about one that changes at the territory changes, as it grows or shrinks or even as things happen to it - a kind of reverse Fisher Kingsort of thing. And, frankly, I think that the idea could do with a bit of focusing.<br /> <br /> But in the end I'm not really bothered. I'll just wait and see what OP comes up with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:04:08-08:00","id":8003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7996#post7996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That narrows the idea, and leaves nomadic packs with nothing. You already can have say, the spirit of your neighborhood as totem, in fact, the totem presented in the Quickstart for Forsaken was just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>i agree though it could be left to DM discrettion, maybe nomadic packs have a totem that just stuck arround with them. Totem is a tricky concept by itself for starting packs as the ban sometimes means that the pack is gonna have their behaviour fixed in one way from the get go.<br /> <br /> If i were to use totems again i wouldnt let player downright make their own or start with one but slowly give it one that fit the general idea of the pack. Unless they are playing a very experience pack","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:20:24-08:00","id":8007,"title":"","content":"Nah, if the theme is gonna be The Wolf Must Hunt... then hunt your damned totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T06:35:03-08:00","id":8020,"title":"","content":"Regarding totems I would like them to stay, they are a goldmine for story ideas and helps enforce the idea that the pack is a tangible bond between pack members. The mechanics and the explanation to *how* they fit on tht character sheet really is in need of rewriting. To mkae it clear, concise (a problem that the werewolf core suffers from from time to time - but Mage has that probelm too IMO), so when we start satting the totem we don't feel the need to drink.<br /> <br /> Having the option to have totems optional would be nice, even if it's a side bar alongs the lines of &quot;if you want your game not to have totoems as the default, that fine, just ignore this bit&quot; that would okay. But to be honest, the totem stuff is optional, don't like it? Ignore it, it's your game and there is any White Wolf men in black that are going to come around your door and &quot;have a word&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the default (if you use them) way to introduce a totem into the game if the group isn't experienced is, &quot;you're playing a newer than new pack, you want a totem, hunt it IC&quot; (which I think is what Ephsy is alluding to). Then once you have done the amazing hunt session/scene that is atmospheric and makes the &quot;Wolf must Hunt&quot; really ring true you sit down and stat up what your boar spirit should look like on paper. <b>The mechanics should fit what you've set out descriptively</b>, the rest of the interaction and story hooks that come with a totem come after, once th werewoves start learning more about this strange new ally.<br /> <br /> I've always felt that, yes the spirit world hates you, but earn the right amount of respect and balance that between making sure the more wild spirits don't claim soneone, and a werewolf's territory can feel like home ground, not behind enemy lines. That should be earned in play (or the set up to a &quot;territory burn&quot; game).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, Idigam Chronicles will most likely be a more concise and smoother version of Werewolf the Forsaken, not a new edition. I think we should bear that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:43:16-08:00","id":8061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=6614#post6614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I'm kinda iffy on more convoluted systems like that. Honestly, I'm thinking of just taking the highest ranking member's effective spirit rank (if using the Primal Urge systems to determine it, because getting high is rare and costly) and adding +1 for being part of a bonded pack. You're not going to get honorary ranked 4's and 5 Werewolves with any consistency; those are high, HIGH Primal Urge types under this idea, legends really. If using the idea that being two ranks higher makes your natural attacks like banes to spirits, it's still keeping things reasonable even if you do get an honorary rank 5 Werewolf in your pack; you're still just getting the benefits on rank 4 and less spirits, and that's in a rare case hunting alongside a true supernatural paragon among werewolves. In most cases your packs effective rank is going to sit from 2 (if you go by the notion their honorary rank is at the bottom for harsher chronicles) to 3 more commonly (going by the idea they start around effective rank 2), with 4, 5 and the very, very rare 6 being seen much less given Primal Urge Costs (even old style Renown Costs for that matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I very much doubt that Renown is going anywhere at all, so I figure that will be the measure for HSR. Or at least I find it likely.<br /> <br /> I like your system, actually, and it works regardless of how one gets to HSR (which is the other thing I was striving to do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:45:05-08:00","id":8064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8020#post8020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, Idigam Chronicles will most likely be a more concise and smoother version of Werewolf the Forsaken, not a new edition. I think we should bear that in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, for those wondering, is why the proposals for severe setting shifts are so jarring and unwelcome; one of the things mentioned back in the days where Sexmurder was the working fandom name for Blood and Smoke was that a goal of the chronicle book was to help bring the mechanics more in line with the fiction. &quot;Like God&quot; is basically one big lead-up to the effects of Lunacy and I feel it's one of the better opening fictions. I'd be rather disappointed if it couldn't make it into the anthology just because some people don't like Lunacy as a concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:49:38-08:00","id":8068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8064#post8064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, for those wondering, is why the proposals for severe setting shifts are so jarring and unwelcome; one of the things mentioned back in the days where Sexmurder was the working fandom name for Blood and Smoke was that a goal of the chronicle book was to help bring the mechanics more in line with the fiction. &quot;Like God&quot; is basically one big lead-up to the effects of Lunacy and I feel it's one of the better opening fictions. I'd be rather disappointed if it couldn't make it into the anthology just because some people don't like Lunacy as a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why dont take this rare chance to look at mechanics agains to see if wheter or not they should continue? why give all mechanics a free pass instead of analyzing if each of then are still needed? Many people agree that some of the more dissonant elements of the both Requiem and forsaken are the left overs the have to carry from the previous iterations of the game, so why dont take a fresh look again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"atta