"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T07:58:38-08:00","id":8079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8068#post8068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why dont take this rare chance to look at mechanics agains to see if wheter or not they should continue? why give all mechanics a free pass instead of analyzing if each of then are still needed? Many people agree that some of the more dissonant elements of the both Requiem and forsaken are the left overs the have to carry from the previous iterations of the game, so why dont take a fresh look again?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Free pass&quot; is not what &quot;don't make useless suggestions like 'completely get rid of Renown and Lunacy'&quot; means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:02:07-08:00","id":8085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8079#post8079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Free pass&quot; is not what &quot;don't make useless suggestions like 'completely get rid of Renown and Lunacy'&quot; means.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rationale behind most of those are worth to look at. At least as a base to what to change those mechanics. Suggestions like replacing lunacy for predatory aura is indeed worth a look. Renown thought? i dont say replace it but it should get a revamp like some of the mechanics in B&amp;S.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T08:58:36-08:00","id":8118,"title":"","content":"The thing is, I think Werewolf the Forsaken <i>works</i>. Granted the mechanics and the core book's tone and discussion needs a rewrite to make them clearer (and in the case of gifts less... &quot;wonky&quot; in practise). Renown as well, it's an elegant (if flawed in <i>some</i> ways) system and I don't see the point of either getting rid of it or turning it into a something borrowed from Changling.<br /> <br /> I do understand that the mantles in Changling are a brilliant little merit (they are one of many amazing things in that stellar line), but that doesn't mean that Renown should be kicked out (because it's an &quot;acopolypse holdover&quot; - which i've never understood the logic of, disciplines are in Vampire, but both of them seem to have them), or change to a merit because the current system has some issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With everything in werewolf, it does have it's rough edges but it's playable - and it's <i>good</i> playable. If the Idigam Chronicles does what Blood an Smoke did which is subtly change some of the focusses and tighten up the rules, but not make a new edition so it's recognisably Forsaken then I'll be happy (and I suspect the majority of fans and those interested). I understand the desire to change things you don't like, but it shouldn't be at the loss of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's what I want primarily out of The Wolf Must Hunt. An updated, concise, available but still recognisably Forsaken Core Book. I would like to fall in love with Werewolf again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:09:32-08:00","id":8124,"title":"","content":"As far as Renown goes? I think now would be a good time to introduce a sub XP system for Renown. The problem with Renown as I've experienced it is that it's some what of an XP sink. Almost like having 5 extra Power Stats. I think that if we had a sub system for XP, like how Mages have Arcane XP, but applied to Renown, it might help &quot;fix&quot; that issue at least. Maybe also add some extra benefits from Renown, like Purity adds to Death Rage checks or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:00:56-08:00","id":8167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7956#post7956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In lunacys case i think the argument of &quot;in the dark ages was necessary&quot; could be use it against it. In previous eras civilization were more spread and isolated so lets say you have a village of 30 people and a pack is doing their bussiness there. That pack would probably be careful as the tenet of the moon already enforce discretion and on top of that they have the protection of lunacy so to a pack to be discovered the should have to careless in front of the one human in said village with willpower high enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not advocating that it be kept as is. I think the willpower should be lowered or that there is more of a rolled aspect of it.<br /> <br /> And even disparate villages, and even more recent past still had levels of communication. In the past one Death Rage in a crowded area would be all it took for people to leave and talk about what they'd seen and where. Trade was a rather common and driving factor, and not isolated to faceless commerce like it is today. Armies frequently invaded different regions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7956#post7956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that in previous era with the tenet of the moon + lunacy is a miracle modern world have any conception of a werewolf whatsoever. Vampires have masquerade enforcer because they lack an automatic failsafe as efficient as lunacy. Its a thing of internal logic of the setting, why enforce the furry masquerade (werewolves don have a name for the masquerade....why is that? ) as tenet when its magically protects itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, every other group has more capabilities to enforce it other than &quot;Oh if we go hide far enough in the woods, nobody will see us.&quot; Vampires have adept slavery and mind control mechanics, but they still have rules about not doing things in public. Werewolves DO NOT have these social talents so readily available, if you got rid of Lunacy, you would only have the rule. And that rule likely wouldn't get very far without the large scale social influence vampires exert over a city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=7956#post7956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could buy on of the two extremes though. Either the furry masquerade is enforced because they lack lunacy or because of lunacy maintaining the furry masquerade is no longer necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think BOTH are necessary, I just don't think Lunacy should be kept as is. It needs to be lessened so that conflict and memory are MORE likely to occur, I just don't think it should be thrown out entirely when, despite whatever you think werewolves are capable of, they don't have the large scale infrastructure capabilities by default to enforce a version of the masquerade like vampires do, nor the dubious lack of laws associated with conventional morality.<br /> <br /> Also you seem to be assuming that Harmony will remain as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:37:41-08:00","id":8208,"title":"","content":"Just would like to point out that not many vampires have memory altering powers, not even 1 in 5, venture elders probably have 3 dots in dominate but the rest, i doubt it, while as of now ALL werewolfs and mages have memory errasing powers that they dont even have to roll or concentrate to use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:43:57-08:00","id":8217,"title":"","content":"And vampires are supposed to be cursed and damned. Why should they have it easy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:48:19-08:00","id":8218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8208#post8208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just would like to point out that not many vampires have memory altering powers, not even 1 in 5, venture elders probably have 3 dots in dominate but the rest, i doubt it, while as of now ALL werewolfs and mages have memory errasing powers that they dont even have to roll or concentrate to use</div> </div> </div> </div>Memory-edits are part of the first dot of B&amp;S Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:21:18-08:00","id":8251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8217#post8217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And vampires are supposed to be cursed and damned. Why should they have it easy?</div> </div> </div> </div>why would Werewolves and mage have it easy too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:26:51-08:00","id":8258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8167#post8167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think BOTH are necessary, I just don't think Lunacy should be kept as is. It needs to be lessened so that conflict and memory are MORE likely to occur, I just don't think it should be thrown out entirely when, despite whatever you think werewolves are capable of, they don't have the large scale infrastructure capabilities by default to enforce a version of the masquerade like vampires do, nor the dubious lack of laws associated with conventional morality.<br /> <br /> Also you seem to be assuming that Harmony will remain as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, im asuming harmony will remain as it is as there isnt any new information about it changing so i have to asume it gonna be the same until a developer say the contrary. But i think you are right, it shouldnt remain as it is right now. I hope it remains modular enough as it is now so one can remove from one own game without having to house rule a lot<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:54:40-08:00","id":8276,"title":"","content":"Have you seen the way humanity works now? Or Integrity? I would assume some major differences will come into use with Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T12:23:32-08:00","id":8292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8276#post8276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen the way humanity works now? Or Integrity? I would assume some major differences will come into use with Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh i know there are gonna change it but i work under the assumption they are not because otherwise before we talk about a lot of stuff we would have to reach a consensus about the new harmony. Many of the things we are discussing of course are gonna change as New New werewolf becomes more a reality","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:08:07-08:00","id":8316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8292#post8292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> oh i know there are gonna change it but i work under the assumption they are not because otherwise before we talk about a lot of stuff we would have to reach a consensus about the new harmony. Many of the things we are discussing of course are gonna change as New New werewolf becomes more a reality</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, happily, &quot;we&quot; don't have to reach consensus about anything, save those folks here who are either already giving input into the book or who will work on it.<br /> <br /> That said, I fully expect Harmony to get an overhaul just like Integrity and Humanity. I don't know why anyone would think differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:33:13-08:00","id":8334,"title":"","content":"My main concern about Lunacy is that it\u2019s now mostly redundant: with Integrity working the way it does, the tendency of mortals to freak out when witnessing a man-beast going on a rampage is already covered \u2014 though I could see something like the current rules being kept as a shorthand for dealing with extras, where you don\u2019t want to have to track Integrity. The only thing not covered is the memory loss that lets werewolves shift into Gauru form in downtown New York City without letting the whole world know that werewolves are real; and I don\u2019t think they should be able to do that anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:01:13-08:00","id":8357,"title":"","content":"Well it could simply be handled by a new condition appropriate to constituting a breaking point for the human, I do think that Memory loss needs some place in the reaction. I feel that they need to have some mechanic associated with that, though I feel Lunacy as is now takes that too far. It is TOO difficult to overcome.<br /> <br /> I would think something more appropriate would be something that factors in additional bystanders, and is more actively rolled, something that is success or fail, rather than willpower based. Maybe composure or resolve alone, with a particular modifier.<br /> <br /> Because say if the breaking point occurs and the average human rolls, they're going to succeed and likely understand whats going on (Resolve+Composure+1-2). Its hard to just shoulder it on Integrity alone and expect it to simply be justified, just as its difficult to think that someone wouldn't have said something. I've always taken the sin primarily to mean &quot;Don't tell anyone&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunacy as is IS overkill, but I feel there needs to be something that fills much of the void and the integrity mechanics simply don't do that by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:37:04-08:00","id":8376,"title":"","content":"Repeating this from the old forums; Give more attention to the non-hishu forms and the specie of the character.<br /> <br /> One of the things that has bothered me a lot when I'm reading book such as Tribes of the Moon, is that when you look at the NPC descriptions, none go beyond hishu. It is like what the character looks like in human form only matters and the other forms are just tools and how one looks in them doesn't factor into the game. And that to me feels like it is sidelining what the character actually is, the five forms are the characer and how they look in those forms should be noted because (obviously) the characters won't only be seen in their hishu. I do not mean that each of the five forms needs to be descriped, just hishu and urhan, so that the ST and the reader gets what the character looks in the between forms as well. Minor thing I know, but I think it adds that sense that the character is a wereWOLF, a shapeshifter and not a human shaman.<br /> <br /> Speaking of human shamans, some concepts in the books can as well seem a bit too distant from a werewolf. Written with the powers in mind, rather than where those powers come from. Example characters should feel like they are werewolves, not random magicians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:45:21-08:00","id":8382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8251#post8251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> why would Werewolves and mage have it easy too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Little thing called suspension of disbelief. If there isn't anything which prevents onlookers from recalling gross supernatural incidents, we would be playing another game altogether. Meanwhile, vampire have whole institutions to the effect of concealing their presence. And those are their plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:40:52-08:00","id":8412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8376#post8376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Repeating this from the old forums; Give more attention to the non-hishu forms and the specie of the character.<br /> <br /> One of the things that has bothered me a lot when I'm reading book such as Tribes of the Moon, is that when you look at the NPC descriptions, none go beyond hishu.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just finished reading Shadows of the U.K., whose last chapter (a list of notable characters that takes up about a third of the book's pagecount and is at least fifty percent werewolves by character-sheet-level writeups) had maybe five percent of its werewolf characters' descriptions <i>not</i> include notes on what their Urhan form looked like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:49:33-08:00","id":8424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8412#post8412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished reading Shadows of the U.K., whose last chapter (a list of notable characters that takes up about a third of the book's pagecount and is at least fifty percent werewolves by character-sheet-level writeups) had maybe five percent of its werewolf characters' descriptions <i>not</i> include notes on what their Urhan form looked like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, I'm glad it had them. I don't myself own the U.K book, so I didn't know ^^''<br /> <br /> But in other books, such a Wolf'sBane, Tribes of the Moon and Lodge Books, they do not have any wolf descriptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:02:38-08:00","id":8437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8382#post8382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Little thing called suspension of disbelief. If there isn't anything which prevents onlookers from recalling gross supernatural incidents, we would be playing another game altogether. Meanwhile, vampire have whole institutions to the effect of concealing their presence. And those are their plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there is something preventing onlooker recalling gross supernatural incidents its called rationalization and social pressure. Even if you go out now and a werewolf in gauru cross the street in front of you, who would believe you? Even with video people would call that a hoax. You can find in youtube a ton of &quot;ghost videos&quot; and maybe in wod 10% of those are real but they get buried in the mix. And even then would you tell that to another person you personally know? I doubt it as going around telling people about vampire and werewolves are real is quick way to be considered crazy.<br /> <br /> It wouldnt be that much of a change setting wise. Im gonna refer to the Dresden files series wich is basically WoD in disguise without the supernatural failsafes full of mages, changeling, werewolves and vampires, demons and even Kue Jin (i bet the author play a lot of masquerade/ascension before writing that series) and even the protagonist at one point reflects about how people are so wired to disbelief the supernatural that the only way they could believe would be throwing a &quot;supernatural pride parade&quot; in the city. Or by going with a more close example, in the queen of the dammed book lestat go to a bunch of guy and tells them he is a vampire and then reflect how protecting the masquerade is useless as its protects itself.<br /> <br /> Hunters being the exception and they are very few and far between. I just would be more interesting to play it without that supernatural failsafe so when a PC fuck up things the consequences are more aggravated and more believable than saying &quot;that this you character fuck up, yeah by chance he just was a willpower 8 character&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bBut more to the point, papa bear said that vampire shouldnt have it easy because they have a curse but why also werewolves? Werewolves have the furry masquerade as integral part of their morality and lodges dedicated to hide their nature so why should they have it easy with some supernatural thingie? Its make the tenet of the moon look like a unnecessary prohibition and the lodges dedicates to preserver the furry masquerade feel redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-11-2013, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:37:29-08:00","id":8458,"title":"","content":"What exactly makes you believe that dealing with the aftershocks of lunacy is easy? It's not nearly a safe-fail as you think. At least not in my games. If you go around butchering people in Gauru, people are going to notice. It's the reason why it's such a highly regarded Oath, by both sides of the Uratha conflict. I've seen PCs getting executed over sheer displays of callous disregard for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:43:56-08:00","id":8464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8458#post8458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly makes you believe that dealing with the aftershocks of lunacy is easy? It's not nearly a safe-fail as you think. At least not in my games. If you go around butchering people in Gauru, people are going to notice. It's the reason why it's such a highly regarded Oath, by both sides of the Uratha conflict. I've seen PCs getting executed over sheer displays of callous disregard for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said it yourself that your interpretation in your games. In my games i just remove the whole thing and nothing is really change more than the werewolves now know that the possibility of a new hunter being born or attracting the wrong kind of attention is very very real. But again thats my games that respond to my and my players needs as your interpretation serves you and your players needs.<br /> <br /> But rules as written sometimes it feels like that oath + lodges + lunacy that protects the furry masquerade is a overkill. I honestly hope that if they dont remove it at least they change it so i works better and as Rani Neferet pointed out, the willpower requirements are way to high right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-11-2013, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T16:58:53-08:00","id":8471,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel the need to comment on this idea that Lunacy is too powerful because &quot;Willpower requirements are too high&quot;. If you go by what the book says, perfectly, mechanically, the letter of the law if you will. Then yeah, it looks like too much. But, what about ST fiat? He/she has final say and controls the game, yeah? On top of that, are there STs who show their players every write up they make? Because I was under the impression you weren't supposed to reveal that info. That alone should be good enough for Werewolf players to not go around shapeshifting everywhere in front of Mortals. They don't know what everybodies Willpower rating is. How can they be certain that they can get away with shapeshifting in public? That's what you play off of. Lunacy is powerful, but it's not perfect. As an ST, you are supposed to play on that and keep your players on their toes.<br /> <br /> Don't let the rules run your games. They are there to help you run your game, not control your game out right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:05:46-08:00","id":8474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8471#post8471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel the need to comment on this idea that Lunacy is too powerful because &quot;Willpower requirements are too high&quot;. <b><u>If you go by what the book says, perfectly, mechanically, the letter of the law if you will. Then yeah, it looks like too much.</u></b> But, what about ST fiat? He/she has final say and controls the game, yeah? On top of that, are there STs who show their players every write up they make? Because I was under the impression you weren't supposed to reveal that info. That alone should be good enough for Werewolf players to not go around shapeshifting everywhere in front of Mortals. They don't know what everybodies Willpower rating is. How can they be certain that they can get away with shapeshifting in public? That's what you play off of. Lunacy is powerful, but it's not perfect. As an ST, you are supposed to play on that and keep your players on their toes.<br /> <br /> Don't let the rules run your games. They are there to help you run your game, not control your game out right.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if they are revising the rules of werewolf why not change/modify a rule that <b><u>you have just say it needs GM fiat</u></b>? Of course everyone make their own house rules in their own games but if New New Werewolf is revision of the rule to fix some issues they have why not fix that one?<br /> <br /> Im not saying that the game doesnt work but i do say it has this flaw that require DM fiat. So if they have this opportunity to fix it. Why shouldnt they do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:31:41-08:00","id":8491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8474#post8474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if they are revising the rules of werewolf why not change/modify a rule that <b><u>you have just say it needs GM fiat</u></b>? Of course everyone make their own house rules in their own games but if New New Werewolf is revision of the rule to fix some issues they have why not fix that one?<br /> <br /> Im not saying that the game doesnt work but i do say it has this flaw that require DM fiat. So if they have this opportunity to fix it. Why shouldnt they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not a problem that needs to be fixed? The truth is, the Storytelling System is based on ST fiat. Yes, there are rules to help govern things, but rules don't run your game. The ST does. Are you saying you want this game to be completly run by rules alone with no judgement calls given from the ST or any work on his part? Hell, the section that talks about Lunacy specifically mentions ST fiat as an element of Lunacy. It even gives ideas on how to boost Mortal Willpower to help them remember.<br /> <br /> There is nothing really wrong with Lunacy. It works just fine for the current system. There's nothing wrong with ST fiat. It's been there from the beginning. Every nWoD game requires it. I don't see why Lunacy, or Werewolf for that matter, has to be some sort of special case. I'm not saying Lunacy shouln't be updated. It should. Hell, I like the idea of it being part of some kind of Primal Aura that you can turn off or on at a whim. That makes crossovers easier. I'm just not a fan of hearing things like &quot; I want the game to run itself&quot;. I know that's not what you're really saying, but that's what it sounds like.<br /> <br /> So I guess what I'm trying to say is, if something needs ST fiat now and again to make things interesting and not predicable, it's not a bug, it's a feature. One that I'm very fond of.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 11-11-2013, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:40:39-08:00","id":8495,"title":"","content":"At least 80% of the rules is ST interpretation, or Fiat. This isn't D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:47:41-08:00","id":8497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8491#post8491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's not a problem that needs to be fixed? The truth is, the Storytelling System is based on ST fiat. Yes, there are rules to help govern things, but rules don't run your game. The ST does. Are you saying you want this game to be completly run by rules alone with no judgement calls given from the ST or any work on his part? Hell, the section that talks about Lunacy specifically mentions ST fiat as an element of Lunacy. It even gives ideas on how to boost Mortal Willpower to help him remember.<br /> <br /> There is nothing really wrong with Lunacy. It works just fine for the current system. There's nothing wrong with ST fiat. It's been there from the beginning. Every nWoD game requires it. I don't see why Lunacy, or Werewolf for that matter, has to be some sort of special case. <u><b>I'm not saying Lunacy shouln't be updated. It should. </b></u>Hell, I like the idea of it being part of some kind of Primal Aura that you can turn off or on at a whim<u><b>.</b></u> That makes crossovers easier. I'm just not a fan of hearing things like &quot; I want the game to run itself&quot;. I know that's not what you're really saying, but that's what it sounds like.<br /> <br /> So I guess what I'm trying to say is, if something needs ST fiat now and again to make things interesting and not predicable, it's not a bug, it's a feature. One that I'm very fond of.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>the funny part is that we are agreeing. That wich i bolded is what i said in post #183. They could go with predatory aura or just lower the cap of the willpower requirement and still leave the GM fiat.<br /> <br /> I like GM fiat and is a great tool but it should never replace good game designing. Is the same as saying &quot;I sell a car with 3 wheels and the extra one in the trunk because i know the client can just put his own tire&quot; And to a <b><u>degree</u></b> a game should run by itself, when we first open the books a fumble to the pages we tend to not deviate so much of the rules as written because we are still feeling our way arround (this by 10000 if this is our first RP book) so the rules as written should be in the best state possible as new DMs are not gonna just adjust rules or GM fiat from the get go and if the system have a part that doesnt work well (as you pointed out with lunacy as written) then such New DM is gonna think the game is badly made or worse his enjoyment of the game is gonna decrease.<br /> <br /> Before you say it. I know there are special DMs out there who take a system for the first time and start just making adjustments willy nilly and those guys are great. I know one who is that type of Dm as is a great trait to have but they are not the majority. The majority of people who buy an RPG book they dont know, they expect it to be able to play it from the box without many complications<br /> <br /> I dont think New New werewolf is made 100% exclusively for the fans, i think its made to attract new blood (new clients) they should try to get the rules as written in the best possible condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","user":"kaho","date":". 11-11-2013, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:03:21-08:00","id":8509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8497#post8497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the funny part is that we are agreeing. That wich i bolded is what i said in post #183. They could go with predatory aura or just lower the cap of the willpower requirement and still leave the GM fiat.<br /> <br /> I like GM fiat and is a great tool but it should never replace good game designing. Is the same as saying &quot;I sell a car with 3 wheels and the extra one in the trunk because i know the client can just put his own tire&quot; And to a <b><u>degree</u></b> a game should run by itself, when we first open the books a fumble to the pages we tend to not deviate so much of the rules as written because we are still feeling our way arround (this by 10000 if this is our first RP book) so the rules as written should be in the best state possible as new DMs are not gonna just adjust rules or GM fiat from the get go and if the system have a part that doesnt work well (as you pointed out with lunacy as written) then such New DM is gonna think the game is badly made or worse his enjoyment of the game is gonna decrease.<br /> <br /> Before you say it. I know there are special DMs out there who take a system for the first time and start just making adjustments willy nilly and those guys are great. I know one who is that type of Dm as is a great trait to have but they are not the majority. The majority of people who buy an RPG book they dont know, they expect it to be able to play it from the box without many complications<br /> <br /> I dont think New New werewolf is made 100% exclusively for the fans, i think its made to attract new blood (new clients) they should try to get the rules as written in the best possible condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what? I totally agree with you. Using the RAW is the best way for new players and STs to get use to and understand a game. But, as I said in my previous post, the Lunacy section mentions ST Fiat as part of Lunacy. Using the RAW, you're supposed to make judgement calls on Lunacy. It has never been supposed to be static. It's always supposed to be changing and unpredicable per RAW. So, it really has nothing to do with special STs or even super creative ones. It has everything to do with fully understanding Lunacy and how it's supposed to be used and how your players can never really rely on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 11-11-2013, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:50:56-08:00","id":8563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8437#post8437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah there is something preventing onlooker recalling gross supernatural incidents its called rationalization and social pressure. Even if you go out now and a werewolf in gauru cross the street in front of you, who would believe you? Even with video people would call that a hoax. You can find in youtube a ton of &quot;ghost videos&quot; and maybe in wod 10% of those are real but they get buried in the mix. And even then would you tell that to another person you personally know? I doubt it as going around telling people about vampire and werewolves are real is quick way to be considered crazy..</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal opinion, but that sounds just as much as, if not more of, a &quot;fail-safe&quot; than Lunacy is at present. And without any potentially crippling mental disorders on top of it. To me, that sounds like Lunacy, but weaker and watered-down.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong - I completely agree with this. In fact, I continually tell people that this is exactly how the Masquerade works, because almost nobody is going to believe you if you claim a widely-liked wealthy philanthropist (for instance) is a vampire. So yes, this is the baseline assumption, as far as I'm concerned. People who go around claiming there are monsters around - vampires, werewolves, and so on - are usually labeled as crazy. Lunacy is just another layer on top of that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:11:43-08:00","id":8570,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the setting and baseline assumptions would be very different if there wasn't some level of protection. This continually ignores the point that the world was not always so skeptical in regards to what someone has seen. People believed in things once upon a time. I mean look at witch hunts, people digging up corpses to stake them and such. These things were believed once upon a time even without their existence. In a world where such things do exist, its hard to believe that this would still be the case if there wasn't some manner of supernatural protection, large scale infrastructure or general capability for memory alteration.<br /> <br /> Hell the vinculum is a powerful masquerade holding tool, even when it potentially threatens it. Its basically innate mind control.<br /> <br /> A setting is built upon a history, even if its set on modern nights, there are some things that make it difficult to have it as essentially our modern world with modern assumptions about the supernatural if the lack of evidence wasn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:31:22-08:00","id":8575,"title":"","content":"Except the WoD -isn't- our world, and humans -are- more complacent in it. Even GMC's rule update PDF talks about this some; people actively don't notice a lot of the weirdness out there consistently. You're not dealing with a world where one Death Rage blows everything out of the water even on national TV; you're dealing with an entire reality where extraordinarily potent beings in numerous niches are working to keep all this hush hush. Lunacy isn't required, let alone ideas of modern/historical divides in perception. Those infrastructures are there, entrenched and have been for a very, very long time to keep things quiet. Humans are complacent in the setting, and willfully (sometimes unwillingly) ignorant of what's going on.<br /> <br /> Outside of 'Plot Hooks', they're not going anywhere; Lunacy is just tacked-on redundancy that does more storyline harm than good in my eyes when it comes to humans becoming threats. Rather than leaving that yep, shit can hit the fan without some bogged down mechanic marginalizing and mitigating that potential until it becomes fairly damn trivial (wasn't it you, Strider who stated that after 8 years of running Cam games for werewolf, you had all of -two- meaningful breaches that weren't white-washed by Lunacy, enough to call for Harmony checks? Or am I thinking another user on the old forums?), instead we get werewolf 'easy mode'.<br /> <br /> To hell with that. I want my conflict, not werewolves with built in Jedi-mind tricks so damn potent it neuters the human threat in the game to an excessive degree. It's entirely my own POV here, but I actually find suspension of disbelief damaged more with the contrived notion of Lunacy, than I do with werewolves just being really damn careful, and avoiding (go figure, due to their Rage) being quite as insinuated in dense human population areas without effort, powers and failsafes put in place, including Lodges and packs that are tasked with maintaining the quiet (and getting rid of those problematic people one way or another) that are intent on blowing things out into the open.<br /> <br /> One requires gameplay, interactions, setting considerations and risk. It requires active effort to maintain. It makes sense that there would be werewolf societies dedicated to just that, with others experimenting more and more on how to integrate or keep under the radar of humans.<br /> <br /> The other requires changing forms and suddenly it's a cake walk unless someone gets lucky with a roll if the ST Fiat gets used (good luck as an average or even an above human getting enough successes to be a problem by the way), or has an extraordinarily high Willpower period.<br /> <br /> I'll take the former; I won't so much as shed a crocodile tear of Lunacy gets tossed into the trash-can. It's just not necessary giving the WoD setting, and never has been in my view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-12-2013, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:19:20-08:00","id":8588,"title":"","content":"Again, I DO NOT LIKE LUNACY AS IS. I think it should change some. But I also feel it is rather necessary to some extent. I think it should be a far more active mechanic not an automatic. I want to see some conflict, but I think your simply dismissing my points and going &quot;Neener neener neener I can't hear you.&quot; There is a big difference between looking the other way when something odd happens, or feeling things aren't as they seem as depicted by what your saying.<br /> <br /> The world IS our world. Whether you like it or not, it has the same history, same basic events. Every major human event has happened, history is as it is in our world except with the exception of supernatural events occuring as well. Werewolves do not have their own large scale infrastructure and by default the other groups don't give two shits about any of the others, they're not dashing to cover up each others fuck ups, they're worried about their own.<br /> <br /> Vampires have inbuilt mind control/slavery with the vinculum. Mages have groups dedicated to keeping humans out of the loop, as well as powers that are essentially made non-existent by the presence of people. Changelings have the Mask. These things are specifically tuned to keeping these things secret, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Werewolves... have a small group of allies. They have antagonists who really don't give a shit about humans.<br /> <br /> Your arguing that because something is one way, it has always been that way and simply dismiss my argument because of a gross assumption. Events in history have far supported my point that people believed throughout history, but with the development of science and general understanding of it, people looked more towards evidence. Your assumptions hold that just because NOW people tend to ignore it, means that they always did. That's like saying that dinosaurs don't exist because humans always ruled the world. You have to have a foundation for behaviors like the dismissive one people have today.<br /> <br /> Yes people NOW actively ignore it, but this simply would not be the case in times when the supernatural was considered very real, and generally &quot;EVIL!!!! KILL IT WITH FIRE&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T23:20:19-08:00","id":8633,"title":"","content":"You misunderstood me, I wasn't saying that -you- liked it as is, I was stating that the idea of it, in general, really doesn't add a whole lot positive to the game. I read where you stated you believe it needs to be altered. It was a general comment on what it's like -as is and if it's kept as a innate memory wipe- while also addressing later on the notions of modern/vs historical mindsets. Some of that post addressed your ideas, not all of it. Wrong context, my bad for not being clear on that. Honestly though, I don't see a need for it at all. Not a bit. I could give a rat's ass if Mages and Changelings and Prometheans, oh my, have things that hide their overt strangeness. Werewolves have their own; it's called adopting Hishu form. Changelings don't look properly human anymore by and large; Prometheans either however they don't have a built in way to shapechange to hide that, so, they've got their effects.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? Change shape, problem pretty much solved. Hell, you can get away with Urhan in many instances. There's nothing stopping Lodges dedicated to keeping things hush hush from existing. There's nothing stopping Fetishes and Talens made to do so. Hell, there's nothing stopping purchased powers that do. Instead, they get a built in dodge.<br /> <br /> Also, your conflating way too much into what I said. But if you're going to argue from the POV that people in the WoD haven't always had an increased level of complacency for, well centuries at least if not longer, I'm going to call BS there. There's been ongoing forces in the setting for as far as can be told... likely all of human history except some really, really ancient times. Perhaps in the glory days with supernatural being overt way back into near pre-history, but otherwise? It's been that way for centuries at least. If not millennia, multiple millenia. &quot;Now&quot; and &quot;Modern&quot; has for a very long time in the setting also been &quot;Then&quot;. Feel free to point out where this watermark you seem to be holding onto is, however, because it sure as hell isn't the Inquisition (which was more of a &quot;wait, what, this shit IS real?&quot; anyhow in some smaller cultural scale instances rather than ongoing awareness).<br /> <br /> The world isn't our world; it's a distorted reflection of it. It's a place riddled with supernatural strangeness, un-events, events rewritten into reality, supernatural conspiracies and active grand forces at play behind the scenes. The entire setting is coloured by that; trying to pretend that somehow human history existed in a vacuum in the setting, and that lack of human awareness is a modern contrivance, I don't think so. There have been tent-poles in many historical Wod setting nods but you're having to go back pretty damn far before you start hitting upon a general stark shift rather than isolated cultural nods.<br /> <br /> Humans have been duped for an excessively long time and that's been written into the setting more than once, in more than one game line. That's not an assumption; that's taking material from various game lines that present things like The Lie and others having been around for a very, very long time. I could ignore that, say &quot;nope, not the case because it's not what I want to run with&quot;, sure, but I'm not going to say &quot;And then there hasn't been these organizations, and hasn't been active efforts to hide the supernatural for a very long time&quot; when it's been repeatedly referenced in historical contexts within the games. That's a long span of recorded history alone that's had that notion in place.<br /> <br /> As for antagonists that don't give a shit about humans... since when? The primary threat Shartha pose is predicated commonly on the use of humans. Ridden? Same thing. Turning areas nasty to cultivate more essence? Generally runs by the influence of humans as well given their the best vehicles to do so in, well most instances with how readily they alter the material world with ease. The Pure? That's where it gets wishy washy outside of breeding stock; then again I wouldn't place any of them as not really giving a shit about humans either. I've no clue where that's coming from unless your solely using Idigam as an example for that given their presentations so far hasn't put too heavy of an interest in them and humanity as a whole, and even then it's not really that supported as an absolute. Most of their issues that Forsaken tangle with are specifically -when- their mess with humans.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to agree to disagree here on quite a few points I suppose. The vinculum is a piss-poor way to keep things hush hush compared to Lunacy, but very good in other areas as far as useful tools assuming you can actually get the person to repeatedly drink from you. It takes investment of their prime resource in Vitae, it takes time, and it takes effort before it has enough effect that you're just going to be able to get a human to shut up without applying other leverage.<br /> <br /> The werewolf? What effort? Change forms. Lunacy automatically pops off. Done unless you run into a rare exception. Once again the difference is effort; werewolves get an easy-mode button. The vampire has to take an active effort, the werewolf has to do shit all. Changelings are just flat-out fucked up at all times, and Sleepers messing with Mage Arcana is an essential part of the setting and played into a few areas above and beyond &quot;They need some means for people to not always remember funky magic effects&quot; when it comes to the Abyss, the Quiescence and more. This is why I said it was a poor comparison, and I'm standing by that.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you're being more hostile than necessary because I just don't happen to agree with you on a point (the necessity of Lunacy given I agree on other aspects). It's not a &quot;neener neener I can't hear you&quot; at all. Only a small portion of the post was even directed at you at all, and that's my bad for not clarifying that. If it was me disregarding you, I wouldn't reading what you say, and putting the effort into a beefy post that, even if I disagree at least on some points (I agree with you on the idea Lunacy needs to be altered; I'm just thoroughly of the mind it's excision is just as good a way of doing it). I'm reading what your saying and either misunderstanding what you're trying to present, or disagreeing with it, but I'm doing anything but brushing it off or trivializing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-12-2013, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:22:48-08:00","id":8714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8575#post8575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of 'Plot Hooks', they're not going anywhere; Lunacy is just tacked-on redundancy that does more storyline harm than good in my eyes when it comes to humans becoming threats. Rather than leaving that yep, shit can hit the fan without some bogged down mechanic marginalizing and mitigating that potential until it becomes fairly damn trivial (wasn't it you, Strider who stated that after 8 years of running Cam games for werewolf, you had all of -two- meaningful breaches that weren't white-washed by Lunacy, enough to call for Harmony checks? Or am I thinking another user on the old forums?), instead we get werewolf 'easy mode'.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may well have been me, given how much Werewolf stuff I ran or oversaw in the Cam/MES.<br /> <br /> However, I don't see &quot;players actually being careful so they don't breach the Oath of the Moon&quot; as a justifiable position behind &quot;get rid of Lunacy.&quot; One does not imply the other. All it means is that the players that were most frequently in my view (which I'll admit was a relatively small percentage of the whole, even if it was still a significant number) were actually smart in how they played. Now, had there been something that would have gone huge, it would have had to come up the Approvals Chain to me, and I never saw that, so I suppose it would be fair to say that a widespread break never happened. I still don't see that as justification for removing Lunacy.<br /> <br /> Quite apart from that, I also see Lunacy as something that can be easily ignored if you don't like it. As such, I don't really get this crusade to remove it - all that does it takes it away from the folks who do like it, and that's something I can't really get behind.<br /> <br /> Would I like to see Lunacy changed? Yes. In fact, based on how the system works now, it almost has to be changed just to fit better within the new rules structure. I'm posting before heading out to work shortly, but later this evening I'll dig up what notes I'd written in regards to Lunacy and post 'em.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:38:41-08:00","id":8720,"title":"","content":"I'd definitely love to see them. The work being put on Predatory Aura's I have going is fine and well, but I'd definitely prefer to see what others have came up that may work better (or at least, get the brain juices flowing in a new direction.)<br /> <br /> For the record, it's less of a crusade to have it gone wholesale (I just wouldn't lament it's loss if it was), and more of wanting the -memory wipe- gone on my end (something that may have been lost in my rambles). I could have it entirely absent in all ways and suffer nothing for it's exclusion.<br /> <br /> As is, I'd rather have something taken from the Blood and Smoke auras as inspiration to provide a nifty effect to reinforce some werewolf themes rather than nothing at all to reinforce things. Besides, Predatory Auras are active rather than passive and pretty damn nifty; few players pass up having another toolset to play around with if it's implemented well. Being made to feel like prey as something of a targeted effect? Awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:34:23-08:00","id":8836,"title":"","content":"Tatter: So, how does your predatory auras work, exactly? It can't be a direct copy from the B&amp;S one, since apparently, it affects Mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T08:48:19-08:00","id":8845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8720#post8720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, it's less of a crusade to have it gone wholesale (I just wouldn't lament it's loss if it was), and more of wanting the -memory wipe- gone on my end (something that may have been lost in my rambles). I could have it entirely absent in all ways and suffer nothing for it's exclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you would. You'd have to completly rewrite Gifts like Mask of Rage and Primal Howl. Since, you know. they allow you to weaponize Lunacy and if you remove it then these Gifts become usless. If you have such a write up for these Gifts so they don't get screwed over, I'd love to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:05:24-08:00","id":8855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8836#post8836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tatter: So, how does your predatory auras work, exactly? It can't be a direct copy from the B&amp;S one, since apparently, it affects Mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Predatory Aura from Requiem now effects humans, is an active supernatural ability also.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:26:56-08:00","id":9098,"title":"","content":"Man, I can't wait to see what the devs have cooked up for us. Because this thread definitely proves I'd rather see their ideas than the general fanbase. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:10:27-08:00","id":9166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8563#post8563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personal opinion, but that sounds just as much as, if not more of, a &quot;fail-safe&quot; than Lunacy is at present. And without any potentially crippling mental disorders on top of it. To me, that sounds like Lunacy, but weaker and watered-down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difference between the two is this: for one what i mentioned is something real and is not magic (spiritual power, fairy dust, whatever) so its part of the world arround us, it feel natural and it makes sense when you think about it. On the other hand Lunacy feels like a very convenient magic solution for a problem that naturally solves itself. It feels fake and forcer, of course this i just say its my personal opinion.<br /> <br /> But personal views about a mechanic aside i agree with you, if lunacy is in the New New werewolf it should remain as modular as it is now so people who enjoy it can have it and those who dont can remove it without much problem. Though im surprise the lenght people go to defending this mechanic and even saying is a integral part of the game as a whole when its occupy the same part of the game that &quot;vampires dont reflect well in mirrors&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8570#post8570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the setting and baseline assumptions would be very different if there wasn't some level of protection. This continually ignores the point that the world was not always so skeptical in regards to what someone has seen. People believed in things once upon a time. I mean look at witch hunts, people digging up corpses to stake them and such. These things were believed once upon a time even without their existence. In a world where such things do exist, its hard to believe that this would still be the case if there wasn't some manner of supernatural protection, large scale infrastructure or general capability for memory alteration.<br /> <br /> Hell the vinculum is a powerful masquerade holding tool, even when it potentially threatens it. Its basically innate mind control.<br /> <br /> A setting is built upon a history, even if its set on modern nights, there are some things that make it difficult to have it as essentially our modern world with modern assumptions about the supernatural if the lack of evidence wasn't there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with the &quot;in the dark ages....:&quot; argument is the following. With lunacy as it is now it wouldn't make any sense for a werewolf to even be killed during the witch hunts. As my previous example before, lets say that a very VERY unfortunate werewolf just transform himself in front of the one guy in his village of 30 with high enough willpower to remember it and somehow such guy manage to convince a mob to get him.<br /> <br /> Thats a classic scenario, the humans form a mob and kill you. However such scenario wouldn't fly because when the mob comes, the werewolf transform and everyone, but the one guy with willpower high enough, run and or assume the fetal position and that poor bastard gets mauled to death.<br /> <br /> But lets say that lunacy does not exist and the mob indeed kill the werewolf, you would think the secret is out but that wouldnt be the case. The village contact a person of authority from a nearby city. Such person of authority comes, this person is well educated or at least he thinks he is and he has to hear the rambling of lowly farmers or villagers talking about a &quot;monster&quot; so they describe the monster to this authority man and he ask to see the body. But all they can show is the body of a normal human (because there is still those other failsafes that the body of a werewolf resumes human form, even if you rip his arm and the werewolf is still alive) so the authority figure doesnt have any proof of the &quot;werewolf&quot; more than the rambling of villagers and a human cadaver. <br /> <br /> So lets say that during the witch hunts of all the people who died because of prosecution a way WAY too generous 5% where true supernaturals, even when they die they dont leave behind any proof behind so thats why i think even in the &quot;witch hunts&quot; the lunacy is not necessary for the setting to sustain itself.<br /> <br /> Even more, maybe those few deaths during the witch hunts accelerate/necessitate the creations of lodges to protect the furry masquerade. And your assumption that the other supernaturals doesnt care if the secret is out for the other species is not necessary true. Remember the game &quot;Vampire Bloodlines&quot;? There one quest from the prince to recover werewolf blood before it could be analize.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T14:15:43-08:00","id":9174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9098#post9098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I can't wait to see what the devs have cooked up for us. Because this thread definitely proves I'd rather see their ideas than the general fanbase. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know, i personally wish Tatterdemalion king and Claire Redfield join in super awesome team to make the New New Werewolf. I would pay for that game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously Taatterdemalion, go make your own werewolf game. I would buy that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:22:14-08:00","id":9230,"title":"","content":"I personally would pay to keep him from it. Claire certainly, but I don't feel you and Tatterdemalion's crusade against all forms of Lunacy to be in the interest of the game. I think SOME measure of memory loss is necessary. In the real world we didn't have evidence because there was none. In the World of Darkness, there was. There were even experts on these various things. Likely the <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Malleus Maleficarum was an </b></span></span> active group that likely did the investigations back then... and it was beneficial for the church to have people believe.<br /> <br /> You had people who travelled and sold trinkets to prevent those fears. The 'educated' were exceptionally rare, and likely officials sent to investigate would, like in our world, bring back reports as stated. There are documents when literacy was even rare, documenting cases of werewolves. Even after the Printing Press there were newspapers that had mentions of vampires being staked. Even the educated believed during much of history. Its only been in about the last 200 years that people have really backed away from folkloric beliefs.<br /> <br /> Again I feel Lunacy as-is is too much, but I feel some memory loss or other protection is necessary for suspension of disbelief in regards to why people don't believe in werewolves. Prometheans only display what they are in rare occasions, and on top of that are extremely rare themselves. Changelings have a powerful magic that protects their true forms from even intense medical examinations. They may be 'odd' but they're hardly supernatural. Their entire society is heavily influenced by hiding as well.<br /> <br /> Despite what others think, the vinculum is a heavy handed and easily applied capability that basically mimics &quot;conditioning&quot; dominate power in some ways. It makes an obedient servant. Then there's the protections against being identified (which may have undergone some changes to make it less overtly supernatural). Vampires also have the ability to basically turn their bodies on as well.<br /> <br /> Lunacy needs toned down, but getting rid of it entirely and saying the world is as it is today, but werewolves are real and people throughout time have probably seen them often (especially in the case of death rage which I'm sure was far more common in past eras as well) but nobody really believes is silly at best, and bordering on Absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:53:43-08:00","id":9307,"title":"","content":"To go along with what Rani is saying about older times and Lunacy, this is actually addressed in War Against the Pure. It states that in older times, like the Dark Ages, Lunacy wasn't as potent because people were more open minded or superstitious. This was mechanically shown with bonuses to Willpower for persons of that time. So, Rani's point is very viable and I agree with it, based on what I've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:37:26-08:00","id":9385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9230#post9230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would pay to keep him from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>uhh we could make a bidding war!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and use the funds of each to pay for the new new werewolf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9230#post9230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunacy needs toned down, but getting rid of it entirely and saying the world is as it is today, but werewolves are real and people throughout time have probably seen them often (especially in the case of death rage which I'm sure was far more common in past eras as well) but nobody really believes is silly at best, and bordering on Absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>i guess we have to agree to disagree there. To me the idea of a power that memory wipes is absurd and just cut many history hooks. And neither i or tatterdalion are saying it should be remove from the game. I just say its unnecessary and i remove it from the my games like a evil tumor but it should be keep for the people who like it and it should remains as modular as it is now. Tatterdalion is saying that it could be changed to predatory aura. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:42:45-08:00","id":9389,"title":"","content":"You know what? I entirely forgot about that reference; I've not been through War Against the Pure beyond it's alternate shifter section for quite some time. If one uses the Babylon chronicle from the Chronicler's guide I think there's some additional ideas there (been a while, haven't ran it), but I -think- that was due to the Ziggurat more than the nature of the world at the time.Could be mistaken there. On the flip-side that's less &quot;The Modern Mind&quot; and more &quot;Cultural expectations color Lunacy&quot; to me; a highly superstitious culture in this era would have the same bonuses with Lunacy as is (and if it didn't, there'd have to be one damn good explanation beyond &quot;Luna did it&quot; for me to buy into it), and they certainly still do exist. It may be easier to divide things less beyond time periods and more regarding cultural assumptions because there still is a heavy amount of variance. <br /> <br /> Then again, how would this be reflected (or even be relevant) with an altered &quot;Lunacy&quot; and -would- it be necessary? If Lunacy is still around, what form does it take? We've got a lot of ideas on what we don't want; the current potency, but not much on mechanical replacements. There's some nod to it in my Instincts overhaul post, but it's not really where I want it to be yet. At least in the form where it messes up memory in any way; I don't like outright wipes, but I don't mind terror making it hard to clearly remember events in the form of penalties to an extent, but certainly not in an un-targetted group effect that automatically pops off. <br /> <br /> There could be room to make their predatory be a group affect to reflect a panicking herd, mind you using the same basic mechanical assumptions; but if it had that level of broad effect, I'd be hard pressed to give it the potency and duration of the Vampire Predatory Auras. There may be a way to present werewolves as being more overall brute force terror (hitting a group of witnesses) to separate it more from the more subtle insidious thing vampires have, though it could use quite a bit more additional thought, it's something I've been mulling over the past few days and want to get a functional system to test run within the next few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:53:10-08:00","id":9392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9389#post9389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, how would this be reflected (or even be relevant) with an altered &quot;Lunacy&quot; and -would- it be necessary? If Lunacy is still around, what form does it take? We've got a lot of ideas on what we don't want; the current potency, but not much on mechanical replacements. There's some nod to it in my Instincts overhaul post, but it's not really where I want it to be yet. At least in the form where it messes up memory in any way; I don't like outright wipes, but I don't mind terror making it hard to clearly remember events in the form of penalties to an extent, but certainly not in an un-targetted group effect that automatically pops off.<br /> <br /> There could be room to make their predatory be a group affect to reflect a panicking herd, mind you using the same basic mechanical assumptions; but if it had that level of broad effect, I'd be hard pressed to give it the potency and duration of the Vampire Predatory Auras. There may be a way to present werewolves as being more overall brute force terror (hitting a group of witnesses) to separate it more from the more subtle insidious thing vampires have, though it could use quite a bit more additional thought, it's something I've been mulling over the past few days and want to get a functional system to test run within the next few.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about this? maybe when there is a group instead of New New lunacy pushing the flee response it could push the fight response so a werewolf just going full gauru risk the mob coming after him and be force to make a blood bath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T19:48:20-08:00","id":9417,"title":"","content":"Now I would love for a more active version to be implemented. I just don't like it so idly dismissed. I think some memory alteration is necessary. Vampires predatory aura is one based on being predators among themselves and humans. While I'm not sure what the duration is against humans, they can easily be waited out by young kindred, then there are condition immunities after. Predatory Aura for vampires are not subtle, its like invoking frenzy but limiting it to body language and a glare or glance.<br /> <br /> If I were to do something, I'd break it into similar concepts, but give conditions associated with werewolves. While Challenging and Beastial aura's are appropriate, Seductive may not be, perhaps a &quot;Lunacy&quot; aura in its stead or &quot;Hunter's&quot; aura. Such could be used to invoke the memory altering persistent condition, those associated with dramatic failure of an Integrity roll may be very appropriate.<br /> <br /> Now one thing I'd like to see is that it wouldn't be a single-target effect like it would for vampires, but perhaps something that can be invoked against multiples at once. I can just see the prospective alpha unleashing a challenging aura against all his packmates at once, asserting a level of dominance over them and inspiring them to give their all for the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T20:25:05-08:00","id":9437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=8720#post8720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd definitely love to see them. The work being put on Predatory Aura's I have going is fine and well, but I'd definitely prefer to see what others have came up that may work better (or at least, get the brain juices flowing in a new direction.)<br /> <br /> For the record, it's less of a crusade to have it gone wholesale (I just wouldn't lament it's loss if it was), and more of wanting the -memory wipe- gone on my end (something that may have been lost in my rambles). I could have it entirely absent in all ways and suffer nothing for it's exclusion.<br /> <br /> As is, I'd rather have something taken from the Blood and Smoke auras as inspiration to provide a nifty effect to reinforce some werewolf themes rather than nothing at all to reinforce things. Besides, Predatory Auras are active rather than passive and pretty damn nifty; few players pass up having another toolset to play around with if it's implemented well. Being made to feel like prey as something of a targeted effect? Awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, fun fact: I'm an idiot.<br /> <br /> I swore I had written down my ideas for Lunacy, but I suppose I didn't. I think I discussed them with someone on gchat a while back, but I'm not digging through chat archives to find them. Or at least, not the chat archives with that person, as there are a lot of messages in there. <br /> <br /> Instead, I did find my initial rework of Primal Urge and the Predator's Menace that I then made pretty(ish) so that folks could read it. I'll link it here, and I'll try to work up some Lunacy stuff in the next few days, as soon as I get less busy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxKbdf9Oylg_T2JDT0ZPRTFydU0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxKbdf9Oylg_T2JDT0ZPRTFydU0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxKbdf9Oylg_T2JDT0ZPRTFydU0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxKbdf9Oylg_T2JDT0ZPRTFydU0/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T20:33:42-08:00","id":9441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9166#post9166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Difference between the two is this: for one what i mentioned is something real and is not magic (spiritual power, fairy dust, whatever) so its part of the world arround us, it feel natural and it makes sense when you think about it. On the other hand Lunacy feels like a very convenient magic solution for a problem that naturally solves itself. It feels fake and forcer, of course this i just say its my personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>We may just have to agree to disagree. Personally, if I would witness an 8- or 9-foot tall supernatural wolf-man-monster-thing doing something terrible/obviously supernatural/etc, I think I'd really prefer to forget it - ideally without a weekend of binge drinking. Might be just me, I dunno. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9166#post9166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But personal views about a mechanic aside i agree with you, if lunacy is in the New New werewolf it should remain as modular as it is now so people who enjoy it can have it and those who dont can remove it without much problem. Though im surprise the lenght people go to defending this mechanic and even saying is a integral part of the game as a whole when its occupy the same part of the game that &quot;vampires dont reflect well in mirrors&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I suspect - and let me point out that I am not on the team to develop or write anything (although man would that be awesome, so if anyone knows the right combination of items to sacrifice to make that happen, by all means share) - that there will be refocusing of various things, the major rules will remain. So Lunacy, Renown, Harmony, shapeshifting, Gifts, and so on I expect to remain, although perhaps they may well, and probably will, behave in a manner differently than they do at present.<br /> <br /> I could be wrong, but I think that there won't be any huge revisions done. Just like B&amp;S is recognizably <i>Vampire: the Requiem</i> (albeit with new and/or refocused portions of setting and/or mechanics), I suspect that the <i>Idigam Chronicle</i> will be recognizable as Werewolf: the Forsaken as currently written.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:33:13-08:00","id":9674,"title":"","content":"I see there's quite a debate going on here, and frankly WoD werewolves have never really clicked for me, so I doubt they will in their GMC incarnation - but it seems like Lunacy could be replaced with/turned into bonuses to triggering Breaking Points, and a note saying that Amnesia is a common resulting Condition for these Breaking Points (remember that &quot;what have you forgotten&quot; question?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:48:01-08:00","id":9731,"title":"","content":"The problem with it doing it through breaking points only is that its much easier to succeed at breaking points even with a penalty than it was to succeed at morality loss. Conditions on breaking points only result on failure(minor conditions) and dramatic failure(conditions including one that has memory loss).<br /> <br /> That has been my main opposition to the &quot;No breaking points do that.&quot; argument. They simply don't except on a DRAMATIC FAILURE. Werewolves do not have large scale infrastructures to keep them hidden like other supernaturals. They're largely isolated groups. They need SOMETHING that helps them in that department.<br /> <br /> I think an active predatory aura mechanic, which was even mentioned as possible in the B&amp;S predatory aura notes, that resulted in some of those conditions would be more suitable. Also, this needs to be from the perspective of PC humans interacting with werewolves as well. If its done with only breaking points, then you can expect that players will rapidly lose integrity when interacting or potentially fighting werewolves,<br /> <br /> There needs to be a balance between the two. I think an active effect is effective, and less punishing to PC humans, while also potentially protecting Werewolves in a way that would make it believable that people didn't BELIEVE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:23:07-08:00","id":9758,"title":"","content":"Apply a penalty to Breaking Points (likely based on the form the Uratha took), and failures are considered dramatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:30:28-08:00","id":9761,"title":"","content":"I'd also rather had it became something that is actively used by the Uratha rather than a pasive effect it has on onlookers. This way the roll could be tweaked against the humans (say, rolling Composure alone).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:43:28-08:00","id":9825,"title":"","content":"You could just have it be a willpower roll. Dramatic failure, temporary severe derangement, failure, temporary derangement, both with added amnesia or focus on wolves, success just accept it as a figment of imagination (or you saw something but hey no big deal) or hoax, exceptional success you saw a werewolf there's no denying it you could identify them in a lineup.<br /> As an added benefit since one of the first complaints (I saw) about lunacy was that it negated the human threat could be that Luna doesn't extend her protection to the Pure, so no lunacy for them. This could correspond to a bonus to willpower in regards to resisting Lunacy by those who have been exposed to the Pure. That way the people most likely to encounter the Pure, either catspaws, voyeurs or werewolf hunters, would have an advantage in spotting Forsake. And there you have a mortal threat.<br /> You could also have people exposed to Lunacy multiple times build up a similar resistance. <br /> <br /> Personally, I like Lunacy. I don't believe it should be as strict as it is, but the idea of Luna covering up for her wolves makes sense (perhaps only at night?). That said I think the changes from GMC have been more about lessening dependence on mechanics and opening things up to more storytelling opportunities (for both sides, players and storytellers), and whatever changes are done should be in line with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:34:56-08:00","id":9987,"title":"","content":"Technically, an Integrity roll is already a Willpower roll (it uses Resolve+Composure).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:49:06-08:00","id":10306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=9987#post9987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, an Integrity roll is already a Willpower roll (it uses Resolve+Composure).</div> </div> </div> </div>But an Umanity roll isn't, B&amp;S spoiler wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:31:02-08:00","id":10319,"title":"","content":"Good point, and that could be against &quot;just let the Integrity(or equivalent) trait handle it&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> EDIT: unless,of course, that Lunacy should only afect mortals. I can't remember, did it affect other supernaturals like Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-14-2013, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:04:44-08:00","id":10355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=10319#post10319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point, and that could be against &quot;just let the Integrity(or equivalent) trait handle it&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> EDIT: unless,of course, that Lunacy should only afect mortals. I can't remember, did it affect other supernaturals like Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Supernaturals were excluded. Actually, depending on which splat one is talking about, the lesser templates (ghouls, etc) are sometimes excluded as well. At least, that's how I've always seen it run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:53:49-08:00","id":10371,"title":"","content":"Even Mages? They are basically human despite magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:09:21-08:00","id":10413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=10371#post10371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Mages? They are basically human despite magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakened Souls and all that jazz, too, though. I'd say if a Ghoul counts, so does a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:44:24-08:00","id":10507,"title":"","content":"If its made into an Aura, I'd like to see it useful against other werewolves, and other supernaturals (And I'm hoping vampire predatory Aura is useful against them as well, but I've got a thread up on vampire forums asking about that currently.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T17:20:46-08:00","id":10925,"title":"","content":"That was my default assumption modelling after the Predatory Aura of Blood and Smoke; it affects other supernaturals as well as humans, the idea would be that you could have a werewolf (or pack with some tinkering) that could get into dominance conflicts via the aura on who are the bigger badasses. That said, this is why I'm a bit iffy on a werewolf getting a group aura; the default assumption is that they're running in a pack (single player and crossover games are usually considered the exception not the rule after all); if they all have the ability innately, little is stopping each of them from doing it on selected targets.<br /> <br /> That being said, I could see there being a mechanic to reflect using Predatory Aura as a fully-fledged pack that amps things up; one roll using the highest of the packs rating perhaps against selected targets? Something where numbers increase it further? As folks are quick to point out; a lone werewolf is frightening; a pack of them is terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T00:50:21-08:00","id":11106,"title":"","content":"I'll just use the teamwork rules, a Primary actor that does the roll, and the others give bonuses to it if they succeed theirs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:12:15-08:00","id":11291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=10413#post10413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakened Souls and all that jazz, too, though. I'd say if a Ghoul counts, so does a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I always thought was weird. Even if it's a minor supernatural template, Lunacy has no effect on them. By all accounts, this means Sleepwalkers are immune too. Hell, if a character has a Psychic Merit, they should also be immune. But, Wolf-blooded aren't immune, they just get a bonus. Why? They're a supernatural template, right? Shouldn't they be immune too? It's just something that never made much sense to me and I hope in the Idigam Chronicle this gets cleaned up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:17:40-08:00","id":11295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11291#post11291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which I always thought was weird. Even if it's a minor supernatural template, Lunacy has no effect on them. By all accounts, this means Sleepwalkers are immune too. Hell, if a character has a Psychic Merit, they should also be immune. But, Wolf-blooded aren't immune, they just get a bonus. Why? They're a supernatural template, right? Shouldn't they be immune too? It's just something that never made much sense to me and I hope in the Idigam Chronicle this gets cleaned up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunacy as a curse-blessing from Luna that manifests in werewolves in part through the incentive against pack-bonding to a Lune may have something to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:58:23-08:00","id":11317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11291#post11291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which I always thought was weird. Even if it's a minor supernatural template, Lunacy has no effect on them. By all accounts, this means Sleepwalkers are immune too. Hell, if a character has a Psychic Merit, they should also be immune. But, Wolf-blooded aren't immune, they just get a bonus. Why? They're a supernatural template, right? Shouldn't they be immune too? It's just something that never made much sense to me and I hope in the Idigam Chronicle this gets cleaned up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I never ran it like this. I actually did the opposite and let it affect <b>everybody</b>, but the splats got to add their respective Power Stats to their Willpower for the purpose of determining where they landed. This meant more powerful ones would brush it off, but Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded, Sleepwalkers, etc got no special advantages.<br /> <br /> EDIT: forgot, I dropped the bonuses for Dalu and Urshul. Lunacy is Lunacy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 11-15-2013, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:03:47-08:00","id":11693,"title":"","content":"Sleepwalkers aren't a minor template; nor Wolf-blooded are. They're merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:07:57-08:00","id":11700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11693#post11693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepwalkers aren't a minor template; nor Wolf-blooded are. They're merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merits <i>that only mortals can have.</i><br /> <br /> Merits <i>that go away when you get a major template.</i><br /> <br /> Merits <i>whose holders are treated as a separate class of entity by several game mechanics.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T19:56:01-08:00","id":11806,"title":"","content":"If I take Unseen Sense that means I'm a minor template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T20:12:28-08:00","id":11814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11806#post11806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I take Unseen Sense that means I'm a minor template?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't read more than two lines of a post I'm not sure what you're doing on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T20:14:52-08:00","id":11818,"title":"","content":"No, but some minor templates get Unseen Sense associated with the particular type of supernatural splat they are affiliated with. Your character would lose that ability if turned into one of the major splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T20:19:55-08:00","id":11822,"title":"","content":"If you use the Wolf Blooded rules from Blood of the Wolf they become a minor template, not just a merit. A psychic is considered a minor template, as another example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T21:15:49-08:00","id":11868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11317#post11317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I never ran it like this. I actually did the opposite and let it affect <b>everybody</b>, but the splats got to add their respective Power Stats to their Willpower for the purpose of determining where they landed. This meant more powerful ones would brush it off, but Ghouls, Wolf-Blooded, Sleepwalkers, etc got no special advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's likely the best way to do it, yeah.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T07:02:02-08:00","id":12039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=11818#post11818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but some minor templates get Unseen Sense associated with the particular type of supernatural splat they are affiliated with. Your character would lose that ability if turned into one of the major splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote where it say they are. And I'm not including Proximi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:05:21-08:00","id":12139,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see an overhaul of the Gift list in a big way. I would like to see, in roughly this order:<br /> <br /> 1. Fewer bullshit loopholes in Gifts. Besides making the Gift less useful, it makes it harder to remember how it works and requires more look-ups. Can I Detect Acorns three times per day or five times per day? Well, let me go look it up and bring the game to a screeching halt. If it's not an important enough detail to bother stopping the game and looking it up, then why the Hell is it even in the book? I really would prefer we avoid times per day restrictions, form restrictions, and target restrictions unless they really make sense.<br /> <br /> 2. Fewer bullshit scales. I see a lot of powers that go bullshit-bullshit-kinda useful-bullshit-OP as fuck. Yeah, I get the purchasing plan, but Promethean manages to do the same thing with half the bloat and nearly none of the crap powers. If you want to keep jumping to the head of the line expensive, fine, but don't make it feel like a punishment to go the long way.<br /> <br /> 3. More consistent design. Mummy is pretty consistent in it's effects which makes it easier to remember how an effect works. Gifts are all over the map. Let's have a tad more structure.<br /> <br /> 4. If Renown stays tied to Gifts, I'd like a given Renown type associated directly with a Gift list rather than with separate Gifts. For example, all Strength list Gifts are Glory Gifts, all Evasion Gifts are Cunning Gifts, etcetera. On the metagame level, it would make combinations easier and clear without a lot of flipping back and forth and planning. I also think it would help round out more about what a given splat is about depending on what Renown is associated with their affiliated Gift lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:15:18-08:00","id":12149,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to see how Essence is gained change. StephenLS said many years ago touching magic rocks was dumb, and he's not wrong. This is how I would like to see it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Moon:</b> Each night, when you call to the moon, you get a point of Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Territory:</b> Your pack, if you have one, holds a territory. Each dawn that begins with your pack still holding that territory, every member of the pack gains a number of essence depending on the size and occult features of that territory; some will be worth more than others.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Hunting:</b> Smaller, weaker spirits - those below your Rank - can be hunted and consumed for Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Bargains: </b>You can trade favors to spirits in exchange for Essence directly. Favors should be weird, difficult, or dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pack</b>: You should be able to freely share Essence with other members of a bonded Pack.<br /> <br /> Personally, i think these would be more interesting than the current set-up. If it results in too much Essence floating around, some methods can e reduced or Essence costs can simply be increased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:17:15-08:00","id":12151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=12039#post12039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quote where it say they are. And I'm not including Proximi.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/unseensenseminortemplate1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T13:34:57-08:00","id":12274,"title":"","content":"Wrong quote, my bad. I meant: Where does it it says non-proximi or Blooded are minor templates, hmm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T13:52:01-08:00","id":12278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=12274#post12274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong quote, my bad. I meant: Where does it it says non-proximi or Blooded are minor templates, hmm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Incoherent question with an annoying &quot;huh, huh?&quot; tacked on the end gets no consideration.<br /> <br /> Imperial Mysteries is pretty much the only book that tackles the concept of &quot;templates&quot; as an in-book thing rather than a fandom shorthand, and the qualification it gives for &quot;lesser templates&quot; is &quot;supernatural beings that lack a central 'power' trait, <b>such as ghouls, wolf-blooded or Proximi.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> Being that even non-Proximus Sleepwalkers are treated differently by a number of effects and Sleepwalker is a prerequisite for Proximus, you should probably just let it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T14:37:46-08:00","id":12300,"title":"","content":"No, the concept of minor template is addressed in Second Sight first. And in no material Wolf-Blooded are treated as such. Point in fact: You can't have multiple minor templates, yet you can be a Wolfblooded Shaman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T15:13:28-08:00","id":12322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=12300#post12300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the concept of minor template is addressed in Second Sight first. And in no material Wolf-Blooded are treated as such. Point in fact: You can't have multiple minor templates, yet you can be a Wolfblooded Shaman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation, please, because literally the only place &quot;wolf-blooded&quot; shows up in Second Sight is in the description for Mind Control, the word &quot;wolfblooded&quot; doesn't show up at all, and the only uses of &quot;wolf&quot; are to refer to White Wolf, Wolf Messings, werewolves, and the aforesaid power description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-16-2013, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T20:29:04-08:00","id":13147,"title":"","content":"You know, something I'd like to see is more threats from the physical side of the Gauntlet. Not just things like Spirit sorcerers and such, but something like an organization that has it out for the Uratha.<br /> <br /> One such group already exists in Forsaken, technically. In War Against the Pure, there's this group called Operation Twelfth Night which knows the Uratha are out there. But instead of blowing the whistle, they seek to control the Uratha and try to exploit them as another natural resource, basically trying to make the Uratha into weapons. Honestly, I'd love to see these guys get some better treatment and made into a more common threat for the Forsaken. Or at least, something like them. And don't anybody say The Cheiron Group! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T07:57:44-08:00","id":13396,"title":"","content":"\u201cWolf-Blooded\u201d is presented as a Merit that reduces an impediment to interacting with werewolves, not as a template. Compare <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Sleepwalker Merit, and contrast <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Proximus template (which was, admittedly, originally presented as a Merit; but that was back when it had virtually no mechanics associated with it). Also compare with Enchanted Mortal and contrast with Fae-Touched: nWoD has a precedent for handling mortals who can \u201cpierce te veil\u201d that conceals supernaturals from mortal scrutiny by means of a Merit, and handling mortals who have supernatural powers beyond mere perception by means of a lesser template. The closest thing that vampires have to a \u201cveil\u201d is the way that living beings are disabled while a vampire is feeding from them; if there were a <b>Vampire</b> counterpart to the Wolf-Blooded, it would be someone who can (usually or always) fight back while a vampire attempts to feed on him. And the closest counterpart that <b>Werewolf</b> has to a ghoul isn\u2019t a Wolf-Blooded; it\u2019s a Claimed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:25:47-08:00","id":13402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=13396#post13396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And the closest counterpart that <b>Werewolf</b> has to a ghoul isn\u2019t a Wolf-Blooded; it\u2019s a Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me leans towards the Skin Thieves over the Claimed. <br /> <br /> Hell, the entire book might as well be part of the Werewolf line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:34:36-08:00","id":13406,"title":"","content":"It was, same as Slashers was a Hunter book but both were repurposed as Blue Books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:51:07-08:00","id":13416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=13396#post13396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cWolf-Blooded\u201d is presented as a Merit that reduces an impediment to interacting with werewolves, not as a template. Compare <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Sleepwalker Merit, and contrast <b>Mage</b>\u2019s Proximus template (which was, admittedly, originally presented as a Merit; but that was back when it had virtually no mechanics associated with it). Also compare with Enchanted Mortal and contrast with Fae-Touched: nWoD has a precedent for handling mortals who can \u201cpierce te veil\u201d that conceals supernaturals from mortal scrutiny by means of a Merit, and handling mortals who have supernatural powers beyond mere perception by means of a lesser template. The closest thing that vampires have to a \u201cveil\u201d is the way that living beings are disabled while a vampire is feeding from them; if there were a <b>Vampire</b> counterpart to the Wolf-Blooded, it would be someone who can (usually or always) fight back while a vampire attempts to feed on him. And the closest counterpart that <b>Werewolf</b> has to a ghoul isn\u2019t a Wolf-Blooded; it\u2019s a Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Blood of the Wolf</b>, Data. It's a goddamn template, unless you feel like arguing that Moon-Puppets and the Baal-Hadad and the parallel example of ghoul families aren't evidence enough that the uragarum are a distinct subset of regular humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-18-2013, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:16:10-08:00","id":13429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=13402#post13402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of me leans towards the Skin Thieves over the Claimed.<br /> <br /> Hell, the entire book might as well be part of the Werewolf line.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s room for more than one. Heck, <b>Skinchangers</b> also includes \u201creverse-Claimed\u201d that are essentially more player-friendly versions of the Claimed. I\u2019d love it if material from that book were refined and integrated into <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> as part of an effort to beef up the threats arising from this side of the Gauntlet (along with sorcerers, Wolf-Bitten<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><sup>1</sup></span>, and Dire Beasts<span style=\"font-size:9px\"><sup>2</sup></span>. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:9px\"><sup>1 </sup><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><u>Wolf-Bitten:</u> mortals who have been bitten by a werewolf and have gained access to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8520-werewolf-the-forsaken-instincts-the-early-incarnation-of-an-overhaul\">Instincts</a> as a result. They\u2019re also more feral than your average human. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\"><sup>2 </sup></span><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><u>Dire Beasts:</u> rare animals that have human-level cleverness (like the Velociraptors from <i>Jurrasic Park</i>), plus Instincts. May or may not be the animal version of the Wolf-Bitten. </span> </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-18-2013, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:58:41-08:00","id":13497,"title":"","content":"We've been playing around with the idea that Wolf-Blooded aren't exactly... well, specifically wolf-orientated at base for our game even if descended from that stock. This may seem a bit oddball but the idea is this; human descendants of werewolf and human matings take on a touch of that spiritual might and heritage themselves; they get some minor benefits (we aren't going to be using lunacy, but they'll get bonuses to resisting the Predatory Aura/Menace and some other tidbits, some things around the same vein as prior though with Unseen Sense etc.), they're definitely more attractive to spirits and they hold more Essence within themselves. Basically, they're people with increased spiritual -potential- rather than say, werewolf potential (though that's part of it). They're wolf-blooded because, go figure, that's who they descend from (for those that use the Baal-Hadad (sp) this may explain why they're of such interest to them) rather than something purely wolf in them. They won't be the guaranteed result of mating, but they won't be rare. Odds are they're are plenty of people walking a city, for instance that all have that potential in them, untapped and unaware beyond how strangeness seems to gravitate to them and vice versa.<br /> <br /> From there, it's the Uratha's bite, claw or something else distinctly intimate and some investiture that catalyses them into becoming werewolves. It doesn't always 'take'; for those that due, their Resonance and spiritual potential brings them into the werewolf fold. Basically it's like a weird, werewolf-style resonance/essence manipulation of sorts. This isn't the default of W:tF obviously, given the bite had a more pragmatic tracking reasoning.<br /> <br /> The reason for this is to make Wolf-Blooded much more important for reasons above and beyond them being your new source of werewolves; they can become other things. In effect, they -all- have the spiritual potential to become funky spirit manipulators or bait. Spirits -will- take an interest in them due to their stronger spiritual imprints and how much more they stand out. Shartha will find them much more delicious and useful. They're more prone to becoming skin-thieves and spirit binders; in all ways, they just have stronger spiritual capabilities available (primarily bought as additional merits). They're also delicious to werewolves given those higher Essence reserves (which with the right merit they can tap into for various effects)... this means that with our setting shift where hunting humans is much more likely to happen, even if not the preferred or accepted norm for many that you need to -watch- your family before something else; spirit, shartha or another werewolf comes calling to see if they'll 'take' as another of their own kind, or simply prey.<br /> <br /> No doubt there are Pure, Ghost Wolves and other Forsaken that may hold animosity towards the Werewolf with her wolf-blooded descendant that would well indeed decide to just off and eat them to land a grievous blow, or 'poach' them and induct them into their own Tribe to turn them on their relative. There's also the issue of your own control; what happens if you get hungry, are low or absent of essence and go into Death Rage around them? They're likely to be your first lunch. What happens if they suffer a 'random' werewolf attack by others, and are catalyzed to change from the trauma? How do the react to you? What if they were a lover of yours, now a werewolf?<br /> <br /> The funky part? Given that latent potential, they could just as easily be catalysed to become something else; never mind Ridden or Shartha bait; other shapeshifters (even if they don't have a strong presence in the setting, we've had one lone individual in our longest running game) may poach them to become like them. That spiritual potential for shapeshifting isn't just orientated to wolves as per my earlier point; it's to -any- shapeshifting. They have by their natures the potential become great allies or great threats to the Uratha; so the Uratha in turn are -very- protective and watchful of their families even if watching from a distance for more reasons than even before. They tend to go weird, and you can bet if the wrong spirit comes around, it's going to try to &quot;guide&quot; them in ways they're not going to appreciate, potentially infecting their Essence with their own Resonance from pacts gone sour and more. We won't even get into what an Idigam might figure out to do with one...<br /> <br /> Sometimes this may not be looked at too askew; a Bone Shadow with a wolf-blooded husband for instance likely won't be surprised if they take on Death-like aspects given her own and her tribes tendency to deal with such spirits for example, nor if he takes a keen interest in spiritual matters related to that when he notices more than the average individual. Perhaps she'll decide to invest him with a bit of her own essence via a &quot;wolf attack&quot; or a vigorous bedroom romp, to see if it 'takes' as another Uratha; a bad idea overall of course given their feelings for one another (and the likely offspring) but, perhaps she will, thinking it will safeguard him further anyhow. Or perhaps she'll find herself coming into conflict if her hubby starts dabbling into skin-thieving rites. Perhaps she'll have trouble because one of the Pure sniffs him out, and takes him (if not leaving him in pieces) as one of their own with the bite. Or worse... something else entirely finds him and he becomes a shapeshifting thing she has no conception of.<br /> <br /> I want there to be a lot more potential with the Wolf-Blooded as a result; obviously more merits they can take to reflect funkier powers (potentially some only 'partially' take, learning select Instincts), but also that, they're prime prey, and prime pickings for others. You can't just be a lay-about with your family and expect everything to be fine with them all; what happens if one turns out to be wolf-blooded and goes down some nasty path and turns on the rest of your family? Hell, you and your pack? I want the temptation to catalyse them into werewolves to be a valid option (and often tragic one) regarding &quot;protecting them&quot;. <br /> <br /> Hopefully this makes sense. It's been quite a bit of brain-storming, but we figured that if Wolf-Blooded were more valuable in general, spiritually (let alone more capable with their own funky supernatural merits etc.) it'd push things further into their importance, whether they change into werewolves or not. Still needs refinement and tweaking, but I figure something -vaguely- ghoul-like regarding a Stamina based Essence reserve and some other things might be a good start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:39:31-08:00","id":13624,"title":"","content":"Moon Puppets are Lune-Claimed. The fact they're perhaps Banned to only choosing Wolf-Blooded as mounts is inconsequential. What about the Baal-Hadad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:42:07-08:00","id":13660,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:darkred\"><b>Please consider the value of common decency before disagreeing someone. We don't mind effective discussion, but flaming people for not being on the same side of an argument is a rules violation.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:08:48-08:00","id":13670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=13624#post13624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moon Puppets are Lune-Claimed. The fact they're perhaps Banned to only choosing Wolf-Blooded as mounts is inconsequential.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Moon-Puppets are intended to showcase the potential of any wolf-blood to become a werewolf, and to demonstrate the inherent connection to the spirit world that even a relative of a werewolf possesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Some wolf-bloods can sense spirits, but all wolf-blooded enable spirits to interact with the physical world by their very presence.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the Baal-Hadad? </div> </div> </div>&quot;The way that the Baal-Hadad truly reproduce themselves is what can most immediately draw them into conflict with the Forsaken. The bull-lords require a wolf-blooded human to reproduce.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T19:27:40-08:00","id":13737,"title":"","content":"Any human can turn into a werewolf. The core-book says so. Either as a whim of Luna who focuses her influences on the helpless victim of her caress, or because, as it's explained there, the blood of Urfarah has since been diluted among every tribe of humanity.<br /> <br /> Baal-Hadad - So?<br /> <br /> It's the same kind of unfortunate circumstances that arrive from single merits as Unseen Senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:28:02-08:00","id":13755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=13737#post13737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any human can turn into a werewolf. The core-book says so. Either as a whim of Luna who focuses her influences on the helpless victim of her caress, or because, as it's explained there, the blood of Urfarah has since been diluted among every tribe of humanity.<br /> <br /> Baal-Hadad - So?<br /> <br /> It's the same kind of unfortunate circumstances that arrive from single merits as Unseen Senses.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/wolfbloodlessertemplate.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/wolfbloodlessertemplaterider.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/sleepwalkerlessertemplate.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Suggestion: Produce actual conclusive evidence (on par with the above explicit statement in Imperial Mysteries to the contrary) that the books do not treat Wolf-Blooded as a template, or else drop the argument so everyone can be spared more of this senseless back-and-forth.<br /> <br /> Prediction: Neither of the above will occur.<br /> <br /> Hope: The above prediction will be proven wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-18-2013, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T07:36:05-08:00","id":14035,"title":"","content":"Suggestion - stop arguing over something so minor, or take it elsewhere<br /> <br /> Prediction - this thread will soon be closed<br /> <br /> Hope - it won't<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway......<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see is revamping the Forsaken and Pure dichotomy as more like rival siblings than out-right hostility, and once that is taken out, up the threat level from the flesh side with human enemies, more emphasis on the Hosts on the flesh side, and more examples of the Claimed making trouble for the Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T07:40:03-08:00","id":14696,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://s718.photobucket.com/user/Ephsy/media/1.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i718.photobucket.com/albums/ww190/Ephsy/1.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"http://s718.photobucket.com/user/Ephsy/media/2.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i718.photobucket.com/albums/ww190/Ephsy/2.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Suggestion - Show me, now, where in any material Wolf-Blooded are defined as template, explicitly.<br /> <br /> Prediction - The above won't occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T08:18:24-08:00","id":14713,"title":"","content":"Did that two pages ago\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=12278#post12278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imperial Mysteries is pretty much the only book that tackles the concept of &quot;templates&quot; as an in-book thing rather than a fandom shorthand, and the qualification it gives for &quot;lesser templates&quot; is &quot;supernatural beings that lack a central 'power' trait, <b>such as ghouls, wolf-blooded or Proximi.</b>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026and you're citing a section talking about how werewolves can't tell if their kids will grow up to be werewolves as proof that the wolf-blooded aren't a template, so I think we're just about done here.<br /> <br /> <br /> One other thing I'm hoping to see is totem rules that can properly account for totems of different Rank, given that the Pure's totems are noted to often be Jagglings and managing that as &quot;treat them as though they instated a ban of at least the worst severity that the corebook puts forth, if not even more severe&quot; is kind of clunky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T09:02:19-08:00","id":14737,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I kinda wish there had been a &quot;Book of Totems&quot; or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:36:50-08:00","id":15143,"title":"","content":"There's a meaty, useful section on totems in Lore of the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:16:35-08:00","id":15458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=15143#post15143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a meaty, useful section on totems in Lore of the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd forgotten. Boy, I wish more people would read that book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:00:16-08:00","id":15553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kaho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=1992#post1992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]That the game takes a stand on wheter the werewolves in a city have a social structure or not. The game now sends mixed signals about it a lot of fluff goes in that every pack it its own island but then you have social rites that work in all werewolves, you have renowns accepted by all werewolf and such.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this a great deal. Some books make it seem that the forsaken packs are at each others throats and that it is literally every pack for themselves. Other books suggest that packs get into alliances and form warparties together. I actually prefer the &quot;every pack for themselves&quot; model because werewolf life should be a brutal survival of the fittest existence which is nasty brutish and short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:26:00-08:00","id":15579,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need to be one or the other, just more clearly explained how one can turn to the other and back. I can see very isolationist packs in a city at each others throats over territory and more. I can also see them banding together for the short term or long term to deal with larger threats. I mean, look at Lodges; honestly they appear to be what happens when one pack or multiple packs go &quot;Well shit, this is a problem...&quot; for quite a few of them, and get together with others to remedy the situation. Though I hate using the term, it's less one or the other, and simply a more &quot;organic&quot; presentation without there being one singular default assumption.<br /> <br /> Right now it's a mish-mash because of writing inconsistency; it can be either (or both honestly in a city with some at each others throats and others in larger scale alliances), but the -presentation- in some areas make it seem like it -should- be this or that by one writer's presentation or writing style, then contradicted by another who wants to go the other road. It does have some trouble with consistency in that area, at least in a way that allows for both to be options without a hard elbow to the ribs due to a writing shift and author bias. Then again, it's W:tF; it suffers from early-series-itis even once you get into a few of the supplements, so the focus is muddled. The game shouldn't railroad you on the social structure in a city. Cutting out one or the other isn't going to help much compared to a more internally consistent explanation on how it shifts gears between social dynamics without it being a square peg in a round hole. With the core book you should have clear, concise rules off the get go to do both without rubbing against the grain.<br /> <br /> The game doesn't need a 'stand' here, it just needs some more focus in the corebook on how this all works, shifts around, Tribal lines get into conflict or hazy, packs expand, shrink, combine and become Lodges, how Tribes may form (yep, you heard me) so you can address these at least in part with the main book without getting the conflicting &quot;pack vs larger structure&quot; impressions many of us have gotten. It's talked about some, but it really could use a cleaner treatment at base given it -is- going to come up consistently in the game. Definitely not an area to shunt off more focus into another supplement instead of hammering it out in the base book to stand on it's own two (four?) feet. Luckily when it comes to areas that just require emphasis, focus or cleaning up, it's fairly easy compared to the areas needing full-tilt overhauls.<br /> <br /> I'd rather have that area be a toolbox, rather than just a power-drill if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:02:34-08:00","id":16374,"title":"","content":"Werewolves should be very much a different species mentality-wise, but I do like how they often try to integrate on some level with the surrounding humanity. I like them brushing up against humanity psychologically-speaking, and having opinions on them, and making friends and enemies and allies and coping with it all in their werewolfy-heads. I like how the werewolves, at best, see us the way we see pets. <br /> <br /> They can grieve and rage when we die, as individuals, but just as the average person doesn't freak out internally when seeing a dead cat by the road like we would if we saw a dead human, the same is true for them. (At least, in my opinion) <br /> <br /> So don't overpay the wolf so much as to make them incapable of forming attachments to humans. Don't cut that angle out of the game. Werewolf seems to talk about the human-werewolf connection issue book-wise way more than Changeling (books focus on the hedge), vampire (they're dead, Jim) and even Mage (focus is on the rest of their life). I like that. It gives me ideas on how to incorporate humanity into the world with them and how to deal with any relationships that come up. The wolf must cleave with the man, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T03:10:10-08:00","id":16548,"title":"","content":"I want open lists of powers. I think a linear 1-5 doesn't benefit or fit werewolves' powers at all. We could either have dot-less lists of powers ala Embeds, or if we want some powers to cost more or less depending on its usefulness, then list of powers with different dot ratings like if Merits or Aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T18:04:16-08:00","id":16886,"title":"","content":"That's why I favor the Instincts and Gifts system. Instincts being along a linear progression of 1-5 that a Werewolf can learn on his own, and Gifts being dot-less powers you can get from spirits by hook or by crook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T11:30:10-08:00","id":17193,"title":"","content":"I'm just treating Instincts at 1-5 in scale of potency, with offshoots at various instinct levels (so multiples available at each &quot;tier&quot;) with Numina gained from spirits as singular, dotless powers with a flat cost. Even with 1-5 Instincts there's plenty of room of having multiple differing iterations of how they progress to reflect individual variance, tribal teachings and anything else that comes to mind. Seems the best bet overall; diversity trumps a lack of it when it comes to players usually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T13:24:14-08:00","id":17270,"title":"","content":"The issue with allowing access to Numina at a flat cost is there is wildly different utility between Numina. They were designed as a short-hand tool for NPCs, who don't really have to worry about experience costs or power progression, and so you end up with &quot;any supernatural effect you desire&quot; as a dot-less Power + Finesse roll. The variation in Numina literally covers from &quot;-2 to perception rolls to being spotted&quot; to &quot;resurrect someone from the dead, making them mortal in the process&quot;. Even at a more moderate range, there's Manipulate Element, Abduct, Blast, Control Animal, Telepathy, Material/Spiritual Vision, Clasp..... All for the same cost?<br /> <br /> I'm running a game where I allow Numina to be purchased, and I quickly ran into problems with balance to the point where I started assigning dot values to Numina. Even that wouldn't work under the GMC experience, though, because having a 'experience per dot' value equates to having a 1-5 dot power without the benefit of getting powers at the lower dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> I understand the argument for Gifts not making sense as the only system of supernatural powers, and I think the Instincts system is a great way for having 'werewolf-y' powers independent from the spirit world. But replacing Gifts with Numina outright has some serious issues with cost and balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T14:22:44-08:00","id":17306,"title":"","content":"Yep, same cost; their mechanics don't -directly- translate over; they'll run a bit differently for the half-fleshed Werewolves and the like. That said, no, it's not having a variable cost. You -only- get them nominally by rank spirit pacts or most commonly hunting down and consuming a spirit wholesale; if you want to hunt down and successfully consume some with the resurrection Numina, more power to you; odds are you deserve what you get without jacking the XP cost higher. They aren't intended to be afterthoughts with what me and another are tinkering with; they're their own plotlines and plot-seeds. I'm still discussing what would be the best way to translate a Numina to a &quot;gift&quot;, but some limitations and tweaks will definitely need to be applied; on the flipside, the Essence costs for most of the nastier Numina makes them prohibitive in common use as well; it's a personal treatment, but it's a precious resource with risky actions to acquire; there is no soaking up Essence from Loci in the games myself and the other ST run, and given you're not going to have an easy time just finding spirits in the material realm -all- the time, that means if you want to blow 3-5 Essence or more (likely limited by your Primal Urge)... it's going to add up with its own issues.<br /> <br /> Many of the beefier Numina are -very- costly in Essence; it's not really an internalized self-balancing system, but those 'Wow' types, assuming you can take down the spirit that has it to begin with, assuming you can find one with it, assimilate it's essence and spend the xp to use it, assuming you consistently have the Essence to blow on the thing... I don't have a big issue with the player having it at a flat cost.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the potency is not consistent even if XP costs are, but it's generally a risk vs reward situation regardless; you're not going to just casually be able to snag them like snacks, and if you got them from a pact... it's because the spirit radically altered your essence/resonance and of course favors for it; that has it's own issues. There isn't any easy way that's not very, very risky. Keep in mind the Rank of the spirits that have those beefier types; you don't get it from discorporating the thing and it sure as hell won't give it up easily. Odds are if you did manage a pact with it, you're on the losing end of the bargain or getting more than you bargained for anyhow when trucking spirits of greater equivalent rank than you.<br /> <br /> The equivalent of Materialize (de-materialize to go into the Shadow) and similar may be common and easy to gain off a low ranking spirit but... how often are you going to see things running around with Blast, Abduct, the various resurrection types and stronger manipulations that -aren't- going to pose a pretty big threat? It's not like going down to the spirit grocery market and saying &quot;I want this numina today&quot;, tossing down some xp and walking out of the store. Some Numina are likely to simply be incompatible too. It's not a direct translation anymore than Aspects etc. for Shartha are. Numina acquisition is meant to be meaningful; trophies of war, battle scars, life changing events of a sort; you fundamentally change each time you take one. If they're just doled out or acquired through 'down time' actions, then they lose much of their impact.<br /> <br /> That said, it really depends on the XP value using GMC experience; buying an old Gift that does something nuts (mass supernatural powers shutdown from what was it, Alpha Gift Lists, been a while since I peeked that one?) is the precise same xp value in GMC if doing a straight translation to learning a Gift that gives you a minor bonus. It'd be costlier to skip ahead to get the beefier, but I wouldn't say by -that- much. The issue isn't the XP value being flat; it's ST's doling out access to the specific Numina like they were candy. Me? If someone wants to take on a spirit capable of mortal resurrection (assuming you can find one with that to begin with), more power to them if they succeed with their pack, let alone individually. It's going to be something pretty epic.<br /> <br /> It sure won't be something puny that I put them up against, the XP will be an afterthought compared to surviving the encounter and who claims the kill to get the Numina. I'm also going by the idea that the number of Numina one can have is going to be related to one's Primal Urge; we're still crunching out what would be the best cap, but given they're fundamental shifts to ones spiritual nature, they're not going to be in endless supply. Most aren't going to have many of them, or consistently potent ones given the difficulty of acquiring them. Seriously, the thing's probably going to be a Rank 5 spirit in a lot of instances for the &quot;holy shit&quot; numina; some of these conflicts to get these numina are equivalent to the old Milestone gifts in scope of what's necessary to get them. The Xp value is -almost- unimportant at that point in all honesty.<br /> <br /> If it's just &quot;And the player says they want it, it's glossed over with a downtime action and the xp is spent to get one -nasty- Numina&quot; then yeah... -that- I see as a problem, or doling out low ranking spirits with consistently potent numina without them being story specific and part of the ongoing plots (not saying you're doing any of this all by the way Seraph, I'm just using a worst case scenario here that definitely makes it more of a problem). Players have access to what's presented as existing in the setting, and what's around, and they need to -work- to get these things within the context of the story. It may seem all golden if they find a beefy spirit with a juicy numina that they believe they can get via a pact/barter/intimidation, but you may well get a situation worse than Dar-Us's at that point. Their acquisition is meant to drive stories; a variable xp level or keeping it high cost isn't really going to fix something when they don't scale naturally and the story doesn't support their access to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-24-2013, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T17:05:55-08:00","id":17388,"title":"","content":"More dynamic fluff.<br /> <br /> Perhaps something with the Lodge of Wires. Blood and Smoke isn't just trying to add some vampire feel to the game, but is expanding upon the story with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:16:10-08:00","id":17964,"title":"","content":"The Pure thread on at the moment has reminded me something.<br /> <br /> What I would also be interested in is having the tribal totems as a more tangible presence. If there's moon banished spirits from Before Time(tm) I damn well (as the ST) want to be able to include the First Pack. This (in my head) is represented by some mechanics or core-book-fluff that includes what it is like to have a gigantic spirit mystically bonded to your &quot;soul&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T15:45:21-08:00","id":17980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=17964#post17964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I would also be interested in is having the tribal totems as a more tangible presence. If there's moon banished spirits from Before Time(tm) I damn well (as the ST) want to be able to include the First Pack. This (in my head) is represented by some mechanics or core-book-fluff that includes what it is like to have a gigantic spirit mystically bonded to your &quot;soul&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>a) The First Pack and the Firstborn are different things, for all that the blending of the two in story gives me theories about Tier 4 werewolves.<br /> b) Tribes of the Moon, The Pure, and Lore of the Forsaken have <i>exactly this.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T05:09:59-08:00","id":18359,"title":"","content":"Oh oops, I always forgot that distinction.<br /> <br /> And I am aware, I have read those books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My point is, I would like that straight up in the Idigam Chronicles <i>from the start</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T06:22:20-08:00","id":18375,"title":"","content":"Things I would like to see in Idigam Chronicles are basically things we eventually got in the sourcebooks, so that it can be referenced again.<br /> <br /> - The Pure tribes detailed with their gifts;<br /> - Pack Tactics;<br /> - The hosts and how they function;<br /> - More on the Bale Hounds;<br /> - More tribal identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, what I think could use some work:<br /> <br /> - More scary Gauru form. I love the concept of a timed bomb you throw, but the explosion needs more power now that we are a lot of WoD books later;<br /> - More uratha society structure, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T14:30:29-08:00","id":18722,"title":"","content":"I posted this in the White Wolf thread in more detail but Werewolf never really clicked for me in its current iteration because it doesn't seem to have a lot of internal conflict built into it. You are automatically part of a pack, and belong to some extent. Most conflicts are external. A renewed focus on Man Vs Beast as an internal conflict would add a lot to the game I think. In fact an Axis of Man Vs Beast and Physical world Vs the Spiritual World would add a lot of potential for internal conflict if it was made a stronger focus. Not saying the game should suddenly become Changeling but most people's idea of a pop culture Werewolf tends to be somewhat like Hulk( you wouldn't like me when I am angry) or Wolverine (I am not a beast I am a man... though I do struggle to not rip people's throats out from time to time). A focus that allowed these kind of characters to be more obviously played from the get go would be a good addition to the game and I think help draw in new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T19:44:25-08:00","id":18893,"title":"","content":"Well I would love more reasoning for stealing territories beyond, its what Werewolves do. Territories is a cool part of the game, but sometimes it feels like it would be more logical to just choose a territory away from people trying to expand, as well as not expanding just because you can when you don't have the manpower to keep it after you win it.<br /> <br /> I would also desire Renown to be purchased with Renown EXP. Proving your Renown through actions seems like a better idea then having a player just give not so Cunning Werewolf Cunning just because they want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T01:19:53-08:00","id":19030,"title":"","content":"You have to do something to earn cunning renown, you don't get to &quot;just give&quot; a character cunning renown because you have XP banked. That's directly from the core rules. I do like the idea of renown XP being awarded as a separate thing from regular XP.<br /> As for stealing territory, loci aren't the easiest resource to come by, so there is plenty of reason for one pack to try and take another's territory to gain control of that resource if it's present on another pack's land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T01:23:13-08:00","id":19033,"title":"","content":"Well okay yeah if you have a Loci defend it like the dickens. :P I guess I was more talking about a new pack that hasn't established territory yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T02:04:39-08:00","id":19049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=18722#post18722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I posted this in the White Wolf thread in more detail but Werewolf never really clicked for me in its current iteration <b>because it doesn't seem to have a lot of internal conflict built into it</b>. <b>You are automatically part of a pack</b>, and belong to some extent. Most conflicts are external. A renewed focus on Man Vs Beast as an internal conflict would add a lot to the game I think. In fact an Axis of Man Vs Beast and Physical world Vs the Spiritual World would add a lot of potential for internal conflict if it was made a stronger focus. Not saying the game should suddenly become Changeling but most people's idea of a pop culture Werewolf tends to be somewhat like Hulk( you wouldn't like me when I am angry) or Wolverine (I am not a beast I am a man... though I do struggle to not rip people's throats out from time to time). A focus that allowed these kind of characters to be more obviously played from the get go would be a good addition to the game and I think help draw in new players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at some of the flaws in the game. One, for example, prevents the werewolf from actually adapting to his lupine shapes. Even Dalu feels off. Another one, makes the Uratha cocky. He feels invincible, because why shouldn't he? he can regenerate from almost anything.<br /> <br /> Lone wolves have it very rough. Ghost Wolves? Even rougher. How do you portray a character after he goes into Kuruth, <b>eats</b> a chunk out of someone, and gets addicted to cannibalism?<br /> <br /> Blood of the Wolf got an amazing section on how Vices color the life of the forsaken. It's pretty varied, it's pretty visceral.<br /> <br /> It's not a problem with the game. It's a problem of not scratching it's themes. It's not the aircraft, it's the pilot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T10:19:28-08:00","id":19244,"title":"","content":"I would say its a problem if that aspect is not clearly presented in the corebook and you need to buy a supplement for it to be emphasised.<br /> <br /> What I really want to see to draw me into a Werewolf game is a strong focus on BEING a Werewolf and the conflict that goes with it. Being a Vampire, Changeling or Mage all have an inherent conflict built into the templete. I think Werewolf needs to explore this more. How do you feel about being a Werewolf. At its best, you are an unstoppable force of nature. You are extremely hard to kill. How does that affect a human psyche? How would a teenager, who has spent all their life being bullied, react to suddenly realising that they never need to be scared of (human) bullies again? That the bullies should be scared of him? Would he lord it over them or not? Would the power overwhelm him? Then the downside. You suddenly feel like tearing out the throat of that guy for simply shoving past you. How many times will this happen before you snap? You find the animal side taking over. The dynamic between the human mind and the animal, raging instincts of a werewolf should be inherently built into the core book and the template. It should be possible to play a chronicle out of the book that has no spirits in it. That has no territory conflicts in it. You should be able to simply play a game about what being a werewolf feels like.<br /> <br /> This should NOT be the whole game. Spirits should have a place. Hunting should defintely have a place. Developing territory and tribal political conflicts should have a place. Exploring the balance between the material world and the spirit world should have a place. The Shamanistic aspects should have a place. But if you want to sell people on playing a werewolf game, you need to make that core werewolf experience feel fun and visceral. All that other stuff that makes Forsaken more distinctive and unique can be layered on afterwards.<br /> <br /> Vampire has a pretty cool setting with lots of weird stuff in it. Sure if you want to, you can play a blood magic slinging priest of the Lancea Sanctum. But the book at its core presents the dynamic of being a vampire and devotes a lot of focus on this dynamic. The Covenants, Blood Magic, Politics are all in the core book but that stuff is presented as being ON TOP OF the core experience of playing a Vampire. Mage does the same thing. You suddenly realise that you can bend the world to your whim (with some drawbacks) Do you go mad with power? This conflict is inherent to the setting before you add in the Exarchs, faction politics and so forth. I think Werewolf should follow suit and have just as strong a focus on the internal conflict in the core book as it does on external conflicts.<br /> <br /> I would like a Werewolf corebook that is similar to Changeling's corebook. It would present several ways you can play the game, internal conflict focused (the experience of being a werewolf), external spirit threats, phyiscal world threats, defending territory and expanding that territory and pack politics should all be viable options straight out of the corebook with supplements giving more focus to each other area as desired. The corebook though should get you fired up to play a certain type of game regardless, you shouldn't need a supplement to play the game in a less narrowly defined way.<br /> <br /> I have only read through the corebook and don't own it so it is possible that I am being slightly too harsh on the original book but for contrast I bought the Mage and Changeling corebooks based on their tv tropes description and the impression of the games given on forums. Reading the corebooks I instantly thought of fun possibilities and got a sense of why people liked the game; especially with the Changeling corebook which is brilliantly written and expressed. I like the idea of werewolves and playing werwolves could be fun, it is something I actively looked into but the default corebook just did not do a lot for me. I am sure the game is good, but the corebook seemed weak in my opinion and so I never bought it. I would relook at the game as whole based on the new corebook but I don't want to buy a load of supplements for the game straight away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T22:02:18-08:00","id":20993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=18375#post18375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things I would like to see in Idigam Chronicles are basically things we eventually got in the sourcebooks, so that it can be referenced again.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <b>Idigam Chronicle</b> is the perfect place to centralize mechanics that, in hindsight, <i>should have been</i> in the core. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=18375#post18375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Pure tribes detailed with their gifts;<br /> - Pack Tactics;<br /> - The hosts and how they function;<br /> - More on the Bale Hounds;<br /> - More tribal identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add the more detailed rules for the Claimed. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T09:54:52-08:00","id":21191,"title":"","content":"I'd leave out the Bale Hounds and Maeljin, save them for a future supplement similar to Book of the Wyrm for WtA. I think they both need to be retooled since the virtue and vice system has been changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:09:56-08:00","id":21772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=21191#post21191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd leave out the Bale Hounds and Maeljin, save them for a future supplement similar to Book of the Wyrm for WtA. I think they both need to be retooled since the virtue and vice system has been changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the Hisil normally on extreme grimdark and the setting ultimately less focused on big evil bastards? The Idigam also get top billing as antagonists, so perhaps the Maeljin can just sit this one out and the Bale Hounds can serve the Moon-Banished instead of the Arbitrary Sin Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:19:02-08:00","id":21854,"title":"","content":"You might have missed the part where the Maeljin are bound to exceedingly toxic portions of the Hisil that corrupt everything within reach. The Shadow is grim, but there are places truly fucked up.<br /> <br /> Also, for someone that doesn't seem to like Forsaken outside of hammering the oWolf thing into the ground you pop up pretty regularly, Dino.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:38:51-08:00","id":21864,"title":"","content":"Pseulak and Thurifuge operate outside of the 7 Deadly Sins range in an interesting way(Deception and Violence) and I figured it would be an interesting step to make the others more encompassing of actions intended to hurt others. I figure culling the number down to the Four Incarnae of Violence, Deception, Indulgence,and Neglect as the four big things that actually resonate with Werewolves on a personal level.<br /> <br /> So the big list goes we have the 8 Incarnae of the First Pack as stabilizing forces in the lives of Werewolves, 4 Incarnae leading them to corruption, and 2 Celestines involved in their Creation.<br /> <br /> Idigam are a recent unleashed evil that drives the setting to shift by their very existence being outside of the norm. Much like the things in the final chapter of Predators, they direct the course of an entire campaign and are bound into the background of the game giving significant weight and interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:54:47-08:00","id":21875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=21772#post21772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't the Hisil normally on extreme grimdark and the setting ultimately less focused on big evil bastards? The Idigam also get top billing as antagonists, so perhaps the Maeljin can just sit this one out and the Bale Hounds can serve the Moon-Banished instead of the Arbitrary Sin Lords.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see much value or sense in assigning the hellhounds-actual-hellhounds faction to serving Tiamat, even without factoring in your known hate-on for WASPLEG as a Vice set, and I don't fancy having <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/review_comments.php?id=1098\" target=\"_blank\">that dumb conversation where someone argues that all the antagonist factions are interchangeable</a> again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T09:52:00-08:00","id":33924,"title":"","content":"Just to give the thread a bit of a prod, Stew has revealed a few hints of what we're working on for Idigam Chronicles over on rpg.net. It's only the very barest of comments, but there's a bit there for those interested <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:04:56-08:00","id":33938,"title":"","content":"Link please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:27:25-08:00","id":33947,"title":"","content":"I'm flailing at my wife's iPad here so I haven't figured out how to do links as yet, but the gist is: - we're doing something different with harmony. It's about balance, not about getting as high a score as possible. - tribe is 'what' while auspice is 'how'. Idigam are the outside context problem. - gifts and renown are going to get plenty of attention. Trust me, we've had a lot of discussion about these areas of the game. You'll note I am the person responsible for the concept of Instincts as per the old thread on rpg.net that I created months ago now. No, that doesn't mean instincts are necessarily a thing in the new book, but it hopefully lets you know that there is at least one person on the team who is thinking in that kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:38:27-08:00","id":33955,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?711826-WtF-Idigam-Chronicle-What-do-we-know/page2\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...-we-know/page2</a><br /> <br /> Is this it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:44:25-08:00","id":33958,"title":"","content":"That's the correct thread, yes. Also, the formatting in my last post disappeared for some reason. I hate iPads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:32:49-08:00","id":33980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=33958#post33958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the correct thread, yes. Also, the formatting in my last post disappeared for some reason. I hate iPads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get a real computer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:42:27-08:00","id":33984,"title":"","content":"Strange that Tribe is the &quot;What?&quot; while Auspice is the &quot;How?&quot;. Tribes being something you chose to join based on ideology and Auspice is something Luna awakened/forced on you to start your Werewolfdom. <br /> <br /> Hmmm, perhaps Tribes are becoming more of a bloodline thing linking you back to your Ancestor that did the dirty deed. Maybe even turning the Firstborn into the original Uratha that killed Father Wolf, but eventually became full spirits and progenitors of their kind. I noticed fluff appeared to be going that direction in several places and can't say I'm against it. So Tribe becomes &quot;What kind of Werewolf are you?&quot; and Auspice is &quot;How is that expressed in you?&quot;. <br /> <br /> Harmony becoming more about balancing your human life with the wolf spirit tearing across the Shadow could be seen as the ultimate expression of High Harmony. I figure the ultimate expression of low Harmony might be a person that's fallen into being two different being that just so happen to have the same body. The titular Werewolf character in cinema that is a normal guy most of the time and then a bloodthirsty monster with no control over himself the other half of the time. <br /> <br /> Seeing how Vampires have Status among Covenant, Clan, and City perhaps Werewolves will have status of Tribe, Auspice, and Territory. Reflecting how they affects both the humans and spirits in the lands they claim, and how well-known they are amongst their own kind in reflecting their ideals. Or the clearer course is Uratha, City, and Shadow. How do you balance being part of all 3 groups?<br /> <br /> No idea, just tossing out what this simple statement is stirring into my head.<br /> <br /> Sad we won't be getting blog posts(damn Apocalypse gameline), but I can't wait to guesstimate at whatever the writers do share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T11:54:26-08:00","id":33994,"title":"","content":"Not sure I should offer any more clarifications or hints at this stage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I will say that you need to look at the 'what' in the context of the rest of the info that Stew put in that section of his comment though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T12:46:20-08:00","id":34025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=33984#post33984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that Tribe is the &quot;What?&quot; while Auspice is the &quot;How?&quot;. Tribes being something you chose to join based on ideology and Auspice is something Luna awakened/forced on you to start your Werewolfdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me that's how it's always been. WHAT the Blood Talons do is fight the good fight, to the bitter end, if necessary. HOW an Irraka would go about it is by spying on the enemies, gathering information, and exploiting a weakness to eliminate the problem in advance if they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:10:03-08:00","id":36131,"title":"","content":"Or throwing dirt in your eyes while kicking you in the dangly bits. Hey, it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T06:57:11-08:00","id":36351,"title":"","content":"Well, the Blood Talon Oath is &quot;offer no surrender that you would not accept&quot;, doesn't say anything about dirty fighting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T05:50:57-08:00","id":38262,"title":"","content":"I have a quick question for you all - are there any particular films or other forms of media that you think are good inspiration for the sort of horror feel that the Hosts and Claimed have?<br /> <br /> The one that leaps to mind for me when it comes to Hosts is the Alien franchise for the initial, invasive nature of the Host shard affecting a victim, but I'm curious what other good sources of inspiration and feel there are out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T10:08:57-08:00","id":38326,"title":"","content":"The Thing, by Carpenter. Not the new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T11:00:18-08:00","id":38345,"title":"","content":"Tetsuo the Iron Man, the Fly, Videodrome, Society, Slither, Thinner, Robocop","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T23:38:57-08:00","id":38622,"title":"","content":"Invasion of the Body Snatchers or any of the derivatives (remakes, The Invasion, Threshold, etc).<br /> <br /> A lot of sci-fi horror will come up here due to the &quot;alien&quot; nature of the spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 12-29-2013, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T14:46:02-08:00","id":39609,"title":"","content":"What do I want to see? The Kickstarter... so I can scream, &quot;<b>TAKE MY MONEY!</b>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T16:19:12-08:00","id":39672,"title":"","content":"Not getting a Kickstarter seeing how Blood &amp; Smoke didn't get one. I just can't wait to see spoilers sometime after the holidays.<br /> <br /> Can't lie, I'm drooling to see how they redo shapeshifting and forms. As a teaser that would be the MAIN thing for a revamp of a game like Werewolf to draw people in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 12-30-2013, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T10:11:15-08:00","id":41806,"title":"","content":"I was thinking (with the other thread about the truth of Father Wolf), about Sumer and the city of Bau. Is it Canon? I like to think so. Perhaps not the part of the modern ziggurat, that's more of a plot that might happen in someone's game. <br /> <br /> After the short bit of Broken Clans and Covenants in Blood &amp; Smoke, I would love to see something like that in Idigam Chronicles. Perhaps lost tribes? Some Forsaken societies like Bau, that rose and fell during the ages?<br /> <br /> Werewolf's history comes from oral tradition, I think. So names get lost in time. Forsaken might have been different (like in Bau) during the ages, but that doesn't translate in oral tradition (&quot;We were different back then, stronger&quot; - gives room to lots of interpretations instead of &quot;Dude, we walked in Gauru like all the fuckin' time!&quot;). Who knows, maybe a lot of what we know happened, happened in a loooonger time frame (The schism between Forsaken and Pure only happened a 1000 years later, for instance).<br /> <br /> Maybe we get hints of history in Idigam Chronicles. Specially more recently (Heck, the return of the Idigam is not a long time ago!). Perhaps a book later down the line with Forsaken in different eras, like Ancient Mythologies?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would love to see more about the Forsaken's history. Something playable, something fresh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:03:49-08:00","id":41901,"title":"","content":"That's actually something I'd like to see as well in regards to the issues present with having an oral tradition of Uratha History. In particular, it really changes the Spirit dynamics as they are reflections of belief. So like how Atlantean History is only a possibility (via Imperial Mysteries) Uratha beliefs actually alter how Spirits remember the patricide. It adds an element of doubt to the Forsaken in that is there status as &quot;Forsaken&quot; purely self inflicted? Is the Pure so blinded by hate that spirits simply just naturally propagate the patricide in a mutually sustaining recursion loop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:59:11-08:00","id":41947,"title":"","content":"Worth noting: the spirits that most directly reinforce the myth of Father Wolf happen to be the ones that have been reciprocally bound to tribes of werewolves (who largely believe and propagate that myth) for hundreds upon thousands of years and most spirits don't need a group to have a reputation as kinslayers and godkillers to have pretext for distrusting weird half-flesh abominations that want to keep them from doing as they please with abandon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T14:06:31-08:00","id":41948,"title":"","content":"The friends of the Uratha aren't the only ones, there's an abundance of enemies who acknowledge it, like the spirit hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T15:19:57-08:00","id":41979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=41948#post41948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The friends of the Uratha aren't the only ones, there's an abundance of enemies who acknowledge it, like the spirit hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hosts are cannibalistic fragmentary demon-bits that the Uratha happen to have tied to Father Wolf via the origin myth they've passed down and no, they don't really do that very much. I've been exhaustively reading the books for the better part of the last year and seen nothing to suggest the shartha do so besides the decidedly slanted take the Beshilu of the United Kingdom present as part of their weird religious fervor.<br /> <br /> The myth of Father Wolf is largely only acknowledged by spirits <i>interacting with werewolves who know the myth. </i>Given how spirits work, <i>this is telling.</i><br /> <br /> Blasphemies is an invaluable book for discussing this subject, as is Geist's presentation of how a krewe mythos solidifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T15:58:03-08:00","id":42002,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much room there will be in the core, but I'd like to see more than just the Azlu and Beshilu detailed therein. The Hosts are just awesome, a truly horrific and dangerous foe for werewolves, and one that gives them plenty of hunting material aside from things like spirits, Claimed and other weirdness. I've used the Hosts extensively as a Storyteller and you can believe that if I get in on the project, I'll be looking to work on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T20:50:35-08:00","id":42138,"title":"","content":"It always bugged me how Werewolf is about faith in something that may never have happened while Mage gets book after book affirming the existence of its fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T21:05:13-08:00","id":42142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42138#post42138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always bugged me how Werewolf is about faith in something that may never have happened while Mage gets book after book affirming the existence of its fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same sense that Demon is filled to bursting with totally reliable sources of information about the origin of its PC group's maker, yes.<br /> <br /> What part of &quot;retroactive cosmic edit-war&quot; and &quot;replica after attempted replica after misattributed replica&quot; is difficult for you to understand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T12:25:31-08:00","id":42411,"title":"","content":"I didn't read the entire thread, so please pardon me if this was already stated.<br /> <br /> Could we please have a backstory for the Pure that doesn't make my eyes roll? As it stands right now it's the equivalent of me deciding to kill a guy because his caveman ancestor decided to brain my caveman ancestor (that may have never happened in the first place). It's just kind of silly. Silly's fine for some things, but I don't think that is the tone that this game is going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T12:45:31-08:00","id":42423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42411#post42411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read the entire thread, so please pardon me if this was already stated.<br /> <br /> Could we please have a backstory for the Pure that doesn't make my eyes roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider seeing an optometrist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it stands right now it's the equivalent of me deciding to kill a guy because his caveman ancestor decided to brain my caveman ancestor (that may have never happened in the first place). It's just kind of silly. Silly's fine for some things, but I don't think that is the tone that this game is going for. </div> </div> </div>If that's how you read <i>the destruction of your ancestral homeland and the eternal tarnishing of your family's reputation</i> then I don't think any amount of adjustment is going to make a werewolf blood-feud make sense to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T14:06:03-08:00","id":42468,"title":"","content":"Yeah... the Pure backstory makes me roll my eyes too, but so do several real-world conflicts, some of which hardly have more factual basis than the Pures possess to justify their war.<br /> So, in this case, it's less a problem with the Pures being silly, and more a problem with humans in general, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T15:36:07-08:00","id":42514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42423#post42423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's how you read <i>the destruction of your ancestral homeland and the eternal tarnishing of your family's reputation</i> then I don't think any amount of adjustment is going to make a werewolf blood-feud make sense to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. I would also read the same if some modern Irish guy decided to attack modern Sweden because of the deaths caused by the Viking raids. It makes about as much sense.<br /> <br /> You know I take it back. It would make more sense because the Viking raids were more recent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:00:12-08:00","id":42523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42514#post42514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do. I would also read the same if some modern Irish guy decided to attack modern Sweden because of the deaths caused by the Viking raids. It makes about as much sense.<br /> <br /> You know I take it back. It would make more sense because the Viking raids were more recent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cute. I like the part where you completely ignore the ongoing reinforcement of the conflict at play from well into the past in favor of assuming that the way this works is some guy out of nowhere deciding to attack people who draw a distant line of descent from the guys who inflicted a grievance upon the guy's distant ancestors.<br /> <br /> We're talking about a species of dominance-minded, easily-angered supernatural monsters who've been running a culture of hatred based, ultimately, upon the notion that the other guys are the reason that, variously, they can't have nice things, the world is a mess, or the species has the enmity of the spiritual world. They have been doing this for basically the entirety of recorded history and have employed sundry psychosocial measures to ensure that the conflict is beaten into their constituents' heads, and all the while at least two greater Incarnae have had a stake in ensuring they continue to fight this war.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your forefathers and my forefathers were brothers when their father ruled over Paradise, but your forefathers are responsible for the destruction of Paradise, so half the world looks at all of us with a default position of borderline xenophobia. For being forced to share in your forefathers' punishment my forefathers swore revenge on yours, and that grudge has been passed down through generations upon generations of People I naturally respect and feel inclined to follow, so now you get to taste silver.&quot;<br /> <br /> I realize it's not as snappy as &quot;guy fights his great-to-the-nth-grandfather's enemy's great-to-the-nth-grandchildren over ancient history,&quot; but it <i>is</i> less of a misrepresentation for its own sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:08:19-08:00","id":42530,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've never had a problem with the Pure and their reasons for hating. In fact, it seems right in line with a lot of the ideological hatred displayed by real-world groups toward other groups. Indeed, it probably has more of a legitimate basis, as Satchel helps describe, and seems realistic based upon the fact that these are packs of inhuman predators who organize themselves into savage animistic tribes and find it easier to place the blame for not ruling the world as hunter-kings on someone else. Hatred is easy. It's simple. It wraps up their world in a neat little bow: These guys are why life isn't the way we want it to be. Their ways are wrong and we need to show why ours are correct by tearing theirs down.<br /> <br /> I have zero problems buying that as an ideology, largely because it's something that we have in the modern world without even needing a <i>Hisil</i> or werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T18:33:42-08:00","id":42619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42523#post42523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have been doing this for basically the entirety of recorded history and have employed sundry psychosocial measures to ensure that the conflict is beaten into their constituents' heads...</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's where it breaks the hardest for me. It's to perfect. Let's also not forget that there is a percentage (we have no idea how high) of werewolves who either deny Father Wolf's existence, have never heard of the guy, and/or think that the Pangaea story is just a myth. It's difficult to get people to kill over what they think is a legend.<br /> <br /> It takes constant work and effort to keep feuds going and werewolves are not immortal. Even the Hatfields and McCoys gave it up after a generation or two. What you're talking about is a perfect transmission of hatred over probably thousands of generations while also evangelizing the 'enemy' to fight against those that they thought of as family with the same hatred.<br /> <br /> The part that makes me scratch my head the most is wondering who thought that a multi-generational, multi-national feud was even necessary. If you want to show the dark mirror of werewolf behavior then doesn't banehounds work better? They also seem to do the whole 'dominated by spirits' thing better than the Pure. If you just want werewolves fighting werewolves doesn't just another pack work just as well? With another pack if a player wants to know why they are attacking I could just say that the invader pack wants their stuff.<br /> <br /> So in short, I find the Pure neither compelling, interesting, or useful. I find no thematic niche where they are the best fit. I find their back story to be a suckers bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42523#post42523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Your forefathers and my forefathers were brothers when their father ruled over Paradise, but your forefathers are responsible for the destruction of Paradise, so half the world looks at all of us with a default position of borderline xenophobia. For being forced to share in your forefathers' punishment my forefathers swore revenge on yours, and that grudge has been passed down through generations upon generations of People I naturally respect and feel inclined to follow, so now you get to taste silver.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot the part where &quot;And we have no idea if any of this even happened in the first place. For all we know, we're fighting because Winter Wolf accidentally marked one of Dire Wolf's trees and Dire Wolf wants revenge.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","user":"Ghost","date":". 01-04-2014, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T19:33:49-08:00","id":42641,"title":"","content":"<b>Ghost:</b> Go read the Pure source-book. Modern Pure? the Myth itself only caters to those deranged enough (read: low Harmony) to have depression over the lost paradise. The other 90% of them? either want to be in the winning team (predominantly those converted after the fact) thus having their life being easier (misguidedly so) or were entirely brainwashed in the process, in some cases being enough to willingly butcher your own families as a rite of passage.<br /> <br /> If you're faced with this kind of persecution, and the only thing you need to do is join, it's hard not to consider it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T23:27:10-08:00","id":42725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=42619#post42619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The part that makes me scratch my head the most is wondering who thought that a multi-generational, multi-national feud was even necessary. If you want to show the dark mirror of werewolf behavior then doesn't banehounds work better? They also seem to do the whole 'dominated by spirits' thing better than the Pure. If you just want werewolves fighting werewolves doesn't just another pack work just as well? With another pack if a player wants to know why they are attacking I could just say that the invader pack wants their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>point</i> of the Pure is to be that middle-road antagonist; the three primary werewolf antagonist groups were intended to be a sliding scale of sympathetic villain, which <i>The Pure</i> admits in the storytelling chapter. The intended breakdown was this<br /> -Rival Forsaken: they agree philosophically on mostly everything; they have different tactics and some tribal jealousies and mistrust, but the main reason packs get into conflict is that they want each others' territory, they step on each others toes when their prey cross borders, wanting their stuff, etc. Werewolves naturally fall to tribalism and hot-headedness, so they clash with their neighbors as a matter of instinct, but at the end of the day, they don't have any deep seated disagreements, and are willing to often work with each other.<br /> <br /> -Balehounds: are absolute monsters. There is no depravity they wan't do; they can't be negotiated with; they have no redeeming philosophy or motivation (sure, there are reasons to become one, which <i>Blasphemies</i> gets into, but they start at severely troubled). They infiltrate packs to destroy from within - any pack - which makes them a universal threat for werewolves. <i>Everyone </i>will put their arguments aside to hunt these guys.<br /> <br /> -The Pure: are a balancing antagonist. The default stance any pack should have for them is fear and hatred; this rarely comes from ideological differences, so much as it does the fact that the Pure outnumber them 3 to 1, and have a reputation for <i>eating </i>their Forsaken enemies alive. Ideology is a good, solid mythical explanation for the root of the conflict - the Bone Shadows are all about spirit lore and the Fire Touched are religious zealots, so they take it seriously at least. More important is the horrific and frequent savagery the Pure (reportedly) bear down on them. Not to mention the Forsaken spend their lives in an endless struggle to keep spirits in check; hearing the Pure serve spirits (and not the festering defilement spirits - just ordinary spirits, who selfishly try to make reinforce their natural influences to the point of imbalance) is a valid point of frustration and contention. Its also a valid recruiting tool (you don't have to pointlessly struggle - you can have badass blessing instead) - and therein is the real point of the Pure.<br /> They are <i>sympathetic antagonists</i>, and they are the most versatile group of enemies in Forsaken. The Pure actually have a lot going for them which a Forsaken might covet (and not desperate Forsaken, down and out on their sanity - just about all of them): large tightly-knit packs, no infighting between tribes, no endless struggle against the spirit world, no need for self restraint. You can be a BAMF, and your 'religion' says you were in the right - which is nice than constant guilt for patricide and world breaking, even if you don't buy into it overmuch.<br /> The Pure can run the full spectrum of occasional ally to baby-raping monsters if the storyteller wants. But. When they are allies, they are with extreme tension and open hatred toward the players. When they are absolute monsters, they're more like playground bullies than Lovecraftian psychos - you can understand how they got there, you can understand the satisfaction they get from it, and you can imagine what it would take for you to join them. But their true role is as an enemy which is terrifying and truly in conflict with the players as a matter of course, but which <i>aren't</i> irrationally so - they can be negotiated with, even allied with if its truly handled well, and which present a truly tempting group to join if you let them tell their version of it.<br /> <br /> As a story element, the role the Pure occupy is distinct and bloody amazing. They are my favorite antagonist to use, and I don't feel a need for them to be revised at all (though I certainly won't object to them being given more attention).<br /> <br /> As for the Pure's in-character reasons for hatred and continuing the war, they are every bit as widely varied and complicated as an individual might have. Its not all about an ancient feud, but frankly, their version of the myth gives them good reasons: their totems were the Eldest, the Youngest, and the Weakest of the firstborn, who had the most to lose; they tried to stop Father Wolf's murder, but were too few to succeed - but they were still punished equally as much... and then Mother sided with the <i>murderers</i>; they know the true nature of werewolves - the greatest predators, the value of Faith and Truth in a shamanistic world, and how to be masters over humans and oneself. In the generational war, the Pure have taken the same grievous losses as the Forsaken, and have no reason to break bread with people who slander them constantly and murder them on sight. But when you get down to a personal level - &quot;how does that Predator King pack feel about one Forsaken one&quot; or how does an individual regard another - that can vary from zealous hatred, to no hard feelings at all, to genuinely wanting unity and friendship (in fact, that's a key belief of the Fire Touched).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> TLDR: They are an amazing antagonist. Seriously, read their book, especially the sections on what social pressures they use to enforce the conflict, and every line about how they make up religious bile that makes a good rallying cry, but are really acting for petty craven politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 01-05-2014, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T14:27:46-08:00","id":43128,"title":"","content":"Is all this hostility really necessary? What happened to polite, civilized discourse oh wait I forgot what game this forum is for. Unbridled aggression and savagery it is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that you would have a point about how long the whole Forsaken/Pure conflict has lasted, Ghost, except for one thing. You're forgetting the supernatural factors in the feud between the Forsaken and the Pure. The fact that spirits are shaped by belief and can shape the world in ways both subtle and overt in turn means that the truth of the feud's origins is both impossible to know and completely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Firstborn are just a bunch of rival wolf spirits, and there never was a Father Wolf. Maybe there was, but the story has been distorted over time. And who knows which came first, the Forsaken/Pure conflict or the conflict between the Firstborn? It doesn't matter. The Firstborn themselves wouldn't be able to tell you the difference at this point. They've become as much the embodiment of the Uratha cultural identity as anything else, so their memories of the past and their agenda for the future are strongly informed by what the Uratha think they are. And the Firstborn enforce that history, and that agenda, through their patronage and manipulation of the tribes. It's a self-reinforcing feedback loop: the Uratha continue their feud because the Firstborn want them to, and the Firstborn want them to because the Uratha continue their feud.<br /> <br /> There is, however, one aspect of the Pure that I don't get. This may be because I have only a passing familiarity with Werewolf; this may have been explained in a book I haven't read yet. Or maybe it's something that should be perfectly obvious but that hasn't clicked for me, for some reason.<br /> <br /> In any case: Why do the Pure have such clear advantages over the Forsaken? Why do they outnumber the Forsaken so severely? Why don't they suffer the Forsaken's issues with in-fighting? Given that the Pure don't even try to reign in their predatory/bestial/monstrous nature, one would think that they'd attract more trouble from non-Forsaken, non-spirit sources such as hunters, mages, vampires, and the like; shouldn't this mitigate their advantages? (Or if other gamelines aren't in the picture, even just modern civilization.) That's not even getting into the fact that if the Idigam are going to be a bigger presence in the Idigam Chronicles (as seems likely), their spirit patrons and allies become less of an advantage. There are <i>things</i> out there that can make the Shadow every bit as perilous for the Pure as for the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> If there are explanations for all of this, I'd like to see them right there in the revised core. (Also right here in this thread, if anyone is willing to explain.) Conversely, if there aren't adequate reasons for this, I'd like to see the Pure revised so that they're roughly on par with the Forsaken, or at least not in a position of such <i>overwhelming</i> advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:19:21-08:00","id":43159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=43128#post43128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case: Why do the Pure have such clear advantages over the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Amazingly, being part of the faction that supports the Shadow's interests over the material world's tends to result in marginally better relationships with the Shadow's constituents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do they outnumber the Forsaken so severely? </div> </div> </div>Conversion and environmental factors. It ebbs and flows based largely on how much of a mess a given part of the world is in at any given moment. The United Kingdom's Pure are actually the minority, though they have the preferred territories and the country's got more pressing problems like a surfeit of Bale Hounds and history literally spilling over itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why don't they suffer the Forsaken's issues with in-fighting? </div> </div> </div>United front against the Forsaken mixed with a cultural emphasis on &quot;The Low Honor the High&quot; over &quot;The High Respect the Low.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that the Pure don't even try to reign in their predatory/bestial/monstrous nature </div> </div> </div>Bzzt. The Pure are not Zi'ir and view low Harmony with roughly the same pity and disdain as the Forsaken, with minor mitigating circumstances like &quot;this is what the Urdaga have driven us to.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not even getting into the fact that if the Idigam are going to be a bigger presence in the Idigam Chronicles (as seems likely), their spirit patrons and allies become less of an advantage. </div> </div> </div>Out-of-context problem does not render the established threats less threatening except by distraction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there are explanations for all of this, I'd like to see them right there in the revised core. </div> </div> </div>Most of the things you're confused about as concerns the Pure are covered in the sourcebook that shares their name, so I'm going to take this as another tally under my primary issue of &quot;Consolidate all the important information about the things that are getting pagespace.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:34:28-08:00","id":43169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=43159#post43159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bzzt. The Pure are not Zi'ir and view low Harmony with roughly the same pity and disdain as the Forsaken, with minor mitigating circumstances like &quot;this is what the Urdaga have driven us to.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Harmony doesn't have killing humans (if there is a real need) as a sin, even bestial werewolves who feel they should rule a wild kingdom can have high Harmony. Among other things, it's about balancing Man and Wolf, Flesh and Spirit. High Harmony doesn't at all mean a &quot;nicer&quot; werewolf, certainly; rather, it means a supernatural predator much more in tune with instinct, reason, spirit, tooth and claw. It means a werewolf with much greater control, even when &quot;control&quot; means letting the Rage flow like the blood from an opponent's throat through your jaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:35:39-08:00","id":43173,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Satchel. That does help. So apparently it's a mix of me working off of faulty information and having not read some key sourcebooks. And it does a lot for my suspension of disbelief to discover that the Pure/Forsaken disparity isn't a universal constant and can evidently vary quite a bit depending on time, place and cricumstances.<br /> <br /> (Although, point of order: I wasn't referring to Harmony with &quot;predatory/bestial/monstrous nature&quot; so much as lack of caution/fear/respect towards humanity; I had understood the Pure to have a contemptuous attitude toward the Herd and little interest in keeping a low profile from ordinary humans, which seems like it could present certain problems in the modern world. I would not be surprised to find that I was mistaken on this point as well, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 01-05-2014, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:42:45-08:00","id":43178,"title":"","content":"[Firstly - thank you, you were right to point out hostility. I didn't write that rant intending to be, but I'm passionate on the subject clearly; I've taken out any personal remarks, as those are not cool. I apologize, Ghost, if anything sounded directed at you personally.]<br /> <br /> <br /> To your questions, Exploding Frogs:<br /> <br /> The Pure, as a rule, do not always outnumber the Forsaken. Their book explains that their history has been a tide of back-and-forth every few decades. One side, in one area, gets a solid advantage (numerically and strategically and organizationally), then whatever problem that inspired this is solved, and they relax and fall to complacency and infighting. The other side takes advantage of that, and they switch places. The presentation assumes that things favor the Pure as a default in order to reinforce the Theme of the world being stacked against the players. However, there are reasons they generally have a numbers advantage: the Pure have exclusive rituals that reveal if a wolf-blooded will undergo the First Change, and to point them toward people currently having a First Change in their territory (which they keep <i>very </i>secret from Forsaken). So they usually get to new werewolves first.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reasons their tribes are more united (in general, because they do have inter-pack/tribe rivalry on occasion, but much less of it) is because that is a socially reinforced ideal. Their propaganda is that they are losing the conflict, regardless of the current situation - they lie about circumstances, rally around every fallen brother, bemoan the Moon and the Forsaken's spirit allies, and do everything else to keep the perspective in all of their minds that in order to survive they need to be united. Multi-tribal packs, regional alliances, and generous trade between packs are all things the Leadership encourages in order to keep the bond - as is psychological torture to develop dependency in their recruits. Like the Forsaken, usually only a serious regional threat really rallies them to a united front, but unlike the Forsaken, they have widespread practices designed to reinforce and keep the bond after the threat is dealt with.<br /> <br /> <br /> How they avoid attracting attention varies between Tribes (and is kind of accidental).<br /> The Ivory Claws are very, very internally focused - purity of the tribe and its bloodline, purity of the self and body - with a lot of time-consuming private practices to make them the Purest of the Pure. They are the least populated Pure tribe, and they're the leaders, and they're elitist jerks. So, in all they don't do much that attracts overmuch attention.<br /> One of the driving goals of the Fire Touched is recruitment, so they work hard to present their best image; they make themselves visible to the Forsaken, and make themselves look respectable and admirable in order to get people to join. The side-effect is that other factions only see that image as well, when they see it at all. While the Fire Touched do like to do things like infect people with serious disease and set them on fire as a matter of practicing their faith, they do these things in seclusion where it won't discourage recruits - they only display these things to other Pure, where it makes a good rallying cry.<br /> And the Predator Kings, well, they tend to be rather remote from most perspectives. Their tribal ban is &quot;honor no tool of human craft&quot;. While some live in the cities, its very uncommon, and those guys <i>do </i>attract a lot of attention. Most of the tribe keeps to the wilds, except on hunting incursions where they use stealth and overwhelming force to take out their targets (like good wolves do).<br /> <br /> It balances out to them not necessarily getting any more noticed than Forsaken as a monster that needs to die. There are things that still make life perilous, but bigger packs, better totem benefits, and stronger spirit allies do become advantageous in the face of that sort of thing. Not always - idigam do wreck their day - but in those cases, no one is really in a good position.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bear in mind, all that is just the default. There are always good reasons for this to not work out - but wouldn't those reasons make an interesting story, more than an interesting status quo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:45:46-08:00","id":43180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=43173#post43173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Although, point of order: I wasn't referring to Harmony with &quot;predatory/bestial/monstrous nature&quot; so much as lack of caution/fear/respect towards humanity; I had understood the Pure to have a contemptuous attitude toward the Herd and little interest in keeping a low profile from ordinary humans, which seems like it could present certain problems in the modern world. I would not be surprised to find that I was mistaken on this point as well, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the Anshega's Oath of Urfarah differs slightly on a number of points from the Urdaga's Oath of the Moon, &quot;The Herd Must Not Know&quot; is a shared tenet between the two and both Oaths contain elements that demonstrate werewolf culture's understanding of Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T15:49:55-08:00","id":43184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=43173#post43173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Satchel. That does help. So apparently it's a mix of me working off of faulty information and having not read some important sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> (Although, point of order: I wasn't referring to Harmony with &quot;predatory/bestial/monstrous nature&quot; so much as lack of caution/fear/respect towards humanity; I had understood the Pure to have a contemptuous attitude toward the Herd and little interest in keeping a low profile from ordinary humans, which seems like it could present certain problems in the modern world. I would not be surprised to find that I was mistaken on this point as well, though.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are cattle. They're prey. That they should &quot;rule&quot; this world is an affront to Father Wolf, to the Pure. <i>We </i>are the greatest predators to ever hunt. <i>We </i>are the strong, and <i>we </i>should rule the weak. This ... this <i>mockery</i> of natural order is a testament to the greatest sin of our estranged kindred. <i>They </i>sundered hunter's Paradise, and <i>they </i>allowed humans to spread like rats in a world still trembling at the passing of Urfarah. Now we're too few to take back what belongs to <i>us</i>. What is rightfully <i>ours</i>. We can't tear down these false jungles of concrete and steel, filled with the odor of prey grown fat and stupid inside their walls. They've forgotten the fear of howls in the valley. They've forgotten what it means to be strong, even for prey, as is the way of things. No, we can't tear <i>them </i>down, but we <i>can </i>tear down the traitorous curs who brought about this imbalance. We <i>can </i>demonstrate our devotion to Urfarah's memory by staining the earth where his bones lie in the blood of the Forsaken. And perhaps when we are finished, Father himself will take notice and wake from death itself, having conquered the one killer <i>no </i>predator escapes. If he doesn't, <i>we </i>will take what is <i>ours </i>when we tear down the wall between worlds.<br /> <br /> First the wall between flesh and <i>Hisil </i>comes down, then the walls behind which the cattle cower.<br /> <br /> \u2014Marcus Stokes-the-Fire, a Fire-Touched tribe leader","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T13:07:40-08:00","id":48427,"title":"","content":"Some basic things I think would make WtF a bit more interesting <b>for me</b>:<br /> <br /> 1. Increased emphasis on &quot;The Pack&quot; over &quot;Garuru&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> While I am a <i>huge</i> fan of Werewolf: The Apocalypse, I'm cool with the &quot;War Form&quot; of a <i>Uratha</i> no longer being the absolute avatar of Killfuck Soulshitter that it once was. The Stat increases are fine with me (although I'd be fine with 9- and 8- Again on Strength/Intimidation checks while in non-human and non-wolf forms) as they are and I don't think that they require any alterations. However, I'd <i>love</i> to see the <i>Uratha</i> gain a comprehensive &quot;pack tactics&quot; system in place <i>at least</i> on the level of HtV's Tactic's system. Although, something new would be neat as well, giving <i>Uratha</i> a near (or blatantly) supernatural pack &quot;mind.&quot;</div> <br /> 2. Changes to &quot;Totem&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> I'm not really much of a fan of the Totem Merit as it stands (and has stood since WtA). It's, essentially, a Merit/Exp sink <b>in my eyes</b>. I would, instead, like to see (as was suggested before) the pack's Totem &quot;evolve&quot; out of their shared experiences and via Forsaken Culture and Rituals. Perhaps as the Pack defeats enemies, increases their territory, performs Pack, Tribal, and Forsaken rites and rituals, and adheres to Tribal and Pack Bans, the Totem grows in power (perhaps via some Totemic XP system used only for this purpose), increasing the Pack's status (or Status) in the eyes of their fellow Forsaken (i.e. as a replacement for the current Renown system). <br /> <br /> The Pack's unity and sense of interconnection would draw directly from their connection to the Totem, which makes it especially dangerous when the Totem becomes manipulative or corrupt in some manner. The only way for a Pack to combat their Totem, a spirit connected to every Uratha in the Pack, would be for them to sever their ties with it and hunt it down like any other spirit (albeit a dangerous one who knows everything about the Pack). This would hurt the Pack's &quot;renown&quot; (if using the idea above), as their job as a Pack would include keeping their Totem in line. </div> <br /> 3. Changes to &quot;Harmony&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> First off, I'm not too huge a fan of calling it &quot;Harmony,&quot; as it, <b>to me</b>, dulls some of the razor edge from the game itself. Secondly, I don't like that there is a difference between &quot;Harmony&quot; and the Oath of the Moon. If anything, I'd like to see the Oath become the bulk of the Uratha's new &quot;Integry&quot; Stat, with additional inclusions based on &quot;Nation&quot; (Forsaken/Pure/Bale Hound), &quot;Tribe,&quot; and, potentially, &quot;Lodge.&quot; <br /> <br /> Another route they could take is remove &quot;Harmony<i>&quot; </i>from the picture entirely, instituting a series of major and minor Bans and Banes in its wake. As the PCs deal with Spirits and/or make Spirit enemies, they would potentially acquire new Bans and Banes in exchange for favors, &quot;gifts,&quot; and/or as punishment by powerful spirits/tribal or local <i>Uratha</i> leaders for indiscretions. This would take the place of the regular &quot;downward spiral&quot; effect of <i>Humanity </i>and <i>Integrity</i>. Of course, these Bans and Banes would not be permanent, but could be &quot;worked off,&quot; so to speak.</div> <br /> 4. Changes to &quot;Gifts&quot;<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> I'd like to see the general system for Gifts shift away from the WtA/previous model. I, personally, would like to see Gifts as something learned &quot;in-house&quot; between pack and tribal members, with <i>Uratha</i> going to Spirits for such knowledge only out of desperation or greed. A Spirit World actively hostile towards the PCs should not be absolutely required to gain the powers described within the book. Pacts with Spirits (or, at least, WtF Spirits) for Favors and Gifts should be a faustian bargain, not a transaction in payment for chiminage. <br /> <br /> I also think it would be neat if Gifts were less like regular powers and abilities and more like Conditions and Tilts. You learn a gift for, like, 3 or 4 Experiences and then, to use it, there is an &quot;Activation&quot; action that, well, <i>activates</i> the Gift. This levies some sort of effect on either the PC or the &quot;battlefield&quot; in some way that remains in effect until the &quot;deactivation&quot; effect occurs. Of course, Essence could be spent in lieu of the &quot;activation&quot; action.</div> <br /> 5. Changes to the <i>Uratha</i> Template<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> Like I mentioned above, I don't mind that the <i>Uratha</i> were &quot;slimmed down&quot; compared to the Garou, but these alterations should have been coupled with increased mechanical support for Pack Tactics from the outset. Another aspect that I don't mind the inclusion of is the &quot;time bomb&quot; aspect of Garuru form. In terms of &quot;buffing&quot; the <i>Uratha</i>, I would like to see the use of this form gain a few additional things: all non-Aggravated Damage is immediately healed, &quot;Garou&quot; Regeneration, and this form is effectively immortal barring damage caused by Banes (such as Silver). Going into Garuru (assuming the rules requiring constant movement toward a target and limited time frame remain in place) should feel like a game changer. Silver shouldn't just be &quot;handy&quot; when taking down a raging Garuru form werewolf, it should be <i>mandatory</i>. This extreme increase in regenerative ability (but only in this form) is what I consider an offset to the Vampire's new &quot;all weapons are Bashing&quot; alteration.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I feel that all Uratha who hit their last Health Box (or beyond) via non-Aggravated damage should get a Stamina + Survival + Primal Urge roll to automatically shapeshift into this form (forgive me if this rule, or something like it, already exists... I don't have a book handy). </div> <br /> As for what I'd like to see in the actual &quot;plotline&quot; of the book... I've got no suggestions. If you folks are doing the same level of superior work as you did with the GMC and BAS, I'll be more than happy. <br /> <br /> Love, Peace, and Chicken Grease,<br /> The Mighty Grendel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1931-the-mighty-grendel","name":"The Mighty Grendel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1931_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T21:35:44-08:00","id":49556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=43184#post43184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humans are cattle. They're prey. That they should &quot;rule&quot; this world is an affront to Father Wolf, to the Pure. <i>We </i>are the greatest predators to ever hunt. <i>We </i>are the strong, and <i>we </i>should rule the weak. This ... this <i>mockery</i> of natural order is a testament to the greatest sin of our estranged kindred. <i>They </i>sundered hunter's Paradise, and <i>they </i>allowed humans to spread like rats in a world still trembling at the passing of Urfarah. Now we're too few to take back what belongs to <i>us</i>. What is rightfully <i>ours</i>. We can't tear down these false jungles of concrete and steel, filled with the odor of prey grown fat and stupid inside their walls. They've forgotten the fear of howls in the valley. They've forgotten what it means to be strong, even for prey, as is the way of things. No, we can't tear <i>them </i>down, but we <i>can </i>tear down the traitorous curs who brought about this imbalance. We <i>can </i>demonstrate our devotion to Urfarah's memory by staining the earth where his bones lie in the blood of the Forsaken. And perhaps when we are finished, Father himself will take notice and wake from death itself, having conquered the one killer <i>no </i>predator escapes. If he doesn't, <i>we </i>will take what is <i>ours </i>when we tear down the wall between worlds.<br /> <br /> First the wall between flesh and <i>Hisil </i>comes down, then the walls behind which the cattle cower.<br /> <br /> \u2014Marcus Stokes-the-Fire, a Fire-Touched tribe leader</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/611/648/000.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T12:33:10-08:00","id":49975,"title":"","content":"Don't forget, as well, that there very may well be Pure that don't fully agree with the dogma. They still do it anyway. Pure Packs are a lot like gangs (well Forsaken packs are too...) in that once you are inducted, there is really only room for duty. Between most wolves not living too long due to the nature of their lives of fury, members who already have blood lust on their brain who may or may not be legit angry over the Father Wolf fiasco, and combine that with powerful spirits who are the masters of that pack. Its easy to see why the hatred continues. <br /> <br /> They are controlled by Spirits and are themselves half Spirit. It seems natural for one to hate the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T20:05:19-08:00","id":51318,"title":"","content":"Along with what has be said above I would like to see something more about the importance of Packs. We know it's a Harmony sin to be a lone wolf but I want to see more into the value/build of a pack.<br /> <br /> Alter the duration of the change. I don't want the way it was in Apocalypse but the fact it last all of a minute or two..That's not really threatening. An hour or two or if it's their auspice moon out then it last as long as the moon is up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:59:35-08:00","id":54847,"title":"","content":"The thing that I would most like to see is foremost a more concrete version of some tribal bans. I have hard time to get my head around the Blood Talons' for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:40:45-08:00","id":55102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=54847#post54847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that I would most like to see is foremost a more concrete version of some tribal bans. I have hard time to get my head around the Blood Talons' for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was both intentional and beneficial. I like that the tribal bans are up to interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T04:47:16-08:00","id":56046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=51318#post51318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along with what has be said above I would like to see something more about the importance of Packs. We know it's a Harmony sin to be a lone wolf but I want to see more into the value/build of a pack.<br /> <br /> Alter the duration of the change. I don't want the way it was in Apocalypse but the fact it last all of a minute or two..That's not really threatening. An hour or two or if it's their auspice moon out then it last as long as the moon is up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yar. Pack tactics, Merits and abilities based off of pack hunting/activity (maybe some Gifts have pack synergy), and fun, detailed hunting rules. Hunting should be something you look forward to doing in game because it tells a story in howls and heartbeats, mud and bone and snapping fangs. Werewolves communicate on the hunt. Each kind of prey is different, offering its own challenges. Hunting shouldn't be just another extended action. It should be its own mini-game, rewarding in its own right.<br /> <br /> Re: Gauru form duration<br /> <br /> As I've mentioned here before, I see two ways to go about it. Either the form is limited and dangerous in proportion to that limitation, or it's not so hindered but not as powerful, either. I'm all for it remaining of very limited duration, but being a complete killing machine while it lasts. I would be okay with it not being a nuclear option and lasting longer (for a scene, for instance), but I think a brief, bloody eruption of Rage fits the game better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:21:45-08:00","id":56180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=55102#post55102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that was both intentional and beneficial. I like that the tribal bans are up to interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Entirely possible but in that case some suggested ways to interperate them should be included. The Fire-touched and the Predator Kings gets all easy to understand Banes. I don't see why the rest of them can't get some that won't leave the ST scratching his head and trying to understand them himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:29:46-08:00","id":56189,"title":"","content":"I didn't think they were that bad, which one are you having trouble understanding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T09:58:25-08:00","id":56204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=56180#post56180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Entirely possible but in that case some suggested ways to interperate them should be included. The Fire-touched and the Predator Kings gets all easy to understand Banes. I don't see why the rest of them can't get some that won't leave the ST scratching his head and trying to understand them himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read Tribes of the Moon? There's a pretty good section on what &quot;Offer No Surrender That You Would Not Accept&quot; means. I'll have to check to see if the other Tribal Bans get similar treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T10:11:39-08:00","id":56211,"title":"","content":"To Oriares: I have it but I have not read it yet.<br /> <br /> I will check it out, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T06:18:56-08:00","id":57378,"title":"","content":"Make it more of a game about werewolves, that I think is really the most important point and both Apocalypse AND Forsaken failed to be one so far in many ways.<br /> <br /> I personally think that in many ways, books like skinchangers did more to be about the idea of a werewolf then Werewolf itself did.<br /> <br /> Vampire managed to do archetypes of vampire legends and vampire fiction, and blood and smoke included the kind of vampires that were left out.<br /> Werwolf needs that, to feel more connected with the different ideas people have about werewolves.<br /> <br /> Make the kind of film werewolf, the out of control, the killing machine a type of antagonist, or something you could become, but focus on the way were animals work around the world, of the connection with magic, curses, divine punishment, being descended from a &quot;god&quot; of sorts...<br /> <br /> All those could have been very colourful backgrounds instead of the rather bland tribes and mostly functionary auspices.<br /> <br /> Make the game strongly about being part human and part wolf and that means actual wolves.<br /> I often found the way wolves are represented in both gamelines to be rather lacking, it felt more like generic monster and weird spirit...<br /> <br /> The shadow, the animism that does fit with werewolves quite well, but I think the spirit world often felt more weird and freaky than, well, something natural, which it should be (there is a lot of horror in that, when you use it!).<br /> I think many eastern media just do that kind of thing better given that belief in spirits, minor gods and similar is still very much a part of such cultures.<br /> A bit less of Geiger and body horror and some more Asian themed horror elements of spirits and possession.<br /> And since there is that weird problem of spirits both all hating you and being the one source of power, why not just ditch the hatred and focus on the fact that spirits are DIFFERENT, alien with very peculiar interests.<br /> Cultures are full of malevolent spirits or just strange ones, keep that duality.<br /> Really, a spirit world more based on the Japanese concept of Yokai, Ayakashi and similar would be a perfect fit that can be very scary without all of it hating you.<br /> <br /> In addition, use the human element more!<br /> <br /> The werewolf as the other, the one who is different, who might be feared, persecuted, unable to really be a part of society, there is a lot of potential in that which is way too often killed of with lunacy and similar which make human opponents less dangerous.<br /> There has been such a rich history of &quot;werewolves&quot;, like witches, being prosecuted, do something with the fear of being turned upon.<br /> Even if you go berserk and kill loads of people, they might come back.<br /> And next time they might kill you.<br /> I found that werewolf tries too much to make all the horror you face come from spirits and all the horror you embody from being a violent monster.<br /> But you really SHOULD be drawn between what you grew up with as a human, your instincts as a wolf and what living in a world full of dangerous spirits and other enemies demands of you.<br /> I hated harmony because it just catapults you away from human values and ignores the interesting conflict of the dual nature and instead ingraining upon you a code of behaviour that feels neither really like wolf nor human nor anything.<br /> <br /> You should really get to care about how difficult it is to retain some of what it means to be human.<br /> <br /> Another thing to explore more would be the ties between humans and wolves.<br /> There is just so much to be done with that, to explain why werewolves are the most common werecreatures, to play with the theme of the early most history of how men domesticated wolves, how they share so many similarities in their social life...<br /> <br /> Make the rage more of an understandable emotional reaction, werewolf often feels like it just slaps a &quot;choleric&quot; sticker on everyone.<br /> You can built rage so nicely as blind panic, as lashing out, as just a mechanism to cope when things become too much, make it more of an instinct, stress how it is necessary to keep you fighting, and not just everyone being a berserker with bad temper.<br /> <br /> And discard the canonical sanctity of the father wolf story from the core book.<br /> Having it presented as the exact and true account of how werewolves came to be just kills the mystery and kills the suspense.<br /> Vampires get so many different interesting origin stories, divine curses, ancient goddesses and monsters, werewolves?<br /> A furry Oedipus myth...<br /> No, even Blasphemies did not fix that issue quite well...<br /> <br /> I also think the big world wide groupings are not too great.<br /> Werewolves operate on a pack basis, they do not even have the sept like in Apocalypse, tribes do hardly make much sense at all.<br /> Reimagining tribes as a sort of &quot;origin&quot; which could make use of there into being one single origin of all werewolves might work better and many of the big global inter werewolf conflicts could just as well be dropped, or be left open for storytellers to use or discard.<br /> <br /> Discarding the taboo of werewolves not being able to mate would also work nicely, it could strengthen the idea of packs as families, quite like a wolfpack where young wolves go out and form their own.<br /> That way, one could also bring back the idea of Metis and Lupus, just, please, with a bit more interesting implementation, with more of an emphasis on inclination towards one or the other half, wolf or man or inbetween.<br /> <br /> All in all, don't waste the opportunity to make it a game that feels more thematic and easier to work in existing story concepts ike it was done with Changeling for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T08:09:55-08:00","id":57443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=57378#post57378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And discard the canonical sanctity of the father wolf story from the core book.<br /> Having it presented as the exact and true account of how werewolves came to be just kills the mystery and kills the suspense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more of Werewolf I've read over the last year the more hilarious this sentiment becomes to me.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is basically second only to Geist in how much acknowledgement it gives to the relative unprovability of any given creation myth. Blasphemies aside, War Against the Pure explicitly brings up the possibility the tribes are not as old as they seem as well as a sidebar highlighting the lack of distinction between &quot;factual&quot; and &quot;fictional&quot; origins, Shadows of the U.K. not only has its Highborn and Commoners take on the difference between the Forsaken and the Pure but it gives the Beshilu a semicoherent <i>religion</i>, and <i>everywhere</i> there are conflicting legends with mutually contradictory claims of truth if taken as historical accounts.<br /> <br /> Spirits echo back the Father Wolf myth because they're talking to werewolves that keep repeating it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, another stick for the &quot;consolidate information&quot; woodpile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires get so many different interesting origin stories, divine curses, ancient goddesses and monsters, werewolves?<br /> A furry Oedipus myth\u2026 </div> </div> </div>You have just proven that you have no idea what the story of Oedipus was about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:21:22-08:00","id":57469,"title":"","content":"Funny, you only seem to support the argument then that it should not be depicted as completely true in the new chronicle then.<br /> The fact is however that the Core and many more books explicitly describe it (even in passages clearly intended for the storyteller only, as in Skinchangers for example) or at least certain aspects as true.<br /> <br /> Arguing that it is not so based on those books is not much different from saying that the tennets of harmony do not ban werewolves mating because it is one of the chroniclers guide options.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as far as the Oedipus symbolism goes, sorry, but I think you should either reread your mythology, your history of psychology or your Forsaken corebook if you miss out the parallels...<br /> The sin of patricide, the punishment for the sin, the allusions to father wolf lording the right to mate over his children, the persistent issue of linking relationships among werewolves to incest...<br /> I think basing a fantasy concept on pseudoscience can be enjoyable, but the time were using Freudian themes to stand out as controversial or similar are over and good riddance to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T14:54:14-08:00","id":57665,"title":"","content":"Note: the fact that storyteller begins their stories as &quot;This is true&quot; doesn't means it always is.<br /> <br /> *Obligatory mumbling about people who doesn't have a grasp on the setting wanting changes which already are present in the supplements.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:16:55-08:00","id":58163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=57665#post57665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: the fact that storyteller begins their stories as &quot;This is true&quot; doesn't means it always is.<br /> <br /> *Obligatory mumbling about people who doesn't have a grasp on the setting wanting changes which already are present in the supplements.*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you directing the second part at me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:48:45-08:00","id":58181,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure it was aimed at Ray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:09:42-08:00","id":58722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=57469#post57469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as far as the Oedipus symbolism goes, sorry, but I think you should either reread your mythology, your history of psychology or your Forsaken corebook if you miss out the parallels...<br /> The sin of patricide, the punishment for the sin, the allusions to father wolf lording the right to mate over his children, the persistent issue of linking relationships among werewolves to incest...<br /> I think basing a fantasy concept on pseudoscience can be enjoyable, but the time were using Freudian themes to stand out as controversial or similar are over and good riddance to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) Oedipus is not mythology, it's theatre/literature.<br /> B) Father Wolf never had anything about the right to mate.<br /> C) All werewolves are descended from the First Pack who all had the same parents. What would YOU call it besides &quot;incest&quot;?<br /> D) Patricide and the consequences are older and more persistent that just Oedipus and are all frickin' over the place in mythology.<br /> E) What pseudo-science are you talking about?<br /> F) What controversial themes are you talking about?<br /> <br /> And, as far as your earlier post, all I can say about that one is to re-examine the Forsaken books. Curses, descended from gods, raging out of control, the dichotomy of man and beast......it's all there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T09:42:02-08:00","id":58800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=58722#post58722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) Oedipus is not mythology, it's theatre/literature.<br /> B) Father Wolf never had anything about the right to mate.<br /> C) All werewolves are descended from the First Pack who all had the same parents. What would YOU call it besides &quot;incest&quot;?<br /> D) Patricide and the consequences are older and more persistent that just Oedipus and are all frickin' over the place in mythology.<br /> E) What pseudo-science are you talking about?<br /> F) What controversial themes are you talking about?<br /> <br /> And, as far as your earlier post, all I can say about that one is to re-examine the Forsaken books. Curses, descended from gods, raging out of control, the dichotomy of man and beast......it's all there.</div> </div> </div> </div>A. Oedipus is both. The play was based on the myth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:45:19-08:00","id":58876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=58722#post58722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B) Father Wolf never had anything about the right to mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ray is monofocusing on this bit from the corebook's section on Harmony that's never mentioned again thereafter:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once, only Father Wolf had rights and privileges to take mates, privileges he denied to his werewolf children. It\u2019s said that Father Wolf even lorded that right over the People, taunting them with his authority. Denied and insulted, the People claimed the right from their harsh Father and slew him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Astute readers will notice that a) this reading has more to do with Freud's notion of the Oedipus complex \u2014 the pseudoscience he was blathering about \u2014 than the actual myth of Oedipus \u2014 the First Pack knew who Urfarah was, no prophecy was involved save for the supposed nature of Father Wolf's ban, and Luna's involvement in the common tale is limited to having the first werewolves sired upon her by Father Wolf and cursing the species after his death, which is hardly analogous to marriage, much less sexual relations \u2014 and b) the reading of this as the reason the First Pack slew their father is in contradiction to the story Ray is claiming as monolithic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T11:59:11-08:00","id":58968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=58876#post58876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ray is monofocusing on this bit from the corebook's section on Harmony that's never mentioned again thereafter:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once, only Father Wolf had rights and privileges to take mates, privileges he denied to his werewolf children. It\u2019s said that Father Wolf even lorded that right over the People, taunting them with his authority. Denied and insulted, the People claimed the right from their harsh Father and slew him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Astute readers will notice that a) this reading has more to do with Freud's notion of the Oedipus complex \u2014 the pseudoscience he was blathering about \u2014 than the actual myth of Oedipus \u2014 the First Pack knew who Urfarah was, no prophecy was involved save for the supposed nature of Father Wolf's ban, and Luna's involvement in the common tale is limited to having the first werewolves sired upon her by Father Wolf and cursing the species after his death, which is hardly analogous to marriage, much less sexual relations \u2014 and b) the reading of this as the reason the First Pack slew their father is in contradiction to the story Ray is claiming as monolithic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew that was in there somewhere, but I couldn't remember where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:10:18-08:00","id":59056,"title":"","content":"Remembered two things I REALLY wanna see in the Idigam Chronicles:<br /> <br /> Splat pages by Abrar Ajmal and chapter intro pages by Ron Spencer! Pretty please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:50:51-08:00","id":59097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=58722#post58722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C) All werewolves are descended from the First Pack who all had the same parents. What would YOU call it besides &quot;incest&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are all descended from the same ancestors, too. I think after a certain point \u2014 by which I mean &quot;eons&quot; \u2014 common ancestor parents has to stop mattering, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Mind you, that is not taking into account spirits and shapeshifting supernatural beasts, either, so....<br /> <br /> Although I'm a fan of the &quot;forbidden love&quot; stories in <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Werewolf</b></span>, but not, um, if they're basically boiled down to &quot;incest.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You know how it works! We're both of the People. We can never be together!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You know how it works! We're brother and sister. We can never be together!&quot;<br /> <br /> One has an ancient, tragic curse born of the supernatural to reinforce the taboo. The other is just disturbing, and not in a fun way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remembered two things I REALLY wanna see in the Idigam Chronicles:<br /> <br /> Splat pages by Abrar Ajmal and chapter intro pages by Ron Spencer! Pretty please. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>love</i> Ron Spencer's art. To me, it's the definitive <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Werewolf </b></span>art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:18:13-08:00","id":59129,"title":"","content":"I think you could easily have forbidden love stories by having lovers from seperate politically opposed tribes, potentially a Pure/Forsaken coupling. You could remove the incest angle entirely and still have fraught love stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:22:33-08:00","id":59135,"title":"","content":"Rival packs, even. Packs aren't always real friendly toward one another, and it'd be much like lovers in two rival gangs. Or families.<br /> <br /> WereRomeo and WolfJuliet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:44:07-08:00","id":59155,"title":"","content":"I think the only reason the devs made Werewolf mating a taboo is so that Werewolf numbers don't exceed humanity's numbers. Personally, I'm not a fan of the Black Birth. I thought it was a cool idea at first, but now, like the Gauru form's stupid drawbacks, I'm all for getting rid of it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:45:52-08:00","id":59158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=59097#post59097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are all descended from the same ancestors, too. I think after a certain point \u2014 by which I mean &quot;eons&quot; \u2014 common ancestor parents has to stop mattering, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> Mind you, that is not taking into account spirits and shapeshifting supernatural beasts, either, so\u2026.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded, for some reason, of the romantic complications of reincarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T14:48:16-08:00","id":59162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=59135#post59135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rival packs, even. Packs aren't always real friendly toward one another, and it'd be much like lovers in two rival gangs. Or families.<br /> <br /> WereRomeo and WolfJuliet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time someone brings that up, I always point to the fiction from <b>Predators </b>and <b>The Rage</b>. It's there, but dammit, Forsaken seems to have really suffered from not having certain things emphasized.<br /> <br /> Just thinking......there's so much that they made possible in Forsaken. Maybe that's the problem: they had too many possibilities given in the corebook to give enough time to any one thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T15:00:03-08:00","id":59169,"title":"","content":"Double checking to see if I'm missing anything-have the Devs started doing open development like Blood and Smoke, or has everything been hush hush?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T15:12:47-08:00","id":59187,"title":"","content":"Apparently there will be a blog, it just hasn't started yet (and will likely not be as active as Bailey's).<br /> There's been very little information given out, except Harmony is being redone, gifts are a big area to fix, and they're really emphasizing the hunt, rather than the kill that Apocalypse focused on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:00:51-08:00","id":59234,"title":"","content":"I can't guarantee I'll be working on <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Idigam Chronicles</b></span> (though I still really want to), but if I do, I'll be giving regular updates myself, at least on what I can.<br /> <br /> Papa Bear, yes, there are a lot of possibilities in <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b></span>, but I think the problem isn't one of quantity. Look at how great <span style=\"color:#990000\"><b>Blood &amp; Smoke: The Strix Chronicles </b></span>turned out. All the potential was there in <span style=\"color:#990000\"><b>Requiem</b></span>, it was just in need of revision, reorganization, a bit of polish, all of which benefits from experience. It'll be the same thing for <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Idigam Chronicles</b></span>. It'll be able to include so much, and with a focus on conciseness and clarity and proper organization, it'll be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T08:48:44-08:00","id":59851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=58876#post58876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ray is monofocusing on this bit from the corebook's section on Harmony that's never mentioned again thereafter:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once, only Father Wolf had rights and privileges to take mates, privileges he denied to his werewolf children. It\u2019s said that Father Wolf even lorded that right over the People, taunting them with his authority. Denied and insulted, the People claimed the right from their harsh Father and slew him.&quot;<br /> <br /> Astute readers will notice that a) this reading has more to do with Freud's notion of the Oedipus complex \u2014 the pseudoscience he was blathering about \u2014 than the actual myth of Oedipus \u2014 the First Pack knew who Urfarah was, no prophecy was involved save for the supposed nature of Father Wolf's ban, and Luna's involvement in the common tale is limited to having the first werewolves sired upon her by Father Wolf and cursing the species after his death, which is hardly analogous to marriage, much less sexual relations \u2014 and b) the reading of this as the reason the First Pack slew their father is in contradiction to the story Ray is claiming as monolithic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least I do not have to stoop to personal attacks...<br /> <br /> It is pretty silly to argue over whether the Oedipus myth, both in its standard form (it is one of the few patricidal myths that actually adds a moral element of guilt, unlike, say Kronos and Uranos) and its use in psychoanalysis influenced the Father Wolf myth, as the Core Book clearly shows the parallels.<br /> <br /> Later books not following up on it as much is besides the point, I think expressing not wanting it to that extend in the Idigam Chronicles is a valid opinion to express.<br /> <br /> I would rather have the stories from Blasphemies in instead of having elements of Father Wolf repeated all over the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T09:52:37-08:00","id":59910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=59851#post59851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather have the stories from Blasphemies in instead of having elements of Father Wolf repeated all over the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>A common people would have a common story and common myths that they tell.<br /> <br /> If there is no common story about the origins of Uratha, then they are not The People anymore, but many people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T22:04:30-08:00","id":60461,"title":"","content":"Part of me is wondering just how familiar Ray is with Native American storytelling as a craft and cultural tool. The function and approach of Uratha mythos is based quite a bit on that structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T08:03:34-08:00","id":60779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=60461#post60461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me is wondering just how familiar Ray is with Native American storytelling as a craft and cultural tool. The function and approach of Uratha mythos is based quite a bit on that structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not everybody gets the benefits of living out in the western US areas like us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, to elaborate on something I said earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=59097#post59097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Papa Bear, yes, there are a lot of possibilities in <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b></span>, but I think the problem isn't one of quantity. Look at how great <span style=\"color:#990000\"><b>Blood &amp; Smoke: The Strix Chronicles </b></span>turned out. All the potential was there in <span style=\"color:#990000\"><b>Requiem</b></span>, it was just in need of revision, reorganization, a bit of polish, all of which benefits from experience. It'll be the same thing for <span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>Idigam Chronicles</b></span>. It'll be able to include so much, and with a focus on conciseness and clarity and proper organization, it'll be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't actually <i>complaining </i>about the host of possibilities in <b>Forsaken</b>. More like I was lamenting on the lack of space to be able to flesh out all the options available. Some people have said they wanted more pack politics. It's in there. Others have said they wanted more about the raging beast/reasoning man. That's in there, too. There's options for so many variations on werewolves and shape-shifters that <i>no one thing </i>got enough coverage to really make it clear <b>it's in there</b> and how to make it work. The supplements did a lot of that work, sure, but when you're trying to get interested in the game, the corebook is always the first stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:25:54-08:00","id":61271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=60779#post60779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't actually <i>complaining </i>about the host of possibilities in <b>Forsaken</b>. More like I was lamenting on the lack of space to be able to flesh out all the options available. Some people have said they wanted more pack politics. It's in there. Others have said they wanted more about the raging beast/reasoning man. That's in there, too. There's options for so many variations on werewolves and shape-shifters that <i>no one thing </i>got enough coverage to really make it clear <b>it's in there</b> and how to make it work. The supplements did a lot of that work, sure, but when you're trying to get interested in the game, the corebook is always the first stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>The degree to which everything is spread out is a little crazy at times \u2014 I'm reading Tribes of the Moon's Bone Shadows chapter at the moment and I was surprised to find reference to a piece of chapter fiction from the Pure, for example, and I recognized character names from Shadows of the U.K. during a cursory readover of Signs of the Moon.<br /> <br /> There's evidently a collection of history and metaphysics in the line, but it's hella dispersed, as I think can be best exemplified by the fact that I found the Lodge books as useful for getting a look at spirit politics as for actual information about lodges. It's particularly worrisome in light of how Werewolf is The Line to deal with the Shadow and yet the relevant information is just scattered in pieces all over the place.<br /> <br /> (To a lesser degree, these tidbits make it conspicuous and explicable why the Shadow is the only major part of the cosmology that the Hedge doesn't open up into - Shadows of the U.K.'s take on interstitial terrain in particular helped drive home that the Shadow is a place between bunches of weirder places in conjunction with the go-to example of Wounds being literal beachheads for the Maeljin's forces.)<br /> <br /> I just really hope Idigam Chronicle can distill all the various tidbits into a single reference - there's all sorts of little aspects of typical spirit behavior that Book of Spirits doesn't really touch on that could do with consolidating to give an idea of how their &quot;alien&quot; thought processes trend, for instance, and the notion of bans as potentially electively plural needs emphasizing outside the context of tribes and packs of werewolves to feed into that, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T12:52:50-08:00","id":61683,"title":"","content":"A complete overhaul of the tribes. For me they have never fit in the setting and were only here because of stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T08:41:10-08:00","id":62201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=61683#post61683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A complete overhaul of the tribes. For me they have never fit in the setting and were only here because of stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because the Tribes <span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>DO</b></span> reflect Stereotypes (though yes, Ideologies is probably a better word). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Personally, I think they fit great in the setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 01-31-2014, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:55:10-08:00","id":62262,"title":"","content":"Stereotypes? The tribes in new world are more about ideologies. I find it funny to see that mentioned here and not in apocalypse, where IT WAS STEREOTYPES. Hell the Get had an entire camp based on being Nazi super werewolves (har har german werewolves). <br /> <br /> I don't think the tribes need an overhaul at all. I do think that a lot of the information that was in tribes of the moon (as far as the feel of the tribes goes) needs to somehow be represented in Idigam. The core book for forsaken did a rather poor job of portraying the tribes, and I cared little for them initially. Tribes of the moon destroyed that though. Each tribe has its own creation story and background, which shows they are not just stereo types. More its an ideological difference between the 9 tribes, and how each one feels things need to get accomplished. <br /> <br /> It's also important to note that the totem spirits are representative of the Uratha's will, as they sought the firstborn out, not the other way around. <br /> <br /> If I wanted anything from the new core book, it would be what they did with requiem. And dammit let's include some friggin rules so we dont get &quot;Check the WoD core book&quot; every 20 pages. (Sure they're doing that though anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T09:37:20-08:00","id":63468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=62262#post62262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...If I wanted anything from the new core book, it would be what they did with requiem. And dammit let's include some friggin rules so we dont get &quot;Check the WoD core book&quot; every 20 pages. (Sure they're doing that though anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember it being said that they'd like to include the base rules as they did in B&amp;S, if that's what you mean. However, they did say it's wasn't a certainty*. I said that it would be an extremely good idea to keep the base WoD rules with GMC updates throughout all new chronicle books if for nothing else than consistency and that it makes the chronicle books all &quot;pick up and play&quot;.<br /> <br /> It can get very confusing for someone new (or returning) to these games to work out what books you need for what. Which is a shame, because there is so much to love right through CWoD, NWoD and GMC-era WoD!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *see monday meeting at some point during some time that I commented...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T18:03:41-08:00","id":64477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=62262#post62262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stereotypes? The tribes in new world are more about ideologies. I find it funny to see that mentioned here and not in apocalypse, where IT WAS STEREOTYPES. Hell the Get had an entire camp based on being Nazi super werewolves (har har german werewolves).<br /> <br /> I don't think the tribes need an overhaul at all. I do think that a lot of the information that was in tribes of the moon (as far as the feel of the tribes goes) needs to somehow be represented in Idigam. The core book for forsaken did a rather poor job of portraying the tribes, and I cared little for them initially. Tribes of the moon destroyed that though. Each tribe has its own creation story and background, which shows they are not just stereo types. More its an ideological difference between the 9 tribes, and how each one feels things need to get accomplished.<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that the totem spirits are representative of the Uratha's will, as they sought the firstborn out, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree there, reading the W20 book i see the tribes of forsaken as little artificial sometimes. They are very role centric organizations, same with Nmage wich is kinda iffy sometimes as it feels like MMORPG roles instead of political organizations. It kinda gives you the impression that all warrior werewolf get along just fine to form the blood talons. While Apocalypse had the Black furies, the get, fianna to a degree, red talons and wendigo who all conform to the warrior werewolf stereotype but where separates tribe because while all of those tribe agree in what to do with things they dont like they disagree in ideological and political issues and so the tribes remain separated and even some like the wendigo remain because of human conflict that bleed out in werewolf society.<br /> <br /> Using the german example. Wouldnt the WW2 affect german and american Talons? How has the tribe remain unified. One way to do it could be to give the options and advices of making the tribes more fractured by it lodges. Because it also confuse some people the role centric organization with the role centric auspice. The difference between a red talon Irraka and a Hunter In darkness Rahu is not so clear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T21:57:23-08:00","id":64589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=61683#post61683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A complete overhaul of the tribes. For me they have never fit in the setting and were only here because of stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between stereotypes and archetypes.<br /> <br /> Stereotype - All Fianna are drunks because they're Irish. All Get are racist because they're German.<br /> <br /> Archetype - Hunters in Darkness are sneaky and silent killers because they are the Fear of the Dark Made Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T00:08:07-08:00","id":64646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=64477#post64477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree there, reading the W20 book i see the tribes of forsaken as little artificial sometimes. They are very role centric organizations, same with Nmage wich is kinda iffy sometimes as it feels like MMORPG roles instead of political organizations. It kinda gives you the impression that all warrior werewolf get along just fine to form the blood talons. While Apocalypse had the Black furies, the get, fianna to a degree, red talons and wendigo who all conform to the warrior werewolf stereotype but where separates tribe because while all of those tribe agree in what to do with things they dont like they disagree in ideological and political issues and so the tribes remain separated and even some like the wendigo remain because of human conflict that bleed out in werewolf society.<br /> <br /> Using the german example. Wouldnt the WW2 affect german and american Talons? How has the tribe remain unified. One way to do it could be to give the options and advices of making the tribes more fractured by it lodges. Because it also confuse some people the role centric organization with the role centric auspice. The difference between a red talon Irraka and a Hunter In darkness Rahu is not so clear</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood Talon Irraka is similar to a military scout. His job is to get in, look around, and get back to his pack, all unnoticed, to relay info about the enemy.<br /> <br /> The Hunter in Darkness Rahu is like a ghost. He's the shadow that breathes down the back of your neck and is gone when you turn around. He's the growl in the night that has no visible source. He is supposed to be noticed, just not seen, and in being noticed, he puts the fear of God in you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:07:03-08:00","id":65088,"title":"","content":"@Lyrics of War<br /> I have not read Tribes of the moons, because I had no interest in the Tribes. Could you describe more precisely what makes Tribes of the moons right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:16:40-08:00","id":65094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65088#post65088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not read Tribes of the moons, because I had no interest in the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank, if you have completely neglected the book about the tribes it is entirely probable that your opinion about how worthwhile the tribes are is irrelevant. There's a reason my most consistently-beaten drum in this thread has been &quot;consolidate and distill the bits from the other books.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you describe more precisely what makes Tribes of the moons right? </div> </div> </div>Examples of different tribal recruitment and initiation practices, three lodges each, milestone Gifts for exemplars of each tribe, lists of common traits of tribe members, stories and legends concerning the tribes' members and patrons, new rites and fetishes relevant to the tribe's practices, three sample characters each, discussions of where tribal stereotypes differ from the reality, and a fairly extensive look at the tribal bans, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:42:29-08:00","id":65102,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the info on the Tribes, a &quot;tribal identity&quot; and how the Auspices can fit nicely within them from <b>The Rage</b> and the nice bits of information on the Tribes and their Totems from <b>Lore of the Forsaken</b><b>.</b><br /> <br /> Yeah, consolidation would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T14:49:31-08:00","id":65161,"title":"","content":"I will say the tribes in forsaken fall kinda flat for me as well. The ones in apocalypse were goofy and full of stereotypes but they each felt different and had their own history. To me tribes in forsaken are more like guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T21:19:24-08:00","id":65379,"title":"","content":"No ser, those are the lodges. The tribes DO feel like tribes if you take the time to learn them. Trust me it's in there. There's a very identifiable mechanic to each tribe and its ideology/appearance/whatever else makes them bond the way they do. Whether its the Storm Lords and their big middle finger to the pure tribes, or the Blood Talons and their 'screw this we'll fix it ourselves' attitude. Really the tribes in new world have the best of the old world tribes without so much the laughably bad stereo-types. They fall flat in the core book for sure, but in the supplements they are infinitely better defined.<br /> <br /> Never mind that each tribe has it's own creation myth, which is in itself pretty friggin awesome. I've found that 90% of the people who keep pushing for the tribes to get completely redone are usually the ones who haven't actually read up on the tribes themselves. Same people try to shoe horn in the Fenrir or the Children of Gaia. There's Lodges for every flavor of player, people just aren't really looking.<br /> <br /> Which again was my wish for Idigam chronicle. Concise rules that don't require a separate core book (grrr point here) and a large chunk of the pertinent data put in the same place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:27:22-08:00","id":65553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65379#post65379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No ser, those are the lodges.</div> </div> </div> </div>See to me the lodges are way better than the tribes. I like how some have nothing to do with the father wolf backstory. You have some that believe in a Greek mythology backstory, a christian one, one that believes in some Norse mythology, and so on., To ME in this setting that would have made more sense as a lot of stuff is kept a mystery. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65379#post65379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never mind that each tribe has it's own creation myth, which is in itself pretty friggin awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have lore of the forsaken and tribes of the moon but I don't remember that. Not saying its not true, but I thought they all agreed on the general course of events. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65379#post65379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Same people try to shoe horn in the Fenrir or the Children of Gaia. There's Lodges for every flavor of player, people just aren't really looking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some tribes would work better than others. I would love a game where the silver fangs and the ivory claws faced off to prove who is the bigger group of assholes. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T06:53:47-08:00","id":65641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've found that 90% of the people who keep pushing for <b>[anything]</b> to get completely redone <b>(or ditched entirely)</b> are usually the ones who haven't actually read up on the <b>[supplements]</b>. </div> </div> </div>Fix'd now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:11:32-08:00","id":65738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65553#post65553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some tribes would work better than others. I would love a game where the silver fangs and the ivory claws faced off to prove who is the bigger group of assholes.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Silver Fangs? Don't you mean the Storm Lords? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T09:11:35-08:00","id":65739,"title":"","content":"Tribal write ups (and Auspice ones as well) that use the tone and feel of the write ups in Tribes (and Signs) of the Moon would be grand. Including the totem stuff from Lore of the Forsaken would be evn better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T12:41:46-08:00","id":65872,"title":"","content":"In tribes of the moon there is at least a section per tribe detailing how the tribe came to be. If you have the book I'm not entirely sure how you missed it... it was one of the more awesome sections of an already good book.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the fix ephsy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T13:20:46-08:00","id":65910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65553#post65553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have lore of the forsaken and tribes of the moon but I don't remember that. Not saying its not true, but I thought they all agreed on the general course of events.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They agree on what happened with Father Wolf, but each tribe has its own origin about how they became a tribe after the Sundering.<br /> <br /> The Hunters in Darkness tracked down Black Wolf and waited outside her den until she came out to meet with them, because they respected her territory.<br /> Destroyer Wolf offered to let the Blood Talons be his servants, but they refused so he killed their alpha, but out of respect for his courage took the tribe on as brothers in arms.<br /> <br /> I don't remember the other three off the top of my head.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T13:58:14-08:00","id":65937,"title":"","content":"Bone shadows had a curiosity in the Hisil and death wolf wouldn't limit their exploration of the shadow until they went too far, then she put the ban in place that makes them respect all things. They were pretty much alien autopsyin everything in the Hisil. <br /> <br /> The Storm Lords tracked down skolis-ur as the last tribe to form and said &quot;lets do this&quot; and skolis in it's rage pretty much told em to 'f' off and let em deal with everything its own way. So one brave little Uratha called it out for being a coward, and showing weakness before the other firstborn. This awakened its leadership ideals (beta of the firstborn) and took them on as their tribal totem. Their ban being to not show others your weakness. <br /> <br /> I can't remember the metal workers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T15:00:05-08:00","id":65988,"title":"","content":"The Iron masters had to answer riddles or something. But that is just how they formed the tribes. They still share the same belief in what happened with the death of father wolf. Its like different branches of the same religion. Its amazing to me that in this setting there is no tribe that discards the entire story that is beyond some regional lodge. There is no christian or Islamic tribe that doesn't believe in father wolf and mirrors the lance in requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T15:49:56-08:00","id":66031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65988#post65988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Iron masters had to answer riddles or something. But that is just how they formed the tribes. They still share the same belief in what happened with the death of father wolf. Its like different branches of the same religion. Its amazing to me that in this setting there is no tribe that discards the entire story that is beyond some regional lodge. There is no christian or Islamic tribe that doesn't believe in father wolf and mirrors the lance in requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribes of the Moon, p121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a newly Changed werewolf wants to join the Iron Masters, she has to demonstrate that she can think on her feet. Sometimes, one of Red Wolf\u2019s tribe will have singled her out before she even knows it. Other times, she proves that she should be a member of the tribe before anyone else can decide. Observers are always on the lookout for werewolves who just don\u2019t do what they\u2019re told. <b>They mark those who question the world \u2014 especially those who question the veracity of Father Wolf\u2019s story.</b> Some reject what they\u2019ve learned without question or just accept it, and the Iron Master moves on. Others think around it. A new Farsil Luhal is likely to have a syncretic understanding of the time before the Sundering that combines her pre-existing worldview with the animistic world. A Christian werewolf may see Father Wolf as an animistic lupine Christ-analogue, an emissary of a higher power who gave his life so that the world could change. A psychologist may see the whole spirit world as a manifestation of the planetary unconscious. Atheists and sociologists both recognize tales of the time around the Sundering as a set of instructions encoded into stories. <b>As a tribe, the Iron Masters have the greatest number of werewolves with divergent opinions of the Father Wolf story.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tribes of the Moon, p127</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Iron Masters make public their recognition of the stories of Urfarah and the Firstborn as myth and allegory. </b>They\u2019re not just stories; they\u2019re instructions. How to act as a werewolf, how to deal with spirits and people: all encoded in an easy-to-learn format designed to be passed down hundreds of generations without the recipient needing anything other than a pair of ears and a brain. Sometimes, the instructions need to change. Sometimes, the cultural background of the listener will get in the way of him learning from an existing story. The Farsil Luhal accept that the easiest way to go forward is to change the words.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Post edited by moderator. Darksider</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  Antagonistic language. 02-05-2014, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:35:09-08:00","id":66056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zap rowsdower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=65988#post65988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Iron masters had to answer riddles or something. But that is just how they formed the tribes. They still share the same belief in what happened with the death of father wolf. Its like different branches of the same religion. Its amazing to me that in this setting there is no tribe that discards the entire story that is beyond some regional lodge. There is no christian or Islamic tribe that doesn't believe in father wolf and mirrors the lance in requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, here's a thought: if <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b> can have additional covenants and such, why can't <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> have more tribes? It should be possible to craft one or more that fit your criteria. Whether or not they'd have Firstborn sponsors may be a separate concern, however. Although, if one expands the concept of &quot;tribe&quot; somewhat, perhaps that wouldn't be necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:08:12-08:00","id":66088,"title":"","content":"Are you referring to the lost covenants?<br /> <br /> Granted, it could happen, and may make sense for there to be lost firstborn (first pack? I get those confused). I always liked Soulless Wolf as the leader of the Ninth Tribe and enjoy the ideas of more.<br /> <br /> However. The covenants are social constructs. While many of them can extend a long way back, they spawned from human belief systems and such. While the tribes, as portrayed, are things that has been there since pretty much the beginning, without regard to what human civilization is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:51:03-08:00","id":66122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=66088#post66088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you referring to the lost covenants?<br /> <br /> Granted, it could happen, and may make sense for there to be lost firstborn (first pack? I get those confused). I always liked Soulless Wolf as the leader of the Ninth Tribe and enjoy the ideas of more.<br /> <br /> However. The covenants are social constructs. While many of them can extend a long way back, they spawned from human belief systems and such. While the tribes, as portrayed, are things that has been there since pretty much the beginning, without regard to what human civilization is doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but one could spin additional idealogies. If they diverge greatly from the Father Wolf mythos or something similarly accepted by &quot;mainstream&quot; Uratha, then it may stand to reason that these tribes have been cast to the side, perhaps millenia ago. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying this should be the default or anything, just spitballing to try and sort out a way that folks interested in that sort of thing might be able to get what they want, yanno? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T18:11:53-08:00","id":66138,"title":"","content":"I bought the tribes of the moon and read the first two chapters... yeah, ignore my post. <br /> <br /> The only thing I would still have to complain about, the term tribe. Cult would fit more, but that is more a matter of taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T18:34:01-08:00","id":66158,"title":"","content":"Well yes it's less about ethnicity and more ideologies. That said though, I prefer the tribes in new world vs old. They do a lot that the old tribes do without the overt stereotypical racial things. The only thing I want more from tribal stuff is a possible mention of Fenris-ur's brother's tribe (rumored), and more on soulless wolf being the patron of the 9th tribe. More bale hounds yo. Blasphemies is however an amazing thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T00:22:40-08:00","id":66302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=66031#post66031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Post edited by moderator. Darksider</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok so basically the iron masters are similar to the carthian movement or the circle in requiem with the members having a million different beliefs. My problem with that is compared to the covenants the tribes seem very static. Since the dawn of time there is only 8 tribes not counting bale hounds, 3 are the bad guys, and if there are people who don't fully agree with the father wolf story they usually just end up in the iron masters? And this happens with little variation world wide? In an area like the middle east where many people are deeply religious, and their religion says the only unforgivable sin is worshiping others beside god they are ok with swearing loyalty to a wolf god? There is no sizable population of religious ghost wolves or a group strong enough to move beyond lodge status? <b>From</b> <b>WHAT I REMEMBER READING</b> the only mention of different political structure is a small area in California where a few people refuse to join the forsaken. I'm not asking for a return to apocalypse tribes but considering how localized the setting in forsaken is its mind boggling that world spanning tribes can exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T05:06:36-08:00","id":66390,"title":"","content":"The idea is they're static because the Firstborn are actually out there, guiding them along. Like Norse pantheism might still exist if Odin and Thor were out there performing miracles for folks and defending them from conversion. There aren't other tribes because there aren't other Firstborn.<br /> <br /> That said, in the books it does discuss the reconciliation of religious werewolves with their changed view of the world once they become werewolves. Not everyone just abandons their previous beliefs, many try to adapt the spirit stuff to their own religion, or vice versa, and an unfortunate other group try to deny it until they go mad. There are mentions of werewolves who have found angels and religious symbols in the Shadow and follow them.<br /> <br /> There's also mentions of werewolves with political differences, which work out pretty much the same. Some may hold their tribe to be a higher priority and not attack others, some may hold their nationality or whatever else to be more important and join in. Some are more concerned about the spirit and so forth. In both cases it really depends on the individual, and perhaps their status in their pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2014, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T10:02:00-08:00","id":66544,"title":"","content":"I believe, Zap, that you might be confused about a fundamental premise of the nWoD line. In cWoD, there was a metaplot, there was canonical history, there was specific information about variations across time and geography; in that sense, it was more static. Sure, variety was accounted for and explained, but it was like having dozens of setting books, and because of the meta-plot, it felt more like the setting was dependent on using that published stuff.<br /> <br /> For nWoD, they wanted to abandon that more or less entirely. Every line is introduced as a &quot;toolbox&quot;. You can take what you want, toss what you don't, and ultimately there's very little to contradict what you do in your stories; there's no &quot;right way to play&quot;. This is one reason the Tribes (or any organization splat) seems broad - so that you have room to come up with regional variations on your own. It is static in the sense you're talking about - 8 Tribes, all over the world, all throughout time, and the published information only really shows the general information about them, giving the impression that it's always been the same. (this is kind of subverted in Tribes of the Moon, where they do a lot of discussion about the tribes in different times and places.)<br /> <br /> They haven't always been the same; that's a silly thing to assume. Like you said, there are thousands of reasons why they wouldn't be. The difference is they didn't publish much about that, so that you can come up with your own. it's a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> If you compare the various settings which have been published, like <i>Shadows of the UK</i> to <i>Hunting Grounds: The Rockies</i>, you will find the diversity you are looking for. They just aren't overt about it because the assumption for the whole game series is &quot;make your own&quot;. That assumption <i>does</i> make it harder to find examples of diversity, but that's what the setting books showcase. Which is appropriate for supplements; I don't think its something that needs to be put into the new corebook, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-06T10:31:51-08:00","id":66565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=66138#post66138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bought the tribes of the moon and read the first two chapters... yeah, ignore my post.<br /> <br /> The only thing I would still have to complain about, the term tribe. Cult would fit more, but that is more a matter of taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throwing in a little Anthropology 101, a tribe isn't always just immediate family relations, they can be bound by region, ideologies, family inter-relations (this one marries that one's chief's daughter) and common beliefs. So, &quot;tribe&quot; still works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T01:23:32-08:00","id":67043,"title":"","content":"But that is exactly it, Papa Bear, tribes do form around usually more than one of those focus points.<br /> Forsaken tribes do exclude the idea of family as a tribe basis as it is done in Apocalypse (some families can end up always being in one tribe, but that is more like every one from family x being in the local chess club), they are not regional but global in a game that explicitely cut down on the higher level of werewolf society (no septs anymore, just individual packs and how they interact with their neighbours).<br /> <br /> They really do focus on ideology and belief, that is, at least the corebook gives not much more than that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I want to say that I think that criticism about just people who have not read all the books clamouring about stuff they want to see changed is a bit hypocritical.<br /> <br /> People, like me, who do apparently like the idea of a werewolf game (otherwise I would not have bought the corebook or anything in the first place), but who do not really like Forsaken as it is will not be likely to buy more and more books if the ones we do buy do not satisfy us - and especially when we cannot get anyone interested to actually PLAY them...<br /> <br /> I think no one in my group was too thrilled about Forsaken, I was not too thrilled, I bought Blasphemies (because it might fix some of my problems) and Skinchangers (which does broaden what kind of shapeshifting myth you can incorporate. And I read a bit of the chapter on other Shapeshifters from War against the Pure and the Pure in a bookstore when I had to wait for someone anyway.<br /> I later bought the chroniclers guides (which had some interesting stuff) and I browsed through a number of other Forsaken books, but my incentive to buy any more was not too great.<br /> <br /> I think as there is in general a lot of RPG books to buy and as I did invest a lot in both the Dark Eye and GURPS as well as in a number of World of Darkness books, I did not really end up going for more with Forsaken.<br /> <br /> ...but I think exactly those who like Werewolves, but do NOT like Forsaken as it is now are the ones who might be won over with an Update.<br /> <br /> Many have said before that the new World of Darkness Lines ARE toolboxes, not prepackaged toys you use as is.<br /> <br /> I think Werewolf shoudl emphasis this more from the start.<br /> <br /> Maybe the problem is that unlike other lines, the concept of Werewolf is quite narrow.<br /> <br /> Vampires get to form their Clans from general stereotypes of vampires, both from fiction and mythology, the Stryx chronicle adds the focus on the more Wiederg\u00e4nger Nachzehrer like Vampires as well.<br /> <br /> But while stories of animal transformation / animal spirits are extremely common, werewolf, both lines though, do focus on a subset, namely both werewolves as a &quot;race&quot; (you are born werewolf, you are not a normal human ever), not on ideas like &quot;magical&quot; shapeshiftings or bargains with suupernatural entities or curses (ll of which Skinchanger did offer) as well as, of course, wolves.<br /> <br /> It is an extreme contrast to lines like, say, Changeling, which are extremely diverse in what they can be.<br /> <br /> I think the fact that people do not like Tribes as much is because without ethnic background, there just is not as much to base differentiation on, so the overlap with Auspices might be hard to avoid completely.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T01:44:18-08:00","id":67051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67043#post67043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I want to say that I think that criticism about just people who have not read all the books clamouring about stuff they want to see changed is a bit hypocritical.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who only read the VtR corebook would have known nothing about the Strix or the contents of the clanbooks. Every snippet of lore that accumulated about the God-Machine between nWoD Core and GMC was in a book that wasn't nWoD Core. FWC's going to include information on Supernal Summoning in it, which wasn't introduced in Mage until Summoners.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople whose sole reading from Werewolf is the corebook are dramatically underinformed about the shape the line has since taken which is likely to heavily inform the direction Idigam Chronicle is going to go. Do you look favorably on a student who only learned American History up to the Civil War saying that current domestic/military policy ought to do something about the emergence of Gatling gun technology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T02:25:05-08:00","id":67074,"title":"","content":"I think though you confuse one fact:<br /> <br /> The corebooks are still supposed to be baseline, unlike history in the sense that it still is supposed to stand as is to be supplemented, not surplanted, especially because it is a toolbox.<br /> History moves on, a toolbox just fills up.<br /> <br /> The idea of a corebook is after all that everything else is optional.<br /> <br /> The Idigam chronicle will replace the core rulebook for all intends and purposes, exactly because a core rulebook is important in shaping a line, I think to say what from the old corebook should go (like for vampires the completely morality based approach to humanity in favour of something I feel comes closer to clarity from the Lost in being how close you still are to what you were) and what should stay is valid, perhaps especially from people who mainly know this old corebook.<br /> <br /> If anything, it makes it clearer which of the additions by later books we may not have read are in need to be made part of the core and not something optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T06:16:18-08:00","id":67142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67074#post67074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think though you confuse one fact:<br /> <br /> The corebooks are still supposed to be baseline, unlike history in the sense that it still is supposed to stand as is to be supplemented, not surplanted, especially because it is a toolbox.<br /> History moves on, a toolbox just fills up.<br /> <br /> The idea of a corebook is after all that everything else is optional.<br /> <br /> The Idigam chronicle will replace the core rulebook for all intends and purposes, exactly because a core rulebook is important in shaping a line, I think to say what from the old corebook should go (like for vampires the completely morality based approach to humanity in favour of something I feel comes closer to clarity from the Lost in being how close you still are to what you were) and what should stay is valid, perhaps especially from people who mainly know this old corebook.<br /> <br /> If anything, it makes it clearer which of the additions by later books we may not have read are in need to be made part of the core and not something optional.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that's why there's the Chronicle books. Because so much of the game is evolving past what the original core book is meant to encompass. There is a disconnect. So, the new book is meant to be an update that encompasses all the updates and things. <br /> <br /> Its also supposed to more focus more on making the mechanics and play style focus to match the fiction of the game. We shall have to see if they can pull it off, though, in a way that attracts new people. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do hope they do bring some of the alternative animal stuff from War Against the Pure, Skin Changers, and the like into Idigam. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T11:43:41-08:00","id":67301,"title":"","content":"Not reading through the rest of the thread because it's long and I see arguments all along it, but I'm echoing the people who desperately want to see Renown reworked or removed. If it has to be there, and it has to be augmented with experience, at least consider Renown beats as a separate thing from regular advancement.<br /> <br /> The other thing I really want them to do is to give werewolves the tools to deal with spirits that aren't immediately outclassed by staying in Dalu all the time with a shotgun. The war form especially needs sprucing up from vanilla Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T13:54:54-08:00","id":67397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67301#post67301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I really want them to do is to give werewolves the tools to deal with spirits that aren't immediately outclassed by staying in Dalu all the time with a shotgun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was already subverted, for a large part, by the God Machine rules on how spirits work. A shotgun counts as a mundane weapon, and only deals Bashing damage to spirits now, whereas the natural weapons of werewolves deal Lethal - and get even more powerful if their Honorary Rank gets to be 2 higher than the spirit, as natural weapons then count as its Bane.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of the most powerful tools are embedded in the Gifts and Rituals - namely &quot;Bind Spirit&quot; and &quot;Read Spirit&quot;......<br /> <br /> I will also be looking forward to any changes to the forms, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T06:37:14-08:00","id":67866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67301#post67301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not reading through the rest of the thread because it's long and I see arguments all along it, but I'm echoing the people who desperately want to see Renown reworked or removed. If it has to be there, and it has to be augmented with experience, at least consider Renown beats as a separate thing from regular advancement.<br /> <br /> The other thing I really want them to do is to give werewolves the tools to deal with spirits that aren't immediately outclassed by staying in Dalu all the time with a shotgun. The war form especially needs sprucing up from vanilla Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, even starting with Mage, with Arcane XP, a lot of the other game lines did have an additional form of XP just for certain things. Both Mummy and Demon incorporate special types of XP (Sebayt XP for increasing Memory, Cover XP for creating/increasing Cover), so I wouldn't be surprised if Idigam chronicle added special/separate Renown XP. Anytime you do something that really exemplifies one of the renown types, gain a Renown Beat or XP sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T09:18:54-08:00","id":67933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67866#post67866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, even starting with Mage, with Arcane XP, a lot of the other game lines did have an additional form of XP just for certain things. Both Mummy and Demon incorporate special types of XP (Sebayt XP for increasing Memory, Cover XP for creating/increasing Cover), so I wouldn't be surprised if Idigam chronicle added special/separate Renown XP. Anytime you do something that really exemplifies one of the renown types, gain a Renown Beat or XP sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is such a good idea that I would house-rule it into any Werewolf game I run, if I had a group with which to run Werewolf games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:15:00-08:00","id":68035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=67866#post67866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, even starting with Mage, with Arcane XP, a lot of the other game lines did have an additional form of XP just for certain things. Both Mummy and Demon incorporate special types of XP (Sebayt XP for increasing Memory, Cover XP for creating/increasing Cover), so I wouldn't be surprised if Idigam chronicle added special/separate Renown XP. Anytime you do something that really exemplifies one of the renown types, gain a Renown Beat or XP sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires get Blood Potency specific experiences from diablerie now and there is a section in blood &amp; smoke about &quot;Blood Beats&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:03:42-08:00","id":68609,"title":"","content":"I want to see Tribe and/or Auspice specific Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T19:31:19-08:00","id":68766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=68609#post68609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see Tribe and/or Auspice specific Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was kicking around a few ideas for things I would do as an &quot;in-between&quot; sort of thing, until <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> was out, Tribal Conditions crossed my mind. I had half a thought to tie them somehow to the tribe's affinity Renown, but I never actually got past the concept stage I don't think. We'll see what happens with the book, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T03:31:15-08:00","id":68938,"title":"","content":"I'd want some kind of update to the changing breeds as well, maybe not all of them, but some like werecats. Or at least a reference to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T09:18:49-08:00","id":69870,"title":"","content":"Something else I'd like to see is the Fighting Styles Tooth and Claw, and Wolfpack get a GMC update. On top of that, make it so that Gauru form can use these Fighting Styles as well. I always found it strange that even though these Styles were made for Werewolves, you still couldn't make use of them in Gauru form. It's my hope that at least this is fixed in Idigam Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T00:59:35-08:00","id":70404,"title":"","content":"Since Vampires got a few thematic fighting styles, I sure hope werewolves will too.<br /> One to emphasise the wolf / near wolf like tooth and claw and one that makes use of having class and increased strength in warform (or near human form too) would be good.<br /> <br /> But I do hope that this will include making the warform a bit less disadvantageous, I did like the unlimited war-form from apocalypse and the Sumer chapter in the chroniclers guide.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also really would like to see other shapeshifters worked in in some form, and if it is only to give them more of a space in the werewolf canon.<br /> Stories all over the world have shapeshifters, many different kinds. I never really liked that Forsaken did away with that to have a clearer focus on werewolves opposed to other shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> If I could wish for any kind of revision, I would love to see the game making &quot;origin&quot; one of the five type axises.<br /> It might be difficult to work, it would be a completely different game where werewolves of quite different types band together out of necessity, but it would be fun to really explore the different stories for how werecreatures came to be, as victims of a curse, born from a uniuon between god / spirit and man, by means of magic (akin to skinchangers, including pacts with supernatural beings), as an animal that turns into a human form or as werewolf deals with it, as an inherited trait.<br /> <br /> ...this is not really feasible for Forsaken, but it still would be fun to see the variety incorporated in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, it would be nice to at least have the mythologically prominent werecreatures appearing in the areas where legends about them are found in some fashion that makes them playable (meaning, not a clear cut enemy from the start).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T20:31:07-08:00","id":71008,"title":"","content":"How is the present War-form disadvantageous? My players can usually kill almost anything they like and scare off all humans nearby in the rounds of war-form that they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T22:06:57-08:00","id":71043,"title":"","content":"I'm on the opposite spectrum from Ray, leave the other shifters out of the core, the game is Werewolf and that is all I want to see in the core as a player option. I don't want a collection of werecritters diluting the themes of Forsaken. No &quot;they're like Rahu, Irraka, etc, but better&quot; nonsense, which is exactly how the Fera came across in Apocalypse. An optional supplement is fine by me, just don't make them part of the core experience and don't use Changing Breeds as a guideline for the supplement (except as a &quot;how not to do this subject&quot; lesson).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T01:45:29-08:00","id":71106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71008#post71008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is the present War-form disadvantageous? My players can usually kill almost anything they like and scare off all humans nearby in the rounds of war-form that they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only really comment on that from the perspective of a NWOD rules apocalypse game (which does lack the main drawbacks of Gauru form), but even there, I did end up choosing Hispo / Urshul form quite a number of times for the benefit of speed alone.<br /> In essence, Gauru has +1 ST +1 size and health and 1/1 armor over Urshul, which gets better DX, initiative and speed.<br /> <br /> For pure combat, that of course gives Gauru the edge, but the I think the disadvantages of having to roll or enter death rage to do anything but attack, attack, attack! and the limits on what kind of merits / tools you can use is rather significant.<br /> <br /> Also, do not forget, you can run around in the other forms with only possible witness holding you back, but if you know you might be walking into an ambush or similar, you cannot simply shift to Gauru and be ready.<br /> Additionally, if you run out of time, you have to spend a turn or a point of essence to shift to the next best form.<br /> Thus, in many fights, that is two points of essence / two turns lost for picking Gauru.<br /> <br /> It of course depends on your style, but I at least thought it more advantageous to build your comat capabilities around Urshul as a Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Darksider: I think I should first state, that I agree with you on two issues:<br /> 1. Changing Breeds was bad, I tried to like it, I wanted to like it and I really could not. Aside from the idea to have a sort of &quot;built your own werecritter&quot; toolbox approach, loads of hunky guys showing of their bodies and a smidgeon of the idea that werecreatures could also be unbalanced in the direction of losing the human side, their was pretty much nothing good about it...<br /> 2. Fera suffered from special snowflake syndrome, the fact that &quot;rarity&quot; based balance does not work in rpg groups and the fact that they annnoyed the people who did want to play werewolf and not second string to someone with cooler powers...<br /> <br /> <br /> I still think though that it takes away from the fun not to deal with non-lupine shapeshifter legends.<br /> If not as somethting directly appearing in the core, there should be, well, room for them, it should be easy to implement them as something that could be playable (maybe with its own chronicle book) and which fits in the werewolf universe.<br /> As I much hope that the idigam chronicle will be open and easy to modify into what you want to play, it should be optional to include them, but I rather would have them in the core than the idea that werewolves ae everywhere, even in places where wolf shifters (or wolves themselves) are not to be found.<br /> <br /> I rather would bend a werewolf game's premise to real world myths and legends than try to press real world legends into a narrow, made up comsology.<br /> Then again I am generally not too much of a fan of the &quot;this is the real truth about (insert name of supernatural entity or other here), all legends just got it wrong, those stupid humans&quot;.<br /> <br /> I always found that to some extend to be an excuse not to do research or trying to force one's ideas down other people's throat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T05:13:53-08:00","id":71187,"title":"","content":"I think it will come as no surprise to anyone that Gauru will be different in the Idigam Chronicles - you'll have to wait and see as to exactly what ways it will be different, but certain existing assumptions about Gauru and its value in various situations will be invalid.<br /> <br /> As for non-werewolf shifters, honestly, word count is a thing that exists and we already have a <i>lot</i> of stuff to fit into the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T06:01:30-08:00","id":71206,"title":"","content":"I think we all are very anxious to see the result, about the Gauru form and in general.<br /> <br /> As far as other shifters are concerned, I would just like to reiterate that it would be nice to see some room being left to make them fit in should there be interest to write a book about different shapeshifters later.<br /> In the same line as werewolf did have room to cross over with other world of darkness lines, I do not think anything more is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T06:47:31-08:00","id":71237,"title":"","content":"I do like me to have some varied werecritters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:42:33-08:00","id":71280,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I have no problem with Fera being part of (or the main focus of) a later supplement that you can take or leave, but if it does get made I want it to be mechanically sound and it has to avoid the &quot;special snowflake&quot; approach. Changing Breeds failed on both accounts. Sorry, tigers are just not physically stronger than elephants and shouldn't confer better physical stat bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:10:06-08:00","id":71442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71280#post71280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, I have no problem with Fera being part of (or the main focus of) a later supplement that you can take or leave, but if it does get made I want it to be mechanically sound and it has to avoid the &quot;special snowflake&quot; approach. Changing Breeds failed on both accounts. Sorry, tigers are just not physically stronger than elephants and shouldn't confer better physical stat bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly.... The problem wasn't even just Changing Breeds, though that book had issues. Its that it was one of four books that ran into issues with bringing alternative were critters into werewolf mainstream.<br /> <br /> At first, we had the Hosts - Rat and Spider, mainly. While not necessarily shifters like the werewolves, they're still kinda part human, part spirit-animal, so I'm counting them here. They got a blurb in Predators, then just kinda... fell flat as a thing. Some one shot entries in Night Horrors, but still not much detail or page count.<br /> <br /> Then, we had Skin Changers. Skin Thief half-template that could have been a werewolf half-template like ghoul or proximi, but kinda fell to the side; a shame, since a wolf blood using a fetish as the agent could pull it off without being so cheesy. And there are also other kinds of half-human, half-animal critters. Kitsune, a snake lady, and more.<br /> <br /> War Against the Pure had ANOTHER chapter on animal stuff. Better mechanics, but still all over the place<br /> <br /> And finally, there was Changing Breeds. Not only was this a mechanical nightmare, not only with existing ones but the creation rules, but also a thematic disaster with the whole return of the eco-terrorist vibe, and a complete lack of ability to really be integrated into the Werewolf cosmology, a key reason for wanting the book for many. <br /> <br /> <br /> Really, if you're going to have alternative shifters.... and, yes, its clearly an issue since we had no fewer than FOUR distinct books on the matter, then you need to make an effort to have some kind of entry into the main core. Want the focus to be on the wolves still? Okay, that's fine. I don't mind. Make them all antagonistic, fine. But there needs to be a set of rules and considerations for alternative were critters from the word go. About one quarter of the books deal with the issue in some manner. There's a clear need for it to be addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T11:10:44-08:00","id":71444,"title":"","content":"I think to get other, regional shape-shifters into Forsaken really just takes some modification or addition of some Mother Luna Gifts. She's already a notorious shape-shifter and the Anybeast Gift allows for some alterations to the various forms already. Skin-Stealing (also a Mother Luna Gift) can allow for the Uratha is alter his human form if he's tasted the blood of the human they're impersonating. Wouldn't take much to combine the two and add a Rite or a Fetish to make it permanent.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers and Changing Breeds (ick!) can handle the cases where the shape-shifter is something so far off from the baseline as to need a different set of rules.<br /> <br /> Too much of the Fera from Apocalypse are, as other have already said, &quot;special snowflake, just like these guys but better&quot; kind of crap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:11:52-08:00","id":71502,"title":"","content":"I think folding in some generic rules for storytellers to build their own other werecritters would be sufficient, essentially updating all of the aforementioned books in one go. As far as actively publishing new Were-splats I might prefer they didn't. The reason why werewolves are based on wolves is because wolves used to be serious nightmare fuel for our ancient ancestors. I think any additional splats might want to take that into account. So something like a Werefox or Weresnake, yes in principle but no Were-elephants or Were-dolphins which are strongly just Weird Shit<sup>TM</sup>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:31:34-08:00","id":71516,"title":"","content":"You know, one thing that occurs to me is that, at least with the Apocalypse, you could just heavily rewrite the initial War of Rage to make sense of things within the continuity. Each 'Were' was supposed to fill a slot in the needs of Gaia, a role to fulfill. It made sense that the wolves weren't as good as the others in the role, although they took it as best they could, and if you just dd some revisions, bam, you now have the Fera filling in the roles of tribes, so long as you carved out a spot for the wolves still. That may create problems as far as people wanting to play [insert tribe here] goes, but you can at least play two versions of apocalypse and have it sort of work.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, it's harder to justify the entire &quot;Other 'Weres' do the same thing you do, but better&quot; because the culture and history of the Uratha is singularly tied into itself(Which, no, is not the same as saying Father Wolf is definitive truth, in case anyone is thinking that). Much of the Forsaken story goes that way. So why do the other 'Weres' exist, and how do you balance essentially probably ten other major templates that share characteristics with your main thing without stepping all over it? Forsaken doesn't offer an easy answer(never read War Against the Pure, so who knows, I might be missing something) because of how diverse it is to begin with.<br /> <br /> I've always been of the opinion that you can either make a Wereanimals game or a Werewolf game, but you can't really have both unless you're okay with some things looking a lot like the others, which most people aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:07:09-08:00","id":71603,"title":"","content":"I do think that having a story tie in is as important as the mechanics, if not more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:27:41-08:00","id":71618,"title":"","content":"You know, there has been a lot of talk here about the war-form, and so on - a lot of character-based stuff. That's to be expected, of course. Folks want to know what new things they can do with their characters.<br /> <br /> But there's been very little talk of the idigam. I mean, the book is called <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> after all. Anyone have any thoughts on what they'd like to see there? (Also, do we have a compiled list of changes folks would like to see, or are they all spread out over 28 pages or whatever? I'll admit I may have missed things this way.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:36:52-08:00","id":71624,"title":"","content":"Including Fera in the core book will exponentially increase the probability of me not buying it, as I am obviously in the camp of &quot;a game about werewolves should be about playing werewolves.&quot; I want all 8 Tribes plus Ghost Wolves, along with a proper setting update due to the reappearance of the Idigam and solid rules reflecting that. I'd like to see the Hisil given a much more detailed write up, with things like &quot;places that aren't&quot; and the Firstborn's den realms given word count. I'd also like a separate book covering new rules for Maeljin (and the Bale Hounds) since they were previously heavily tied to the 7 Deadly Sins and the GMC revisions have moved away from that particular conceit. I like the &quot;werewolves are cursed by the Devil/demons&quot; trope, which the Bale Hounds certainly fill, but it really doesn't belong in the core rules. As an addendum I'd also like to see the wolf-blooded beefed up in power and status similar to ghouls in Requiem. They deserve at least minor template status (biological family also shouldn't be considered part of the Herd) and it never made sense to me that they were susceptible to Lunacy but ghouls weren't.<br /> <br /> Fera just don't bring anything worthwhile to the base setting and its themes IMO, the argument that there are other shapeshifter myths doesn't hold water for me because there are plenty of variations of the vampire myth, yet Requiem/B&amp;S doesn't go out of its way to include those as playable sub splats, I'd like Werewolf to share that degree of focus, and I sure as shit don't want to see Werewolf turned into Exalted. The core book will have a limited word count and I want that focused on the stars of the game line, not wasted on bit players that will never see use in one of my games. It's fine if you want something different, it just means we don't want the same thing out of a game based on werewolves. I can at least appreciate that Changing Breeds tried to give Fera their own theme to play with, independent of Forsaken's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:10:38-08:00","id":71650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71618#post71618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, there has been a lot of talk here about the war-form, and so on - a lot of character-based stuff. That's to be expected, of course. Folks want to know what new things they can do with their characters.<br /> <br /> But there's been very little talk of the idigam. I mean, the book is called <b>The Idigam Chronicle</b> after all. Anyone have any thoughts on what they'd like to see there? (Also, do we have a compiled list of changes folks would like to see, or are they all spread out over 28 pages or whatever? I'll admit I may have missed things this way.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm writing the Idigam rules section so this is certainly something I'd be interested to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:19:02-08:00","id":71657,"title":"","content":"Well, to be fair, The Strix Chronicles discussion before the book was released was more about the rules changes than the Strix themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:52:48-08:00","id":71674,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Lovecraftian weirdness in the Idigam's presentation and flavor (for some of them at least.) It would also be more interesting (to myself at least) if they sometimes worked at cross purposes with each other and weren't one monolithic front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:56:16-08:00","id":71678,"title":"","content":"@Papa Bear: True, but I saw a bunch of discussion about the Strix, too, if only because opinion seems divided on them. Some folks like them, and others seem to loathe them (or at least that's been my impression). :-)<br /> <br /> @Darksider: I would be very, very surprised (like, <i><b>incredibly </b></i>so) if the idigam were presented as a monolithic front. I don't think there is anything to worry about there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:09:11-08:00","id":71687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71674#post71674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see Lovecraftian weirdness in the Idigam's presentation and flavor (for some of them at least.) It would also be more interesting (to myself at least) if they sometimes worked at cross purposes with each other and weren't one monolithic front.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm feeling pretty good about that: until I read the Strix section of <i>Blood and Smoke</i> I was worried about the same thing with the Strix. Fortunately they turned out to be as varied as the vampires.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily need the write-up of dozens of individual Idigam like I got for the Strix, but a spectrum of Idigam would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T17:55:48-08:00","id":71753,"title":"","content":"Strider, don't overlook the simplistic &quot;every spirit hates the Uratha&quot; presentation in the original core book. I want the devs to stay away from that kind of presentation because it's too simplistic. That's what I was thinking of when I mentioned a monolithic front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T19:55:40-08:00","id":71797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71753#post71753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strider, don't overlook the simplistic &quot;every spirit hates the Uratha&quot; presentation in the original core book. I want the devs to stay away from that kind of presentation because it's too simplistic. That's what I was thinking of when I mentioned a monolithic front.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to second that!<br /> <br /> I feel Forsaken had a lot of issues with too much simplicity in many regards, but that one is definitely one of those weird things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71444#post71444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think to get other, regional shape-shifters into Forsaken really just takes some modification or addition of some Mother Luna Gifts. She's already a notorious shape-shifter and the Anybeast Gift allows for some alterations to the various forms already. Skin-Stealing (also a Mother Luna Gift) can allow for the Uratha is alter his human form if he's tasted the blood of the human they're impersonating. Wouldn't take much to combine the two and add a Rite or a Fetish to make it permanent.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers and Changing Breeds (ick!) can handle the cases where the shape-shifter is something so far off from the baseline as to need a different set of rules.<br /> <br /> Too much of the Fera from Apocalypse are, as other have already said, &quot;special snowflake, just like these guys but better&quot; kind of crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, I really think that is not a good idea.<br /> <br /> If it is werewolf and not just any kind of were-creature, then PLEASE do not make werewolves the thing behind legends of other shapeshifters...<br /> <br /> If people want wolves, let them stay wolves and not cover up as a hyena or panther or such.<br /> It would also in a sense repeat the problem of using one cultures myths to be behind supernatural phenomena all over the world.<br /> I personally think Requiem with its bloodlines and archetype like clans was rather good at covering vampire myths across the world, even better with the stryx now, so let were creature stay diverse too.<br /> <br /> I think it will for sure not fit into the core as rules, but I think it would be great if the new Idigam chronicles gave story hooks or openings to connect to a possible later &quot;Fera&quot; book.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I think any further discussions might be better put to a different topic, after all, if there are enough people here interested in a &quot;Fera chronicle&quot;, then maybe we can get one to be made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T21:40:27-08:00","id":71814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71516#post71516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Forsaken, it's harder to justify the entire &quot;Other 'Weres' do the same thing you do, but better&quot; because the culture and history of the Uratha is singularly tied into itself(Which, no, is not the same as saying Father Wolf is definitive truth, in case anyone is thinking that). Much of the Forsaken story goes that way. So why do the other 'Weres' exist, and how do you balance essentially probably ten other major templates that share characteristics with your main thing without stepping all over it? Forsaken doesn't offer an easy answer(never read War Against the Pure, so who knows, I might be missing something) because of how diverse it is to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I'm trying to keep this argument going, but I'd like to disagree. If you're willing to put a little work into it, this isn't as much of an issue as you assume. I've included other Changing Breeds in the werewolf game I'm running, with original mythology, and no one has felt their roles &quot;stepped on&quot; or any other issues of redundancy or too deep a schism in the cosmology (though Doubt and Blasphemy are two of the themes I'm using....)<br /> <br /> To give some examples of Fera with other purposes that I've used:<br /> -Were-foxes purpose is to help spirits enter and influence the material, and humans to shape the Shadow. They decide whose wise enough to be the exception to Father Wolf's law, and pushing those that abuse the other realm too greatly. They do this without the knowledge or agreement of werewolves, of course.<br /> -Were-lions claim a heritage of kingship and stewardship over humankind, becoming leaders, warriors, and judges; they also prey upon humans which fall out of balance with nature.<br /> -Were-rats were given the purpose of making sure humanity's waste didn't poison the world. Natural processes return resources to nature, but humans haven't learned that yet, so rats clean up after them; they also try to reconcile artificial and natural spirits, put into conflict by human expansion. The Beshilu (and their own selfishness) has undermined them, though.<br /> -Were-bears are drawn to the deepest parts of the wilds, being natural wanderers, and come across anomalies which they guard as a consequence - verges, ancient horrors, forgotten Wounds.<br /> <br /> These aren't roles which the Uratha or others <i>can't </i>fulfill, and like I said, I play around with Doubt by giving alternate creation myths and different roles - I tried to give options to my players - but they're purposes the same way &quot;keep humans and spirits separate&quot; is the Forsaken's purpose without stepping on toes. (Lions may toes-step a little, but I don't put any wolves in Africa, and designed lions to be their foils in several ways - like being descended of Helios). From my players' feedback, I've subverted the snowflake syndrome and worked them into Forsaken's setting well enough to be interesting, not upsetting.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just wanted that it can be done, and in interesting ways. I would not advocate making other Changing Breeds a default part of the setting; perhaps another supplement that revises the creation rules and makes clear how they can be used, but I don't feel a strong need for it. <i>War Against the Pure</i>'s rule set (though it could benefit from revision and expansion) has been ample enough for me; I'd rather see more along the lines of <i>Predators</i> and <i>Skinchangers</i>.<br /> <br /> To me, there's already room for other Fera in <i>Forsaken</i>; ie, there's nothing which contradicts doing what you want with your own story. It may take some work, but the best uses of them in Werewolf are going to be fan projects personal to the Storyteller and chronicle.<br /> If there was to be a re-imagined Fera template, I'd actually enjoy something along the lines of Lost Light's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\">fan project</a> more; their own unique game setting, which, in true WoD tradition, is compatible enough for crossover.<br /> <br /> /my two cents","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:15:04-08:00","id":71888,"title":"","content":"Well, taking ideas from how Blood And Smoke did things...<br /> <br /> 1) As we have the Embrace be the regular, normal and default way of creating a vampire but we also have Revenants, Post-Mortem Embraces and the Strix (that cover most of the folkloric vampire as just a demonic-posessed corpse), why not port something similar to Forsaken?<br /> <br /> The People still became what they are due to something triggering the First Change (they may have been Wolf-Blooded themselves or some distant memeber of their family, or maybe it's just a choice of Luna herself). That'd be the default.<br /> Maybe sometimes when a werewolf attacks (bites) someone, they get infected by the spiritual nature of the werewolf and become something similar to folklore werewolves, uncontrolled change under a given Moon-phase and always into death rage (something like the Revenants of Blood and Smoke). Maybe there is a Rite that can give them more control and efectively became one of the People after swearing and Oath to Luna. I figure the Pure would look down on them or use them as shock troops or cannon fodder. Or maybe not! Maybe they are not tainted by Luna and can become truly Pure trough some Rite of their own.<br /> <br /> 2) Other shifters. At least some of the old info we have on the Idigam shows that thay can pretty much do whatever thay want with Essence. What if some of the other legends about shifters are mock creations of the Idigam? That doesn't mean they'd be unplayable, but at least will tie them into the werewolf mythos.<br /> Or maybe they are just some sub-type of claimed (like Siten-Uzu)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:30:40-08:00","id":71893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71888#post71888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, taking ideas from how Blood And Smoke did things...<br /> <br /> 1) As we have the Embrace be the regular, normal and default way of creating a vampire but we also have Revenants, Post-Mortem Embraces and the Strix (that cover most of the folkloric vampire as just a demonic-posessed corpse), why not port something similar to Forsaken?<br /> <br /> The People still became what they are due to something triggering the First Change (they may have been Wolf-Blooded themselves or some distant memeber of their family, or maybe it's just a choice of Luna herself). That'd be the default.<br /> Maybe sometimes when a werewolf attacks (bites) someone, they get infected by the spiritual nature of the werewolf and become something similar to folklore werewolves, uncontrolled change under a given Moon-phase and always into death rage (something like the Revenants of Blood and Smoke). Maybe there is a Rite that can give them more control and efectively became one of the People after swearing and Oath to Luna. I figure the Pure would look down on them or use them as shock troops or cannon fodder. Or maybe not! Maybe they are not tainted by Luna and can become truly Pure trough some Rite of their own.<br /> <br /> 2) Other shifters. At least some of the old info we have on the Idigam shows that thay can pretty much do whatever thay want with Essence. What if some of the other legends about shifters are mock creations of the Idigam? That doesn't mean they'd be unplayable, but at least will tie them into the werewolf mythos.<br /> Or maybe they are just some sub-type of claimed (like Siten-Uzu)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm running by in my game's WTF overhaul; Wolf Blooded is just a name; they're the offspring of spiritually potent/Shadow-touched entities. They have the potential to become werewolves if triggered; sometimes strong enough Resonance is left from their parents to make them into werewolves, but more often it's a bite, an attack, something that alters the Resonance of their essence to be conducive. Unfortunately for werewolves, it also means -other- entities find these spiritually potent people just as interesting. Not only as wonderful prey (extra Essence beyond a normal human, sometimes odd abilities due to it; see Second Sight and Book of Spirits etc. merit wise among other ways to up their untapped potential), certains others find them more hospitable to possess or achieve synthesis with. And that's beyond weighing in what their relevance is to possible other shapeshifters out there and Idigam.<br /> <br /> Werewolves call their offspring that bear that wolf-blooded; really, they're spirit-blooded. It's also meant to make them precious; you -want- to protect your family. Spirits and similar entities like Shartha are very, very likely to take an interest in them, I wanted to reinforce that family was not only important like it is for wolves, but there's some paranoia and inherent horror to be descended from a werewolf, and a reason for them to pay close attention or keep a tight family; things tend to go strange among them even if they never turn into a werewolf themselves.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to present the idea of poaching; that is, individuals of other packs, tribes etc. taking an interest in the descendants of other werewolves as prime breeding stock -and- werewolf recruits if forcibly changed in course of the story. Nothing like having your daughter be taken when your vigil slipped, and turned by a Pure to bolster their pack numbers when you're a Forsaken who was hoping to hell she'd be free of horrors of werewolf existence. Things like that that hit home hard. Even if something isn't introduced in Idigam chronicles in that vein, I'll be keeping that with the overhaul we're using. Not suffering from Lunacy is... well, irrelevant. Not using that. Their importance is their potential, and how readily someone close to you can be compromised or twisted. &quot;Cursed&quot; family lines? 7th sons of 7th sons and the like turning into Werewolves? Other ideas in that vein? Hell yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:43:53-08:00","id":71899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71753#post71753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strider, don't overlook the simplistic &quot;every spirit hates the Uratha&quot; presentation in the original core book. I want the devs to stay away from that kind of presentation because it's too simplistic. That's what I was thinking of when I mentioned a monolithic front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got ya. Well, since the book is in Stew's capable hands, development-wise, I would suspect we'll be okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:43:09-08:00","id":72035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=71893#post71893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also wanted to present the idea of poaching; that is, individuals of other packs, tribes etc. taking an interest in the descendants of other werewolves as prime breeding stock -and- werewolf recruits if forcibly changed in course of the story. Nothing like having your daughter be taken when your vigil slipped, and turned by a Pure to bolster their pack numbers when you're a Forsaken who was hoping to hell she'd be free of horrors of werewolf existence. Things like that that hit home hard. Even if something isn't introduced in Idigam chronicles in that vein, I'll be keeping that with the overhaul we're using.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a theme in our current game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T15:53:57-08:00","id":72284,"title":"","content":"I guess I would also like to get more info about what happened during their exile on the moon. I mean weren't they basically sitting on Luna for a few thousand years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:37:04-08:00","id":72742,"title":"","content":"That would be the case, but I think physical =/= spiritual. Not entirely certain the moons physical representation is that of the spiritual representation. Can Luna exist without the moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T14:21:52-08:00","id":72818,"title":"","content":"I'd certainly like to see the Idigam as -threats- to the world. They aren't necessarily interested in, say, wrecking the world as we know it, but they should have the capacity to do so if the mood strikes them. So they'd be more than just another spirit to deal with, so to speak. Not all of them, of course, but at least a couple.<br /> <br /> I really enjoyed the stuff from the Night Horrors book about them being able to just pluck souls from bodies and replace them with spirits. The book suggested that only the (I forget how to spell its name) one from the Rockies defeated by Max Roman was able to do that, but it might be possible for others to do. Things like that, that go against the entire system, would be good. Being able to subvert rules of the World of Darkness that people take for granted like we do the laws of physics. Being able to rip templates from people and put them onto other things, even stacking templates in some mad amalgam of things, that sort of thing too.<br /> <br /> I liked how the Strix chronicle gave some example Strix, with a wide variety of motives and strangenesses (one of them that hunts other strix, others that prey on humans, others on vampires, etc). So it would be nice to see a wide variety of sample Idigam. I think there's a hard-to-resist tendency among player to look at books and think, 'okay, that's it, that is all there is,' and getting rid of that inside the box thinking is an important part of these games.<br /> <br /> Lastly I think it would be interesting to show what happens to those who decide to willingly follow the Idigam, as it doesn't matter how dangerous stuff is, if people (even Uratha) can see it as a path to power or fulfilling some other need, they'll take the risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-15-2014, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T21:53:59-08:00","id":73000,"title":"","content":"My wish list for IC<ul><li><b>Tribes to Function Like Other NWOD Secret Societies or to be Replaced\u2014\u200b </b>The problem I had with W:tF was that there were few situations in which a mixed tribe pack felt appropriate for the story. Other games, particularly Requiem and Mage, by virtue of centering around more individualistic character archetypes, had an easier time justifying why characters from mutually antagonistic factions might yet work together. In W:tF, the emphasis is more on the group, and being insular, so the mixed pack is more of an exception than a rule, story wise. It also did not help that there was little mechanical importance to the Tribes after character creation. Two possible solutions would be to tie Favored Gift access to a Status Merit or, as a way to play up the underdog angle in W:tF, have the First Pack Spirits that patronize the Eight Tribes function as philosophical paths to discover during or after character creation, represented by a Merit.</li> <li><b>Simpler Alternate Form Attribute Math/ Folding Father Wolf &amp; Mother Luna Gifts into the Base Template\u2014 </b>l would prefer it if, as was done in B&amp;S, alternate forms did not add directly to individual attributes, but rather gave flat die bonuses to certain rolls, which could be accessed out of form through Essence expenditure. Keep agg access limited, through merits primarily, as with form-stealing.</li> <li><b>Renown Should do More/ Function More like Arcana\u2014 </b>allow more improvisation in regards to what a character can do with Renown. Allow players to burn Essence to attempt to use Gift-like Effects they hadn't already mastered.</li> <li><b>Cost Gifts Like Rotes\u2014 </b>the story costs for learning gifts should be more than enough.</li> <li><b>Make Hosts/Claimed Viable Tier 2-3 Character Templates\u2014 </b>\u200bPredators was my favorite splatbook for NWOD (and to a lesser extent, Freak Legions, for OWOD), so I'd love it if the math allowed for playable Claimed and/or Hosts.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:19:23-08:00","id":73060,"title":"","content":"First of all, werewolves (and others gamelines) need something, that make them as powerfull as B&amp;S-vampires. What do you think, which rules must be fixed for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T00:39:35-08:00","id":73077,"title":"","content":"There are 29 pages prior to this one with answers to your question. Please take the time to look through them, there is definitely a consensus about Gauru form needing to be buffed, both stat and duration wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T01:23:42-08:00","id":73086,"title":"","content":"Gods don't let them change the Tribes. I will ALWAYS play my blood talons like the tribes of the moon presentation. Same for storm lords. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T03:02:49-08:00","id":73118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73077#post73077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are 29 pages prior to this one with answers to your question. Please take the time to look through them, there is definitely a consensus about Gauru form needing to be buffed, both stat and duration wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give me the link for something specific? I'd liked the hauserules of LOOK for gifts and for forms. But even with my own modification it's too weak for B&amp;S. I mean, my average-good Rahu/Blood Talon had 15 dice of lethal damage with 8-again from under Armor 2 - but it's still pathetic compared with the B&amp;S -vampire, made \u200b\u200bat the same price of expirience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 02-16-2014, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T08:15:11-08:00","id":73200,"title":"","content":"TheBadWolf, how exactly did those two match up? I'm just curious how you built those, and how you came to that conclusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T08:49:36-08:00","id":73212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73200#post73200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm just curious how you built those</div> </div> </div> </div>Usual good Rahu-martial artist (PU 3) - Strenght 3 (6 - in Gauru), Brawl 4, Specialization 1 + Claws 1+ spending 1 WP (+3). In total: 15. And 8-again to Strenght and Armor [Prima Urge/2]/[Primal Urge/2] (rounded up) is from houserule<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/2828-fixed-and-houseruled-werewolf-forms\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...werewolf-forms</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 02-16-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:59:08-08:00","id":73321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73212#post73212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usual good Rahu-martial artist (PU 3) - Strenght 3 (6 - in Gauru), Brawl 4, Specialization 1 + Claws 1+ spending 1 WP (+3). In total: 15. And 8-again to Strenght and Armor [Prima Urge/2]/[Primal Urge/2] (rounded up) is from houserule<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/2828-fixed-and-houseruled-werewolf-forms\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...werewolf-forms</a></div> </div> </div> </div>And what was the vampire like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T13:08:45-08:00","id":73325,"title":"","content":"If you're going to put werewolves up to the same 'level' as Blood and Smoke, you're going to have to do more than just increase the power of gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T13:32:43-08:00","id":73338,"title":"","content":"I have some (probably controversial) suggestions.<br /> <br /> Cut the &quot;near-human&quot; and &quot;near-wolf&quot; forms, leaving <i>just</i> human, gauru, wolf. Feels more elegant and streamlined mechanically and in terms of the setting, those are the only three you really actually need to reflect Forsaken society as presented. Treat the two non-human forms with more depth and just...straight up drop the other two. I know it's kind of a tradition for Werewolf games, but if Vampire dared to modify the &quot;burst into flames upon sunlight&quot; rule, if only mildly, then I can see Forsaken diverging more from its Apocalypse ancestor.<br /> <br /> Second, the Wolf-Blooded should be straight-up immune to Lunacy, just like Ghouls and Sleepwalkers. The Wolf-Blooded fill that same game niche as ghouls, sleepwalkers, witnesses, etc, so just let them have the immunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T14:10:26-08:00","id":73359,"title":"","content":"Now, as I just got done reading the rest of the thread, I have some more ideas:<ul><li><b>Simple Regen Mechanics\u2014 </b>i think a Hybrid of what was introduced in Demon (i.e.: heal the right most lethal/bashing each turn) and B&amp;S (Downgrade Mundane Damage) would suffice, spending Essence for extra/Agg.</li> <li><b>Crunchier Spirit Predation\u2014 </b>use Diablerie/Pacting rules for gaining Special XP for Gifts and PU, with consequences (read: Character Options) for eating stranger/more powerful spirits, namely Bans, Banes, and weird special powers (NO NUMINA).</li> <li><b>A &quot;the Good, the Bad, and the Worst&quot; Treatment of Tribes/Patrons, Including a Faction that &quot;Fights Fire with Fire&quot;\u2014 </b>\u200brelating to that last idea, there should be a faction, not necessarily a tribe but maybe a network of rogue Uratha, that try to use the methods of the Magath to take the fight to the Idigam, like the Marauders or Centimani. I kind of want something that's not quite Bale Hounds, not quite Pure, to act as the Red Herring/untrustworthy packmate for the game.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T14:36:11-08:00","id":73383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73325#post73325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to put werewolves up to the same 'level' as Blood and Smoke, you're going to have to do more than just increase the power of gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of cause. The LOOK houserules gifts seems pretty well... but not enogh.<br /> And what was the vampire like? <br /> I don't remember his traits, but nevermind - any usually lethal damag for him was just bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","user":"TheBadWolf","date":". 02-16-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:23:03-08:00","id":73434,"title":"","content":"Also, they should drop the damage penalty for silver weapons. It's not even true for bullets, and the system doesn't have nearly enough granularity to sustain it for melee weapons. If necessary, say that silver-blades have lower durability than comparable steel ones, but that's as far as it needs to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:33:06-08:00","id":73437,"title":"","content":"TheBadWolf, this isn't a thread about houserules, it's about things people want to see in the Idigam chronicles. To summarize what's gone before, people want boosts to the different forms, stronger Gifts, XP costs that make sense and keep werewolves competitive with other splats (like what you seem to want compared to B&amp;S), better Totem rules, better explanation/exposition of the Hisil, variety of antagonists, mechanics that aren't wonky and are easy to understand and probably some other things that I've missed. I left out the Fera because the opinions seem to be mixed on the issue. I'd like to see them redone myself, just not as part of the core, others disagree.<br /> <br /> There are houserule threads but I don't have the links available or the time to hunt them down at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:35:07-08:00","id":73440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73434#post73434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, they should drop the damage penalty for silver weapons. It's not even true for bullets, and the system doesn't have nearly enough granularity to sustain it for melee weapons. If necessary, say that silver-blades have lower durability than comparable steel ones, but that's as far as it needs to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd expect the silver damage rules will get a bit of modification, simply because weapons work differently in GMC than in pre GMC rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:55:23-08:00","id":73451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=73440#post73440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd expect the silver damage rules will get a bit of modification, simply because weapons work differently in GMC than in pre GMC rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine so - as it stand silver bullets could be frankly ridiculous!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T02:32:11-08:00","id":74177,"title":"","content":"As some mentioned housreules (and big controversial changes), why not keep the tradition from the chromnicler guide and make another supplement about how to really alter werewolves that encorporates the new rules?<br /> <br /> Werewolves without much control and no connection to the shadows, with fewer forms, lesser werewolves that are more like Skinchangers...<br /> <br /> As wererwolf has a distinct flavour, even one little chapter about how to make it a different game would likely be nice and maybe a good way to appease people who want more radical changes.<br /> <br /> I think this and the Fera discussion showed that we just want quite a few different things when it comes to all that goes BEYOND better mechanics and a general clean up of the rules.<br /> <br /> In general, I think werewolf tried too much to sell one rather specific image instead of a broader gallery.<br /> It is really good if writers are passionate about what they think is a good game, but ultimately, it is the storyteller and the players who bring it to life and they all have their own idea about what makes a good werewolf story.<br /> <br /> I think trying to make the game so that it opens up to as many of those ideas as possible while still offering lots of interesting storyhooks is the most important.<br /> <br /> last tangent about other shifters: I quite disagree with Thorbes suggestion about having them be sired as a werewolf mockery by the Idigam or similar.<br /> Just let them be their culturally distinct thing, don't make them mere satellites orbiting the Forsaken.<br /> There are so many legends or fictional ideas about shapeshifters that work well with the Forsaken setting about spirits and the shadow, all the stories featuring animal gods or bloodlines can work wonderfully to make werewolf like part spirit shifters.<br /> I think the only thing one might have to worry about is the fact that by now, a good deal of other lines have claimed certain shapeshifting myths (Selkies and similar by Changeling for example), so I would not try to hard to work shifters in whose mythological origin better suits another line (Though a reference to them could help).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T02:44:01-08:00","id":74178,"title":"","content":"I think there needs to be a reason for werewolves to interaction with humans. In the current gameline is seems like the only reason werewolves interact with humans is because they can't breed with anyone else. Which honestly seems to be an arbitrary and a little bit squicky of a restriction. Honestly I think the whole ghost children thing in so non-compelling and uncomfortable that I would immediately strike it from any chronicle I run. Werewolves are just too disconnected from humans, which is really weird when you consider they're basically half-human half-wolf spirit hybrids.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I just think it's a little silly when compared to other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T03:37:41-08:00","id":74184,"title":"","content":"I agree there, I think it is noticeable with quite a lot of things, including harmony, that the part of &quot;being human&quot; is rather neglected, the only thing tying werewolves to the human side is their own past, which I think given how dealing with humans was so essential in many other lines is a bit unfortunate.<br /> <br /> As said before, Harmony should be more about balancing human and wolf, and less just about obeying spirit rules.<br /> <br /> I also think werewolf with the ever rising social penalties makes it a bit too easy to cast those areas aside, I think I would much prefer there to be the option not to be burdened by them.<br /> <br /> Why not make the social penalties only appear when Primal Urge is higher than your composure (measuring how well you can keep the primal nature in check) or alternatively the targets resolve? Or the higher of both?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:04:16-08:00","id":74351,"title":"","content":"Last thing: bring back Metis and Wolf-born. It'd be easy to do, just have an at creation merit that trades a Tell in human form for bonuses to rolls in Dalu and gauru for Metii and Urshul and Urhan for Wolf-born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:34:38-08:00","id":74368,"title":"","content":"Ok no. There is already a wolf born in the world but he's sorta the anti christ of werewolves.<br /> <br /> Why are people constantly trying to shoe horn apocalypse stuff into forsaken? I get that you lot love your apocalypse but do some friggin reading into the world before declaring it was stupid in the first place. DO NOT bring back METIS in my core game play. The UNIHAR represent something darker for a purpose.<br /> <br /> Lets not forget in the tribes of the moon book, theres a rumor that black wolf (as the alpha pair) might allow two forsaken to breed successfully with each other. Go with that. Some big epic chronicle to gain such a favor from black wolf.<br /> <br /> If you simply MUST have apocalypse style lore and events within your forsaken game, spend the 3 or so dollars and get the translation guide. Don't champion for what I consider to be a drastic change to the lore of a game that I frankly love.<br /> <br /> passionate rant aside, I really don't see why people are so into the apocalypse style with this setting. It's almost like cramming resident evil 5 Chris Redfield into silent hill. It might be fun for a minute, but it doesn't mesh with the over all theme. It seems to me that a lot of the revisions people want are essentially people trying to turn forsaken into apocalypse 2.0. That is something I do not want. It's something my players don't want. With a book like the translation guide available, I find myself wondering why more people do not just go with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-18-2014, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:05:24-08:00","id":74392,"title":"","content":"Seconding the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/BigNo\" target=\"_blank\">Big No</a> on bringing back Metis and Lupus. Werewolves that are wolves first and people second can be handled thru something else (spirit-ridden, skinchangers, etc). Werewolves that are born from two werewolves don't need to be playable. Not sure what that really brings to the table in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 02-18-2014, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:14:57-08:00","id":74403,"title":"","content":"I had a notion where the pc for a werewolf born werewolf would have some slightly better standing with the garou form. Extra stability in garou, high primal urge from the get go... renown amongst the spirit wilds for being what he is (let's be honest here, the spirit world WOULD notice that, for better or ill). I also gave him the benefit of having an Unihar twin that murdered his parents and wants him dead. Sorta like a personal stalking that doesn't stop.<br /> <br /> Even had a little scenario where the players pack would be in the sewers trying to stop the beshilu from chewing the gauntlet down and being just too late, with this now 20 something year old Unihar materializing in the physical from that. Course the PC for the werewolf born wouldn't be telling anyone else his secret. It is still blasphemy to almost all forsaken and pure alike. If anything the pack might think he was the parent of said Unihar, until such time as he decided to reveal his secret to them. <br /> <br /> Garou form would get stabilization from that due to the rumors from the forsaken about how the war form was the original true form of the Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:19:21-08:00","id":74405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74184#post74184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think werewolf with the ever rising social penalties makes it a bit too easy to cast those areas aside, I think I would much prefer there to be the option not to be burdened by them.<br /> <br /> Why not make the social penalties only appear when Primal Urge is higher than your composure (measuring how well you can keep the primal nature in check) or alternatively the targets resolve? Or the higher of both?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to agree on the Harmony part, personally. And how do you mean, in regards to the rising social penalties? I want to say that you're saying the way the Uratha drive off/scare normal humans away then logically pushes human interaction to the side, but I want to make sure that I'm reading you correctly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T11:24:25-08:00","id":74406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74405#post74405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I happen to agree on the Harmony part, personally. And how do you mean, in regards to the rising social penalties? I want to say that you're saying the way the Uratha drive off/scare normal humans away then logically pushes human interaction to the side, but I want to make sure that I'm reading you correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume he means the mechanical penalty that a rising Primal Urge inflicts on social rolls when interacting with humans other than Intimidation checks (starting at -1 at PU 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:56:43-08:00","id":74486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74351#post74351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last thing: bring back Metis and Wolf-born. It'd be easy to do, just have an at creation merit that trades a Tell in human form for bonuses to rolls in Dalu and gauru for Metii and Urshul and Urhan for Wolf-born.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the very obvious reason this won't happen and wasn't included at the beginning is because Metis serve the same purpose as Ghost Children, which is kind of... not a good thing to reinforce. It seems like it's supposed to invoke fears relating to incest, but as a supernatural equivalent I feel that it falls very flat, especially because they're an unfortunate consequence of only heterosexual couples. I think werewolf would really be better off not thinking too much about reproduction, they always come up with something that's uncomfortable, but just short of horrifying. Which is understandable, because it's really hard to do reproductive horror without doing something incredibly sexist and disturbing, which is honestly probably not what most people come to a game about werewolves for.<br /> <br /> As for Wolf-born, they're pretty obviously avoided in Forsaken because of the bestiality connotations and because Forsaken appear to be part human, part wolf spirit. Which makes sense because actual wolves do not behave in the same pack like behaviors that drive Frosaken social interaction. Which is based on human myths of wolf behavior, all the more reason the connection to humans needs to be emphasized as far as I'm concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:51:44-08:00","id":74537,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:15px\">At least Apocalypse (CWOD in general) had an internally consistent cosmology. And, as it has been mentioned by others on this thread, that the taboo against werewolves interbreeding is a bit silly. Now, no one is telling anyone that they have to play with options they don't care for, but at least the option should be there. Ridden aren't really a viable option because RAW, the template isn't balanced for PCs, which is why I asked that it be given a redux.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u200b</span><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The problem with Forsaken, as opposed to most of the other games in this line, is that are few consequences for going bad that result in a more or less playable character, apart from joining the Pure or becoming a Bale Hound, which most of the time ends up getting you killed in game. It's better to roleplay the screw-ups in your characters arc than allow yourself to be fiated out of existence.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:12:04-08:00","id":74590,"title":"","content":"I definitely prefer unihar to metis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T16:29:35-08:00","id":74621,"title":"","content":"Unihar definitely add more to the horror element over that of the metis. Unless you're going with the first ronin... which is essentially an Unihar anyway as far as I look at them. <br /> <br /> The incestious relationship of the werewolves and the taboo previously seemed silly because the flaw was having mutant babies. It being taboo in new world is because it literally breaks your brain, ad produces monster spirit babies.<br /> <br /> Besides without the Unihar, &quot;The Breeder&quot; Idigam loses something of a point for the storyline. And I happen to think he's a fun concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T17:14:24-08:00","id":74651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74392#post74392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Werewolves that are born from two werewolves don't need to be playable. Not sure what that really brings to the table in Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how some people would like it better if werewolves could breed together. In some chronicles I have played the GM will throw npcs at players for romance and children and all that stuff. unless they are using the everything you ever wanted setting from the chroniclers guide most people reject that stuff outright. A lot of people don't care for the fact that the game says most werewolf parents are either a absent one or subject their partner to severe domestic violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1303-zap-rowsdower","name":"zap rowsdower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1303_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T17:26:11-08:00","id":74662,"title":"","content":"Me, I'm satisfied with the Everything You Ever Wanted Hack from FCG and the Translation Guide as far as mixed relationships go. I don't need that in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T20:26:21-08:00","id":74752,"title":"","content":"The entire point of them needing to breed with humans was explicitly included in the game to give werewolves the need to interact with humans. In Apocalypse one never needed to socially interact with a non werewolf , the developers specifically wanted to get away from that, as per Ethan when Forsaken came out. It's an idea that I prefer remains in place. Besides, I've run out of good bestiality jokes, heard more than enough bad ones during the Apocalypse days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:05:36-08:00","id":74786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74752#post74752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire point of them needing to breed with humans was explicitly included in the game to give werewolves the need to interact with humans. In Apocalypse one never needed to socially interact with a non werewolf , the developers specifically wanted to get away from that, as per Ethan when Forsaken came out. It's an idea that I prefer remains in place. Besides, I've run out of good bestiality jokes, heard more than enough bad ones during the Apocalypse days.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea that the only solution for incentivizing Werewolf-Human interaction is reproduction is a little silly, immature and short-sighted. It also does nothing to remedy the problem for homosexual characters or heterosexual character that don't want children. I mean really, could something be any more contrived?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:10:37-08:00","id":74790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74786#post74786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the idea that the only solution for incentivizing Werewolf-Human interaction is reproduction is a little silly, immature and short-sighted. It also does nothing to remedy the problem for homosexual characters or heterosexual character that don't want children. I mean really, could something be any more contrived?</div> </div> </div> </div>I submit the pointed reminder that characters who don't want to have children who they are by no means culturally expected to rear themselves are probably not going to play well in a game whose driving focus is that they have been tapped for duty-bound involvement in a forever-war holding back the disparate elements of the living world from consuming everything, particularly not when matters of legacy and family are likewise so close to front-and-center.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:50:09-08:00","id":74804,"title":"","content":"I... I don't know. I think Lunacy is okay, but the automatic memory wipe... just seems too forced, unnatural, and also often removing any need of roleplaying. I wish the memory wipe part of the problem were gone. Maybe as one of the gifts or some powers like that, but memory alteration as of now seems way too weird and uninteresting, even illogical. The running-away-in-horror part makes sense, but automatically altered memory seems... just not right.<br /> <br /> The ban on breeding between werewolves... I wholeheartedly agree with what Knit-I-Fine said. It is, along with the memory aspect of the Lunacy, I always always edit out when I run my games. It really hinders the game's theme of running a pack as a family or at least pseudo-family.<br /> <br /> About power-scale though, I believe that the developers will handle this well. As for personal preferences though, I agree with the idea that the forms should really be three, man/wolf/wolf-man. (To be honest, I actually almost never ran the other two forms, nor have seen other players do that.) But yeah, I doubt they will change that. At least, I wish the other two forms will get more attention and made into distinct, different, forms that matter in certain niches. As of now, they really are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T03:14:38-08:00","id":74863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74804#post74804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ban on breeding between werewolves... I wholeheartedly agree with what Knit-I-Fine said. It is, along with the memory aspect of the Lunacy, I always always edit out when I run my games. It really hinders the game's theme of running a pack as a family or at least pseudo-family.</div> </div> </div> </div>A family is more than people in committed sexual relations...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T03:21:27-08:00","id":74867,"title":"","content":"Well, I never though that the Unihar was doing its job as being scary and horrible, what it did for me was trying too hard and just seeming silly in the end.<br /> <br /> No, Metis were not really perfect either and maybe wolf blooded did not click well with some people, which admittedly I think is pretty silly (It is not even technically bestiality if you ARE for all intends and purposes an animal, albeit a smarter and more human like one), but I think that was one of the parts where Forsaken lost me, in not being about wolves, but as was said, the myths of wolves.<br /> <br /> The problem is that it is mostly an excuse to have outdated science (behavioural biology in this instance) excused &quot;because it is not about how real wolves are&quot;. The whole alpha and pack thing is about outdated and thus not entirely accurate understanding of canine social structures (As in about as accurate as basing human social behaviour entirely on a group like the kids from Lord of the Flies, not necessarily wrong but incomplete).<br /> <br /> I think it SHOULD be more about the wolf and also about the myths of wolves, but not about misconceptions of wolves which are actually rather modern.<br /> <br /> <br /> And again, I think the best solution might really be to bring the book with dedicated options.<br /> <br /> See, some people, want werewolf families like in &quot;Everything you ever Wanted&quot;, some want wolfborn and werewolf/werewolf children who are not freaks or murder spirits, some though apparently want nothing that is a bit like Apocalypse, no fera, no Lupus, no Metis, no real social structure above the pack.<br /> <br /> Personally, mechanics aside, if it stays too much like the core of Forsaken is now, I will likely buy the book for fresh rules but discard large portions of the setting (or not play the game with another storyteller who runs it by the book).<br /> <br /> I think at heart, it is a very divisive issue, if you change things, people like me will like it, if you keep it more of the same, the people who preferred Forsaken the way it was will like it, both liking it though is... hard.<br /> <br /> If you manage to make a compromise, with options like the chroniclers guide maybe, which actually does please everyone though, you get my respect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T05:12:35-08:00","id":74894,"title":"","content":"I would change the Lunacy part. I don't like it's authomatic according your Willpower dots. I'd require a Resolve + Composture roll, with different outcomes depending on whether the roll is a success, and extraordinaty succes, a failure or a dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> Offer us different ways of organizing werewolf society (I think WaTP -or another book, I'm not sure which one- had different models of that. I also from B&amp;S the chapter from the dominions. I loved that, and I think it could be done something similar to werewolves. Different hunting grounds, with different models of running werewolf sopciety there. In some of them, the main element is the pack, but in other ones, may be the tribes are more important. In another, the Forsaken (or Pure) society can be hierarchized in a similar way to Kindred. And can even be some &quot;heretical&quot; hunting grounds: may be one in wich Predator Kings and Hunters in the Darkness are allied together to protect natural environment against more &quot;urban&quot; werewolves, etc...<br /> Currently, werewolf lacks of a well defined internal organization beyond &quot;pack is the most important, tribes are not&quot;. I think tribes role should be emphatozed, but also there should be different models of organization for werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T05:36:56-08:00","id":74909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ray White</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74867#post74867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it SHOULD be more about the wolf and also about the myths of wolves, but not about misconceptions of wolves which are actually rather modern.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's honestly a completely different game idea. When I first went to werewolf I was hoping for something more grounded than the animistic take that WoD provides, but that's the only thing we've ever been offered. The game is, whether anyone likes it or not, about spirits. And Spirits seems to be by and large representation of humanities interpretation of the world, whether that be more modern or ancient understanding.<br /> <br /> There is great potential for a werewolf game that isn't so spirit focused, but that's not what we have, and that's obviously not what the writers want to give us. (What with the spirit antagonists in the very name of this next edition.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T06:15:07-08:00","id":74923,"title":"","content":"So if spirits were removed from the game, or given less focus, who would you want to be the antagonists for werewolves?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the spirit is mostly a reflection of the real world, so while you could fight a crime spirit or a toxic waste spirit, you could also fight criminals or polluters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2014, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T06:27:24-08:00","id":74931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74923#post74923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if spirits were removed from the game, or given less focus, who would you want to be the antagonists for werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of antagonistic prospects. Other werewolves and humans might take the focus (like in changeling, where others of your own kind are the main adversary and the otherworldly beings are put in reserve for big bads). Spirits could still have a place in werewolf without being the driving force behind werewolves themselves. There's also other shapechangers, which could take the form of werewolf like beings, or entirely inhuman abominations of flesh.<br /> <br /> I don't think you'll ever find a shortage of ideas, if you really commit to it. Not that I think it'll ever happen in a W:tF. The game is what it is, and I can't fault it for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T06:44:05-08:00","id":74936,"title":"","content":"But those things do exist in the game. Other werewolves act as anagonists in the form of Pure and Bale Hounds and even other Forsaken, humans as the ones who influence the spirit and just cause trouble. Pretty much every other shapechanger from War Against the Pure and Skinchangers are made as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T08:32:31-08:00","id":74988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=74804#post74804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... I don't know.<br /> About power-scale though, I believe that the developers will handle this well. As for personal preferences though, I agree with the idea that the forms should really be three, man/wolf/wolf-man. (To be honest, I actually almost never ran the other two forms, nor have seen other players do that.) But yeah, I doubt they will change that. At least, I wish the other two forms will get more attention and made into distinct, different, forms that matter in certain niches. As of now, they really are not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Wow, The Urshul (Combat) and Dalu (Ritual) forms are heavily used in our game (well, all the forms are to be honest). They all have their uses.<br /> Hishu (Human Interaction), Dalu (Ritual), Garou (War), Urshul (Combat), Urhan (Sneaky). We hit each form (except Garou) multiple times in a session for each character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T09:38:25-08:00","id":75011,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultcf83-2.html?g=posts&amp;t=71889\" target=\"_blank\">A lively discussion about the notion of Breeds in <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b></a>. Particular high-points of the topic in question:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Forsaken</b> doesn\u2019t lend itself to the concept of WtA\u2019s Metis. More generally: if Idigam Chronicles were to include the notion of Breeds, I\u2019d expect there to only be two: born-in-human-form, and born-in-wolf-form.<br /> <br /> 2. The \u201cimplied bestiality\u201d issue can be taken off the table by making the \u201cborn as a wolf\u201d Breed be the result of two werewolves mating. This has its own implications: it would mean that werewolves who grow up as wolves would either be raised by one or both of their werewolf parents or would need some sort of adoptive parent; so I don\u2019t consider it to be an ideal solution. But if implied bestiality is otherwise going to be a show-stopper, this provides an alternative. And all you\u2019d lose would be the ghost children and possibly the stigma against werewolf mating with werewolf, both of which I wouldn\u2019t miss.<br /> <br /> 3. The \u201cimplied bestiality\u201d issue is invariably brought up by people who think that furry fandom is a bunch of sexual deviants; the validity of said arguments tend to suffer as a result of this bias. In particular, people who express interest in the notion of Breeds almost never express interest in bestiality. \u200b<br /> <br /> 4. It\u2019s worth noting that the \u201cborn-as-a-human\u201d Breed that is currently the only option in WtF isn\u2019t without its own problems, most notably implied domestic abuse.<br /> <br /> 5. I\u2019d like to see wolves in WtF presented as \u201cfantastic wolves\u201d of the sort featured in <i>The Jungle Book</i>, rather than as scientifically accurate portrayals of real-world wolves. That is, present them as valid characters in their own right, not just as pets or monsters. Wolves should be just as valid and interesting an option for antagonists as spirits are. In a setting that features ordinary humans who are ignorant of the monsters hiding in the shadows, it\u2019s not much of a stretch to say that they underestimate wolves, too. More generally, I\u2019d like to see WtF support <i>actual</i> furry fandom, instead of shrinking away from supporting them because of the misplaced distaste voiced by the anti-furries crowd.<br /> <br /> 6. If a link is to be made between &quot;spirit vs. flesh\u201d and \u201cman vs. wolf\u201d, I\u2019d like to see the wolf aspected toward the flesh <i>at least</i> as much as the man is; possibly more so. While contrasting WtF against WtA shouldn\u2019t be a high priority, it <i>would</i> be a nice contrast if, in WtF, a werewolf\u2019s spirituality was more closely associated with his <i>human</i> nature than with his <i>wolf</i> nature.<br /> <br /> 7. Better still, though, would be to play up the notion that \u201cspiritual\u201d vs. \u201ccarnal\u201d is more a matter of Harmony: it takes a balance of one\u2019s human and wolf natures to be effective when interacting with spirits, and becoming too wolf-like is just as likely to close the doors to the spirit world as becoming too human-like. I could even see reworking Harmony so that low-Harmony results in you becoming more spiritually dead rather than becoming more spirit-like: leave the latter for Primal Urge. The relationship between Primal Urge and Harmony should be one of low Harmony interfering with Primal Urge\u2019s strengths and high Harmony restraining Primal Urge\u2019s drawbacks. <br /> <br /> 8. Mating shouldn\u2019t be the primary reason for werewolves to interact with humans. A secondary reason, perhaps (albeit a <i>distant</i> second); but not the main one. The main reason should be that staying in touch with your human nature is vital to maintaining Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:29:16-08:00","id":75051,"title":"","content":"but ya'll are ignoring that there are already wolf born werewolves. Its like a 1 in a billion chance. READ THE LORE PEOPLE.<br /> <br /> I find myself wondering how many of you really read the material, and how many just jumped on the band wagon after reading negative thoughts about the main book &gt;&lt;<br /> <br /> Yes there are some legitament complaints to the way the systems work, but I do believe those are already being addressed (gifts, war form...) But as Tymeaus pointed out each form seems to have a purpose. Its less about how its presented in the book and more about how YOU use it. There's nothing saying you can't use whatever form for whatever, just rules saying there's consequences. You want to war form for everything? Go you. Be prepared to deal with a lot of spirits of violence.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm slightly afraid the devs are going to listen to half of what was here and radically change a game that I love. It happens to MMO's all the time, I don't want to see it here. I've got every book currently released for Forsaken in one way or another (pdf or print) and I would prefer for this world of darkness to stay relatively similar. I'm all for a few changes, but radically changing the core lore? That is something I will NEVER get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-19-2014, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:49:36-08:00","id":75060,"title":"","content":"Before you accuse people of not reading the lore, make sure you\u2019ve got your facts straight:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">While the Forsaken tell stories of wolves that can assume the forms of men, such beings are legendary in the modern world. None of Luna's chosen can lay claim to being wolf-born first. Rumors claim that some werewolves among the Pure Tribes do begin life as wolves and spend most of their time in feral form, but no one among the Forsaken can confirm this.</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> page 61.</div>So no, WtF does <i>not</i> already include wolf-born, except as a wild rumor: part of the original design team\u2019s effort to quash any possibility of catering to furry fandom, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:53:37-08:00","id":75065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75060#post75060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before you accuse people of not reading the lore, make sure you\u2019ve got your facts straight:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\">While the Forsaken tell stories of wolves that can assume the forms of men, such beings are legendary in the modern world. None of Luna's chosen can lay claim to being wolf-born first. Rumors claim that some werewolves among the Pure Tribes do begin life as wolves and spend most of their time in feral form, but no one among the Forsaken can confirm this.</span><br /> \u2014 <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> page 61.</div>So no, WtF does <i>not</i> already include wolf-born, except as a wild rumor: part of the original design team\u2019s effort to quash any possibility of catering to furry fandom, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good quote. Though I'm not sure you understand the furry fandom if you think wolf-born is the focused desire of that crowd in a werewolf game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T10:55:36-08:00","id":75067,"title":"","content":"I want to second Uxas opinion on making social structures that are above the pack a bit more important, or at least give them room somewhere.<br /> I think I said it before, but that vagueness about anything beyond packs made tribes and lodges seem a bit at odds with the description to me.<br /> <br /> About Spirits:<br /> <br /> No, I do not think you need to toss aside spirits, quite the contrary, particularly animal spirits / gods are usually something very integral to shapeshifter legends.<br /> <br /> I think though I would like to see spirits done more in the line of working with existing myths instead of, what I personally see as forcing a made up cosmology on of them.<br /> Shintoistic Japan is full of loads and loads of spins on spirits with a lot of potential (I can comment less on native American spirit law though).<br /> <br /> But animal spirits should be about the animal, about the legends, not primarily just about primarily modern concepts.<br /> I often thought Forsaken also still had a bit too much of that notion that really evil spirits where all stemming from humans / civilization, despite all the rich possibilities for really impressive and dangerous natural spirits.<br /> <br /> In short, embrace the wolf in wolf spirit more, make a more diverse struggle between what you are, the carnal, the spiritual, the wolf, the man..<br /> <br /> And yes, I also think the idea of making wolves as such more of something to deal with interesting.<br /> Be it normal wolves, or materialised wolf spirits, I think there is a good deal you can do with nature, just look at the way many Japanese works deal with nature spirits / animals, there is so much in terms of inspiration which I fear I did not see as much in Forsaken as I would have liked to.<br /> <br /> <br /> And seriously, if vampires can avoid shouts of Necrophilia and people are okay with all the carnage and gore werewolves are packaged with, then this should really be much less of an issue...<br /> Honestly, I find it sometimes a bit disturbing that people have more issues with wolf-shaped werewolves and normal wolves mating compared to all the violence and the idea of domestic abuse and similar, let alone the notion of cannibalism...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:27:59-08:00","id":75091,"title":"","content":"In Night Horrors, Urazakh-Angir is the son of a werewolf and a wolf. But he's considered a bit of a messiah, obviously not the norm.<br /> <br /> As for spirits, I think there's a sense of hesitancy with the core book. But, as I said in another thread, it's similar with all the core books, and these seem to be problems they're dealing with in the new Chronicles books.<br /> I always took the spirit to be, effectively, the same as the animism and shinto beliefs. I've always gone farther and seen the various gods of different mythologies (such as those showcased in Scion) as powerful spirit beings. But the books beat around the bush in that regard, which is annoying on one hand, but seeing how much flak they've taken for certain aspects in cWoD is understandable.<br /> <br /> I don't believe the books are saying humanity is the source of evil or anything, some of the Bale Hounds of Sloth, for instance, are betting on the eventual heat death of the universe (no action = ultimate sloth), It's just with humans going out and doing things, creating spirits of emotion and artifice and conflict, there does tend to be a lot of those spirits, that doesn't make them necessarily evil, any more than someone getting mad about something is evil. There are entirely disruptive and antagonistic spirits that are solely creations of the reflections of nature. One thing I thought the books got across well was that any sort of spirit (from a spirit of joy or rivers to a spirit of greed and guns) is capable of being evil just as it is capable of being good, though more often than not they're just there, doing their thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:59:21-08:00","id":75106,"title":"","content":"In tribes of the moon there is a rumor of a hunter in darkness who went mad and started rutting a wolf and it eventually took. His brood still hunts in those mountains. So yes, it is there.<br /> <br /> edit: Thanks for that nofather. But yes, before discrediting the &quot;rumors&quot; in the books, realize that the entire lore is nothing but rumors. Perhaps the reason there is no wolf born is due in part to it being so taboo in their culture. Never mind that the wolf born (also created from a hunter in darkness interestingly enough) is sterile, and possibly being controlled by something bigger. It's all in there, there's just consequences. Again, read das lore. I should note though, that what is in the core book is NOT a reflection of later supplements. Hopefully Idigam chronicle involves some of the more fun &quot;rumors,&quot; so people can see half of what they want is already in there. The main issue with Forsaken right now is how awful the core book is for information, at least information that's relevant to the lore. It's mostly just a &quot;here's a set up now go to town&quot; book.<br /> <br /> I'm also looking forward to having built in rules in the book itself. none of this &quot;buy the WoD book for your rules&quot; nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-19-2014, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:15:47-08:00","id":75160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75065#post75065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good quote. Though I'm not sure you understand the furry fandom if you think wolf-born is the focused desire of that crowd in a werewolf game...</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not <i>my</i> understanding of furry fandom that I was referencing; and yes, I <i>do</i> think that the devs in question had issues on that front. <br /> <br /> Lyrics of War: congratulations. You\u2019ve managed to point out an obscure example in a book that dealt largely with oddball cases. I guess when you say \u201cread the lore!\u201d, you mean \u201cmemorize every bit of obscure trivia before you comment on anything\u201d. I\u2019ll agree that it will be good when a lot of these facts that are currently tucked away in various supplements will be centralized in the core book. But I suspect that the motive for doing so will have more to do with making the information easier to use than with telling people \u201cI told you so!\u201d<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:24:53-08:00","id":75171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75160#post75160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not <i>my</i> understanding of furry fandom that I was referencing; and yes, I <i>do</i> think that the devs in question had issues on that front.<br /> <br /> Lyrics of War: congratulations. You\u2019ve managed to point out an obscure example in a book that dealt largely with oddball cases. I guess when you say \u201cread the lore!\u201d, you mean \u201cmemorize every bit of obscure trivia before you comment on anything\u201d. I\u2019ll agree that it will be good when a lot of these facts that are currently tucked away in various supplements will be centralized in the core book. But I suspect that the motive for doing so will have more to do with making the information easier to use than with telling people \u201cI told you so!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Data, on a scale of one to ten, how glad are you that your old signature didn't carry over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:37:54-08:00","id":75178,"title":"","content":"Viva referencia obscura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T13:55:02-08:00","id":75187,"title":"","content":"Relevance to the discussion at hand beyond being a snide jab Satchel?<br /> <br /> Back on topic. Taking those glossed over or scattered references that should be essential to presenting the game -is- an enormous thing for me and Idigam Chronicles; pointing that supplement x talks about this or that topic is fine and well (and has been done repeatedly until that dead horse was turned into a beaten pulp), but you've got a -big- problem when the core book itself doesn't address basic or intrinsically important game aspects in a concise and evocative way.<br /> <br /> Forsaken has a huge problem with that right now; it got some great material rolling more and more as time went on, but it's a kick to the balls to have to be reliant on them to get the real evocative stuff rather than the damn corebook. I could give a flying fuck if something is dealt with in more detail in Blood of the Wolf, for instance when it comes to Idigam Chronicles; supplements are great for adding additional ideas, options or digging into a topic in more depth, but the old W:tF corebook suffers badly from glossing things over that it really aught not to have. I should be picking up Idigam Chronicles and running into the exact same persistent issue that many, -many- have (and brought up and addressed here and elsewhere) it does right now.<br /> <br /> A sentence or two on a subject in a Corebook is rarely enough to something that's a common and problematic experience for all werewolves. Even a paragraph or more at times isn't. We have precisely that going on right now with the old Corebook. I've went through many, many players who picked the damn thing up, read it from cover to cover and went &quot;Uhhhh...&quot; and not from poor reading skills. These are published fucking -authors- who were left scratching their head on topics in the core presentation from the brevity. That should be a major concern, well above and beyond &quot;but my Gauru form isn't a near unstoppable tank&quot;.<br /> <br /> And yet, that's where the bulk of the focus gets put by many vocal posters, and (oh my gracious) someone goes &quot;uh, I ran into some really deficient areas in the game that I felt didn't get presented well, or addressed enough&quot; it's a figurative dog-pile by others who seem to have the &quot;Correct reading (which just so happens only to match up with their -personal- reading)&quot; the bulk of others just seem to be magically without.<br /> <br /> What, you think it's isolated? It's not. I can understand a defensive reaction to &quot;protect&quot; ones loved game, but I love it too. I'm just patently unwilling to skim every supplement I have (which is all of them) to try to find a single sentence, maybe a paragraph if I'm lucky that somehow &quot;fixes&quot; these issues. It doesn't fix them. It doesn't draw a new player in. It doesn't let someone who only has the core (and that's the only book they should need) get complete toolbox to get rolling with. All it does is trump up an older or experienced player as somehow being better, because they invested more money and spent so damn long reading and re-reading obscure references they can remember them off the top of their head. And that reference? It's the magic problem solver. &quot;Oh, but they DID talk about Wolf-blooded over here... so you're wrong&quot; as a past example. Really? Frankly put, the level of treatment, and the kind of treatment the Wolf-Blooded got even in later supplements -was insufficient and poor to everyone I know that has read the damn sections-. You think that is hyperbole? Just my reading? One others? No, lets try groups of people that I know, and commonly brought up elsewhere. You'd think that's indicative of a problem, and that's just one example.<br /> <br /> I'm seeing a distinct trend where a handful (no, really, a handful) would rather sit around and regurgitate &quot;You're just not reading it right&quot; in half a dozen different wordings rather than address things that are big, big problems in the game and the core presentation. Inevitably it's new players who aren't invested W:tF forum veterans bringing this up too, and quickly the old dogs converge and start nipping at their balls because it doesn't agree with their long, long-term settled outlooks on W:tF. The supplements aren't sufficient right now, they never were, and being reliant on them for basic things was a problem that hit the game right in it's canine testicles and ovaries more than once, and hardly rarely.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to play sin-eater and flat out say it nice and harshly; fuck the existing supplements. I like many of them, I have used them, but I'm expecting enough of a shift with the game that I understand that much if not most of the material will be out of date or patently irrelevant. I also don't have a problem with that, but I -am- concerned that this heel-digging going on here is indicative of a larger problem; the &quot;I don't want a new edition (face it, it is) to change so much that I have to buy new books to support it&quot; toxicity that riddles the RP gamer crowd. I sure as fuck shouldn't be picking up the Idigam core, and then going back to Blood of the Wolf to get what I need out of the game regarding fundamental things to do with the character and it's place in the game setting.<br /> <br /> Luckily, I don't remotely think that's going to be the case at all; if Blood and Smoke is any real indicator (hell, many recent games), they're right on the ball overall and not playing apologist in their overhauls. I like that. A lot. I like even more that I'll soon have a new Forsaken book that I want; it may well end up not matching up with what I wanted to see for the game, or, really not fall in line with my existing long-term chronicle (in which case, I'll just be using the portions that jive), but I'm kind of sick of this elitist bullshit that's been cropping up frequently as of late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 02-19-2014, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:00:26-08:00","id":75193,"title":"","content":"Note: fixing for King over there is doing away with half the written fluff - entirely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:19:48-08:00","id":75207,"title":"","content":"You expect the written &quot;fluff&quot; in Idigam Chronicles -not- to diverge and change from what was written prior at all... or are you insinuating something else entirely? I expect to see some &quot;fluff&quot; changes to go along with the mechanical changes when it's completed, there is no denying that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:39:13-08:00","id":75220,"title":"","content":"While I'm not a fan of the tone the conversation has taken on, I have to say that if what Tatterdemalion King predicts comes to pass-that is, the nullification of the fluff in previous supplements-I'll actually be <i>relieved.</i><br /> <br /> I sadly haven't had a chance to play Werewolf. I only have the core book, and I never had the passion to run the game for my players like I did for Changeling or other RPGs.I'd keep up with releases for werewolf, because I'm really, <i>really</i> intrigued, but was put off by the amount of supplements. I didn't want to get into a game and then want to rush out and buy everything, especially after what I heard about, say, <i>Changing Breeds</i>.<br /> <br /> But after <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> invigorated my desire to play Vampire, I'm really looking forward to something similar with <i>The Idigam Chronicle.</i> Perhaps my preference <i>shouldn't</i> count for as much considering I'm for all intents and purposes a werewolf n00b, but I'm glad that I can safely ignore previous splats in future conversations so long as I preface my discussions with [TIC].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:40:04-08:00","id":75223,"title":"","content":"There is admittedly a &quot;diggin in o' heals&quot; on my end, but to a certain extent. I love the lore, I love the tribes and the world. But the mechanics need a great deal of change, from rites and gifts to how certain things work. <br /> <br /> Its a bigger pain in the ass (a thought I had while driving) that all my defense of things comes from at least 4 different books. For players and storytellers to get a proper grasp on the characters they currently need at least 4 books: Forsaken; The Pure; Tribes of the Moon; Signs of the Moon; Blasphemies; and MAYBE Rage. That in itself is crap, and I am in agreement with you King. I'd rather not have to cite the 11 or so source books to prove that this stuff exists, which is really (as you said) what I and I think a great many other people are looking forward to Idigam for. <br /> <br /> Hopefully it's like Blood and Smoke (I love the layout and look of that book) and they continue that trend of awesome. <br /> <br /> Long story short, they don't need to change the lore at all, but they definently need to change how its presented. My main argument comes against people trying to infuse too much apocalypse into Forsaken. I find it grating, and if they do actually do that, all it will end up doing is eventually becoming Apocalypse 2.0, which I don't think the majority of us want. We just want a more accessible game, with most of the relevant information right there at our fingertips.<br /> <br /> We certainly got it with the w20 core book. Friggin love that thing. It's big, sexy, and all right there for me. Forsaken on the other hand is a dull read, with a constant &quot;check x page of WoD for the rules of xxxxxxxxxx.&quot; <br /> <br /> And yeah Weaver, I spent money on books so I'm certainly gonna pull random references from things. Especially the things that stand out, which are a majority of the complaints on here. Half the complaints on the tribes are things that can be found in the respective works, which as has been stated needs to be incorporated in the next core.<br /> <br /> I'm not against a new edition, rather I'm all for it. I just don't want a drastic shift in lore. I don't want the Blood Talons to turn into some new age version of the Get of Fenris. I like that the Tribes represent something of a more ideological thread. When I first read about the tribes in the core book I hated them. Reading the Tribes book completely changed that mind set, and made me realize how badly I could ruin the current set up if I championed for them to be more like the Apocalypse tribes. <br /> <br /> I also realize I sound like a dick half the time. Not my intent... most of the time. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T14:45:08-08:00","id":75228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75207#post75207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect to see some &quot;fluff&quot; changes to go along with the mechanical changes when it's completed, there is no denying that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too think some changes to the fluff are going to happen. However, I don't think it's going to be as grand as you seem to be implying. Blood &amp; Smoke still resembles Vampire the Requiem. Yes some changes were made to fluff, and definitly the mechanics, but it's still the same game. No offense, but you seem to be confusing &quot;clarifying&quot; with &quot;changing&quot;. There's a big difference between the two. I believe more clarifying will be done then any real changes to fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:02:54-08:00","id":75247,"title":"","content":"One thing I think we can mostly agree upon, make the minor bad guys playable and mechanically robust in the new book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:08:25-08:00","id":75252,"title":"","content":"what are minor bad guys to you? The ridden? The Pure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:08:41-08:00","id":75254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75247#post75247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think we can mostly agree upon, make the minor bad guys playable and mechanically robust in the new book.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you define as minor bad guys?<br /> <br /> 'Cos Forsaken has a <i>lot</i> of antagonist types and, again, I sadly have to remind people that word count is a thing we are beholden to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:14:38-08:00","id":75259,"title":"","content":"Change? sure. Completely divesting the game of stuff like Lunacy, 2 of the five forms, renown, rites? Fuck no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:17:45-08:00","id":75263,"title":"","content":"Minor bad guys? Like juveniles? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:20:18-08:00","id":75266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75259#post75259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change? sure. Completely divesting the game of stuff like Lunacy, 2 of the five forms, renown, rites? Fuck no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you are <b>SOOOOO </b>picky about these things!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">((Yes, that was a sarcasm bomb I just dropped.))</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:22:27-08:00","id":75269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75254#post75254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sadly have to remind people that word count is a thing we are beholden to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that guy, I'm sure our opinions differ, I'm not a fan of spirit claimed or hosts being playable, though mechanics for making them would be fantastic.<br /> I would like the Pure, at least, to be able to be made. Perhaps the Bale Hounds too (I love the Bale Hounds, they really are the best). They were both made out to be major antagonists in the old core book, but not really fleshed out until later, to the point that it was easy to misunderstand what they were about and what made them not-Forsaken (for instance removing the silver marks of Luna's renown)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2014, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:25:42-08:00","id":75276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75252#post75252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what are minor bad guys to you? The ridden? The Pure?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, include gift lists for the Bale Hounds and the Pure. If Claimed get the reboot they need, they should take up no more space than Stigmatics or Ghouls, assuming spirits are getting slightly more page count than they did in DtD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:29:12-08:00","id":75283,"title":"","content":"Pure are totally playable, as are bale hounds. I think they should be able to include the bale hounds gift set in the idigam book, considering in blasphemies it only takes up about 3 pages. The pure might be a bit harder, though character creation shouldn't be that hard. If they have the sections like they did in W20 they can easily incorporate the Pure. They don't need to have all of their gifts, just the majoring differing ones aye? If they can take the information from the pure book (Running a pure game might be really fun) and slim it down it shouldnt be too big of a hit to their culture. But word count is an issue. The thing is only what... 290... or so pages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:31:48-08:00","id":75286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75223#post75223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long story short, they don't need to change the lore at all, but they definently need to change how its presented. My main argument comes against people trying to infuse too much apocalypse into Forsaken. I find it grating, and if they do actually do that, all it will end up doing is eventually becoming Apocalypse 2.0, which I don't think the majority of us want. We just want a more accessible game, with most of the relevant information right there at our fingertips.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I agree with this; it\u2019s a big part of the reason why I\u2019m a fan of making the spirit world less mandatory in the game; that alone would go a long way to distancing Forsaken from Apocalypse. That said: just because Apocalypse does something that Forsaken currently doesn\u2019t (such as more than one playable Breed), that doesn\u2019t <i>necessarily</i> make it a bad thing to include in Forsaken \u2014 as long as it\u2019s done in a way that enhances Forsaken\u2019s themes rather than undermining them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75223#post75223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah Weaver, I spent money on books so I'm certainly gonna pull random references from things. Especially the things that stand out, which are a majority of the complaints on here. Half the complaints on the tribes are things that can be found in the respective works, which as has been stated needs to be incorporated in the next core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Referencing them is one thing; implying that the people making suggestions should read everything before suggesting something is something else entirely, as it borders on telling people to shut up. In short, I wouldn\u2019t have had nearly as much of a problem with your post if you had left out the \u201cread the lore!\u201d line and the subsequent snide comment about people who suggest things.<br /> <br /> As for what should be playable in Idigam Chronicles: the Forsaken should be playable; anyone beyond that is gravy, and should be cut if word count becomes an issue. That includes the Pure, Bale Hounds, Claimed, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-19-2014, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:35:41-08:00","id":75289,"title":"","content":"yeah that is a thing. But look, we have hexmeister asking for a gift list for the Bale Hounds and it's already in book form! But this is more again the same problem. I also realize it's unfair of me to assume people have the money to spend on all these books. I got them all back when they released when I had less financial responsibilities (i.e. house payments and all that) so it was easier then. Being a nerd is an expensive hobby.<br /> <br /> that said.... HEXMEISTER, if you want the bale hounds gift lists I can give you some fine examples. The tainted moon list is A LOT of fun to work with. The requirements to get it are a bit nuts though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T15:52:22-08:00","id":75297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75276#post75276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the very least, include gift lists for the Bale Hounds and the Pure. If Claimed get the reboot they need, they should take up no more space than Stigmatics or Ghouls, assuming spirits are getting slightly more page count than they did in DtD.</div> </div> </div> </div>A further question for you - I assumed when you said 'playable' you meant 'players can play characters of this type', whereas you might instead mean playable as in you can run NPCs of this type out of the corebook. Can I get a clarification on which one you're wanting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T18:50:00-08:00","id":75377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75259#post75259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Change? sure. Completely divesting the game of stuff like Lunacy, 2 of the five forms, renown, rites? Fuck no.</div> </div> </div> </div> And if you'd read the thread regarding the changes for -our game-, you'd see where the forms thing was specifically for our chronicle; overall it's assumed many (most?) would want to keep them as innate aspects, and I don't see that as a problem. That's specifically addressing some problems we had in that regard; it's not the expectation that it should be adopted wholesale. Chronicle specific. Having all 5 to me isn't a big thing if they got a differing treatment than currently.<br /> <br /> Divesting renown: not as is, not at all. Know how me and the other changed it? We stop using the term renown. What it was is covered by Honorary Rank and Tribal Status. It's a terminology shift, really the only real thing done is not rail-roading gameplay by what was previously required to go up in it, and taking it out as a hard power cap. In mechanical terms? It's just covered by other pre-existing areas. I just don't see much use in the term anymore, it's a redundancy.<br /> <br /> Rites? To each their own there. I'm not a fan of a non-nonsensical system that's predicated on &quot;it's anything, and everything that doesn't fit the 1-5 list. Also, stuff&quot; so instead, there are alternate Instinct levels instead of a grab-bag. Seems clean. The focus of what rites are and what they do are tighter; Essence/Shadow manipulation, externalizing the influence of a werewolf on it's spiritual environment where instincts are more the internal. That's not an excision; that's a change of focus and shuffling of what goes where. Also, some rites make more sense as Numina anyhow (see the rite of healing. Healing Numina anyone?), which keeps those aspects -still- accessible.<br /> <br /> Lunacy? Some mass human group debuffer? Integrity already covers this in part with some of the Breaking Points it has with humans. The rest is wrapped into the Predatory Aura and treated as something less ridiculously potent to keep humans a legitimate problem, but one that requires -action on the part of the werewolf- to fully exploit, just like with vampires. It's an edge. Want people to take off much more easily? Hit them with the Flight aspect of the Predatory Aura. Want to even more fucking scary? Instincts, Merits, more... I just don't need it overwhelmingly like it was, and it was something my players thought was goofy before. As is the default idea is they travel in packs; that's multiple people capable of whammying multiple others with the aura, those that -don't- do what most humans presented with a situation like that in the wod does: run like hell, rationalize or ignore it.<br /> <br /> What you're calling excision is closer to revision, shuffling things around and refocusing. Nothing in what I've tried or my co-ST with our tinkering thus far entirely removes things entirely; even wonky gifts from before are easily kept as Numina of one sort of another.<br /> <br /> The real issue isn't that I'm taking stuff -out- of the game, or my co-writer (actually, we're intending to add -more-); it's that it's different enough from the prior iterations that you don't like it due to the level of change present. And as I've said before, brace for impact; the level of differences you've cited as desiring before would barely make for the GMC rules updates and may as well be an errata. I'm expecting heavy changes. In fact, I know heavy changes are coming down the pipe on par with Blood and Smoke at the least.<br /> <br /> Prepare to be have your expectations dashed. I wouldn't be surprised if my and my co-st's takes on things don't even go as far, but keep in mind I'm primarily presenting ideas that address problems I've ran into playing or running the game, or ideas that me, my co-st or my players were very interested in. It's going to from that perspective, and it's going to heavily differ if you've been running your games without that sort of experience. In the end you're dealing with an overhaul, not a minor rules update, and no matter how much you stomp your foot on the forums, threadcrap, and pull the equivalent of putting your fingers in your ears going &quot;lalala&quot; because people have differing tastes and ideas on where they want to see the game going is going to avert that. I can agree to disagree. The difference? I'm actually backing up the ideas myself and others have presented as ways to update or adjust the came with -actual constructive content-. Instincts were the tip of the iceberg. The newest draft with other systems is just one portion of a lot more. I don't expect you to like the ideas, I don't expect that level of content from you either (it's a lot of goddamn work), but I don't need the treatment I and others have been getting from you over it when we present something you just don't like, especially when it turns into something ongoing and hostile in tone.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice if you did the same instead of constant passive-aggressive jabs at me and others who're trying to present material and ideas, see how they work, learn, revise and otherwise look at the potential of W:tF above and beyond some minor fiddling and stop-gaps. All I have to say on the matter, Ephsy; we have very differing outlooks, obviously, but I'm getting very tired of what you've been doing and I'm not alone in this (so don't you dare right it off as just me taking issue with this as a quick way to dismiss it).<br /> <br /> Want to make an impact and change my outlooks or ideas on this? Show -us- what you want to see the game to be like, a consolidated list, some mechanical idea suggestions, some meat, -something- that we can look at collectively (and by we, I mean this forum) and go &quot;Huh, never thought of it that way, that could work better!&quot; or &quot;That's a good idea, lets try that out&quot;, or even &quot;That doesn't work for my game, and here's why&quot;. As it stands I've seen more pissing on others by you than that, consistently, especially when it's not some echo-chamber with a couple others you see eye-to-eye with. It's been brought up, it has been discussed, and as much as I'd love to continue to contribute on this forum I'm seeing a handful of toxic posters like you making this place very uninviting to do that in. Anything that doesn't directly jive with your personal tastes gets attacked, along with the players who present it though rarely with any meaningful explanation, or constructive criticism. That in of itself isn't fun; it's only worse when there's more people doing it, and there has been for fuck sakes. And when it's not overt insults over it (or mod intervention), it's subtle jabs and pot shots, selective reading and intentionally twisting what people say. You're bringing nothing new to the table. <br /> <br /> Until that happens, that is, I see something with some meat to it more than &quot;I don't like what you like and I'm gonna hammer you with it any chance I get&quot;, something more than attitude, insults, passive-aggressive jabs, instigation attempts and all the other crap you've been pulling I really don't see further need addressing you..It's going nowhere and it isn't appreciated. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T19:19:22-08:00","id":75385,"title":"","content":"TK, almost everything you've accused Ephsy of at the end of your post you've managed to do within the body of your post. Glass houses my friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T22:35:18-08:00","id":75451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75297#post75297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A further question for you - I assumed when you said 'playable' you meant 'players can play characters of this type', whereas you might instead mean playable as in you can run NPCs of this type out of the corebook. Can I get a clarification on which one you're wanting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, but definitely the first. Especially for Claimed, which now that I think about it, make a bit more sense as this SPLAT's Tier 2 then Wolf-blooded, what with the supernatural merits presented in GMC. What I mean to say is that they would work better IMHO without a power stat, as Claimed built RAW are a little wonky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T23:26:16-08:00","id":75461,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:15px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75289#post75289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah that is a thing. But look, we have hexmeister asking for a gift list for the Bale Hounds and it's already in book form! But this is more again the same problem. I also realize it's unfair of me to assume people have the money to spend on all these books. I got them all back when they released when I had less financial responsibilities (i.e. house payments and all that) so it was easier then. Being a nerd is an expensive hobby.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75289#post75289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">that said.... HEXMEISTER, if you want the bale hounds gift lists I can give you some fine examples. The tainted moon list is A LOT of fun to work with. The requirements to get it are a bit nuts though.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Well, I do have those books, but, if my DnD and Masquerade experience have taught me anything, it's that it is easier to ask for something dodgy if it's in the main rulebook you are using. I feel that these aspects of Uratha society should be approached in a similar fashion to the way Promethean approached the Centimani and Pandoran Transmutations, i.e.: anyone could learn them, but using them around the wrong crowd would cause problems, and not being part of the right group, the group that truly understands the finer uses of those powers, generally results in that knowledge driving you mad, doing irrevocable harm to your relationships or in rare cases, slowly killing you. Having it there creates a useful degree of tension, especially in a world where falling victim to your own moral relativism is almost a given.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T03:07:32-08:00","id":75504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75451#post75451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both, but definitely the first. Especially for Claimed, which now that I think about it, make a bit more sense as this SPLAT's Tier 2 then Wolf-blooded, what with the supernatural merits presented in GMC. What I mean to say is that they would work better IMHO without a power stat, as Claimed built RAW are a little wonky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Honest question here, I'm not being snide or anything - given the aforementioned wordcount issue, would you prefer to see the book have rules for making Claimed, Pure, Bale Hounds etc playable as player characters, or would you prefer to see the words and space put into filling out playing Forsaken further?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T03:32:18-08:00","id":75515,"title":"","content":"Making Idigam playable.<br /> <br /> *OBVIOUSLY*<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T07:53:49-08:00","id":75618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75504#post75504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok. Honest question here, I'm not being snide or anything - given the aforementioned wordcount issue, would you prefer to see the book have rules for making Claimed, Pure, Bale Hounds etc playable as player characters, or would you prefer to see the words and space put into filling out playing Forsaken further?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitly fill out playing Forsaken further. I have never been interested in playing things like the Pure, Bale Hounds, and especially Claimed. Claimed? Really? These things as antagonists, as well as the Hosts, are one of the things that sold me on this game in the first place. The Pure and Bale Hounds probably should get a little fleshed out for the the Idigam Chronicles, but keep the Claimed as &quot;bad guy&quot; material. Don't waste the space and word count on making them playable, please.<br /> <br /> That being said, I wouldn't mind if the Claimed Condition was further fleshed out. As presented in the GMC, it left me kinda wanting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T08:07:07-08:00","id":75628,"title":"","content":"I should note that Claimed was written the way it is in GMC to set up Idigam Chronicle using Claimed as bad guys. GMC has <i>how</i> spirits Claim victims, but we didn't have room for any Dread Powers. So we left them for future books to figure out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T08:14:37-08:00","id":75634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75628#post75628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that Claimed was written the way it is in GMC to set up Idigam Chronicle using Claimed as bad guys. GMC has <i>how</i> spirits Claim victims, but we didn't have room for any Dread Powers. So we left them for future books to figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Well thank you for clearing that up. I look forward to what you guys have cooked up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:03:35-08:00","id":75659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75634#post75634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see. Well thank you for clearing that up. I look forward to what you guys have cooked up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mayhem, shenanigans, pants-shitting terror, and blood, mostly. Oh the blood. Seriously, it's all over my kitchen. It's terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:40:42-08:00","id":75696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75504#post75504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ok. Honest question here, I'm not being snide or anything - given the aforementioned wordcount issue, would you prefer to see the book have rules for making Claimed, Pure, Bale Hounds etc playable as player characters, or would you prefer to see the words and space put into filling out playing Forsaken further?</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:15px\">As I was saying earlier, making Pure and Bale Hounds playable from day 1 shouldn't tread too much on the Forsaken's page count, as most of their stuff can be tacked onto the Gifts material anyway, adding maybe 5 pages to the mechanical portion of the book. What's left of their material is probably going to be in the fluff anyway. As for Claimed, all that needs to be accounted for is the value of being able to step sideways, which in CB was about 15 xp, and costing out Influences. RAW from DtD, this version should be a lot simpler to design, really only taking up as much space as Stigmatics. Again, I bring it up because Claimed are a better fit for Supernatural Merits than Wolf-blooded, IMHO. At most, you'd be looking at 12 pages of material that I'd really want out of approximately 290.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T10:07:42-08:00","id":75715,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I've posted on this thread, but it seems to have moved on, which is good for the discussion on what we would like to see!<br /> <br /> Regarding the &quot;PC status&quot; for Claimed/Bale Hounds/Pure? Please leave it out (by default) of the core Idigams Chronicles. That way we get extra words on concentrating the (frankly) brilliant game line back into a single core book. If at the end there's space for that sort of stuff, then yeah that'll be good. Although writing this has mad me realise that what I mean to say about PC status would be that enough mechanics to allow the GM to build interesting antagonists with a tool-set to give them 'dread powers'. More word count would be able to add more to the mechanics and information. I feel that a word-set that includes rules and advice on running those guys as full PCs can be in another book. I'm sure the Idigam Chronicles is going to sell, and that we'll have more werewolf books in the future. There's space in that future to hit on stuff like this, that isn't that relevant to a core book that is putting all the gameline's development over the years back in to book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75628#post75628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note that Claimed was written the way it is in GMC to set up Idigam Chronicle using Claimed as bad guys. GMC has <i>how</i> spirits Claim victims, but we didn't have room for any Dread Powers. So we left them for future books to figure out.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC you wrote the spirit rules for GMC. Does this mean you'll be the one behind this sort of thing for Idigam? If so, that would be grand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Concerning Tatterdemalion King's points, first a caveat; I have no interest in your game, in not going to play in it, and it isn't (from what I've seen) the Forsaken that gt me into the line in the first place. So I'm not making coments on that game (I would have no right to, you haven't asked me for feedback :P ). So the following comments touch on how I feel to Werewolf the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75377#post75377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divesting renown: not as is, not at all. Know how me and the other changed it? We stop using the term renown. What it was is covered by Honorary Rank and Tribal Status. It's a terminology shift, really the only real thing done is not rail-roading gameplay by what was previously required to go up in it, and taking it out as a hard power cap. In mechanical terms? It's just covered by other pre-existing areas. I just don't see much use in the term anymore, it's a redundancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick with Renown is, it is quite obviously magical Status. I'm not even going to try to defend that, because it's obvious!<br /> <br /> That said, Renown should stay. Werewolves in nWoD should have their status as a magical power because it is *entirely thematic* that a group of Tribal beings have some sort of status built from spiritual power. I think the problem with renown at the moment is that it might not be clear enough, or obviously thematic enough. The fact that it could very easily be houseruled to be used as status should be used <b>in conjunction</b> with it's supernatural advantages. This is a stat that belongs in Werewolf, regardless whether this was in Apocolypse (which I couldn't care less about, and never impacted by initial buy in to Forsaken).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75377#post75377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites? To each their own there. I'm not a fan of a non-nonsensical system that's predicated on &quot;it's anything, and everything that doesn't fit the 1-5 list. Also, stuff&quot; so instead, there are alternate Instinct levels instead of a grab-bag. Seems clean. The focus of what rites are and what they do are tighter; Essence/Shadow manipulation, externalizing the influence of a werewolf on it's spiritual environment where instincts are more the internal. That's not an excision; that's a change of focus and shuffling of what goes where. Also, some rites make more sense as Numina anyhow (see the rite of healing. Healing Numina anyone?), which keeps those aspects -still- accessible.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does someties feel that way, doesn't it? Which is a shame. Look at how Geist does ceremonies (if you haven't, do - Geist is a lovely line, tat like werewolf, needs some TLC), they're thematic as hell. I always liked the rituals that were incredibly cultural, wether it was the funeral rite or the rite of the last stand (or whatever it's called, my bookshelves aaaall the way across the room). Rites rewritten fluff wise (mechanically wise, they're okay as far as I'm concerned, they just need to be added to the new extended actions paradigm, a la blood sorcery in Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> The way that the supernatrual powers (specifically Gifts and Rites) are thematic (<b>not</b>mechanically), and how this is written, could benefit a lot (IMO, remember) from looking how Geist did it. For all it faults, Geist <b>feels</b>like the game it's selling. Some bits of Forsaken are a bit old, and not the tightest thematically. That said, there are awesomely thematic stuff out there, just look at the Tribes and Auspices books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75377#post75377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunacy? Some mass human group debuffer? Integrity already covers this in part with some of the Breaking Points it has with humans. The rest is wrapped into the Predatory Aura and treated as something less ridiculously potent to keep humans a legitimate problem, but one that requires -action on the part of the werewolf- to fully exploit, just like with vampires. It's an edge. Want people to take off much more easily? Hit them with the Flight aspect of the Predatory Aura. Want to even more fucking scary? Instincts, Merits, more... I just don't need it overwhelmingly like it was, and it was something my players thought was goofy before. As is the default idea is they travel in packs; that's multiple people capable of whammying multiple others with the aura, those that -don't- do what most humans presented with a situation like that in the wod does: run like hell, rationalize or ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the way Lunacy works should be updated now that we've seen how well the new predatory aura works, and how conditions get into the game.<br /> <br /> But then again, I would be very surprised if the forum users aren't preaching to the choir when they wink-wink-nudge-nudge this to the developers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75377#post75377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real issue isn't that I'm taking stuff -out- of the game, or my co-writer (actually, we're intending to add -more-); it's that it's different enough from the prior iterations that you don't like it due to the level of change present. And as I've said before, brace for impact; the level of differences you've cited as desiring before would barely make for the GMC rules updates and may as well be an errata. I'm expecting heavy changes. In fact, I know heavy changes are coming down the pipe on par with Blood and Smoke at the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I don't think Blood and Smoke changed much. My opinion is that it's still very much Requiem. Hell, the only affect it has had on the Requiem game I'm in right now is that the mechanics are far more fun to play around with. I would be very surprised (and, I have to admit disappointed, which may heavily affect my opinion) if Forsaken changed as much as you seem to expect. Then again, I'm sure we are both heavily biased towards what we want out of the game - I just think you want a game that's like Forsaken, but not the mainstream Forsaken that the line represents.<br /> <br /> Different opinions, but I'm hating on you - we can disagree amiably of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just wished we would cut ALL the passive aggressive from everyone. It doesn't help, it massively derails the thread and won't (and never has) added to the discussion. It just kills the thread for a week or so, until someone comes back and goes, &quot;um guys? I had this thought about what I would like....&quot; and it starts over again. It's a tad frustrating to have to scroll though (which I want to, I love Forsaken.<br /> <br /> *Looks back at the post*. Blimely, that the largest post I've ever done O.o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:22:06-08:00","id":75755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=75715#post75715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks back at the post*. Blimely, that the largest post I've ever done O.o</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-sarcastic round of applause for the accomplishment, good sir. Well done.","s