"value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:01:34-07:00","id":95883,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who got major nostalgia from that song?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:16:35-07:00","id":95899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95883#post95883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who got major nostalgia from that song?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not alone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Right then. We've got something more concrete for people to chew on now. Thoughts on the new Harmony?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:16:48-07:00","id":95900,"title":"","content":"I love the concept as presented. However, I think the presentation of the Harmony meter needs a serious rework then. Having Harmony 10 be one of the two worst spots is very counter-intuitive, not just compared to other game lines, where 10 is the highest and &quot;best&quot;, but higher number are generally associated with better in general. &quot;Harmony 10&quot; <i>looks </i>like a good spot to be.<br /> <br /> Maybe some sort of &quot;+&quot; and &quot;-&quot; system? But that would not really fix the underlying issue, since &quot;+5&quot;, whether that is too spirit or too human, still looks &quot;good&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:27:39-07:00","id":95914,"title":"","content":"I note that &quot;higher Harmony&quot; meaning &quot;more human&quot; says interesting things about the Ithaeur, assuming rites still work off of Harmony.<br /> <br /> It also seems to lend a curious context to the auspices' &quot;signature&quot; forms being arranged with the Rahu getting the midpoint form - Gauru may be a synthesis of man and wolf, but it's definitely the most spirit-like of the five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:28:04-07:00","id":95915,"title":"","content":"I find &quot;Harmony 10 isn't necessarily a good thing&quot; is a really great idea. The sweet spot is now 5, so you should strive to balance. I think that's a great idea and greatly represent the theme it suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:39:29-07:00","id":95925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95914#post95914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that &quot;higher Harmony&quot; meaning &quot;more human&quot; says interesting things about the Ithaeur, assuming rites still work off of Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Rites will not be as closely tied to Harmony since it states in the post that it is not a dice pool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Harmony is not used as a dice pool</i>, and it isn\u2019t a resistance trait. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:46:09-07:00","id":95931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95925#post95925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Rites will not be as closely tied to Harmony since it states in the post that it is not a dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Work off of&quot; does not necessarily mean &quot;roll,&quot; I note - the old Death Rage stimulus chart appears to be replicated in concept, for example, and Geist's modifiers to ceremonies for high or low Synergy is still a partial predication on the splat's Integrity stat, as is Changeling's occasional bonuses to rolls from low Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:04:17-07:00","id":95940,"title":"","content":"Why not 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, and 0 can be reached from 1 on either &quot;side&quot;. Then you've still got a &quot; you're an NPC&quot; state, and higher is still always better. The only thing you'd have to do is add a qualifier if you're Harmony 3 (spirit) or Harmony 3 (human).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:04:38-07:00","id":95941,"title":"","content":"Resposting here from the blog, but; This might be more a playstyle thing I've seen, but I think high Harmony could be a bit more punishing to show its an unnatural state for an Uratha. Because I've seen people play Uratha that never shifts outside hishu unless there is combat (and even then, using essence to shift), and who never go into the shadow. How would the Harmony drawbacks be punishments to players who play them as normal for uratha?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:58:03-07:00","id":95971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95900#post95900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the concept as presented. However, I think the presentation of the Harmony meter needs a serious rework then. Having Harmony 10 be one of the two worst spots is very counter-intuitive, not just compared to other game lines, where 10 is the highest and &quot;best&quot;, but higher number are generally associated with better in general. &quot;Harmony 10&quot; <i>looks </i>like a good spot to be.<br /> <br /> Maybe some sort of &quot;+&quot; and &quot;-&quot; system? But that would not really fix the underlying issue, since &quot;+5&quot;, whether that is too spirit or too human, still looks &quot;good&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think there's a problem with having a high value not be positive. I imagine that the final draft will make it fairly clear that high and low are both bad, and it helps with the feel of something you need to balance, not something to max out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95914#post95914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that &quot;higher Harmony&quot; meaning &quot;more human&quot; says interesting things about the Ithaeur, assuming rites still work off of Harmony.<br /> <br /> It also seems to lend a curious context to the auspices' &quot;signature&quot; forms being arranged with the Rahu getting the midpoint form - Gauru may be a synthesis of man and wolf, but it's definitely the most spirit-like of the five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rites no longer work off of Harmony.<br /> <br /> The five forms aren't a parallel to the Flesh -&gt; Spirit metre of Harmony.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95941#post95941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resposting here from the blog, but; This might be more a playstyle thing I've seen, but I think high Harmony could be a bit more punishing to show its an unnatural state for an Uratha. Because I've seen people play Uratha that never shifts outside hishu unless there is combat (and even then, using essence to shift), and who never go into the shadow. How would the Harmony drawbacks be punishments to players who play them as normal for uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death Rage triggers are a pretty brutal penalty for Uratha trying to (or accidentally managing to) maintain a high Harmony and cling to their human side. If they do still use shapeshifting in combat, they're suffering because they have to both spend Essence <i>and</i> make rolls to change form - and remember, you haven't yet seen what we've done with the forms themselves. Not being able to enter the Shadow has fairly significant impact for an Uratha; characters who willingly never go into the Shadow <i>anyway</i> are, one might say, already voluntarily punishing themselves by limiting their capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:09:29-07:00","id":95975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95971#post95971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Death Rage triggers are a pretty brutal penalty for Uratha trying to (or accidentally managing to) maintain a high Harmony and cling to their human side. If they do still use shapeshifting in combat, they're suffering because they have to both spend Essence <i>and</i> make rolls to change form - and remember, you haven't yet seen what we've done with the forms themselves. Not being able to enter the Shadow has fairly significant impact for an Uratha; characters who willingly never go into the Shadow <i>anyway</i> are, one might say, already voluntarily punishing themselves by limiting their capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm mainly asking this, because I've seen it become a problem in some games where players want to play their Uratha as mostly human. I am quite certain the Kuruth and forms will help to support trying to have a balanced harmony ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T15:18:29-07:00","id":95984,"title":"","content":"See, now I really wish we had collectively picked Kuruth last week. Oh well, we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T16:22:41-07:00","id":96034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95971#post95971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't think there's a problem with having a high value not be positive. I imagine that the final draft will make it fairly clear that high and low are both bad, and it helps with the feel of something you need to balance, not something to max out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is not necessarily in having a high value be negative, but &quot;Harmony 10&quot; in particular implies &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot;, which it is not, since Harmony 5 is &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot;. If the trait itself was called &quot;Dissonance&quot;, for example, it would be more logical and intuitive that a low value is best. Zero dissonance is best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Made more understandable 03-21-2014, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T16:34:42-07:00","id":96045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=95971#post95971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The five forms aren't a parallel to the Flesh -&gt; Spirit metre of Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Applicability and goofy speculation are kind of a thing that I do. If anyone takes that as inadvertent misinformation I will be the first to apologize, but going &quot;this seems like a neat probably-coincidence&quot; is basically a third of how I engage with WoD material. I've made <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/crazyroom.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">conspiracy theorist jokes</a> about it.<br /> <br /> Thank you for clarifying, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-21-2014, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T16:48:18-07:00","id":96051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96034#post96034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The problem is not necessarily in having a high value be negative, but &amp;quot;Harmony 10&amp;quot; in particular implies &amp;quot;highest possible Harmony&amp;quot;, which it is not, since Harmony 5 is &amp;quot;highest possible Harmony&amp;quot;. If the trait itself was called &amp;quot;Dissonance&amp;quot;, for example, it would be more logical and intuitive that a low value is best. Zero dissonance is best.</div> </div> </div> </div> A low value isn't best either though. A 1 is just as bad as a 10. An intermediate value is actually what you want, with 5 being ideal. So neither name would really fit unless the numbers were changed. Honestly though, that's all just presentation. I love the idea of the mechanic itself, they can call it poopypants 14 and I'll still enjoy the way it works. The labeling is just extra flair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T17:13:57-07:00","id":96059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96034#post96034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is not necessarily in having a high value be negative, but &quot;Harmony 10&quot; in particular implies &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot;, which it is not, since Harmony 5 is &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot;. If the trait itself was called &quot;Dissonance&quot;, for example, it would be more logical and intuitive that a low value is best. Zero dissonance is best.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot; anymore, though. There is only &quot;balanced Harmony,&quot; or &quot;imbalanced Harmony.&quot; In the latter case, now you know which way it's imbalanced - toward the flesh, or toward the spirit (if the number is high or low, respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T17:43:13-07:00","id":96079,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't think, when the time comes to play, people will be having a problem with thinking 10 out of 10 is most balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T19:14:29-07:00","id":96121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96059#post96059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no &quot;highest possible Harmony&quot; anymore, though. There is only &quot;balanced Harmony,&quot; or &quot;imbalanced Harmony.&quot; In the latter case, now you know which way it's imbalanced - toward the flesh, or toward the spirit (if the number is high or low, respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Balanced Harmony&quot; is tautological. The greatest possible Harmony is perfect balance between two things. As such, under the new rules, Harmony 5 is, in fact, the highest possible Harmony, as it is perfect Harmony. The intuitive thing, however, would be to expect Harmony 10 to be the highest possible Harmony because higher numbers imply greater values.<br /> <br /> I realise this all sounds pedantic and might be because of my job background, but I genuinely find this would be confusing for new and old players, who do not read the forums regularly.<br /> <br /> A scale that is much more intuitive would be:<br /> <br /> 0<br /> 1<br /> 2<br /> 3<br /> 4<br /> 5 - Highest Possible Harmony<br /> 4<br /> 3<br /> 2<br /> 1<br /> 0<br /> <br /> You would only need some tag for the Too-Human-End and the Too-Spirit-End.<br /> This could even appear as a pyramid instead of a scale on the character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 03-21-2014, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T19:22:34-07:00","id":96124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96121#post96121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could even appear as a pyramid instead of a scale on the character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean a <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/Scale_of_justice_2_new.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">scale</a> instead of a meter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T19:25:40-07:00","id":96125,"title":"","content":"I certainly derped there, my apologies, but yeah that works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T22:15:33-07:00","id":96188,"title":"","content":"No one thinks a 10 on the pain scale is &quot;the best&quot; so it's a matter of presentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T22:19:46-07:00","id":96191,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rather not have confusion over which Harmony 1 I'm talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T00:23:35-07:00","id":96224,"title":"","content":"Without Breaking Point (disharmony?) examples I'm kind of scratching my head on this one; the sliding scale isn't bad, reminds me heavily of Kult rpg's balance system heavily (not a bad thing), or condensing Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom into one chart instead of two seperate ones so the sliding scale runs more neatly.<br /> <br /> What the blog didn't give me any headway on though is how this addresses the wolf aspect of werewolves in regards to Harmony. Flesh (human flesh) and spirit, yes, wolf and man? How is that being handled? Assuming that the wolf-like insincts and nature is the spirit side seems very oddto me given how spirits have consistently been preseneted, so I have to ask; where does a portion of you being a -wolf-, an honest-to-goodness wolf weigh into that mix? Is it rolled up into the highly Shadow portion of Harmony (wolf-spirit)? Is that what Primal Urge now more firmly represents? Something else entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T02:32:03-07:00","id":96252,"title":"","content":"Tatterdemalion King, I guess the wolf part IS the spirit part. After all, werewolves come from a wolf spirit and are cousins to the Firstborns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T04:37:22-07:00","id":96271,"title":"","content":"I guess I'd prefer a scale that goes something like this:<br /> <br /> Flesh 5<br /> Flesh 4<br /> Flesh 3<br /> Flesh 2<br /> Flesh 1<br /> Balance<br /> Spirit 1<br /> Spirit 2<br /> Spirit 3<br /> Spirit 4<br /> Spirit 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T04:59:20-07:00","id":96280,"title":"","content":"That'd definitely be more understandable.<br /> <br /> Other way to do it is to change the name Harmony for another that presented less disonance with the concepts it tries to represent. If I have a Trait called Harmony that goes from 1 to 10, the initial thought is that 10 is the best posible point at wich I can be. Wich is not.<br /> <br /> I must also note than in a 1 to 10 scale, 5 is not the middle (though it is now 0 to 10, isn't it?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T07:09:12-07:00","id":96328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tatterdemalion King</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96224#post96224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without Breaking Point (disharmony?) examples I'm kind of scratching my head on this one; the sliding scale isn't bad, reminds me heavily of Kult rpg's balance system heavily (not a bad thing), or condensing Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom into one chart instead of two seperate ones so the sliding scale runs more neatly. What the blog didn't give me any headway on though is how this addresses the wolf aspect of werewolves in regards to Harmony. Flesh (human flesh) and spirit, yes, wolf and man? How is that being handled? Assuming that the wolf-like insincts and nature is the spirit side seems very oddto me given how spirits have consistently been preseneted, so I have to ask; where does a portion of you being a -wolf-, an honest-to-goodness wolf weigh into that mix? Is it rolled up into the highly Shadow portion of Harmony (wolf-spirit)? Is that what Primal Urge now more firmly represents? Something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that's really under the purview of Harmony. I'm guessing we will see more of the wolf aspect when we start getting into Primal Urge, the forms, and some of the powers. Also, I assume a lot of the balance of wolf and man will come through in the Breaking Points, like you said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T05:11:32-07:00","id":96831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=96280#post96280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd definitely be more understandable.<br /> <br /> Other way to do it is to change the name Harmony for another that presented less disonance with the concepts it tries to represent. If I have a Trait called Harmony that goes from 1 to 10, the initial thought is that 10 is the best posible point at wich I can be. Wich is not.<br /> <br /> I must also note than in a 1 to 10 scale, 5 is not the middle (though it is now 0 to 10, isn't it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 0 to 10 now, yes.<br /> <br /> I feel fairly confident that the write-up of Harmony will make it quite clear and comprehensible how the scale works and that high is not necessarily better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T14:00:54-07:00","id":97030,"title":"","content":"It may seem silly, but puting the Harmony trait horizontally rather than vertically may help with that (also only marking the dot you are at, instead of filling all of them till that).<br /> <br /> Up or down (specially if it looks like a metter filling up) has certain conotations that a right to left positioning of a single dot doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T14:27:03-07:00","id":97045,"title":"","content":"I think Thorbes has a pretty good idea there. I suppor this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T06:54:12-07:00","id":97493,"title":"","content":"Seconded on the horizontal Harmony bar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:38:03-07:00","id":97509,"title":"","content":"...Maybe.<br /> <br /> I can't think of a reason not to beyond uniformity of character sheets, but even with understanding the visual evocation of it(and don't get me wrong, it is visually evocative of what we're going for), I can't really compel myself to say go for it either.<br /> <br /> I guess my biggest argument against it would be the complete rearrangement of the character sheet around that one move would be a pain in the ass to work out, and since I'm not involved with the layout of anything in Idigam anyways, the point's moot. Still, while I like the idea, I wouldn't be heartbroken if they kept it simple on themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"Arcane