ds both extremes (Which bring major benefits and drawbacks), but which make you effectively pick a side?<br /> <br /> Something like:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">o <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">o </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">o </span><span style=\"font-size:18px\">o</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T12:14:53-07:00","id":97654,"title":"","content":"Two desirables in an Integrity/Morality scale? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T14:50:02-07:00","id":97767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=97619#post97619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it's a little unprecedented, they could always play with size of the dots, larger towards the center smaller towards the ends. Looking something like this:<br /> ( <span style=\"font-size:8px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">o <span style=\"font-size:12px\">o </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">o</span> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">o </span><span style=\"font-size:8px\">o</span> )<br /> <br /> That'd probably dismiss any lingering doubt as to where on the scale you want a character to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly gets the idea in a just quick look.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just a quick question, if Harmony is not rolled for anything anymore... do we really need it on a numbered 0-10 scale? Can't we simply have the scale with one size saying Spirit and the other Man or something?<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">ooooo<b>o</b>ooooo</span> <b>Man</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 03-24-2014, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T15:28:38-07:00","id":97800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=97767#post97767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It certainly gets the idea in a just quick look. EDIT: Just a quick question, if Harmony is not rolled for anything anymore... do we really need it on a numbered 0-10 scale? Can't we simply have the scale with one size saying Spirit and the other Man or something? <b>Spirit</b> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">ooooo<b>o</b>ooooo</span> <b>Man</b></div> </div> </div> </div> The numbers might be used in determining modifiers to the breaking point roll. In fact, they probably are since the blog said the further you are from 5, the easier it gets to slide further in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:16:04-07:00","id":97837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=97767#post97767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It certainly gets the idea in a just quick look.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just a quick question, if Harmony is not rolled for anything anymore... do we really need it on a numbered 0-10 scale? Can't we simply have the scale with one size saying Spirit and the other Man or something?<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit</b> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">ooooo<b>o</b>ooooo</span> <b>Man</b></div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't believe having the numbers is mandatory, it certainly can help. That way the numbers can be referenced in regards to specific breaking points. Otherwise it can be pretty convoluted trying to describe what level you are at.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:19:03-07:00","id":97842,"title":"","content":"Health track has modifiers atached and does without numbering the dots, for example, so it's not without precedent either.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It does get more convulted than just referencing <b>Wisdom 4</b> (for example) if we have to say <b>Wisdom 1 towards Spirit</b> so maybe the idea is not worth it as it will trade one complication (isn't Wisdom 3 worse than 7?) for another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 03-24-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:32:36-07:00","id":97852,"title":"","content":"One problem with having the track without numbers would be NPC stats. How would you show their Harmony without printing their track?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T18:20:38-07:00","id":97945,"title":"","content":"A valid point. I think descriptors could work for that though. I mean how do the players know how far along someone is without discriptions anyway? Its not like the story teller just hands out their npcs stats at the start of a game.<br /> <br /> So descriptions like &quot;cannot open a door first&quot; or other things showing bans... etc etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T19:05:27-07:00","id":97980,"title":"","content":"Honestly, is anyone besides me pretty much dying to know how bans will come into play with the new Harmony overhaul? I may just be one messed up guy, but I thought the concept of taking bans at lower levels of Harmony was a really fun thing to plan out and roleplay.<br /> <br /> My favorite one had to do with a Hiriraka who was at Harmony 2 mostly because he enjoyed nothing more than a good old Pure slaughter. I decided to go with a stealth thing and at Harmony 5, he was unable to stay in a room that had not been dark for any period of time that he had noticed. This manifested as simply flicking the lights off and on a single time. At Harmony 2 however he was actively destroying light bulbs if they glowed too brightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:43:11-07:00","id":104515,"title":"","content":"I kinda want better senses systems. What do I mean by this? Wolves can detect a fingerprint by scent for weeks after it was laid, if an impostor shows up dressed as one of my characters' packmates I should know immediately when my senses are heightened. Sound is nearly as important. Dogs (and wolves) can differentiate humans by the sound of their footsteps, and of course, can hear sounds far beyond the the human range of hearing. Each emotion we feel leaves behind a distinct pheromone in our sweat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:09:57-07:00","id":104795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=104515#post104515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda want better senses systems. What do I mean by this? Wolves can detect a fingerprint by scent for weeks after it was laid, if an impostor shows up dressed as one of my characters' packmates I should know immediately when my senses are heightened. Sound is nearly as important. Dogs (and wolves) can differentiate humans by the sound of their footsteps, and of course, can hear sounds far beyond the the human range of hearing. Each emotion we feel leaves behind a distinct pheromone in our sweat.</div> </div> </div> </div> It would admittedly be nice, but that false mustache and perfume bath are rather convincing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T07:27:02-07:00","id":104803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/416-the-wolf-must-hunt-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-idigam-chronicles?p=104515#post104515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda want better senses systems. What do I mean by this? Wolves can detect a fingerprint by scent for weeks after it was laid, if an impostor shows up dressed as one of my characters' packmates I should know immediately when my senses are heightened. Sound is nearly as important. Dogs (and wolves) can differentiate humans by the sound of their footsteps, and of course, can hear sounds far beyond the the human range of hearing. Each emotion we feel leaves behind a distinct pheromone in our sweat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last game I ran, I gave the werewolf an automatic +1 to all Perception rolls, even in human form, and in addition to the bonuses they got for changing forms. Once a person starts to get used to being a scent-based quadruped, even the sight-based biped form starts to notice certain smells and sounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T12:35:02-07:00","id":105020,"title":"","content":"I wanna see dog whistles be an imminent threat! Wait... What? Oh in that case maybe just something similar to the new vampire sense rules but more broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}